window.FWN_FEY_EVOLUTION_MERCHANT_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_FEY_EVOLUTION_MERCHANT_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":101,"title":"Chapter 101: Radiance Envoy","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Lin Yuan noticed that his hand was white and slender, but it wasn’t feminine at all as the bone structure and lines were distinct in an appropriate way. When looking at his palm, it was white while blushing red, showing off the unique blood vessels that belonged on the palm.","Is this my hand?","Lin Yuan had always been on the path of a graceful person. When his excellent grace was combined with his sunshine-like appearance, he looked to be reliable, fresh, and tidy.","However, Lin Yuan’s hand wasn’t what it was right now. As an ordinary 18-year-old person, Lin Yuan developed calluses in his palms from all the hard work.","His body might have recovered after being able to sense spirit qi, but the skinny Lin Yuan wasn’t considered fit. Nonetheless, other than his hands, Lin Yuan realized that his body looked as though it was meticulously carved out right now.","Is this the strengthening effect of the Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia’s nectar?","From the moment one’s parents gave birth to them, they would have their own unique gene model. During growth, the genes would develop flaws that would prevent a person from evolving toward the gene model.","The Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia’s nectar capability was to cleanse the body’s impurities and strengthen the foundation. The nectar’s energy compensated for the flaws within the body and allowed the body to evolve toward the flawless gene model.","After leaving the hot spring, the skin would automatically repel the water from the spring. His skin wasn’t exaggeratedly white, as it had a faint honey color.","Lin Yuan walked in front of the mirror and realized that he still looked the same in the mirror, but his looks were far more exquisite. He had a prominent youth’s gracefulness, and it was fused with the fragrance of plants and the warmth from the sun. It formed a truly remarkable aura.","Lin Yuan involuntarily gasped as he actually felt that the person within the mirror was really handsome. But after thinking that the person in the mirror was him, Lin Yuan quickly shook his head.","How can I be such a self-obsessed person!?","For the next few days, Lin Yuan enjoyed the spiritual ingredient delicacies the Moon Empress cooked in the Radiant Moon Palace. However, the Moon Empress didn’t let Lin Yuan know she was the one that cooked the food.","During the day time, the Moon Empress would call for Lin Yuan to visit the breeding room. She wouldn’t teach Lin Yuan anything special and would just allow Lin Yuan to watch as she evolved and enhanced feys.","Lin Yuan was watching seriously. Due to the methods the Moon Empress displayed and Genius’ shared knowledge, Lin Yuan discovered that the appropriate combination of spiritual ingredients could greatly aid the evolution of feys.","Lin Yuan’s method might be drastically different from regular Creation Masters, but it was still incredibly beneficial for Lin Yuan.","As Lin Yuan watched seriously, the Moon Empress was also very delighted and would show her methods in great detail. From time to time, she would even inform and give advice on several things.","It might just be a few short days of contact, but their connection was already not as estranged as the beginning. Lin Yuan was already slowly accepting the Moon Empress as his Master, while the Moon Empress meticulously treated Lin Yuan as her disciple.","The Moon Empress realized that the relationship between a Master and disciple wasn’t as simple as addressing each other so. After accepting each other, the Master and disciple would pour in their heart and affection.","During these few days, Lin Yuan noticed that the Moon Empress didn’t just have the Vine Birds in the breeding room that could act as helpers. There was also a little rabbit that would constantly be eating radish. It seemed like the radish in its hands would never be eaten completely.","Every time Lin Yuan wanted to carry it, the little rabbit would dodge and hop somewhere else to play by itself.","On this day, after the Moon Empress was finished nurturing feys, she called for Lin Yuan and asked, “What plans do you have afterward?”","Lin Yuan pondered for a moment before answering the Moon Empress’ question. “I am planning to open a store in the Royal Capital next year. I will need to return to the Xia Region and handle some matters.”","The Moon Empress nodded in response and said, “Be it a Creation Master or spirit qi professional, there will be plenty of encounters along the way, like adventures into dimensional rifts, or capturing feys in primitive forests or the barren rivers. All these are things that must be experienced. Going to the Royal Capital is indeed a great choice.”","Lin Yuan nodded. This world was massive, and it was basically without any boundaries. He was striving to increase his strength in order to have the capability to venture into this world.","However, Lin Yuan had another ambition, and that was to become a member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence. As such, Lin Yuan spoke of his thoughts and received a refreshing smile from the Moon Empress.","“Then you need to work hard! Since you are thinking of competing for the Radiance Hundred Sequence, then I shall also tell you that the Radiance Hundred Sequence is only the beginning. The Radiance Hundred’s system is to pick out candidates for Radiance Envoys.”","Radiance Envoy was a term that Lin Yuan heard for the first time. He had never heard of it, be it in the news or the Star Web.","The Moon Empress looked at Lin Yuan and said, “There are only five Radiance Envoys, and they are the Radiance Federation’s true steel-like pillars among the young generation. The Radiance Envoys would only be selected from the Radiance Hundred Sequence.”","After speaking, the Moon Empress muttered for a moment and continued speaking, “The Radiance Federation is massive, but this world doesn’t just have the Radiance Federation. The Freedom Federation and the Azure Federation are also comparable with the Radiance Federation. These three major federations are on par. There is also a group that was formed up by 100 smaller federations. The Radiance Envoys represent the Radiance Federation’s youth federations to compete with the young generations from other federations.”","The Moon Empress’ words shocked Lin Yuan. The Radiance Federation was also so massive that it was hard to find the borders, but there were actually two more federations that could compete with the Radiance Federation. With the addition of over 100 smaller federations, Lin Yuan truly couldn’t imagine the size of the world map.","Radiance Envoy was a term that made Lin Yuan’s blood boil. It was a combination of honor and also a mission. The responsibility of the Radiance Envoy was to achieve glory, and it was an immense task.","The Moon Empress patted Lin Yuan’s shoulder while her eyes were filled with encouragement and eagerness. Previously, when Lin Yuan had expressed his intention to rely on himself, the Moon Empress had really been having a headache. However, the Moon Empress was also proud of Lin Yuan’s choice, and such a personality was something that was hard not to admire. Nonetheless, as a mentor, the Moon Empress wouldn’t do less than what was required of her.","“The Spirit Guards have information that there is an anomaly at the River Luster Forest, and the situation isn’t clear yet. After a period of time, I will bring you there to take a look.”","Lin Yuan’s eyes lit up as he had yet to really see the outside world, especially the wilderness, mountains, and forests.","There were plenty of feys in the wild, and feys controlled each piece of territory. This didn’t allow regular people to enter. Now that there was a chance, Lin Yuan was rather excited.","“You can go and shop around in the Royal Capital for the next few days. Apart from the Radiance Hundred Sequence, you can even create your own guild club if you have some thoughts. Guild clubs are allowed to form a five-man team to fight in guild battles. The top-ranked teams aren’t inferior to the Radiance Hundred Sequence. There are plenty of Sequence members from the Radiance Hundred that are part of the five-man teams in these guilds.”","The Moon Empress had already put in plenty of work to teach Lin Yuan. During the last few days, the Moon Empress’ conversations with Lin Yuan contained more words than what she would normally utter for two months.","Even if it was some of the minor details, the Moon Empress would explain clearly. The forming of a guild club flashed in Lin Yuan’s mind, and he was actually rather interested."]},{"number":102,"title":"Chapter 102: Plans for Departure","paragraphs":["Lin Yuan was only interested in establishing his own guild club for a moment before he gave up on the idea. It wasn’t the correct timing to form a guild club now.","A guild club’s function was to nurture one’s own team—a team of five members that were appointed to participate in combat competitions. To find teammates for combat, it was truly a task that must be meticulous. Teammates during combat must be able to trust each other mutually. Only with mutual trust would a team be able to exhibit the strongest combat power.","A strong team never relied on any hero ideology. Each of the members would have their own roles, power offense, agile offense, defense, control, support, healing, and many other aspects to achieve the balance. It was the strongest combination that would be able to present the best state of the team.","In terms of the choice of teammates, Lin Yuan would be very cautious. He, too, knew that he wasn’t qualified to form a team as of now. After all, he was still too weak. It wouldn’t be late to start planning after he reached the 100th floor of the Star Tower and entered the Celestial Stairway.","Before leaving, the Moon Empress called out to Lin Yuan and tossed an exquisite pendant. “Take this.”","Lin Yuan received it and realized that it was a leaf-shaped pendant, which was just like a jade carving. Instead of saying that it was suitable to be worn on the neck, Lin Yuan felt it was more suitable to be a brooch on the chest.","Noticing that Lin Yuan was observing this leaf-shaped brooch, the Moon Empress explained, “This is a Diamond fey storage box. There are corpses of all sorts of dimensional lifeforms. From Class 1 dimensional lifeforms for bronze-grade to Class 4 dimensional lifeforms for platinum-grade. Don’t you have a source-type lifeform? You can use these dimensional lifeform corpses to feed it.”","After speaking, the Moon Empress made a gesture, stating that Lin Yuan could leave. She then continued to concoct the spirit fluid in her hand.","When leaving the Moon Empress’ breeding room, Lin Yuan was holding the leaf-shaped brooch.","I already heard that the Diamond fey storage box developed by Ostrich Logistics is normally used as high-grade accessories, and it is entirely different from fey storage boxes below platinum-grade.","Lin Yuan didn’t have any concept of it until now. He held this delicate brooch—a Diamond fey storage box—and allowed his spirit qi to pour in. Lin Yuan could see there was a football-field space within the Diamond fey storage box. All sorts of dimensional lifeform corpses were already sorted by their classes.","If these corpses were fed to Red Thorn, it was probable that Red Thorn might evolve to bronze-grade in no time. Apart from the corpses, Lin Yuan noticed there were two pots of strange plants growing in the corner.","Lin Yuan used his True Data to check and realized they were two Platinum production-type feys. One of the pots was a Cane Luffa, and it was especially used as nutritional fodder for omnivorous feys. The other was the Celery Vine, a rare nutritional food for herbivorous feys.","Be it the Platinum Cane Luffa or the Celery Vine, they were both several times more expensive than the Platinum Usnea.","Platinum Usneas were considered extremely rare production-type feys. After reaching platinum-grade, the production quantity of the Usneas would be astonishingly huge. A single pot of Platinum Usnea would be able to produce 100 Platinum Usnea vines to feed large quantities of feys.","Be it the Cane Luffa or the Celery Vine, their production quantity would be relatively lesser and would only produce enough to feed one or two feys. Therefore, the Platinum Usnea would hold a superior advantage in terms of quantity. However, the Cane Luffa and Celery Vine didn’t just contain energy, but they also contained a trace of effect in activating innate bloodlines.","As long as a fey could activate its innate bloodline, even the spiritual ingredient price would be expensive. In addition, these were feys that would produce a certain amount of spiritual ingredients every single day.","It seemed like Red Thorn, Chimey, and Genius could have a change in daily food. The Diamond fey storage box was considered a luxury item and was expensive, but as compared to the items contained within the fey storage box, it paled in comparison.","Lin Yuan recalled how the Moon Empress nonchalantly tossed the Diamond fey storage box to him and quickly dismissed him, causing him to feel warmth. It was a kind of concern from seniors that Lin Yuan lacked in his life. Even if he felt such feelings before, it was a long time ago, so Lin Yuan treasured every moment of such sentiments.","After returning to the pavilion that he resided in, Lin Yuan realized that Liu Jie had sent quite a number of messages to him during the past few days. When Lin Yuan read the messages, it turned out that Liu Jie had found a few good spots in the Royal Capital, and they were priced appropriately.","The locations were relatively suitable to open stores, and Lin Yuan couldn’t help but get amazed by Liu Jie’s work efficiency. As a past Sequence member of the Radiance Hundred, even though he had been missing for two years, it was still rather easy for him to find a suitable place to open a store in the Royal Capital.","However, Lin Yuan wasn’t especially satisfied with these stores as they were rather small in space. After seeing the Radiant Moon Palace’s scenic style, where every place was filled with feys, Lin Yuan had an idea. He wanted to design and decorate his store too.","He knew that it would definitely be incomparable with the Radiant Moon Palace, but he wanted to set up a certain style and aura. After the Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus fully recovered in his Spirit Lock spatial zone, Lin Yuan was planning to plant it in his store’s courtyard. Therefore, the store must be bigger.","Otherwise, they would need to shift to another store because there wasn’t enough space. If that was the case, they might as well find a big enough space, and it was fine even if it was in a secluded area. A fine liquor didn’t have to fear being deep in the alley. Lin Yuan was very confident in himself.","Lin Yuan immediately replied to Liu Jie, indicating that he wanted a bigger store.","Lin Yuan felt that since he was already in the Royal Capital, he should arrange a time to meet with Liu Jie tomorrow afternoon.","It had been a few days since Lin Yuan had logged into the Star Web. He noticed that he had received many messages, and most of them had come from a single individual. It was that violent-tempered woman who had visited his store previously. It was already October, and Lin Yuan had promised to heal her daughter’s fey, which had injured roots, after October.","Now that it was October, the violent-tempered woman was obviously unable to sit still.","You Are Finished if I Prick at You[1]: Master, I have already prepared the Revival Soil. I wonder when you are free to take a look at my daughter? I am in the Royal Capital, where do you reside? I can bring my daughter to look for you!","Lin Yuan didn’t expect the violent-tempered woman to be a resident of the Royal Capital. He simply sent a message, arranging to meet her tomorrow morning. The place was set at the Royal Capital’s Creation Master Association.","Lin Yuan didn’t have his own store yet, so if he wanted to heal the injured fey of the violent-tempered woman’s daughter, he could only do it in the Creation Master Association. Class 2 Creation Masters were able to use the breeding rooms in the Creation Master Association for free. After all, Lin Yuan couldn’t bring the violent-tempered woman and her daughter to the Leaning Moon Mountain.","After logging off the Star Web, Lin Yuan stretched himself. He had already arranged for everything tomorrow. After healing the fey in the morning, he could go and look for Liu Jie in the afternoon.","However, Lin Yuan forgot about Cheng Rui, who had been looking at him with jealous eyes, which had turned into resentful eyes now. Cheng Rui would also be in the Royal Capital’s Creation Master Association!","[1] Star Web name for the violent-tempered woman"]},{"number":103,"title":"Chapter 103: Feast for the Eyes?","paragraphs":["On the next morning, the sunlight shone into the pavilion that Lin Yuan was residing in.","Genius curled up its two white tails and laid on Lin Yuan’s stomach. When Genius had been sleeping yesterday night, it might have felt that the clothes on Lin Yuan weren’t comfortable, so it had used its little paws to lift up Lin Yuan’s clothes. Presently, Genius was lying on Lin Yuan’s belly and having a great dream.","Chimey was currently having a great sleep right beside Lin Yuan’s neck. After arriving at the Radiant Moon Palace, Chimey had yet to log into the Star Web, so it didn’t know there was huge unrest in the Star Web when it wasn’t around.","It was fine during the first day of Chimey’s disappearance as many thought it was a normal host’s break. But when it was the second day, the third day, and until one entire week, Chimey’s fans were having a riot. It included Lord Ranger, who was Sequence #87 of the Radiance Hundred and Chimey’s top fan. Everything was unrelated to Lin Yuan and Genius.","The wastrel trio back then had already changed, and they were beyond their previous statuses.","Once Lin Yuan woke up, Genius and Chimey also woke up because of Lin Yuan’s movements.","Early in the morning, Genius and Chimey had been pestering Lin Yuan. Genius was rather composed, but Chimey was extremely mischievous when it was noisy. They only calmed down after Lin Yuan fed Genius the Cane Luffa’s fruit and Chimey the Celery Vine.","It was the first time Genius and Chimey were eating such nice food. Their eyes were sparkling as they ate, and they had satisfied expressions.","As for Red Thorn, Lin Yuan placed it inside the leaf-shaped Diamond fey storage box. Being a source-type lifeform, Red Thorn knew what food was most suitable for itself. Lin Yuan had already planned out Red Thorn’s evolution path, so the insect corpses within the Diamond fey storage box were considered an evolutionary paradise for Red Thorn.","After consuming numerous insect corpses, Red Thorn was now in a deep slumber. During these few days, Red Thorn had already reached Elite VII/Flawless. Lin Yuan asked for Red Thorn to slow down its speed of evolution and to enhance its quality.","Given such a huge amount of alien insect flesh and blood, Lin Yuan believed that Red Thorn wouldn’t need too long to become an Elite/Epic lifeform.","During this period, the people on the Leaning Moon Mountain had already gotten to know Lin Yuan. He wasn’t the one to take the initiative to know people on the Leaning Moon Mountain. It was the people of Leaning Moon Mountain who all urgently wanted to know Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan was the Moon Empress’ disciple, and it might not be officially announced, but anyone clever would be able to see Lin Yuan’s status in the Leaning Moon Mountain. How could any foolish people be residing in a place like the Leaning Moon Mountain?","This morning, Lin Yuan didn’t eat breakfast on the Leaning Moon Mountain. Instead, he went to greet the Moon Empress and departed from the Leaning Moon Mountain early.","Lin Yuan’s first visit to the Royal Capital was when he rode on the Blue Jade Pegasus and had a rough look at the Royal Capital’s thriving state. Since a long time ago, Lin Yuan had wanted to walk around and look around the streets. Finally, there was a chance.","Within the Royal Capital, the thriving situation Lin Yuan had witnessed on the Blue Jade Pegasus’ back and seeing it personally was entirely different.","When walking on the Royal Capital’s main street, Lin Yuan could feel the energetic Royal Capital that was bursting with vitality early in the morning. Lin Yuan couldn’t help but notice several billows of cooking smoke within the prosperous city.","Lin Yuan noticed a small fey store selling golden and tough dough fritters and sesame balls before walking inside.","At first, he only ordered one dough fritter, one sesame ball, and one bowl of mung bean milk. There were plenty of customers seated around.","When Lin Yuan ate these delicacies, he rubbed his stomach and felt that it wasn’t filling at all. Therefore, he ordered a basket of soup buns.","Lin Yuan realized that his appetite had grown significantly after consuming the Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar.","After finishing the meal and paying with the Star Web Card, Lin Yuan didn’t notice that plenty of people were watching him in the shop when he was eating. They were eating at a much faster pace too.","The lady boss, who had constantly been busy in the kitchen, involuntarily muttered after seeing this scene. “Is this what they mean by a feast for the eyes? A handsome person is actually able to increase the appetite? The number of people at the shop today didn’t increase, but from the looks of it, it seems like I will be selling 50% more food than normal!”","After walking out of the shop and in just a few steps, Lin Yuan saw a young couple.","The woman opened up the bottle of coke and drank a mouthful. She then looked at the bottom of the cap and widened her eyes to say, “Hubby, what does ‘another bottle’ mean?”","The man looked at his girlfriend and replied casually, “I don’t know either.”","As a result, the woman simply threw the bottle cap on the ground, and the duo walked away.","Lin Yuan looked at the bottle cap on the ground and took another glance at the Royal Capital’s main street, which didn’t really have a speck of dust. It made this red bottle cap particularly prominent. As such, Lin Yuan simply picked up the bottle cap and just as he was about to throw it into the trash bin by the side...","The big-eyed woman knocked on her boyfriend’s chest and said with a lively tone, “Earlier on, the bottle cap was actually a gift voucher. We made a bet saying you would treat me to a meal tonight! I told you that someone would definitely pick it up!”","Lin Yuan was currently tossing the bottle cap into the trash bin and felt as though a murder of crows flew over his head[1]. Lin Yuan really wanted to go over and say that he didn’t see the wording on the bottle cap. However, Lin Yuan didn’t do so, as it would only make him look like a foolish person.","This lowly couple was really harsh. After showing off their sweet love, they still wanted to make themselves happy over others’ misfortune.","It was actually a kind of habit for Lin Yuan to pick up the bottle cap. It was the same in the small alley outside his small store in Xia Region. If there was anything dirty, Lin Yuan would clean it up himself. If he didn’t do so, the cleaning staff would only come by once a week. It was fine for the first few days, but after the third day, the accumulated dust in the alley would affect the customer’s mood when they entered the store to purchase goods.","Therefore, Lin Yuan would clean up the alley every two days and place all the dirty items into the trash bin. After many days and months, it had turned into Lin Yuan’s habit.","Lin Yuan arrived at a junction and called for a Speed-Hoofed Donkey Car. It was already impossible to see any Thick-Hoofed Donkey Car in the Royal Capital. The Thick-Hoofed Donkeys were Elite feys and were rather slow. The Royal Capital was using Speed-Hoofed Donkeys that were Bronze feys, and their speed was significantly faster.","After riding on the Speed-Hoofed Donkey Car for nearly an hour, Lin Yuan arrived at the Royal Capital’s Creation Master Association. The distance to the Royal Capital’s Creation Master Association was much further than he imagined. Of course, it also proved how massive the Royal Capital was.","Lin Yuan was wearing the Class 2 Creation Master crest on his chest, so someone welcomed him as soon as he entered the Royal Capital’s Creation Master Association. Lin Yuan booked an ordinary Class 2 Creation Master’s breeding room, and just as he finished booking the room, he saw the violent-tempered woman with a frail-looking girl, whose eyes didn’t have any brightness. They were standing in the corner of the main hall.","Seeing that Lin Yuan was walking toward the mother and daughter, the attendant quickly said to Lin Yuan, “They said they arranged an appointment with a Creation Master here. Therefore, I allowed them to enter. If you feel uncomfortable, I can immediately chase them out.”","Lin Yuan quickly shook his head, but he suddenly heard a rather familiar voice. “Who is the one that received these two individuals?! How can the Creation Master Association allow anyone to enter and stand in the main hall? Do they have an appointment?”","Lin Yuan looked toward the voice, and it was none other than Cheng Rui. However, Cheng Rui didn’t look the same as he was a few days ago. He was insufferably bossy and domineering!","[1] It is to express an awkward situation"]},{"number":104,"title":"Chapter 104: Kicked","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Lin Yuan frowned after hearing the statement. Cheng Rui’s insufferably arrogant words were truly stinging to the ears. It felt as though he treated the violent-tempered woman and her daughter as lower lifeforms. In fact, he didn’t even treat the mother and daughter as humans. Otherwise, he wouldn’t be talking with such tone and eyes.","Every Creation Master Association’s management would be different. Most of the rules in the Creation Master Association were set by the current management members. Take the Redbud City’s Creation Master Association, for example. They had very lenient requirements for people participating in the Creation Master exams. They just required proof that they passed three primary lifestyle-class spirit qi occupation exams and could register for the Creation Master exam.","In the Royal Capital’s Creation Master Association, before the three lifestyle-class spirit qi occupation’s exams were verified to be done, no one was permitted to enter the Creation Master Association for the exam. Furthermore, the Royal Capital’s Creation Master Association canceled the services they previously provided for people to take the knowledge occupation exams in the Creation Master Association.","When compared like this, it was obvious that Redbud City’s Creation Master Association was much more amiable. The harsh management rules of the Royal Capital’s Creation Master Association were subtly raising the bar for the status of Creation Masters that were already very high. It wasn’t a friendly place at all.","The attendant that was serving Lin Yuan earlier hurried and bowed to Cheng Rui. He then spoke in a tone that was trying to curry favor. “Young Master Cheng, this pair of mother and daughter said they arranged an appointment with a Creation Master. Therefore, I allowed them to enter.”","When Cheng Rui heard the response, he looked at the mother and daughter with disdain and asked, “What is the name of the Creation Master you arranged an appointment with? Report his name and let Xiao Zhang check!”","The attendant who served Lin Yuan earlier was also Xiao Zhang, so he quickly patted his chest as a guarantee. He then sneaked a glance at Lin Yuan, who he abandoned at the side. In Xiao Zhang’s mind, Lin Yuan was a new Class 2 Creation Master, and even though he was young, he looked talented at a single glance. However, when compared with Cheng Rui, Lin Yuan was pale in comparison.","In actual fact, it wasn’t due to the difference in talent. Cheng Rui’s status was already there as he wasn’t just known as the No.1 Creation Master of the young generation, but he had even gotten the Tribunal Sun title when he was just a Class 2 Creation Master. Most importantly, Cheng Rui’s grandfather was a pinnacle Class 4 Creation Master.","Just based on Cheng Rui’s grandfather, there wasn’t a single attendant in the Royal Capital’s Creation Master Association that wouldn’t spend the effort to curry favor with Cheng Rui.","The violent-tempered woman stood there in a daze. She had conversed with Lin Yuan on the Star Web and only knew of Lin Yuan’s Star Web name, but she couldn’t possibly give Lin Yuan’s Star Web name, right!? If she was to say of it now, she might just be treated as a nuisance and be chased away.","When Cheng Rui saw that the violent-tempered woman was staying silent for a long time, he threw the documents on the table harshly. It scared the girl with the lifeless eyes so much that she withdrew into the violent-tempered woman’s embrace.","The violent-tempered woman’s fiery temperament was now completely held back in the Creation Master Association, but she was shivering after getting treated in this way by Cheng Rui.","Cheng Rui cast a glance at Xiao Zhang and yelled, “Chase them out! How dare they come to create trouble in the Creation Master Association? Ban them from entering the Creation Master Association for an entire year!”","The violent-tempered woman’s head was filled with sweat. Her daughter’s fey was injured in the roots, and it must not be dragged on anymore. If this dragged on, it would only be wasting her daughter’s potential.","During the past year, the violent-tempered woman would feel a stabbing pain in her heart whenever she saw how her lively daughter had transformed into the current daughter with lifeless eyes.","Lin Yuan was now feeling extremely agitated in his heart, and at the same time, he had an extremely bad impression of the Royal Capital’s Creation Master Association. It was evident that this wasn’t Cheng Rui’s first time doing something like that. Such actions would definitely be seen by the management of the Royal Capital’s Creation Master Association. Therefore, it was only possible if the management was silently consenting to Cheng Rui’s behavior.","Just as Xiao Zhang was about to chase the violent-tempered woman out, Lin Yuan came over and said, “Her appointment is with me! I have already booked a breeding room. Bring us there now.”","When the violent-tempered woman saw Lin Yuan, her eyes were instantly filled with brilliance. She quickly pulled her daughter and called out to Lin Yuan as a ‘Master’.","The attendant was also delighted after seeing Lin Yuan as he finally didn’t have to chase anyone out. Those who came to the Royal Capital’s Creation Master Association were either experts or respected individuals. They were spirit qi professionals that were here to evolve their feys or to upgrade the quality of their feys. Of course, some had been gathering funds for a long time to heal their feys with injured roots. These people with injured feys were considered pitiful people, after all.","The world of spirit qi professionals was a pragmatic world, and it was more so in the world of Creation Masters.","The Royal Capital’s Creation Master Association could perfectly describe what it meant to trouble heroes with money.","Cheng Rui’s insufferably arrogant expression suddenly went berserk after hearing Lin Yuan’s words. All of the resentment within his heart was spread toward his eyes.","Just as Xiao Zhang was about to bring Lin Yuan to the breeding room, Cheng Rui let out a strange peal of laughter out of everyone’s expectation. Cheng Rui walked near and stood less than one meter away from Lin Yuan. He looked at the Creation Master crest on Lin Yuan’s right chest and said, “I originally thought that you would be able to succeed that day! It turns out that you failed too!”","When a low-class Creation Master had a Master that was a Class 4 Creation Master or above, they would have a master-disciple relationship. The disciple would then include a mark on their Creation Master crest that belonged to their Master.","When Cheng Rui had found out that he no longer had any chances of taking the Moon Empress as his Master, he already had an additional Spine Gu’s pattern added to his Class 2 Creation Master’s crest, which had two stars.","The Spine Gu looked life-like, and even then, the golden rings were drawn with extreme detail.","Cheng Rui had already gotten his grandfather to be his Master. Therefore, his Creation Master crest naturally included Cheng Wu’s pinnacle Class 4 Creation Master’s mark.","Cheng Rui had only worn this new Creation Master crest for a few days. When Cheng Rui saw that Lin Yuan’s crest was still empty, he felt silently delighted in his heart. At the same time, the resentment in his heart produced a sinister and cruel feeling.","Cheng Rui knew that he wasn’t a match for Long Tao and couldn’t do anything to Long Tao, so he shifted all his hatred toward Lin Yuan. Cheng Rui then shifted his eyes toward the violent-tempered woman and said, “You called him ‘Master’? Is he even worthy? He is just someone with dogshit luck.”","After Cheng Rui finished speaking, he heard an extremely pleasant voice that was clear and distinct. But in the ears of Cheng Rui, it sounded extremely stinging. “Luck is also a kind of capability. It is true that a Class 2 Creation Master is far from being worthy of being called a ‘Master’, so you aren’t worthy either!”","Cheng Rui was filled with disbelief, as he had already investigated Lin Yuan’s background previously.","“You were born in a lowly place like Redbud City’s Xia Region. How can a person of such lowly status dare to be so rude to me!? You even dared to talk back!”","Subconsciously, Cheng Rui returned with a classic criticism to ask about the mother with vulgarity. However, before Cheng Rui could even react, he was kicked in the stomach by Lin Yuan and fell backward."]},{"number":105,"title":"Chapter 105: Immeasurable Importance","paragraphs":["Cheng Rui was stupefied by this kick and felt a wringing pain in his stomach. Since young, this was the first time Cheng Rui was kicked in his stomach, and he was sent falling onto the ground.","Cheng Rui only had one thought in his mind, and it was constantly being repeated.","How dare he!","After consuming the Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar, Lin Yuan’s spirit qi professional rank hadn’t increased, and he was still a C-rank spirit qi professional. However, Lin Yuan’s body had a significant increase in strength. When furious, Lin Yuan’s kick caused Cheng Rui to suffer quite badly.","If Cheng Rui wasn’t a C-rank spirit qi professional, too, his gastric juices might have been vomited out.","The attendant, Xiao Zhang, didn’t think there would be anyone who would dare to make a move in the Royal Capital’s Creation Master Association, especially when it was to beat up Cheng Rui.","Xiao Zhang quickly went over to help Cheng Rui up. However, Cheng Rui was so pale while he held onto his stomach. Even after being supported by Xiao Zhang, Cheng Rui still wasn’t able to get up.","The violent-tempered woman and her daughter were flabbergasted by the sudden change of events.","After Lin Yuan gave his kick, he still had an extremely unpleasant expression. Parental love was always in the most sacred place within Lin Yuan’s heart. He might have lost his parents at a young age, but for the young Lin Yuan who had transmigrated, he remembered every moment in his heart.","After Cheng Rui insulted his parents, Lin Yuan was so angered that he actually couldn’t restrain himself from kicking him. Lin Yuan was a person of great temper, and after handling the fey store and encountering all sorts of customers from a young age, he was already rather trained. Despite that, when the sacred place in his heart was disturbed, Lin Yuan didn’t hesitate to use all his strength to execute this kick of anger.","This was also the first time in eighteen years that Lin Yuan had used violence on others.","After a long moment, Cheng Rui was finally able to stand up with Xiao Zhang’s support. Cheng Rui ground his teeth and looked at Lin Yuan with vicious eyes. “You actually dared to hit me! Not only so, you actually dared to make a move in the Royal Capital’s Creation Master Association! Such audacity!”","Cheng Rui then pushed away Xiao Zhang’s support and said in a cold voice, “Why are you still holding me for? Hurry up and call the enforcer here. Even if he is a Class 2 Creation Master, if he dares to make a move in the Royal Capital’s Creation Master Association, he shall not leave this place!”","Once Cheng Rui’s statement ended, an aged voice yelled out with rage, “Cheng Rui! Are you insane?! What are you shouting for?”","Lin Yuan looked toward the voice and realized that he had seen this person before—it was none other than Elder Du that he had met at the Radiant Moon Palace.","Elder Du walked to Lin Yuan’s side and smiled as he said, “Lin Yuan, why didn’t you tell me that you were coming to the Royal Capital’s Creation Master Association? If you are visiting again next time, you just have to look for me directly. Tell me any request you have, and I shall arrange it for you.”","Lin Yuan might have a bad impression of the Royal Capital’s Creation Master Association, but since Elder Du was a Class 4 Creation Master, Lin Yuan still nodded with respect.","Cheng Rui was now filled with shock and anger. After seeing Elder Du’s attitude toward Lin Yuan, Cheng Rui involuntarily recalled everything that happened in the Radiant Moon Palace. He then said loudly to Elder Du, “Elder Du, he actually made a move in the Royal Capital’s Creation Master Association! We must punish him! Otherwise, how can the Creation Master Association retain its authority!?”","Elder Du frowned and looked at Cheng Rui with unpleasant eyes, while his heart was cursing at Cheng Rui. Because of this ignorant child, Envoy Cold Moon berated me, and he nearly brought huge trouble to me. Yet he didn’t learn his lesson and is still stirring trouble?","Cheng Wu might have already arrived in the Royal Capital’s Creation Master Association, but he had been in seclusion ever since. Thus, Elder Du still hadn’t had time to report to Cheng Wu about Cheng Rui’s matters.","Cheng Rui might be a member of the Royal Capital’s Creation Master Association while he was the Vice President, but Cheng Rui was still the grandson of the pinnacle Class 4 Creation Master, Cheng Wu. If Elder Du disciplined Cheng Rui without permission, it might cause Cheng Wu to have a bad opinion of Elder Du.","Therefore, Elder Du had constantly been waiting for Cheng Wu to exit from seclusion.","But now, Cheng Rui was actually causing trouble again. Elder Du spoke in a cold tone. “Cheng Rui, have you not acted violently in the association many times? If there is any punishment to be given, it shall be given to you first!”","Elder Du looked at the enforcers that were surrounding the scene and yelled, “You are all dismissed! What are you trying to do by making such a din in the main hall!?”","Elder Du then asked the attendant Xiao Zhang to stay behind and find out the exact situation.","Elder Du was the Vice President of the Creation Master Association, and Xiao Zhang didn’t even have the chance to speak with Elder Du during normal times. Now that Elder Du was asking, Xiao Zhang explained all the details and even told of Lin Yuan’s request.","Elder Du’s face was turning increasingly unpleasant as he listened, and by the end, it was completely darkened. He glared at Cheng Rui before saying to Lin Yuan, “Come, let this old one bring you to my breeding room. You may use it as you please.”","Lin Yuan shook his head and pointed at the violent-tempered woman before replying, “There is no need to trouble Elder Du. I am just here to help a friend to heal the fey’s injured roots. An ordinary breeding room is good enough.”","Elder Du laughed heartily and said, “There is no trouble at all! Since that is the case, let me bring you to the Class 2 Creation Master’s breeding room. It just so happens that I am going upstairs too.”","Elder Du then led Lin Yuan upstairs. The violent-tempered woman followed behind and was completely stunned.","After a conflict, it was actually the Vice President of the Royal Capital’s Creation Master Association that personally resolved the problem. Furthermore, the Vice President seemed to be leaning toward this youth that was walking in front of her.","What background does this youth have, and how influential is his background?","In fact, the violent-tempered woman wasn’t the only person to think like this. Everyone in the Royal Capital’s Creation Master Association was also looking at the figure of that youth that vanished toward the stairs. Cheng Rui was left behind with an ashen expression, while his hand was still holding onto his stomach that had just been kicked.","Cheng Rui didn’t know what Elder Du was thinking. Just by looking at Lin Yuan’s Creation Master crest, Elder Du should know that Lin Yuan didn’t manage to become the Moon Empress’ disciple.","If Elder Du found out about Cheng Rui’s thoughts now, he might have burst out all of his suppressed anger earlier and given Cheng Rui a huge slap.","Elder Du had already noticed the Creation Master crest on Lin Yuan’s chest. However, not every Creation Master would allow their newly accepted disciple to wear their symbolized crest. Some Creation Masters would temper their disciples and choose to make them wear regular crests, not allowing their disciples to receive special privileges.","Apart from that, some disciples wouldn’t wear their masters’ symbolized crest on their chest. After all, not everyone wanted to use their masters’ reputation and wanted to rely on themselves.","The Moon Empress, Bamboo Monarch, and Chef Supreme would never wear the only three Class 5 Creation Master crest on their chests. But did that mean that the three esteemed individuals weren’t Creation Masters?","However, Elder Du overestimated Cheng Rui. It was natural for Cheng Rui, who wanted to show off all of his glory and trump cards, not to understand such things.","Elder Du had just returned after going to send off Ling Xiao, who was preparing to return to Redbud City. From the conversation with Ling Xiao, Elder Du had found out that the youth in front of him was no longer an ordinary youth, but someone with immeasurable importance!"]},{"number":106,"title":"Chapter 106: Road of Redemption","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Cheng Rui left the first floor of the Creation Master Association silently and immediately headed for the breeding room where his grandfather was in seclusion. Just as he was hesitating to open the door and call for his grandfather, his face revealed a complex expression. It was a mix of resentment and fear.","Finally, as he gritted his teeth and prepared to open the door, it was the door that opened up first. An elder with black glossy hair stepped out of the door.","Cheng Rui didn’t expect that his grandfather would end his seclusion at this moment. He quickly greeted, “Grandfather, after this seclusion, your hair is now completely black. It is another progress!”","The elder laughed, but his laughter contained a little feminine tone. “During this seclusion, the Gold Ring Spine Gu has upgraded from Fantasy IV to Fantasy V. I didn’t waste ten years of effort for nothing!”","After hearing the news, Cheng Rui’s face was delighted at first, but he suddenly changed to a pitiful tone and said, “Grandfather, look at the Creation Master crest on my chest. I didn’t succeed in becoming the Moon Empress’ disciple.”","The elder looked at where Cheng Rui pointed and frowned. “The Royal Capital’s Creation Master Association has already created a commotion by giving you a title as a Class 2 Creation Master. You are also the No.1 Creation Master among the young generation, and you still failed?”","The elder then continued looking at the crest on Cheng Rui’s chest as he carried on talking. “Change your crest too, and wear a regular Class 2 Creation Master crest. I am your grandfather. Why are you making me your Master by wearing this crest? Finding a Master is to allow you to have one more reliance. Elder Du is rather nice to you. I will look for him later and see if he is willing to accept you as his disciple.”","Cheng Rui took down the crest on his chest embarrassedly. But after hearing his grandfather mention Elder Du, Cheng Rui’s face changed. If his grandfather looked for Elder Du, Elder Du would surely tell his grandfather of his actions in the Radiant Moon Palace. By then, he would definitely have to suffer a beating.","But now, Cheng Rui hated Lin Yuan to the extreme. He had a hot flash in his heart, while his eyes flickered before he said, “Grandfather, I didn’t get the preference of the Moon Empress in the Radiant Moon Palace mainly because Redbud City’s Lordess Ling Xiao brought a youth with her.”","Cheng Wu’s pupils contracted as he knew his grandson too well. If it was a matter of vengeance, Cheng Rui would have already taken revenge. Now that Cheng Rui was looking for him, it meant that he wasn’t able to resolve it and was looking for his help.","“What background does the youth have for Ling Xiao to bring him to the Radiant Moon Palace?”","Cheng Rui then spoke of the information that he had found out about Lin Yuan. It was rather easy to find information on Lin Yuan. Since Lin Yuan had registered as a Class 2 Creation Master, the Redbud City’s Creation Master Association had already obtained simple information about him.","Cheng Wu listened and looked at Cheng Rui. “You can’t even settle a young Class 2 Creation Master yourself? You have to look for me?”","Cheng Rui suddenly squeezed out two drops of tears and said with a grievance, “Elder Du has a preference toward him. Earlier on, when he kicked me, Elder Du still defended him.”","Cheng Rui then lifted up his shirt after speaking, and even he was immediately shocked. He started to curse at Lin Yuan repeatedly as his stomach now had a purple footprint.","Cheng Rui knew that his grandfather was most afraid of him crying, so he would always do this to beg for his grandfather’s help. There was nothing that couldn’t be done. In addition, this wasn’t the first time he had sought out revenge.","When Cheng Wu saw the footprint on Cheng Rui’s stomach, his face turned dark as he yelled out, “That nobody Du is the one that invited me to the Royal Capital’s Creation Master Association. Now he actually watches as someone else bullies my grandson! Does he even have me, Cheng Wu, in his eyes?!”","Cheng Wu only had one grandson, and when Cheng Rui was young, his first fey had been a small Spine Gu that had split off from Cheng Wu’s source-type lifeform, the Gold Ring Spine Gu. Because of that, Cheng Rui had suffered badly. Also, Cheng Rui’s parents had passed away when Cheng Rui was young, while Cheng Wu couldn’t spend much time with Cheng Rui due to his status as a Class 4 Creation Master. Therefore, Cheng Wu always felt that he owed something to Cheng Rui.","Upon seeing the purple footprint on his grandson’s stomach, the eyes of Cheng Wu, who had a fiery personality, turned gloomy.","When Cheng Rui noticed that, he heaved a sigh of relief in his heart. His grandfather’s expression indicated that he was going to help with his revenge.","“Grandfather, you can’t blame Elder Du either. That kid, Lin Yuan, is rather talented.”","Cheng Wu said in a sinister tone, “What use is talent? Being able to grow up is real capability! Have you forgotten that I taught you to either endure or be ruthless!?”","Cheng Rui quickly replied, “I remember grandfather, so I wish to stomp on him personally! I want to watch as my Spine Gu empties out his spinal cord!”","After a short conversation between the grandfather and the grandson, they left the Royal Capital’s Creation Master Association silently.","Presently, Lin Yuan was checking on a pitiful fey. It was a Bronze Tough Leaf Chrysanthemum.","A healthy Tough Leaf Chrysanthemum was considered a rather good, power offense-type fey. The chrysanthemum leaves could be flung out like a flying blade, dealing slicing damage and slight paralysis poison.","The petals of the chrysanthemum could gather energy quickly and shoot out poisonous energy.","But this Tough Leaf Chrysanthemum in front of Lin Yuan already had withered stems. The petals and leaves looked like they were dehydrated, and they were struggling just to stay up.","The petals looked as though they were about to fall off, and there were only a few stamens left.","The violent-tempered woman stood nearby and asked Lin Yuan apprehensively, “Master, is there a possibility to heal this Tough Leaf Chrysanthemum?”","When asking this question, the violent-tempered woman’s heart tensed up. Previously, she had looked for other Creation Masters. She had spent half a year seeking connections and plenty of money to get help from a Class 2 Creation Master.","As a result, the answer had been negative. It was unknown whether that Class 2 Creation Master had found it troublesome to heal the fey, or he purely had not wanted to do it.","Of course, no matter what the reason was, the violent-tempered woman wasn’t qualified to question him because the law of survival existed between spirit qi professionals and Creation Masters.","Lin Yuan looked at the state of the Tough Leaf Chrysanthemum and didn’t hesitate when he nodded and replied, “Yes.”","This Tough Leaf Chrysanthemum might look miserable and might die at any moment, but with Lin Yuan’s current healing capability, healing a Bronze fey with damaged roots wasn’t a problem at all.","When Lin Yuan was a D-rank spirit qi professional, he was already able to heal the damaged roots of Bronze feys.","It just so happened that he could use this opportunity to see what the healing speed for Bronze feys was, now that he was a C-rank spirit qi professional.","The instant Lin Yuan nodded, the violent-tempered woman suddenly started to wail. It felt as though everything she had suppressed for a long time was finally given relief.","She was smiling while she was crying. It was tears of joy and happiness mixed within a tart feeling.","The violent-tempered woman’s daughter’s eyes were dull and not very lively. The moment Lin Yuan nodded, her eyes turned bright as she fixed her gaze on Lin Yuan. She then revealed a pleasantly surprised smile.","When Lin Yuan saw the smiles, he felt touched for a moment. These smiles looked as though the light at the end of the tunnel. It made Lin Yuan even more determined to walk on the path as a Creation Master.","A Creation Master’s path shouldn’t be to stand at the top and look down at all people with cold eyes. It should be built up by smiles and rescues, forming a road of redemption."]},{"number":107,"title":"Chapter 107: Corrosive Petals","paragraphs":["In reaction to the mother’s and daughter’s display of emotions, Lin Yuan didn’t know what to say. He wasn’t adept at handling emotional moments. Therefore, he didn’t know how to deal with others’ bursts of emotions.","As such, he said, “Go to the rest lounge outside the breeding room first. It will take a little time. Once I heal the roots of the Tough Leaf Chrysanthemum, I will inform you to enter.”","The mother and daughter’s best consolation was to heal the Tough Leaf Chrysanthemum’s injured roots quickly.","When the violent-tempered woman heard Lin Yuan’s words, she quickly scratched her head and repeatedly thanked Lin Yuan. She then led her daughter to the rest lounge outside the breeding room.","Lin Yuan calmed his mind and circulated the spiritual power within his body to inject the spirit qi into this Tough Leaf Chrysanthemum, which was considered withered.","During the spirit qi circulation process, Lin Yuan could feel that his spirit qi circulation speed was several times faster.","When the Tough Leaf Chrysanthemum received healing from the spirit qi, it underwent an immediate transformation.","The first to recover was the rhizome, which was already withered. It was now rapidly growing white root structures.","In just a short moment, the white roots had already replaced the previously withered roots.","Lin Yuan used his hands to rub at the withered portion of the roots. They all started to fall off like a shattered layer of skin.","The Tough Leaf Chrysanthemum was constantly growing new flower petals too. Soon, all of the flower petals recovered too. However, the color of the petals was still rather pale.","Lin Yuan took a bottle of mountain spring water from the breeding room’s table and poured it on the roots. He then continued to circulate the spirit qi.","It took less than 20 minutes to recover the Tough Leaf Chrysanthemum’s injured roots. This time, Lin Yuan didn’t even use the Pure Land of Bliss to heal the Tough Leaf Chrysanthemum.","During the Class 2 Creation Master exam, Lin Yuan had taken two hours to recover the Bronze Shear Pincers Crab’s injured roots. That was when Lin Yuan had used Morbius’ exclusive skill, Pure Land of Bliss. If he hadn’t used the Pure Land of Bliss, he would have needed around four hours.","But now, Lin Yuan didn’t use the Pure Land of Bliss, yet he only used 20 minutes to heal the roots of a Bronze fey.","Using simple calculations, after promoting to a C-rank spirit qi professional, Lin Yuan’s speed of healing a Bronze fey was now faster by nearly ten times.","It might also be because Lin Yuan had purified his body’s impurities after drinking a bowl of Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar. Even if that was the case, after promoting to a C-rank spirit qi professional, Lin Yuan’s Creation Master capability underwent an overwhelming transformation.","Lin Yuan might still be slightly below the standard of a Class 3 Creation Master, but it wasn’t significant.","After sensing that the Tough Leaf Chrysanthemum was now healthy, Lin Yuan let out a breath.","The Tough Leaf Chrysanthemum’s petals were now plump, and the leaves were also massive. The edges of the leaves looked particularly sharp too.","However, due to the Tough Leaf Chrysanthemum’s injured roots, its entire body was severely dehydrated and still required a large replenishment of water.","Half of the bottle of mountain spring water was now absorbed by the Tough Leaf Chrysanthemum. Lin Yuan continued to circulate his spiritual power to replenish the water in the Tough Leaf Chrysanthemum quickly. However, Lin Yuan felt that he encountered a subtle but also rather obvious grade limit.","The grade limit was something that Lin Yuan was familiar with. He checked on the Tough Leaf Chrysanthemum and realized that it was a Bronze X fey. It was just one step away from reaching silver-grade.","Since Lin Yuan could already feel the grade limit, he simply hastened the circulation of spiritual power to break through the limit.","In just a short time, when the spirit qi broke through the grade limit, the Bronze Tough Leaf Chrysanthemum started evolving.","It grew to half a meter in height from its previous 30-centimeter height. The leaves were much more vibrant in color as well. The stem grew out with new leaves. It only had one flower at first, but there were eight flower buds now. The flower buds were all gradually blooming.","The newly grown flowers were much smaller than the first flower, but they would surely grow to a similar size with enough time.","Lin Yuan used True Data to check on the Tough Leaf Chrysanthemum and involuntarily let out a satisfied smile.","[Fey Name]: Tough Leaf Chrysanthemum","[Fey Species]: Chrysanthemum species/genus","[Fey Grade]: Silver (1/10)","[Fey Type]: Grass","[Fey Quality]: Normal","Abilities:","[Leaf Blade]: The leaves on the stem can be shot out for long-distance physical damage.","[Flower Bud Cannon]: Flowers can gather energy to shoot out poisonous energy attacks.","[Corrosive Petals]: Scatter the flower petals to conduct an area attack. The petals have paralysis and corrosive attributes.","Exclusive Skill:","[Enhanced Poison Attributes]: Enhance the poison attributes, causing poison effects to enter deeper.","The Tough Leaf Chrysanthemum didn’t just have a simple physical attack, as it could also use its poison attributes to injure and kill other feys. However, this Tough Leaf Chrysanthemum only had paralysis poison. When used together with the bronze-grade exclusive skill, Enhanced Poison Attributes, it allowed the Tough Leaf Chrysanthemum to deal good damage.","Its silver-grade ability, Corrosive Petals, allowed the Tough Leaf Chrysanthemum to have an additional corrosive attribute on top of the paralysis attribute. When used with Enhanced Poison Attributes, it boosted the Tough Leaf Chrysanthemum’s offense capability.","Paralysis poison provided a great control but weak lethality. However, it was now lethal with the corrosive poison.","The silver-grade ability was also able to provide a great AOE attack. It provided a great combination with Leaf Blade or Flower Bud Cannon.","One could say that the Tough Leaf Chrysanthemum had a very successful evolution.","Lin Yuan’s objective for visiting the Creation Master Association was to fulfill the violent-tempered woman’s promise and help her daughter heal her fey. He had completed his agreed promise now.","Lin Yuan had a feeling that it was rather troublesome to use the breeding room in the Creation Master Association. Therefore, if he was going to accept another request to heal the roots of a fey, he would wait until his store was officially established.","For now, Lin Yuan would mainly accept customized nurturing for feys or to sell precious feys. Doing so would allow him to accumulate Radiance dollars rapidly.","The cultivation of the body was a process of constant progress. All living things in this world would be improving, so it would be a regression if one stagnated.","Lin Yuan called for the violent-tempered woman and her daughter to enter.","When entering the breeding room, the mother and daughter were rather nervous. But after seeing the bigger and entirely different Tough Leaf Chrysanthemum, they were stunned.","Lin Yuan smiled at the violent-tempered woman’s daughter and asked, “Aren’t you able to recognize your own fey?”"]},{"number":108,"title":"Chapter 108: Sudden Ambush","paragraphs":["The violent-tempered woman’s daughter was in a daze. She activated her spiritual energy, and the Tough Leaf Chrysanthemum was withdrawn back into her spiritual spatial zone without any obstruction. She was first pleasantly surprised but immediately widened her mouth in shock. “My Tough Leaf Chrysanthemum should be Bronze, but it is now Silver!”","Lin Yuan nodded. “This Tough Leaf Chrysanthemum has good potential. Its silver-grade ability has quite a good lethality, and when used together with the other abilities, it gives an overall boost. Next time, if you meet a Horn Demon again, your fey won’t suffer damage to its roots.”","The violent-tempered woman quickly bowed to Lin Yuan and constantly thanked him. She then took out the Revival Soil that she had prepared but was a little hesitant. “Master, previously, our agreement was 500 grams of Revival Soil. I have obtained more, and this bag has 600 grams. However, I didn’t prepare the fee for the evolution from Bronze to Silver. I wonder if you can spare me a few days...”","Lin Yuan took the Revival Soil and shook his hand. “100 grams of extra Revival Soil is enough for the compensation. Furthermore, I am the one that decided to evolve the Tough Leaf Chrysanthemum to Silver and didn’t ask for your opinions. As such, I don’t need extra compensation.”","This bag of Revival Soil wasn’t cheap, and because of the great benefits it had for plant-type feys, its price wasn’t any lower than gold-grade dragon beast blood. A bag of Revival Soil at 600 grams would probably require close to 300 Radiance dollars. This price might still be relatively lower for other Creation Masters to heal a Bronze fey’s roots, but it wasn’t ridiculously cheaper. Moreover, the violent-tempered woman must have used quite the effort to find this bag of Revival Soil.","After speaking, Lin Yuan didn’t give the violent-tempered woman and her daughter any chance to thank him as he took the Revival Soil and left the breeding room.","The violent-tempered woman’s daughter was completely engrossed in the joy of her fey’s recovery and evolution, but the violent-tempered woman’s eyes were moist again.","Living in the Royal Capital might look to be glamorous, but how could anyone know of the pressure and sorrow of an ordinary woman who had to support her daughter? After experiencing a harsh and cold of life, the violent-tempered woman had put on a mask. It was a hard mask to protect the soft insides.","But now, she felt a warm light that was peaceful and powerful. A young and talented Creation Master was actually so kind in nature. It was extremely praiseworthy.","When Lin Yuan left the Royal Capital’s Creation Master Association and took just a few steps, someone called him from behind. Lin Yuan turned around and noticed that it was Elder Du that called him.","Elder Du was walking over quickly and laughed heartily as he said, “Leaving so soon? This card is for you. The next time you revisit the Royal Capital’s Creation Master Association, you can just present this card to the main hall’s attendant, and they will bring you to see me. In the future, I will help you to handle anything you require.”","Lin Yuan received the card from Elder Du. Since it was a gift from an elder, Lin Yuan naturally wouldn’t refuse. However, Lin Yuan didn’t plan to return to the Royal Capital’s Creation Master Association.","Nonetheless, Lin Yuan still said, “I have troubled Elder Du. Elder Du is busy during normal times, so this junior naturally wouldn’t dare to disturb you.”","Elder Du looked at Lin Yuan, and his smile got brighter. Since Lin Yuan had helped him out at the Radiant Moon Palace, coupled with Lin Yuan’s calm and composed attitude and his talent to directly pass the Class 2 Creation Master exam, these factors caused Elder Du to admire Lin Yuan even more.","Elder Du involuntarily made a comparison with Cheng Rui and felt that Cheng Rui was utterly inferior. Upon recalling that he had personally conferred the title of ‘Tribunal Sun’ to Cheng Rui, Elder Du felt a burning pain on his face.","After bidding goodbye to Elder Du, Lin Yuan looked at the time and noticed that it was only 10:00 in the morning. His appointment with Liu Jie was at 15:00, and there were still five hours in between.","Lin Yuan didn’t have any other arrangements, so he contacted Liu Jie. After calling him, Liu Jie informed Lin Yuan that he was currently viewing a house in the suburban area. The houses in the suburban areas were relatively secluded, but their environment was superior.","Instead of saying that it was a house, it was actually a plot of land that took up 5,000 square meters. Beside the land was a small, man-made lake, and the lakewater was from the spring water up the mountain.","The surrounding greenery was rather good too, and it was truly a place with great scenery. However, it was rather secluded, so the large piece of land’s price wasn’t considered too expensive.","As such, Lin Yuan decided to meet Liu Jie in advance to see what the land looked like. After asking for the location, Lin Yuan called for special transportation that was exclusive to the Royal Capital, the Wind Travel Pigeon.","The Wind Travel Pigeon was the Royal Capital’s exclusive flying fey, and it was extremely hard to train. A special Wind Travel Pigeon trainer was required, and the Wind Travel Pigeon would only be able to transport customers after two years of training.","The Wind Travel Pigeon was an extremely popular flying fey in the Royal Capital, and its unique point was that it didn’t need anyone to control it. The trainer simply had to tell the Wind Travel Pigeon to fetch the customer from a certain place to a certain destination.","The Wind Travel Pigeon had evolved from the messenger pigeons after the Spirit Qi Awakening, and it was a Silver fey. The flying speed wasn’t considered fast, but the price wasn’t low either. A single return trip would cost 0.5 Radiance dollars.","Since Lin Yuan was at the Royal Capital, he should try all its specialties. Everyone said that a Wind Travel Pigeon’s back was more comfortable than the softest bed.","Lin Yuan only waited for a moment, and a white pigeon with a three-meter wingspan stopped beside him. Lin Yuan walked over and showed the order on his mobile phone to the Wind Travel Pigeon. The Wind Travel Pigeon then shook its wing and placed it on the ground as an indication for Lin Yuan to get onto its back by stepping on its wing.","When Lin Yuan was riding on the Wind Travel Pigeon’s back, he felt that its feathers were soft and silky. It didn’t feel like a regular feather and was more like top-grade silk.","The Wind Travel Pigeon didn’t fly high nor fast, but the speed was at least five times faster than the Speed-Hoofed Donkey Car. Another unique trait of the Wind Travel Pigeon was that0 the travelers could view the scenery. The objective might be for travel, but the customers on its back were able to admire the Royal Capital’s beautiful view.","As soon as they flew out of the Royal Capital’s city area, they arrived at the northern suburban area. Taking reference to the distance and the Wind Travel Pigeon’s speed, Lin Yuan estimated that he would need around 10 minutes to reach the arranged location he was going to meet with Liu Jie.","Lin Yuan was looking at the scenery of the suburban area. The Wind Travel Pigeon was flying around 25 meters in altitude, while some of the canopy plants like the willow trees were able to reach a height of 20 meters. When flying at a low altitude, Lin Yuan’s breaths were filled with plant fragrance.","At that moment, the Wind Travel Pigeon suddenly let out two intense cooing sounds.","Immediately after, Lin Yuan noticed a gray energy beam hitting the Wind Travel Pigeon’s wings’ left side. The impact of the energy beam was extremely powerful, and even Lin Yuan could feel the pressure. The left half of the Wind Travel Pigeon’s body was blasted open with a wound and a burst of blood mist!"]},{"number":109,"title":"Chapter 109: How Dare You!?","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","After the sudden ambush, the Wind Travel Pigeon rapidly flapped its right wing and was cooing as it fell toward the ground. When the Wind Travel Pigeon was falling, it turned back to look at Lin Yuan with a very anxious feeling.","When it was around three to four meters away from the ground, the Wind Travel Pigeon felt as though it had lost all energy. At the crucial moment, the Wind Travel Pigeon turned and wrapped its right wing around Lin Yuan to protect him. Its head crashed onto the ground as dirt flew up, resulting in instant death.","In fact, when the Wind Travel Pigeon turned to protect Lin Yuan in mid-air, it had already lost its life. When falling from such an altitude, its final form of defense was actually used to protect a complete stranger.","This was just a mission entrusted by the trainer to a fey and the professionalism of a Wind Travel Pigeon as a flying fey.","Since the Wind Travel Pigeon had protected him by using its body to relieve the impact, Lin Yuan didn’t suffer any severe injuries. However, the impact of the fall still made Lin Yuan uncomfortable.","Lin Yuan understood that someone targeted him. He wasn’t a person to form any feud with others, so the only person who would ambush him could only be Cheng Rui.","After emerging from the Wind Travel Pigeon’s right wing, Lin Yuan looked at the Wind Travel Pigeon, which lay on the ground—its eyes were going to be permanently closed. The blast injuries on the left side of the body and the impact from the fall made the Wind Travel Pigeon’s corpse look abnormally miserable.","At that moment, Lin Yuan heard an arrogant and vicious voice. “You didn’t expect this, right!? Since you kicked me, I shall take your life!”","Lin Yuan could see a dark-faced elder standing beside Cheng Rui. When looking at his facial features, Cheng Rui had a slight resemblance to the elder.","An insect-type creature, around the length of an arm, with multiple legs, was crawling on the elder’s shoulder. Evidently, this insect-type creature had shot out the earlier gray energy ray. This multi-legged insect creature was rather familiar to Lin Yuan, and it was rather apparent that it was the Spine Gu’s enlarged version.","However, as compared to the Spine Gu Cheng Rui had summoned during the contest, this Spine Gu had plenty of golden rings on its body. The golden rings gave the sinister Spine Gu a very bizarre appearance.","Lin Yuan didn’t hesitate and circulated his spiritual power to summon Red Thorn and Chimey. At the same time, Genius used Tool Transformation to transform into a pair of glasses for Lin Yuan to wear.","At that moment, Lin Yuan could hear the elder speaking to Cheng Rui. “You can’t even defeat an insect like him? His strongest fey is just Bronze, yet you actually needed to look for me? If you didn’t want to take revenge personally, a casual energy beam from the Gold Ring Spine Gu would have been able to blast this kid and that unlucky Wind Travel Pigeon into pieces.”","Cheng Rui summoned his fey, the Gold Spine Gu, which crawled out of Cheng Rui’s hukou acupoint. It was so painful that Cheng Rui ground his teeth. “Grandfather, had it not been someone protecting him, I would have finished him!”","Cheng Wu frowned and said in an impatient tone, “Then hurry up and make your move. This place might be the suburban area, but to make a move on a Class 2 Creation Master, it will still cause an inevitable commotion.”","Every Creation Master was the Radiance Federation’s capital, and thus, killing a Creation Master was considered a serious matter in the Radiance Federation.","Cheng Rui smiled sinisterly at Lin Yuan and said, “It is not bad that your Creation Master talent is enough for you to be brought to the Radiant Moon Palace! Elder Du is also protective of you. However, your talent will be destroyed in just a moment. After you lose your arms and legs, let’s see what else you can be proud of!”","Lin Yuan unsealed the Spirit-Gather Goldfish’s exclusive skill, Spirit Qi Imprint. All of the spirit qi accumulated by his Bronze Spirit-Gather Goldfish suddenly burst out of the Spirit Qi Imprint on Lin Yuan’s back.","At the same time, Chimey quickly executed Turbulence and used Sound Thrust to attack Cheng Rui. Lin Yuan then poured all his spiritual power into Red Thorn, allowing its spiky vines to rapidly extend and wrap at Cheng Rui.","Lin Yuan had an immense amount of spirit qi, and it was enough for Red Thorn’s vines to instantly extend by 20 meters.","Just as Lin Yuan’s all-out attack was about to reach Cheng Rui, a cold snort resounded, and the Gold Ring Spine Gu on Cheng Wu’s shoulder let out a hissing roar.","A gray energy wave disintegrated all of Lin Yuan’s attacks and severely injured Red Thorn, Chimey, and Genius.","Genius was no longer able to maintain its Tool Transformation state and fell onto the ground beside Lin Yuan. He felt intense pain as there was a hot surge within his stomach, and he vomited fresh blood.","Lin Yuan had been aware that things weren’t going to be good for him, and there wasn’t any chance for resistance. Thus, he had executed an all-out attack on Cheng Rui. Unfortunately, he hadn’t expected for his all-out attack to be easily countered by the Gold Ring Spine Gu’s casual burst of energy.","Cheng Rui was drenched in a cold sweat. Lin Yuan’s sudden attack had been about to reach him and kill him. It made Cheng Rui shocked and afraid, but the resentment in his eyes was even more concentrated now.","Cheng Rui didn’t think that his carelessness had nearly allowed Lin Yuan’s attack to send him to his grave. The shock that Cheng Rui received was instantly converted into overwhelming hatred. The hatred dyed the resentment with colorful mania as Cheng Rui yelled, “If my Spine Gu doesn’t drill your spinal cord empty, I shall give up my family name, Cheng! You just die of a slow and agonizing death as the Spine Gu slowly chew on your spinal cord.”","Lin Yuan struggled to get up. The intense pain ravaging his entire body might just cause Lin Yuan to collapse on the ground again. Lin Yuan wiped off the blood on the corner of his mouth, but the movements aggravated his injuries and made him vomit another mouthful of blood again.","At the same time, the severely injured Chimey, Genius, and Red Thorn also stood up.","Cheng Rui and Cheng Wu adapted their attacking stances. Just as Cheng Rui was about to kick Lin Yuan, Red Thorn shot out a mouthful of corrosive fluid.","Cheng Rui was already prepared as the Spine Gu was brandished like a blade to block Red Thorn’s attack. It also sliced off several of Red Thorn’s vines.","But just as the Spine Gu was attacking at Red Thorn, Chimey let out a weak chirp, sending three Sound Thrusts at Cheng Rui at a close range.","It shocked Cheng Rui, but a forceful wind blocked Chimey’s Sound Thrust. Then, Lin Yuan, Chimey, Genius, and Red Thorn were sent flying back by a few meters again.","Lin Yuan wanted to struggle to stand again, but he couldn’t. Upon seeing Red Thorn, Genius, and Chimey collapsed on the ground, Lin Yuan circulated his leftover spiritual power to withdraw them into his spiritual spatial zone.","Lin Yuan looked at the proud afternoon sun in the sky and felt that it was much more glaring than usual. In this life and death situation, Lin Yuan suddenly felt that the wind by his ears was light and indifferent.","Cheng Wu frowned and looked at the incompetent Cheng Rui. “You nearly died in the hands of this insect twice. Do you not understand that a lion will use all its strength even when hunting a rabbit? I shall teach you another lesson on what is fast and ruthless.”","Just as Cheng Wu’s words faded, the Gold Ring Spine Gu rapidly shrunk down and flew toward Lin Yuan’s spine at the neck. The Gold Ring Spine Gu generated an air-piercing sound as it flew.","Right at that split moment, Lin Yuan suddenly felt that the Royal Capital’s sky had turned dark. A new moon was suspended in the sky, nearly covering the proud afternoon sun, as an enraged voice reverberated throughout the horizon.","“How dare you!?”"]},{"number":110,"title":"Chapter 110: Cold Moon Lone Disk","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","The afternoon sun was shining gloriously when a bright moon suddenly appeared and lit up the entire sky with moonlight.","At that moment, several experts in the Royal Capital lifted their heads simultaneously to look at the cold moon in the sky that covered the sunlight.","Amongst the experts was a 30-year-old man whose eyes resembled a middle-aged man that had gone through countless experiences. He was holding a jade bamboo and frowning with an appalled expression. “It is the Moon Empress’ Cold Moon Lone Disk!”","One had to know that among the Moon Empress’ feys, the Cold Moon Lone Disk was mainly used for killing. What exactly happened for the Moon Empress to summon the Cold Moon Lone Disk?","Opposite the man with the jade bamboo was a middle-aged man in red armor, and he was holding a black stone1. When the cold moon appeared in the sky, the black stone dropped on the board and disrupted the black and white stones. It interrupted the game that was about to settle with a winner.","“Bamboo Monarch, has the Moon Empress’ Cold Moon Lone Disk reached the Myth Breed? I wonder how much stronger is the Cold Moon Lone Disk as compared to back then...”","The Bamboo Monarch held the jade bamboo and said with a grave expression, “You know of the Moon Empress’ temper too. Since her Cold Moon Lone Disk appeared, something major must have happened.”","The Bamboo Monarch turned into an afterimage after speaking and headed for the place where the cold moonlight was. The red-armored man also left afterimages as he followed the Bamboo Monarch.","The Spirit Guards HQ was considered the place with the strongest combat power within the Royal Capital. Multiple individuals wearing Spirit Guard crests were entering and exiting the headquarters.","In the Spirit Guards HQ’s Chief Hall was a rather skinny and masked woman. Her eyes flashed as she looked at the cold moon through the window and said, “A tall moon high up in the sky. A blade that has been withdrawn for ten years. Why are you making a move again? I hope that the situation isn’t like the previous time.”","After speaking, the black-clothed masked woman vanished from the Chief Hall. A few pieces of paper floated down from the table, making them look lonely.","In the imperial court of the Royal Capital’s Radiance Imperial Palace was an old man in the main seat. Two middle-aged men, who had similarly overwhelming prowess, were seated on his left and right.","The old man looked at the cold moon that had suddenly appeared and knocked on the table with his finger, while the other hand held his forehead. He turned to look at the two middle-aged men and muttered for a moment before he said to the man on the left with a cold face, “Iron Prison, go and find out what happened to make the Moon Empress so enraged. When a tree falls in a horizon of mountain trees, it is as clear as when the moon shines down on the river1. I hope that the Moon Empress’ radiant moon of wrath isn’t going to be scorching like the incident ten years ago.”","A man in golden armor stood up from the seat on the left with his blade in hand and acknowledged in a cold tone. “Yes.”","Subsequently, the golden-armored man vanished from the left seat.","The man on the right seat looked as though he had a smiling face. He involuntarily asked, “Your Excellency should know of Iron Prison’s temperament. Aren’t you afraid that Iron Prison will only further infuriate the Moon Empress?”","The old man looked at the smiling man on the right seat and said, “Cicada Song, if Iron Prison doesn’t go, the person that infuriated the Moon Empress will not have any chance of survival.”","The smiling man said without paying much mind, “The Moon Empress isn’t easily enraged. Since the Cold Moon Lone Disk appeared, it means she has the intention to kill. Those who infuriated the Moon Empress naturally have to pay the price, even Iron Prison. Therefore, I should go too.”","The old man stayed silent for a moment and nodded. The smiling man then vanished from his seat the instant that old man nodded.","...","After a loud “How dare you!?” echoed, the moonlight of the cold moon poured toward this place.","Lin Yuan felt as though the moonlight had a healing effect. In just a short moment, all the pain and the internal burning sensation of his body was slowly vanishing due to the moonlight’s nourishment.","However, Cheng Rui and Cheng Wu were feeling something that was entirely different.","The moonlight instantly disintegrated Cheng Rui and the Spine Gu on his body. Cheng Wu’s Diamond/Fantasy V, Gold Ring Spine Gu was also immobilized after getting fixated by the moonlight.","Even though the Gold Ring Spine Gu was a Diamond/Fantasy V source-type lifeform, when illuminated by the moonlight’s radiance, its feelers, legs, and armor were still slowly disintegrated.","Cheng Wu’s body was also feeling something strange as the moonlight’s radiance illuminated him. He felt that his body was burning up, but it was a burning sensation without pain. However, he could clearly feel that the cells within his body were constantly vanishing. In just a short period of time, three fingers from his left hand had already disintegrated.","Cheng Wu immediately yelled, “Will the Moon Empress, please be merciful! I don’t know what wrong I have committed for the Moon Empress to personally punish me!”","A woman wearing moon-colored robes descended along with the moonlight. In just a split second, she stood beside Lin Yuan. A small rabbit, which was eating a radish, was on the moon-robed woman’s shoulder.","The small rabbit looked at Lin Yuan and hopped off on him. It used its small claws to scratch on the radish for a long time before pulling off a small piece of radish skin. It looked at the radish skin with heartache while looking at Lin Yuan with dislike. The small rabbit lifted its head to see that the Moon Empress was looking at it, so it unwillingly placed the radish skin in Lin Yuan’s mouth.","Lin Yuan’s body was already recovering under the moonlight’s radiance when he suddenly fully recovered. He had a strong feeling that his body was quickly reverted to its prime condition when the radish skin entered his mouth. Even Red Thorn, Chimey, and Genius, which lay injured in his spiritual spatial zone, instantly recovered.","When the small rabbit saw that Lin had recovered, it quickly opened up Lin Yuan’s mouth and pulled out the radish skin. It then cleaned the radish skin on its fur before pasting it back onto the radish carefully.","Lin Yuan stood up and noticed that the Moon Empress was looking at him with concern. Before he could speak, the Moon Empress said with self-blame, “When you left, I should have asked either Cold Moon or Mystic Moon to follow you. It is my negligence. I didn’t think that someone would actually dare to make a move in the Royal Capital’s suburban area.”","As soon as the Moon Empress finished her statement, the domineering moonlight felt as though it was going to penetrate the sun.","Cheng Wu was currently circulating all his spiritual power to resist the moonlight that was penetrating through all pores. He wanted to recall the Fantasy V Gold Ring Spine Gu, but the moonlight didn’t allow it to move an inch.","Once the Moon Empress spoke to Lin Yuan, Cheng Wu’s entire body was drenched. The depths of his soul emitted a sensation of terror as he plopped and knelt on the ground. He couldn’t even say what he wanted to say.","Cheng Wu’s heart was shocked and sorrowful when the moonlight completely disintegrated Cheng Rui, but now, Cheng Wu was filled with hatred toward his own grandson.","My grandson sought revenge on the Moon Empress! This insect-like kid actually had an overwhelming backer like the Moon Empress!?","In normal times, Cheng Wu would wish for a chance to bootlick the Moon Empress. Unexpectedly, he had actually taken the initiative to touch the barrel of a gun that he should have never even gotten close to!"]},{"number":111,"title":"Chapter 111: Moonlight Flare","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","The Moon Empress looked at Cheng Wu, who was kneeling on the ground, and waved her hand without any expression on her face. The Fantasy V Gold Ring Spine Gu was then wrapped around by the muslin-like moonlight, causing it to let out a miserable scream.","Even if the Gold Ring Spine Gu was a Diamond/Fantasy V fey, it still wasn’t able to resist the moonlight at all. In fact, when it was trying to scream, the moonlight trapped its voice and couldn’t get emitted at all.","The serene and beautiful moonlight actually concealed a murderous intent, merciless and sharp. The Moon Empress was even going to give Cheng Wu the chance to explain.","Just as Cheng Wu felt the Gold Ring Spine Gu deteriorating, he became mournful and pounded his head on the ground as he kowtowed and said, “I beg the Moon Empress to spare my life. I, Cheng Wu, am willing to use the rest of my life to serve under the Moon Empress!”","The Moon Empress had a bone-chilling expression, but her voice was still mild and gentle. However, the mild and gentle voice carried an unreserved killing intent.","“Since you wished to kill This Empress’ disciple, you should have known that a killer must be prepared to get killed too.” The Moon Empress paused for a moment and continued. “You are not worthy to serve under This Empress. Repent under the moonlight.”","After hearing the Moon Empress’ words, Cheng Wu’s eyes turned lifeless, and he even forgot to circulate his spirit qi for a moment. Thus, the moonlight instantly disintegrated one of his arms.","The Moon Empress didn’t conceal the killing intent in her words as she wanted Cheng Wu to know that he wasn’t going to escape this calamity. Cheng Wu had never expected that this kid he treated as an insect was actually the Moon Empress’ disciple. If it was some other form of relationship, he might be lucky enough to keep his life.","Earlier on, he had made a move on the Moon Empress’ disciple—a move to kill. Had it not been for the Moon Empress’ obstruction, his Gold Ring Spine Gu might have emptied Lin Yuan’s spinal cord now. At that thought, Cheng Wu’s heart turned into dead ashes.","Just as Cheng Wu felt he was going to vanish under the moonlight, a jade-green bamboo leaf suddenly appeared and hovered over Cheng Wu’s head. The jade-green bamboo leaf was emitting bright green radiance, blocking the concentrated moonlight for Cheng Wu. However, in just a few seconds, the bamboo leaf gradually vanished and was also completely disintegrated by the moonlight.","A white-clothed middle-aged man holding a jade bamboo appeared beside Cheng Wu. The middle-aged man kicked Cheng Wu, sending him flying a dozen meters away and allowing Cheng Wu to leave the most concentrated spot within the moonlight.","Immediately after, a red-armored man appeared beside Cheng Wu, and he emitted spiritual power with a wave of his hand to block off the moonlight that wasn’t considered concentrated.","The red-armored man quickly said, “If the Moon Empress’ Cold Moon Lone Disk continues to emit the moonlight, Cheng Wu will really disintegrate. Will the Moon Empress please reconsider...”","While speaking, the red-armored man released a strand of spirit qi and covered Cheng Wu. The spirit qi strand revolved around Cheng Wu’s body, but it was unable to recover his injuries. As such, the red-armored man was appalled.","He had already heard of the incredible exclusive skill of the Moon Empress’ Cold Moon Lone Disk. The Cold Moon Lone Disk’s exclusive skill, Sublimation, was able to transform any substance into a fourth state apart from gaseous, liquid, or solid states. It would turn the substance into nothingness. After seeing it personally today, it was truly worthy of its reputation.","Cheng Wu might be a pinnacle Class 4 Creation Master, but he had only formed a contract with the source-type lifeform. The Gold Ring Spine Gu was able to enhance the Creation Master’s capability, but it wasn’t really adept in combat. Nonetheless, it was still a Diamond/Fantasy V source-type lifeform, yet it couldn’t even resist the moonlight.","While thinking like that, the red-armored man felt a chill in his heart. His combat strength might be superior to Cheng Wu, but as he sensed the moonlight and looked at the cold moon in the sky, he couldn’t help but wonder how long he could have endured within the moonlight.","When the Moon Empress saw that someone was actually trying to protect Cheng Wu, she frowned. At the moment she frowned, the moonlight emitted a flaring prowess.","The man with the jade bamboo coughed lightly and said, “Moon Empress, Cheng Wu is still a pinnacle Class 4 Creation Master. Even if he really offended you, you have already punished him. He has already lost an arm. Are you able to give This Monarch face and spare Cheng Wu’s life?”","As soon as the Bamboo Monarch finished speaking and saw the Moon Empress’ expression, he could tell the situation wasn’t good. The Moon Empress waved her hand in the sky, while the moonlight revolved around her hand with the cold moon’s color.","The Moon Empress sneered and said, “Give you, the Bamboo Monarch, face? When have I, the Moon Empress, given anyone a face? Could it be that you wish to have your Purple Bamboo Forest have both the sun and moon together for an entire month?”","The three questions the Moon Empress posed made the Bamboo Monarch put on a helpless expression. He was well aware of the Moon Empress’ temper and knew that it was impossible for her to spare Cheng Wu on his account.","Despite that, the Bamboo Monarch glanced at Cheng Wu first before he frowned lightly and said in a serious tone, “Each pinnacle Class 4 Creation Master is the Radiance Federation’s capital. Hence, This Monarch requests for the Moon Empress to be merciful again.”","The Moon Empress said with a cold voice, “The Radiance Federation’s capital? Since when can the Radiance Federation’s capital make a move on a young Class 2 Creation Master? Such capital is already corrupted!”","The Bamboo Monarch finally looked at Lin Yuan, who stood beside the Moon Empress. He looked at the bloodstains on the ground and on Lin Yuan’s body. It was still bright red and had yet to dry up. The blood was so bright red because Lin Yuan’s inner organs had been ruptured, and he had vomited out.","The Bamboo Monarch used his peripheral vision to shoot an arrow-like glance, filled with disgust, at Cheng Wu. He then said to Lin Yuan with a gentle voice, “Young friend, the Moon Empress has already stopped Cheng Wu from making a move against you. Why don’t I ask Cheng Wu to compensate you with some precious spiritual ingredients? I will make sure that he resolves this hatred and will not seek trouble with you ever again.”","Lin Yuan was initially shocked that he could see the Class 5 Creation Master, Bamboo Monarch. Two of the three Class 5 Creation Masters of the Radiance Federation were present.","The Bamboo Monarch’s voice might sound gentle and pleasing, while the way he addressed Lin Yuan as a young friend might seem friendly, but was Lin Yuan really able to refuse this proposal?","Before Lin Yuan could speak, the Moon Empress’ hand revolved with radiance before she grasped it. The Fantasy V Gold Ring Spine Gu was then enveloped in moonlight and started struggling violently under the sudden moonlight flare.","The flaring moonlight instantly sublimated the Diamond/Fantasy V lifeform into the air and turned it into undetectable particles of dust.","“Should I take this as the Bamboo Monarch trying to make things difficult for my disciple? Worms appear from rotting flesh, holes appear in dried up fish. Anything corrupted and rotting should be eliminated. Is the Bamboo Monarch thinking that flowers can be grown from rotting wood and bloom with radiance?”"]},{"number":112,"title":"Chapter 112: Greatest Leniency","paragraphs":["When Lin Yuan heard the Moon Empress’ words, he felt warmth in his heart. The Bamboo Monarch’s tone might have sounded gentle, but it was unquestionable. Subsequently, the Moon Empress’ statement was to protect him.","When the Bamboo Monarch found out that the youth beside the Moon Empress was her disciple, he revealed a surprised look on his face before he smiled and said, “I congratulate the Moon Empress for obtaining a great disciple.”","Presently, the Bamboo Monarch knew that nothing he said was going to be useful. Cheng Wu’s attack on the Moon Empress’ disciple was no different than courting death. He watched as the Moon Empress sublimated Cheng Wu’s Gold Ring Spine Gu with the moonlight and didn’t show any signs of obstruction.","After the Gold Ring Spine Gu was disintegrated, Cheng Wu’s originally bloodless face was now even paler, and he was perspiring with cold sweat. The Gold Ring Spine Gu’s death left an immense mental trauma on Cheng Wu’s spiritual energy.","Cheng Wu’s physical injuries didn’t make him suffer as much as the mental trauma. It was unbearable!","All of a sudden, a rather charming voice echoed from the horizon. A masked and black-robed woman arrived while she stepped on air. “The Moon Empress is truly incredible and has directly sublimated this Gold Ring Spine Gu. Cheng Wu had only formed a contract with this source-type lifeform. So, since it is already dead, I wonder if the Moon Empress’ anger is appeased.”","Although the black-robed woman’s mask made it impossible to fully see her face, her eyes were still exposed. She was looking at the Moon Empress with a complex expression.","The Moon Empress lifted her head and looked at the black-robed woman with complex eyes too. However, her expression didn’t change. “It is none of your matters if This Empress’ anger is appeased. As a Chief Guard, why are you not overseeing the Spirit Guards? Are you really that free?”","Lin Yuan looked up at the sky after hearing the words. This black-robed woman is actually the Chief Guard of the Spirit Guards? She is the current era’s top-class expert!","The black-robed woman was now standing beside the Bamboo Monarch as she said, “Xiyue[1], the punishment is enough. You are not young and are already a Class 5 Creation Master. You are the Radiance Federation’s pillar and should know when to punish and reward.”","As soon as the black-robed woman finished speaking, an intense spirit qi wave surged, and a golden-armored middle-aged man appeared next to the red-armored man. He walked past the red-armored man, grabbed Cheng Wu up from the ground, and said in a loud voice, “Chief Guard Ye is right. Cheng Wu is a pinnacle Class 4 Creation Master recognized by the Creation Master Association. Even if he is at fault, he should only be judged first before being punished. Now that the Moon Empress has punished him, leave the rest to me.”","The red-armored man flashed and arrived in front of the Bamboo Monarch. He had to quickly stand away from the gold-armored man. He then silently complained. Why is Iron Prison here too? It is fine if he is here, but he actually dares to speak to the Moon Empress like this? Isn’t he trying to seek trouble?","Given the style that Iron Prison handled matters, he would probably suffer in the Moon Empress’ hands. The red-armored man looked at the Bamboo Monarch and realized that the latter was looking at Iron Prison with a displeased expression. He didn’t know that the Bamboo Monarch was also saying, ‘Not good!’, in his heart.","Iron Prison handles matters in a straightforward manner. Putting it in a nice way is to say that it is his dominance, but is his dominance useful against the Moon Empress? If this isn’t a foolish act, then what is?","Cheng Wu nearly killed the Moon Empress’ disciple. Now that Iron Prison arrived, he actually went against the Moon Empress and ordered her... I don’t even dare to do it!","Cheng Wu had also come back to his senses now and recalled that he was still a respected pinnacle Class 4 Creation Master and very useful to the Radiance Federation. At that thought, Cheng Wu’s mind lit up, so he looked at the gold-armored man who had grabbed him and said, “Lord Iron Prison, I beg you to save me!”","Cheng Wu then turned to look at the Moon Empress. “Lordess Moon Empress, I, Cheng Wu, know I am wrong! I am willing to give up all my wealth to your great disciple! I just hope for you to spare my life!”","When Iron Prison heard Cheng Wu calling him for help, his face turned unpleasant. He might be a straightforward person, but he understood that this would make it seem like he was directly opposing the Moon Empress.","However, Iron Prison didn’t throw Cheng Wu away from his hand and continued to say with a cold face, “Lordess Moon Empress has already given the punishment. You have to set your punishments and rewards apart.”","The Moon Empress sneered and stood in the air. The concentrated moonlight felt as though it had turned solid before it swept at Iron Prison.","“This Empress is the Moon Empress, therefore, my punishment to Cheng Wu is a reward too. So how am I not setting the punishment and reward apart? Since you wish to take Cheng Wu away, then I shall see if you, Iron Prison, have the capability to do so!”","Wherever the Moon Empress’ moonlight swept across, there would be moon-colored ripples. It was utterly beautiful, but everyone who saw it felt a shiver in their spines.","Iron Prison suddenly activated his spiritual energy and summoned a prehistoric dragon beast that was roughly forty meters in size. The dragon beast spat out energy in preparation to defend against the moonlight.","When the Moon Empress saw Iron Prison summoning his fey, her eyes sparkled with cold light. At the same time, the bright moon in the sky suddenly burst out with radiance. The moonlight was like water with ripples, and within those ripples, a bare-footed young girl in a dress made out of the cold moon walked down from the moon.","The young girl’s long hair was the extremely concentrated moonlight, and her gorgeous face had a 70% resemblance to the Moon Empress!","The moment the young girl walked down the moonlight, it felt as though sparkling stars accompanied the moonlight. The prehistoric dragon beast immediately let out a pitiful roar and was sent flying.","Subsequently, the Bamboo Monarch and the black-robed woman each shot out an energy beam to help block the moonlight’s attack.","The Bamboo Monarch looked at the Moon Empress with shock but also pleasant surprise. “Moon Empress, your Cold Moon Lone Disk has reached Myth II!”","The red-armored man beside the Bamboo Monarch looked at the girl that walked out of the moonlight with shiny eyes.","Myth II, feys could transform and take a human form!","The Moon Empress stood in the sky and sneered. “Bamboo Monarch, you old thing. Your Ink Point Emperor Bamboo was already a Myth Breed a few dozen years ago. This Empress doesn’t believe that your Ink Point Emperor Bamboo hasn’t reached Myth II yet.”","The Moon Empress took a glance at the Bamboo Monarch and another glance at the black-robed masked woman before saying, “Since you wish to fight, This Empress shall not hold back! This Empress has been secluded for ten years, and it seems that none of you put This Empress in your eyes!”","After speaking, the Moon Empress lifted her shoulder, and the small white rabbit that was gnawing on the radish suddenly turned extremely purple. Just as its fur was reaching its peak of purple, a voice suddenly echoed from the skies, and it sounded rather urgent.","A man, who originally had a smiling face, was yelling out to the Moon Empress with an urgent expression, “Moon Empress, have you forgotten about the incident ten years ago? You have been in seclusion for ten years. Isn’t it because you weren’t able to forget that incident from ten years ago?”","The voice was extremely urgent, and when the Moon Empress heard this statement, she paused and went silent for a moment.","She waved her hand, and the lone moon in the sky instantly vanished. The afternoon sun became glaring like normal again. The Moon Empress turned around and pulled Lin Yuan before soaring into the sky.","She didn’t turn back to look at anyone, but her cold voice echoed. “Cheng Wu tried to murder This Empress’ disciple, Radiance Federation’s Class 2 Creation Master, Lin Yuan. His punishment should be death. Since all of you used the incident ten years ago to stab at This Empress’ sore spot, Cheng Wu shall be imprisoned to cleanse his sins.”","The Moon Empress paused for three seconds before she continued saying, “He shall not be released unless he dies. This is already This Empress’ greatest leniency.”","[1] Literally sobbing moon"]},{"number":113,"title":"Chapter 113: Transformation of Attitude","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","The Moon Empress brought Lin Yuan back to the Radiant Moon Palace. After checking on his injuries carefully, she said with concern, “It is my fault. When you left, I didn’t even think to let someone follow you. You have been shocked, but it is also good. This incident taught you something that I don’t know how I should have taught you.”","While speaking, the Moon Empress paused for a moment and looked at Lin Yuan’s in a very serious manner. “Everything you possess in this world is nothing as compared to your strength.”","Lin Yuan nodded after hearing the Moon Empress’ words. At that moment, Lin Yuan was looking at the Moon Empress with eyes that were entirely different from before. Previously, Lin Yuan might have known that the Moon Empress was his Master, but he was still in the process of adaptation. After all, no relationships were built overnight.","However, when Cheng Wu had tried to kill him, and he had been helpless to resist, it was the Moon Empress’ moonlight that had saved him. It was the current era’s absolute expert that had protected him.","Had it not been for Lin Yuan, would the Moon Empress have to make things difficult for Cheng Wu? Would all those experts have gathered?","Lin Yuan was indescribably touched. After having to face the harsh world and reality with determination since the age of eight, now that he had been protected from this crisis, a sore feeling arose spontaneously.","It was a kind of feeling that Lin Yuan couldn’t divulge and could only suppress it in his heart. The unfamiliar term ‘Master’ was suddenly engraved within his heart at the age of 18.","When the Moon Empress saw Lin Yuan looking at her, she frowned and looked at Lin Yuan with concern. “It is definitely a shock to experience such an incident for the first time. But it will not happen in the future, Master is here.”","Lin Yuan’s eyes had this sore feeling, but it was very dry, and no tears would flow out. Although his eyes were dry, his heart was filled with plenty of warmth.","Lin Yuan pursed his lips for a long time and opened his mouth but couldn’t say a thing. He was only able to speak after a moment. “I am no longer afraid now. I know that in this world, one’s strength will always be the foundation to protect oneself.”","Seeing how Lin Yuan recovered so quickly, the Moon Empress nodded with satisfaction.","Lin Yuan recalled when all those experts mentioned the incident that happened ten years ago. However, if the incident involved all those pinnacle experts, it wasn’t possible to read about it on the Star Web.","At that moment, Lin Yuan noticed the Moon Empress handing over a box. Three crests were inside the box, and they were the same crests as the ones Lin Yuan had received after passing the Class 2 Creation Master exam.","However, each crest had an additional and abnormally exquisite carving—the symbol of a crescent moon!","When Lin Yuan received the Moon Empress’ box, he immediately bowed and called the Moon Empress as Master.","A smile appeared on the Moon Empress’ cold face. She then handed a token, which was warm to the touch and pure like jade, to Lin Yuan. The jade token was engraved with two crescent moons, and they were connected on the top and bottom tips, giving off an ancient feeling.","“This is the Radiant Moon Token. Previously, you refused all of my gifts. Now that you have already gone through the ceremonial rites to have me as your Master, I don’t know what to give you either. Take this Radiant Moon Token, and if you need any spiritual ingredients, you can just bring this Radiant Moon Token to the Radiant Moon Palace’s spiritual ingredient vault.”","Lin Yuan solemnly received the Radiant Moon Token. After experiencing this incident, his attitude was already different.","Before the life-or-death experience, Lin Yuan had been thinking to rely on himself and take each diligent step on his own. He might still be thinking like this, but his mind was now a little open.","His persistence to rely on his own capability to collect spiritual ingredients was indeed correct.","He had already gone through the ceremony rites, and the Moon Empress was now officially his Master. Lin Yuan knew that his greatest challenge right now was to collect spiritual ingredients. This was also why his feys’ quality had yet to reach the Legend quality. It also resulted in Lin Yuan having three Willpower Runes for nothing.","His Jasmine Lily was already Bronze X/Epic. He only lacked a few spiritual ingredients to upgrade it to the Legend quality. By fusing the Willpower Rune he had comprehended in the mountains, the Jasmine Lily could evolve into a Fantasy Breed.","If that was the case, Lin Yuan would be able to possess a Bronze Fantasy Breed. Ling Xiao had previously mentioned that the earlier the fey progressed to a Fantasy Breed, the greater the potential.","Therefore, Lin Yuan was very ambitious and wanted Red Thorn to also reach the Legend quality at Bronze. Once Red Thorn reached the Legend quality, he would be able to fuse it with the Willpower Rune he had comprehended during the massacre, allowing Red Thorn to become a Fantasy Breed too.","Lin Yun had comprehended the third Willpower Rune when he had been observing the change of day and night. This Willpower Rune might be a little compatible with Chimey, but it still lacked a little. Chimey’s exclusive skill was Clear Sky, and it carried the power of the sun. However, this Willpower Rune involved the change between day and night, so Lin Yuan had another plan for this rune.","Lin Yuan was still able to contract one more fey or a source-type lifeform with an extremely low spiritual energy requirement. As of now, Lin Yuan had never even been in a rush to form a new contract. If there was a suitable fey that was compatible with the willpower rune he comprehended during the change of day and night, Lin Yuan wouldn’t mind having an additional fey.","After getting attacked by Cheng Wu, Lin Yuan had already prioritized the increase of his strength as the most important matter now. It wasn’t difficult for Lin Yuan to increase his strength, and all he needed was time.","Thus, Lin Yuan made a slight adjustment to the plan he had in his mind. For the next year, he set his goal on increasing his strength. Given the Radiant Moon Palace’s spiritual ingredient","resources, Lin Yuan believed that he would undergo a transformation during this one year.","Seeing that Lin Yuan accepted the Radiant Moon Token, the Moon Empress was extremely happy. “Go and rest well for the next two days. Your physical injuries might have recovered, but if you feel anything wrong with your spirit, tell me.”","As a Master, the Moon Empress knew that there were things that she wasn’t able to provide guidance, such as the first kill or the first escape from death.","These transformations to the attitude were things that a spirit qi professional had to overcome themselves, and a Master could only give guidance.","Lin Yuan left the Moon Empress’ inner palace and returned to his pavilion. He sat on the chair as his mind was still flashing back with the scene of the Gold Ring Spine Gu flying toward his neck area. However, Lin Yuan wasn’t afraid and was filled with courage instead.","After experiencing this formless setback, Lin Yuan knew that he had to work hard to become stronger.","He entered the Spirit Lock spatial zone and checked on Red Thorn, Genius, and Chimey. After seeing that they were doing fine, Lin Yuan was finally relieved.","Red Thorn’s vines that were sliced by the Spine Gu had also grown back out. Unexpectedly, the Red Thorn’s quality had upgraded from Flawless to Epic after this battle. It was also at Elite IX.","Lin Yuan was delighted. Red Thorn’s quality upgrade might have been related to the battle, but it was mainly due to the nutritious flesh within the diamond-grade fey storage box. After all, Red Thorn’s evolution relied on consumption.","If it consumed large quantities of flesh, Lin Yuan believed that Red Thorn would evolve into the Bronze in the next day or two. It would allow Red Thorn to welcome its first exclusive skill. By then, it would be Red Thorn’s first and true metamorphosis as a source-type lifeform."]},{"number":114,"title":"Chapter 114: The Legendary Blue Flash Purple Butterfly","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Lin Yuan didn’t withdraw Genius and Chimey into his spiritual spatial zone, nor did he let them reside in the pavilion. Instead, he kept them within the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","The Platinum Cane Luffa and the Celery Vine were placed on the table inside the Spirit Lock spatial zone by Lin Yuan. An ordinary wooden table was gradually turned into jade due to the spirit qi concentration that was ten times more concentrated than the outside world. It was now extremely exquisite.","Lin Yuan now had an idea to place more wooden materials within the Spirit Lock spatial zone and allow them to turn into jade after a period of time. Turning wooden to a jade-like texture might not be useful, but it was very rare. The great appearance also allowed the price to be marked up, especially jade-textured furniture were considered luxury items.","When Genius and Chimey were hungry, they could just consume the Platinum Celery Vine and Cane Luffa from the table. After experiencing that battle earlier and seeing Lin Yuan vomiting blood, Genius and Chimey were obediently sticking onto Lin Yuan.","After every minute or two, Chimey would be chirping noisily beside Lin Yuan’s ears, and it would only relax after Lin Yuan guaranteed that he was fine.","Genius was also crouching on Lin Yuan’s shoulder and saying, “Yuan, I was scared to death. I am useless and couldn’t be of any use in combat.”","Lin Yuan quickly rubbed Genius’ head until it let out a comfortable purr. Lin Yuan then said, “Had it not been for your glasses form, allowing me to dodge the qi force at the crucial moment, I might not have been able to crawl up after the first wave of attack. Therefore, Genius is great!”","Genius meowed a few times after hearing Lin Yuan’s response and climbed up the table to seek a comfortable position before sleeping soundly.","After seeing Lin Yuan praising Genius, Chimey chirped loudly and flew beside Lin Yuan’s ear again. Lin Yuan then chuckled and plucked off a leaf of the Celery Vine before feeding it to Chimey. “Chimey’s Sound Thrust is great too. Had it not been for Chimey’s Sound Thrust, it would have been impossible to nearly injure Cheng Rui.”","After Lin Yuan’s praise, Chimey ate the small teared up shards of Celery Vine leaves happily. Once it ate and drank to its fill, it flew toward Genius’ head with satisfaction before sleeping within Genius’ fur.","The battle earlier had exhausted plenty of Genius and Chimey’s spirit. The easiest way to replenish the spirit exhaustion was to have a great sleep.","As for the Gold Wind Speed Rapid Antelope, Lin Yuan had already placed it for sale on his Star Web store. Plenty of people offered to buy it—their offers great at that—but Lin Yuan hesitated to sell it.","Lin Yuan walked to the water tanks beside the spirit pool and noticed that many of the Five Fortune Ranchu eggs had already hatched. Numerous small fish were swimming within the water tanks, and they were less than half a centimeter long.","The Spirit-Siphon Goldfish’s baby fish didn’t require any food when in an environment with rich spirit qi. However, Lin Yuan still scooped the first batch of baby fish into another water tank. The baby fish had poor vision, and due to the rapid growth in this rich spirit qi environment, they might just eat up those eggs that had yet to hatch.","The spirit pool also had plenty of Normal Spirit-Siphon Goldfish that had evolved into elite-grade. However, these Elite Spirit-Siphon Goldfish only dared to swim at the border of the spirit pool. Only Lin Yuan’s contracted Spirit-Gather Goldfish, Blackie, would be able to enjoy the central and spacious part of the spirit pool.","From time to time, it would sink to the bottom of the pool to consume one Butterfly Shell, giving off a truly relaxed feeling.","All of a sudden, Lin Yuan noticed a very interesting scene. The Spirit-Gather Goldfish, Blackie grabbed a Butterfly Shell and swam toward the edge of the pool. It then brandished its tail to push aside two Elite Spirit-Siphon Goldfish, leaving behind a female Five Fortune Ranchu.","Blackie spat out the Butterfly Shell toward the female Five Fortune Ranchu, and after seeing the female Five Fortune Ranchu carefully eating the Butterfly Shell, Blackie then turned back with pride and swam back to the center of the pool.","After the female Five Fortune Ranchu ate the Butterfly Shell, it swam toward the center of the pool carefully.","Blackie didn’t bother about the female Five Fortune Ranchu that swam over, but when other Elite Spirit-Siphon Goldfish swam over, Blackie would ruthlessly swing its big tail to chase them away.","Lin Yuan was flabbergasted and involuntarily recalled about the fiendish couple when he had picked up the bottle cap. He suddenly felt as though he was fed with dog food by his own fey and said silently in his mind, “Animals have emotions and feelings too.”","At that moment, Lin Yuan suddenly heard an extremely delicate sound. He turned around and noticed that the butterfly cocoon he had placed on the table had cracked open lightly. A newborn Blue Flash Butterfly was trying its best to emerge.","The newborn Blue Flash Butterfly’s wings were still very tender as they were all crumpled together and couldn’t extend fully.","Lin Yuan only walked over and watched without doing anything else. A butterfly’s first obstacle was to extend its wings, and it was the hardest obstacle that plenty of butterflies weren’t able to overcome. However, once it overcame this obstacle, the butterfly wouldn’t have any more obstructions and would be able to soar freely in the blue skies.","But once the Blue Flash Butterfly extended its wing fully, Lin Yuan was stunned—the wings weren’t blue but purple!","Lin Yuan was dumbfounded and didn’t hesitate to use Morbius’ exclusive skill, Spirit Lock, to set this purple-winged Blue Flash Butterfly as a spirit-locked fey.","Lin Yuan was unable to come back to his senses even after forming the contract with the Blue Flash Butterfly.","Am I really that lucky to form a contract with a Blue Flash Purple Butterfly that almost never appears within the Blue Flash Butterfly species?","The Blue Flash Purple Butterfly was considered the purest existence among the Blue Flash Butterflies. As soon as it hatched from the butterfly cocoon, it would go through an evolution toward the ancestry line, awakening the flawless model among the Order Lepidoptera.","Blue Flash Purple Butterflies were truly too rare, so rare that they only existed in ancient texts before the Spirit Qi Awakening. Most of the people treated the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly as a species that didn’t exist, and they were feys that existed only in concepts.","Even fey pageants treated the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly as Fantasy Breeds that weren’t Fantasy Breeds.","Because of Blue Flash Purple Butterflies’ legend, the Blue Light Goddess Butterfly, which evolved from the Blue Flash Butterfly, was actually put at the first place during fey pageants. However, the officials weren’t able to determine if Blue Flash Purple Butterflies actually existed. After all, it wasn’t possible to prove the Blue Flash Purple Butterflies’ existence just by taking reference to the ancient texts.","Therefore, the Purple Light Goddess Butterfly’s absolute beauty wasn’t taken into consideration for the Blue Light Goddess Butterfly’s ranking. Otherwise, the Blue Light Goddess Butterfly wouldn’t have fallen out of the top three due to its inferior abilities.","When Lin Yuan looked at the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly and checked True Data’s information, he couldn’t help but slap his forehead. The Blue Flash Purple Butterfly was indeed a fey that evolved toward the flawless model when hatching from the butterfly cocoon.","The basic ability of a Normal Blue Flash Purple Butterfly, Silence Scale Powder, was entirely different from the Silence Scale Powder from a Blue Flash Butterfly.","The Blue Flash Butterfly’s scale powder could be scattered by great winds and other natural environmental effects, especially when the scale powder was washed off by rainwater, so its Silence ability would lose its effect.","However, the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly’s Silence Scale Powder had the strongest trait as it had the ability to attach. After contacting the target, the tiny scale powder would sink into the target’s skin.","Unless it was an incineration ability, such as Blazing Flame that could burn off the scale powder’s powerful effects, great winds would have a tough time removing the scale powder from inflicted targets. At the same time, rainwater would only enhance the effects of the scale powder on the skin.","The Blue Flash Purple Butterfly is truly powerful!","Lin Yuan let out an involuntary sigh. From now on, the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly was no longer a legend, as there was one in Lin Yuan’s hands!"]},{"number":115,"title":"Chapter 115: Scale Powder Halo","paragraphs":["As a flawless model of the Blue Flash Butterfly, the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly naturally could not escape the curse of its abilities. Its Normal ability was still formidable, but its future abilities were all rather useless. However, it was not an immense influence on Lin Yuan, as he only needed the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly’s basic ability.","The Blue Flash Purple Butterfly’s Normal ability, Silence Scale Powder, had the exceptional trait to attach, and it was definitely a divine ability among the control abilities. If he used it appropriately, it could certainly affect the situation of a battle and catch the opponent off guard.","After forming a contract with the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly, Lin Yuan started to channel spirit qi toward the Normal Blue Flash Purple Butterfly that was only the size of half a palm.","In just less than one hour, the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly’s body was shaking rapidly and scattering layers of glistening scale powder. Soon, Lin Yuan evolved this Blue Flash Purple Butterfly from Normal I/Normal to Elite X/Epic. Then, he continued evolving the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly into Bronze.","The Blue Flash Purple Butterfly’s shaking body suddenly released a light purple halo. It had an indescribable beauty, and it could only be described as a calming purple.","The layers of scale powder surrounding the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly suddenly burst out and formed an illusory halo zone that was around half a meter. The spirit qi that Lin Yuan was channeling had already broken through the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly’s bottleneck, and it was now officially a Bronze fey.","After evolving into a Bronze fey, when the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly flapped its wings, it would produce a blue-purple light and spread out the scale powder that surrounded the body. It felt as though the illusory halo was shattered.","A Blue Flash Purple Butterfly that was more than twice as big as before and bigger than a fist flew out of the halo and landed on Lin Yuan’s shoulder.","The butterfly with a purple halo on his shoulder made it seem like an immortal ascension.","As a straight guy, when Lin Yuan looked at the Bronze Blue Flash Purple Butterfly, he suddenly could understand why beautiful feys were so expensive and made people scramble for them.","Every glance at it was a wonderful experience.","The Blue Flash Purple Butterfly fluttered its wings and danced around Lin Yuan intimately.","Since the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly had reached Epic at elite-grade, three exclusive skills naturally appeared when it evolved into a Bronze fey.","Lin Yuan looked at the exclusive skills.","[Hard Scale Powder]: The scale powder is like fine metallic powder. Rubbing onto the scale powder might cause cuts by the sharpness of the fine surface.","In Lin Yuan’s opinion, this exclusive skill was relatively useless.","The Blue Flash Purple Butterfly’s Silence Scale Powder needed to be light so that it could spread quickly when released.","However, the Hard Scale Powder would not enhance the control effect of the Silence Scale Powder. Instead, it would affect the release of the Silence Scale Powder and its attachment.","Such an exclusive skill was the most pathetic.","If the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly was not evolved from an Epic at Elite, this exclusive skill would ruin a rare fey like it.","This was why so many spirit qi professionals were eager to have their feys reach Epic before they advanced to Bronze at Elite.","Lin Yuan skipped this exclusive skill and looked at the second one.","[Flashing Wings]: Quickly increases flying speed. With the scale powder on the wings, it allows flying to be as fast as a flash.","This exclusive skill increased the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly’s survivability. It was reasonably a wonderful ability for support-type feys with control abilities, especially feys with almost no defense like the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly.","It could greatly increase the mistake tolerance in a battle, but it was of little use for Lin Yuan. The Blue Flash Purple Butterfly was Morbius’ spirit-locked fey, and Lin Yuan was wearing the Morbius bracelet. Therefore, he could release the ability of the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly by raising his hand.","Although summoning the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly to release the Silence Scale Powder would increase the Silence Scale Powder’s effect, the Flashing Wings skill was not very useful to the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly. It did not need to appear every time it released the ability.","Lin Yuan wanted to have a look at the third exclusive skill. If it was still incompatible, he could only choose the versatile Flashing Wings as its exclusive skill.","However, when he saw the third exclusive skill, he could not help but wear a smile.","[Scale Powder Halo]: Its scale powder contains a powerful reflective effect. The multi-faceted reflection will cause the target being enveloped by the scale powder to suffer from light pollution and lead to dizziness or brief blindness.","This might be a useless exclusive skill for other Order Lepidoptera or butterfly feys. But for Lin Yuan, who could only use the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly’s basic abilities, the Scale Powder Halo was a divine skill. This was because the Scale Powder Halo directly enhanced the control effect of its basic skill, Silence Scale Powder.","When the Silence Scale Powder was scattered, the Scale Powder Halo would produce a powerful illusory light through the light pollution, causing dizziness or brief blindness to the target.","This exclusive skill allowed the Silence Scale Powder to achieve dual control.","At the same time, the Scale Powder Halo ensured the Silence effect of the Silence Scale Powder.","The Scale Powder Halo would provide a head start. When a controlled target came back to its senses, they would have missed the best time to avoid the Silence Scale Powder. At that time, while they would be removing the Silence Scale Powder, Lin Yuan’s other feys would attack.","Each fey had thousands of exclusive skills, and it was not easy to select a suitable exclusive skill among them. Some people would even get the exclusive skill needed for Bronze before forming a contract. But it was easier said than done to get a specific exclusive skill.","Lin Yuan could not help but think of the girl with the braised egg head. She had reserved almost her 15th Web-Spraying Spider from him. She still could get the exclusive skill she wanted, the Transparent Spider Web, from the previous dozen of Web-Spraying Spiders.","Lin Yuan felt he had experienced two miracles from the moment he had his breakthrough today.","The first miracle was that a Blue Flash Purple Butterfly with a probability of 1 in 10,000,000 had flown out of the cocoon of the Blue Flash Butterfly. The other one was that the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly actually obtained a suitable exclusive skill.","The Blue Flash Purple Butterfly had only reached Bronze, so the Silence Scale Powder’s effect was not yet strong.","However, if the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly matured and had the Silence Scale Powder with Scale Powder Halo, it would certainly be a very powerful control ability on the battlefield."]},{"number":116,"title":"Chapter 116: Path Protector","paragraphs":["Lin Yuan had sent a message to Liu Jie when he had returned to the Radiant Moon Palace earlier. After experiencing a life-and-death ordeal, Lin Yuan was really not in the mood to look at houses anymore.","He had evolved the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly from Bronze I/Normal to Bronze X/Epic. However, he currently had no plans to evolve it into Silver, as the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly’s future potential was related to when it would evolve into a Fantasy Breed.","Lin Yuan was not an absolute perfectionist, but this concerned his future, so he suppressed the grades of all his feys at Bronze X. Another reason was that the grade and quality of Morbius were related to its spirit-locked feys.","A spirit-lock fey could not be changed, so each of them was of utmost importance. Any feys stuck at a certain grade would simply be a disaster for Lin Yuan, as the grade of Morbius would also be forced to be stuck at the lowest grade of the spirit-locked feys.","When the feys evolved into Fantasy Breed at Bronze, Lin Yuan could raise the grade of the feys without it being forced to be stuck at Bronze.","At first, he had been thinking about how to get two Mahogany Tree Cores for his Jasmine Lily to evolve from Epic to Legend. Yet, now, he only needed to take the Radiant Moon Token and find the spiritual ingredients he needed in the treasure trove at the Radiance Palace. Thus, the next thing he had to do was to evolve Jasmine Lily to Legend and fuse the Willpower Rune that he had gained an insight back at the mountains. That way, the Jasmine Lily would become his first Fantasy Breed fey.","Lin Yuan did not know how strong a Bronze Fantasy Breed would be, but he believed that it would definitely be stronger than a fey evolved into a Fantasy Breed at Silver. A fey’s evolution into a Fantasy Breed was beyond its inherent genetic model. It was an evolution toward the feys in fantasies. It would break through the Fantasy Five Transformations and evolve into a Myth Breed fey.","Lin Yuan had shallow knowledge before and only knew about the Fantasy Breed, but not the Myth Breed. Nonetheless, he had now gotten to know and see it.","Lin Yuan finalized the path that Jasmine Lily and his other feys would take after becoming Fantasy Breeds.","Morbius had yet to wake up from its slumber. In fact, not much time had passed since Morbius fell asleep. However, it had never woken up, and Lin Yuan was worried.","At that moment, there was a change in Morbius’ attributes.","Lin Yuan’s vacant Bronze Spirit Lock position was also filled.","[Fey Name]: Morbius","[Fey Species]: ???","[Fey Grade]: Bronze (10/10)","[Fey Type]: Spatial/Mystery","[Fey Quality]: Epic","Abilities:","[True Data]: All complicated information that is invisible to the eye is turned into data. Information that is turned into data might contain truth that cannot be distinguished on the surface.","[Calm Mind]: Passive ability. Effects of Calm Mind can be improved according to the fey’s grade. Calm Mind can stabilize the mind and has a certain probability of resisting negative conditions.","Exclusive Skill:","[Spirit Lock]: Morbius’ spatial zone can be used to nurture feys. The initial grade of the fey that Morbius’ spatial zone can nurture must not be higher than Morbius’ grade. Morbius isn’t able to increase its grade by itself, so its grade will be increased along with the fey’s grade that it nurtures. At the same time, Morbius can obtain the initial ability of the fey that it nurtures. However, Morbius will not obtain abilities when its grade increases. Whenever Morbius increases a grade, it will be able to nurture one more fey. Morbius’ method of growth will remain unchanged.","[Pure Land of Bliss]: The Spirit Lock spatial zone will produce soil that is great for recovering near-death fey’s injuries. The fey’s recovery time will be determined by the grade of Morbius and the dying fey.","[Normal Spirit Lock]:","Jasmine Lily: Bronze (10/10), Epic","Ability – [Heal]: Rapidly recovers external injuries and gradually recovers vitality.","Exclusive Skill – [Recovery Imprint]: Accumulate the healing energy that is released by the Jasmine Lily during normal times. The contractor can activate the imprint to release the accumulated healing energy.","[Elite Spirit Lock]:","Spirit-Gather Goldfish: Bronze (10/10), Epic","Ability: [Spirit Injection]: Restore a certain amount of spiritual power at once and gradually restore the lost spiritual power.","Exclusive Skill – [Spirit Qi Imprint]: The spirit qi that is constantly released to the environment will be stored within the Spirit Qi Imprint instead. It will be branded on the contractor’s body, and the contractor can release spirit qi contained within the Spirit Qi Imprint.","[Bronze Spirit Lock]:","Blue Flash Purple Butterfly: Bronze (10/10), Epic","Ability: [Silence Scale Powder]: Releases special scale powder with a silence effect, causing the target in contact with it to cannot communicate with spiritual power or use abilities.","Exclusive Skill – [Scale Powder Halo]: Its scale powder has a powerful reflective effect. The multi-faceted reflection will cause the target being enveloped by the scale powder to suffer from light pollution and lead to dizziness and even brief blindness.","When looking at Morbius’ information under the True Data, Lin Yuan felt that it was really hard to find a stronger healing-type or support-type feys like Morbius in this world.","Each of Morbius’ abilities corresponded to a fey, and the abilities of each fey corresponded to the exclusive skills. This allowed Lin Yuan to enhance Morbius’ abilities according to the path he wanted.","After devouring a vast amount of flesh from dimensional lifeforms, Red Thorn had evolved into Elite X/Epic. Unfortunately, Lin Yuan could not help Red Thorn reach from Elite X to Bronze. Red Thorn needed to devour a vast amount of flesh and break through the barrier by itself.","It was difficult for feys to break through this barrier, so it would take Red Thorn some time to evolve into Bronze.","The most important thing now was to evolve the Jasmine Lily into a Fantasy Breed. Therefore, Lin Yuan had to head to the Radiant Moon Palace to obtain the spiritual ingredients required for his Jasmine Lily to evolve into Legend.","He walked out of the pavilion and walked toward the Radiant Moon Palace.","From time to time, Lin Yuan could see some rare feys blooming or playing on the lawn in the flower garden next to the Radiant Moon Palace.","Before Lin Yuan reached the Radiant Moon Palace, he saw Cold Moon approaching him.","Upon seeing Lin Yuan, Cold Moon bowed slightly and said in a clear voice, “Young Highness, the Moon Empress has invited you to go to the inner palace.”","Lin Yuan, who was startled to see Cold Moon bowing to him, quickly responded, “Senior, I can’t afford your salutations.”","Lin Yuan respected experts. Not only did Cold Moon bow to him, but she also addressed him as Young Highness, which made Lin Yuan feel uncomfortable all over.","Cold Moon looked at Lin Yuan, her usual cold expression tinted with a little warmth.","“The Moon Empress is the master of the Radiant Moon Palace in Leaning Moon Mountain. Mystic Moon and I are her retainers, while you are her disciple and kin, so you deserve my salutation. After all, you’re also the young master of the Radiant Moon Palace in Leaning Moon Mountain.”","Cold Moon paused and then added, “Not only do you deserve the salutation from Mystic Moon and me but also many people from the Radiance Federation.”","Cold Moon frowned when she recalled Lin Yuan being attacked by Cheng Wu.","“The Moon Empress invited you over, probably to assign an expert that can protect you. There are errant people everywhere. Before you grow up, you will need a Path Protector.”","Lin Yuan frowned. His Master, the Moon Empress, actually wanted to arrange a Path Protector for him?"]},{"number":117,"title":"Chapter 117: When a Fox Has Seven Tails","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","‘Path Protection’ was a very sacred term in the hearts of the Radiance Federation.","Path Protection referred to protecting a youth’s safety and growth, as well as the path of a very young unsurpassed talent.","A youth’s Path Protector would protect them from all the dangers encountered on the journey of growing up. As a bystander, a Path Protector would watch the path they were protecting, which was also the growth of the youth.","Those who were qualified to become Path Protectors were required to have a Willpower Rune. The Path Protector would then swear an oath at the Willpower Rune and protect the youth’s growth with all their might and even their life until they were satisfied with it.","The Path Protector would then activate their oath again and take on the duty of the youth’s butler.","They would not just protect the growth of the youth as a bystander.","If a Path Protector was dissatisfied with the path they were protecting, the Path Protector would dissolve the rune oath with the youth once the youth grew up. From then on, the Path Protector would leave the youth and no longer protect them.","Generally, the youths with Path Protectors were all from prestigious and high-ranking families. This was due to the fact that an expert would not gain any real benefits after becoming a Path Protector. They were just gambling on the youth’s future.","If the path they were protecting ceased to exist, the Path Protector would suffer a backlash from the Willpower Rune. The Path Protector would do their best to protect the youth’s future until the youth matured. Thus, a Path Protector’s protection was somewhat like the rite of a knight before the Spirit Qi Awakening.","Of course, a Path Protector did not just protect indiscriminately. Before the youth grew up, a Path Protector could only take action in the event of a life-and-death situation. It was a kind of life protection.","Usually, even if the youth suffered insults and endless torture, the Path Protector could only watch if it was not a life-and-death situation.","The resistance that a youth encountered might seem hard, but they were of utmost importance for the transformation of the youth’s mentality or strength. This was because each step of the growth of the youths, especially the geniuses, was like stepping on thorns. Only when they stepped over the thorns could they reach the true heights and be at the top with a magnificent view from above.","Lin Yuan had common knowledge about the Path Protectors, but he did not expect himself to have one. Even if the Moon Empress was his Master, he did not expect to have an expert protecting him closely one day.","Lin Yuan did not feel that this was a bad thing. He might not be able to adapt to it at first, but he did not need to worry about being assassinated.","On the journey, when Cold Moon told Lin Yuan about Cheng Wu’s sentence with a cold expression, her eyes would flash with cold light when she mentioned Cheng Wu.","“The Sin Cleansing Pool’s five Sin Cleansing Weeping Willows had been taken away because the Spirit Guards wanted to suppress the feys. Currently, Mystic Moon has replanted these five Sin Cleansing Weeping Willows. The Sin Cleansing Spring in the Sin Cleansing Pool is rather blocked, and Mystic Moon has also asked for it to be repaired and opened up. With the enhancement of the Moon Empress’ moonlight, Cheng Wu could probably repent in the Sin Cleansing Pool during his numbered days.”","Lin Yuan knew little about the Sin Cleansing Weeping Willows and the Sin Cleansing Spring in the Sin Cleansing Pool that Cold Moon had mentioned.","However, all the people ranging from 10-year-olds to 80-year-olds from the Radiance Federation would have heard of the Sin Cleansing Pool. This place that made people shudder had countless legends. Only the vilest people would be imprisoned in the Sin Cleansing Pool to cleanse their sins.","Cheng Wu would not have a good time in the Sin Cleansing Pool.","Lin Yuan did not express any opinions on Cheng Wu’s sentence, as he did not want to make things difficult for the Moon Empress. He would never go easy on someone who wanted to kill him.","However, Lin Yuan also understood that he relied on the power of his Master, the Moon Empress, to do everything, and not because of his own strength.","But this was only temporary. He believed that he would have a place in this world eventually.","When he arrived in the Radiant Moon Palace’s inner palace, he saw the Moon Empress combing the snow-white fur of a beautiful seven-tailed fey.","This fey was a white fox with seven tails. Its eyes were dark green, and its beautiful appearance exuded elegance. Its gaze could make anyone feel the unparalleled cruelty coming from it.","At that moment, an ordinary rabbit that was eating a carrot jumped onto the Moon Empress’ shoulders while constantly eating the carrot.","When this rabbit jumped onto the Moon Empress’ shoulder, the white seven-tailed fox suddenly lowered its head.","In Lin Yuan’s opinion, it seemed to be afraid of this rabbit. It slowly prostrated with its tail slightly curled up. This was how fox feys expressed their submission. Even though these feys were known for their arrogance and rarely submitted even to death, this fey was actually submissive.","The fox feys had always been outstanding among the beast-type feys, as few were comparable to them. Furthermore, fox feys were very rare, so it was usually hard to see them, let alone a white seven-tailed fox.","Lin Yuan remembered something recorded in some books on supernatural fables in his previous life.","When a fox has seven tails, a series of calamities will ensue. When a fox has nine tails, the world will be in chaos.","Before Lin Yuan could examine this white seven-tailed fox in front of him, the Moon Empress had finished combing its tail. She then raised her hand and stored this seven-tailed fox in the spiritual spatial zone.","Cold Moon went forward and said, “Moon Empress, your Calamity Sun-Swallowing Fox has evolved from six tails to seven tails. It seems to have evolved into Myth I.”","The Moon Empress nodded and saw Lin Yuan. Then she waved her hand and said as a smile spread across her face, “Now that you’re here, I guess you should have escaped from being assassinated.”","The Moon Empress examined Lin Yuan’s expression and was also relieved. Previously, she had been thinking about how to enlighten him.","Lin Yuan chuckled and revealed his white teeth, looking very cheerful.","“I’ve made you worried, Master.”","Actually, Lin Yuan was not frightened because of the previous assassination. His expression had looked ugly because Lin Yuan truly recognized how weak he really was after the assassination.","After living two lifetimes and died once, ordinary people could not imagine Lin Yuan’s firmness.","When Lin Yuan addressed her as Master, the Moon Empress beamed with joy right away, which left Cold Moon dumbfounded.","Cold Moon could not remember how many years it had been since the Moon Empress had smiled so happily!"]},{"number":118,"title":"Chapter 118: Mother of Bloodbath","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Cold Moon also revealed a rare smile on her normally cold face. She wasn’t just happy for the Moon Empress; she was actually influenced by the atmosphere.","After some casual talk, the Moon Empress’ face suddenly turned serious and stern.","“I have been considering and feel that it is better to pick a Path Protector for you early. If you are in danger, at least, your safety is guaranteed.”","Lin Yuan didn’t refuse and nodded. “Master, I shall listen to your arrangement.”","The Moon Empress’ smile was maintained on her face as Lin Yuan didn’t refuse. This disciple that she had accepted was rather strong-minded and wasn’t very used to relying on her. Therefore, as his Master, the Moon Empress struggled to speak some of the words.","Now that Lin Yuan accepted in such a straightforward manner, the Moon Empress made a rare joke. “Your Path Protector is in this inner palace and within your vision. Let’s see if you can find the individual.”","Lin Yuan looked around the large hall, and his eyes finally landed on Cold Moon. He involuntarily thought, Master wouldn’t have arranged for Cold Moon to be my Path Protector, right!?","Cold Moon smiled and looked at Lin Yuan; she didn’t speak nor nod.","At that moment, Lin Yuan suddenly felt a weight on his shoulder, while a strange voice echoed from it. The voice sounded rather chilly, and it made his hair stand on end. However, this eerie female voice was also abnormally pleasant.","“Kid, where are you looking? Your Path Protector is here!”","When Lin Yuan felt a weight on his shoulder, he knew that something had landed on it. He turned around and noticed that a red and crystal sculpture-like spider had actually landed on his shoulder.","The spider legs had bright red crystal-like hair and were so red that they were dazzling as if dipped in blood. Its outer shell looked like it was sculpted from a red crystal, bright red at that, that gave off a cruel beauty. This spider lifeform looked just like a flawless product of heaven.","However, its eight slender legs and body were filled with spikes that exhibited its prowess.","At the same time, Lin Yuan felt as though he could smell a faint aura of blood from this spider. It was as if it emitted a layer of sticky blood energy.","As Lin Yuan was observing this red crystal-like spider, the latter was also observing Lin Yuan carefully.","Lin Yuan observed for a moment before he turned to look at the Moon Empress, who nodded. “That’s right. This is your Path Protector. Mother of Bloodbath. It is a Suzerain/Myth I fey.”","After hearing the Moon Empress’ words, he couldn’t help but exclaim in his mind, My Master actually got a fey as my Path Protector, and a Myth I at that? But what is Suzerain grade?","“Suzerain fey?”","Before the Moon Empress could speak, the Mother of Bloodbath was already replying, “Suzerain-grade is above diamond-grade, Suzerain—”","Before the Mother of Bloodbath could finish talking, it suddenly closed its mouth as it could see the Moon Empress looking at it with cold eyes.","The Moon Empress looked at the Mother of Bloodbath with anger. My fine disciple is finally asking a question. As his Master, I haven’t even given my guidance, so why are you trying to answer?","The Moon Empress ignored the Mother of Bloodbath’s initial explanation and started from the beginning again. “Diamond-grade isn’t actually the limit. Suzerain-grade comes after diamond-grade. Suzerain feys will be able to produce a domain that is in accordance with their exclusive skill. The sky of moonlight that you saw previously was Cold Moon Lone Disk’s domain power.”","Lin Yuan was carefully noting down the Moon Empress’ words and heard her saying again, “This world doesn’t just have human experts, but also fey experts. For a fey to evolve into a Fantasy Breed, the easiest method is to form a contract with humans. Once its quality reaches Legend, and the fey fuses with the contractor’s Willpower Rune, it can become a Fantasy Breed. However, this isn’t the only method for a fey to become a Fantasy Breed.”","The Moon Empress paused for a moment, and when she noticed that Lin Yuan was listening intently to her, she nodded with satisfaction and continued. “A fey without a contractor will generally reach its limit at Diamond. However, if it can upgrade its quality to Legend at the Diamond, then they might have a chance to comprehend a Willpower Rune. It would allow them to fuse with the newly comprehended Willpower Rune and become a Fantasy Breed.”","Lin Yuan was flabbergasted. This was his first time hearing that a fey could evolve into a Fantasy Breed without a contractor. However, according to what the Moon Empress said, a fey would need to be at least diamond-grade before it could become a Fantasy Breed.","Lin Yuan couldn’t help but recall the two Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassias planted at the Radiant Moon Palace entrance as they were already Diamond X/Legend. They were probably waiting to comprehend a Willpower Rune to upgrade into a Fantasy Breed.","Before Lin Yuan could continue thinking more, the Moon Empress continued speaking. “A wild fey might be able to become a Fantasy Breed at diamond-grade, but it would still be stuck at diamond-grade. It can only evolve to suzerain-grade after its quality reaches Fantasy V.”","Lin Yuan gasped with admiration as the evolution of lifeforms in the river of life was one that never rested. After hearing the concept of suzerain-grade for the first time, Lin Yuan involuntarily asked, “Is suzerain-grade much stronger than diamond-grade?”","The Mother of Bloodbath couldn’t keep its mouth shut anymore. “Diamond and Suzerain are two completely different levels. It isn’t possible to even compare them. When a Fantasy V fey evolves to the suzerain-grade, it will experience a World Cleansing. Only those who evolve to suzerain-grade after the World Cleansing have the possibility to reach Myth Breed. The Moon Empress rescued me during the World Cleansing, and thus I am willing to be the Path Protector for a young runt like you.”","The Mother of Bloodbath revealed a slight trace of fear when mentioning the World Cleansing. Hence, Lin Yuan understood that the World Cleansing was considered an opportunity and also a calamity for feys.","The beautiful thing about life was that it would transform and undergo rebirth after a calamity. If it couldn’t surpass the calamity, then the evolution process would cease to exist in the river of life.","The Moon Empress looked at Lin Yuan solemnly and said, “This is considered a top secret of the Radiance Federation. Only king-class experts are qualified to know, so most of the people place their attention on the quality of feys and neglect their grade, which is the most fundamental attribute. In order to evolve to suzerain-grade, the fey will have to reach Fantasy V at diamond-grade. In the eyes of any Suzerain fey, all feys that aren’t at the Suzerain are just ants that are slightly more powerful.”","Lin Yuan didn’t know much about the Myth Breed. He only knew that it was above the Fantasy Breed. But now, he learned that in order to reach the Myth Breed, a fey had to reach Fantasy V and evolve to suzerain-grade first.","Lin Yuan had always felt doubtful as to why all the Fantasy Breed feys were only at diamond-grade. He finally understood now. Only when a Diamond/Fantasy V fey reached suzerain-grade would the said fey be able to get access and ascend into a Myth Breed!"]},{"number":119,"title":"Chapter 119: Law Rune","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Blood-colored energy filled the entire inner palace. Even the dozens of sparkling Diamond lotus flowers in the lotus lake were over-enveloped. The few Platinum Spirit-Siphon Goldfish were all hiding under the lotus leaves and didn’t dare to reveal themselves.","The blood-colored energy made Lin Yuan feel as though he was in a bottomless pool of blood that he couldn’t escape from. The viscous blood seemed like it could devour everything.","A strange female voice with a special tone, cruel and with a hint of solemnity, echoed. A blood-colored rune was shot out of the Mother of Bloodbath’s back, and it was emitting blood-colored waves of light.","“I, the Mother of Bloodbath, use the Law Rune to activate the oath, concluding the Path Protector’s contract and becoming Lin Yuan’s Path Protector.”","After the statement concluded, Lin Yuan felt a trace of energy splitting off from the blood-colored rune and landing on his body. It made Lin Yuan have a subtle feeling that he was connected with the blood-colored rune.","Once the Path Protector contract was formed, the Mother of Bloodbath was now officially Lin Yuan’s Path Protector. From this moment on, Lin Yuan would also have his own Path Protector.","After forming the Path Protector contract, the Mother of Bloodbath looked as though she had exhausted a lot of energy and said with an unwilling tone, “Kid, you are really lucky to form the Path Protector contract. With the influence of my Law Rune, you will have a much easier time to comprehend Willpower Runes.”","When the Mother of Bloodbath was speaking, it was stretching around its hair-filled spider legs. It looked at Lin Yuan with its red eyes as though he was enjoying all the benefits.","Once the Mother of Bloodbath finished speaking, it turned to speak with the Moon Empress seriously. “I am indebted to the Moon Empress for giving me a new life. This time, I shall treat this as repaying the favor to the Moon Empress.”","The Moon Empress looked at the Mother of Bloodbath and spoke in a cold tone. “Protecting and becoming the Path Protector of This Empress’ disciple. This Empress shall accept the conditions.”","The Mother of Bloodbath didn’t say anything else. It turned into a red crystal spider that was only one centimeter long and extremely exquisite with a red flash of energy. It then jumped into Lin Yuan’s hair gently before vanishing within his hair.","As a Path Protector, the Mother of Bloodbath didn’t have any feelings toward Lin Yuan. It was only willing to become his Path Protector, just to repay the life-saving favor. As such, the Mother of Bloodbath wouldn’t give any preferential treatment to Lin Yuan. It would only do what a Path Protector had to do and made sure that he wouldn’t get killed.","The blood-colored energy gradually fused into Lin Yuan’s spiritual energy, giving a lift to Lin Yuan’s spirit. He felt as if the whole world was much clearer.","All of a sudden, Lin Yuan felt he was going to comprehend something as if he could grasp something if he reached out his hand. However, there was also a vague layer of window paper.","But what is the Law Rune that the Mother of Bloodbath mentioned?","Lin Yuan opened his eyes after the comprehension and saw the Moon Empress smiling at him. Before Lin Yuan asked, the Moon Empress said, “When the Mother of Bloodbath became your Path Protector, you comprehended a trace of the Law Rune that the Mother of Bloodbath possesses. It is great as you will be able to comprehend Willpower Runes in the future. The most difficult thing for the young generation is to comprehend the world’s Willpower Runes. Presently, Sequence #1 of the Radiance Hundred already possesses three Willpower Runes.”","The Moon Empress’ objective for saying this was to give Lin Yuan motivation and also pressure. She wanted Lin Yuan to know his advantage, as well as the state of the strongest expert among the young generation.","Lin Yuan suddenly clenched his fist tightly. Don’t I have three Willpower Runes in my spiritual spatial zone? However, I have never told this to anyone yet. I might lack strength, but in terms of the number of comprehended Willpower Runes, I have unknowingly reached the level of the No. 1 expert of the Radiance Federation’s young generation.","Lin Yuan obviously knew that he had obtained an advantage that others could only dream of having. It was to obtain a trace of the Law Rune’s energy and gain enlightenment, which would definitely increase the comprehension ability of Willpower Runes.","However, Lin Yuan still didn’t know what a Law Rune was. When the Moon Empress saw Lin Yuan’s pondering eyes, she explained, “After evolving to Suzerain at Fantasy V, if the fey wishes to reach the Myth Breed, the Willpower Rune will need to transform into the Law Rune.”","The Moon Empress then said nonchalantly, “Willpower Runes are to comprehend the will of the world, while Law Runes are to comprehend the laws of the world before turning them into something to be used. Therefore, there’s a huge gap between Myth Breeds and Fantasy Breeds.”","After asking some knowledge-related questions, Lin Yuan and the Moon Empress conducted a question and answer exercise. Once Lin Yuan asked a question, the Moon Empress would use her experiences to answer. Simultaneously, the Moon Empress was also helping Lin Yuan strengthen the foundation of his knowledge.","The questions and answers were truly a joy for the Master and disciple pair.","Once Lin Yuan left, Cold Moon walked toward the jade-like table and picked up a small delicate pot that looked like it was made of glazed porcelain. She then poured out a cup of tea that was amber in color.","Cold Moon handed the teacup to the Moon Empress and said, “Lordess, it has been a long time since you have been so happy.”","The Moon Empress picked up the cup of tea and took a sip of the amber-colored tea, which left a refreshing, sweet aftertaste.","“It truly feels great to have a disciple. I feel very proud as I see a young fellow growing step by step. It feels as if I am looking at my young self.”","When the Moon Empress spoke, the corners of her mouth were curved up slightly. Perhaps this was the satisfaction of a Master passing down knowledge to the disciple.","...","After exiting the Radiant Moon Palace’s inner palace, Lin Yuan headed toward the Radiant Moon Palace’s other side, where the spiritual ingredient vault was.","Lin Yuan already had the Revival Soil, so he just required a liter of Grasswood Fountain Water and two Mahogany Tree Cores. These two spiritual ingredients might be rather rare in the outside world, but Lin Yuan was truly worried that he wouldn’t be able to find them in the Radiant Moon Palace’s vault. After all, the grade of these spiritual ingredients were obviously lower than the regular spiritual ingredients in the vault.","A red crystal spider was within Lin Yuan’s soft hair, lying there quietly, and it was like a one-centimeter sculpture. It was none other than the Mother of Bloodbath. It was currently in a strange state. When inside Lin Yuan’s hair, the Mother of Bloodbath could constantly feel Lin Yuan’s body emitting very pure spirit qi. Feys loved pure spirit qi, and when the Mother of Bloodbath sensed Lin Yuan’s spirit qi, it felt that it wasn’t as bad as it imagined to be his Path Protector.","Feys had very simple thoughts, and Lin Yuan’s plant spirit qi made the Mother of Bloodbath feel amiable. Thus, its impression of Lin Yuan was naturally better than before.","Lin Yuan knew that the Mother of Bloodbath was lying in his hair, so he said, “Senior, I will need to trouble you in the future.”","The Mother of Bloodbath let out a light snort and lifted its legs before jumping onto Lin Yuan’s nose. “There is no need to call me Senior. You may address me as Mother of Bloodbath. During normal times, don’t call me. Unless you are in a certain death situation, I will not interfere.”","After speaking, the Mother of Bloodbath jumped off from Lin Yuan’s nose and landed on the leaf-shaped Diamond fey storage box on Lin Yuan’s chest. It looked as though there was a decorative red crystal spider on the leaf, and it was extremely exquisite.","Even if someone looked carefully, it was impossible to see that the spider was a living creature."]},{"number":120,"title":"Chapter 120: Path of Original Intention","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","After walking to the Radiant Moon Palace’s spiritual ingredient vault, Lin Yuan noticed there were three spirit attendants in light yellow robes. He had even encountered two of the spirit attendants before as they were the ones that had come to clean up the pavilion.","Since Lin Yuan had heard the idle conversation carried by the wind, he could still vaguely remember their names. The one with the exquisite make-up was called Jin Qi, and the one without make-up was called Wen Yu. As for the other girl, Lin Yuan had never encountered before.","When the trio saw Lin Yuan approaching, Jin Qi’s eyes lit up as she hurried to bow. “Lord Lin Yuan, it has been a long time!”","Lin Yuan nodded and took out a token, carved with two crescent moons, and said, “I am here at the vault to retrieve some spiritual ingredients.”","Jin Qi quickly responded, “What spiritual ingredients does Lord Lin Yuan require? I will go and prepare them right now.”","Lin Yuan scratched his head and said, “I need one liter of Grasswood Fountain Water and two Mahogany Tree Cores.”","When Jin Qi came forward, she had the intention to block off Wen Yu and the other spirit attendant. She didn’t even want to give Wen Yu and the other spirit attendant a chance to speak. She thought that she would definitely serve Lin Yuan to his satisfaction for whatever spiritual ingredients he requested.","But when she heard that the requests were one liter of Grasswood Fountain Water and two Mahogany Tree Cores, she was rather confused and stood there in a daze for two seconds. The other spirit attendant that Lin Yuan didn’t know walked over and said to Lin Yuan in a respectful tone, “Lord Lin Yuan, the vault does have Mahogany Tree Cores, but there isn’t any Grasswood Fountain Water. Because the stream at the waist of the Leaning Moon Mountain is made up of Grasswood Fountain Water. If you need it, I will go and fetch some for you now.”","Jin Qi silently glared at the young girl. She didn’t think that a two-second daze would allow someone to cut into the conversation. When the young girl saw Jin Qi glaring at her, she glared back seamlessly.","Until now, Jin Qi didn’t really understand why Lin Yuan wanted the Mahogany Tree Cores and Grasswood Fountain Water, but she still interrupted with decisiveness. “Lord Lin Yuan, I will go at the waist of the mountain and fetch the Grasswood Fountain Water for you.”","Lin Yuan was rendered speechless as his speculation was actually correct. The spiritual ingredients he required were rare outside but weren’t even qualified to enter the Radiant Moon Palace’s vault.","An entire stream of Grasswood Fountain Water? How many liters is that? The amount of wealth is absurd.","Jin Qi immediately prepared to set off for Leaning Moon Mountain’s waist to fetch the Grasswood Fountain Water upon seeing Lin Yuan nod. But when she was about to leave, she suddenly thought, Wouldn’t I be giving others the chance if I go and fetch the Grasswood Fountain Water?","Jin Qi made a quick counterplan and pulled along the young girl that had interrupted her. “Xi Xi, accompany me to fetch the Grasswood Fountain Water. Since Lord Lin Yuan requires some, we will fetch more and store it in the vault.”","The young girl called Xi Xi was reluctantly pulled away from the Radiant Moon Palace by Jin Qi.","This was the lesser of two evils principle. In Jin Qi’s eyes, Xi Xi had more competitive power than Wen Yu.","The thoughts of a young girl were things that Lin Yuan wouldn’t understand and wouldn’t be able to guess either.","Presently, only the spirit attendant named Wen Yu was left. Lin Yuan gestured and said, “It just so happens that I need some other spiritual ingredients. Why don’t you help me with it?”","Wen Yu bowed and waited for Lin Yuan to continue. He then wrote down all the spiritual ingredients he required on a piece of paper. These were all spiritual ingredients required for Genius and Chimey to reach the Legend quality.","Genius and Chimey might not have a suitable Willpower Rune yet, but their quality could be upgraded to Legend first.","Wen Yu received the paper and replied, “Lord Lin Yuan, these spiritual ingredients are all available in the vault. I wonder whether you will wait here for me or enter with me.”","Since Lin Yuan had nothing else to do, he said, “We will enter together then.”","Once inside the Radiant Moon Palace’s vault, Lin Yuan saw all sorts of spiritual ingredients, and they were all sorted into boxes of different materials on various racks. Due to the different traits of the spiritual ingredients, their storage boxes had to be particularly specific too. Lin Yuan was truly dazzled by the different types of spiritual ingredients.","Wen Yu was very familiar with this place, so she took just a moment to gather everything that Lin Yuan required and store them in a fey storage box. When Lin Yuan received the fey storage box and was preparing to exit with Wen Yu, she suddenly coughed violently.","Wen Yu used a handkerchief to cover her mouth, but the handkerchief was still dyed with some fresh blood. Evidently, she had coughed out earlier too.","After the violent coughing, Wen Yu turned and bowed to Lin Yuan. “My apologies, Lord Lin Yuan. I have been rude.”","Lin Yuan could see that Wen Yu was rather apprehensive when she spoke. He looked at Wen Yu and said, “There is nothing rude. Humans are mortals. How can anyone remain healthy all the time?”","Wen Yu let out an apologetic smile. Lin Yuan then recalled about that night’s idle conversation and asked, “The competitive pressure among spirit attendants must be tough, right?”","Wen Yu nodded as she replied, “The spirit attendants will go through a selection every year. If we don’t reach the standard, we will lose our qualifications to be spirit attendants.”","After Wen Yu replied, Lin Yuan posed a question that stunned her. “If the competition between spirit attendants is so intense, is it worth it to risk injuring the roots to save someone?”","Wen Yu didn’t expect the conversation that night to be overheard, and she really didn’t know how to answer Lin Yuan’s sudden question.","Her talent was originally ranked in the top three, but after she rescued someone and injured her roots, her performance had declined, and she was at the bottom now. She was already determined that she would be the one to lose her qualifications as a spirit attendant.","Since then, she had suffered all sorts of bullying and suppression from her comrades. The person she had rescued had been filled with gratitude at first, but the said person gradually distanced themselves from her and even started to bully her too.","This was the harsh reality. Did Wen Yu regret it? Perhaps!","But why didn’t she even think before rushing over without regard? Was it foolish? It might seem a little foolish now.","Nonetheless, no matter how foolish or regretful she was, her actions back then were in accordance with her true self.","When Lin Yuan saw Wen Yu biting her lips and not giving a reply after a long time, he smiled.","After suffering all the bullying and suppression, if she is able to say that she doesn’t regret it without hesitation, that would definitely be false. She is truly a genuine and kind person, which is rather hard to find.","Lin Yuan turned around and gestured. “Later on, you will help me to bring the Grasswood Fountain Water to the pavilion I am residing at. I will return first.”","While walking back, the Mother of Bloodbath, which had stayed silent until now, spoke. “Why? Has she touched you, and you wish to heal her injuries now?”","The Mother of Bloodbath’s tone sounded mocking. Feys that were able to reach this current state had already disregarded sympathy. Natural selection and survival of the fittest—those were the feys’ iron rules.","Lin Yuan shook his head and said, “Since she chose her own path, then she must persist and grit her teeth to go on.”","The Mother of Bloodbath didn’t respond and continued to lay on the leaf. It then heard Lin Yuan saying again, “But I wish to tell her when I am still capable that her path of original intention isn’t wrong.”","After speaking, Lin Yuan walked on with determination. At the same time, something undetectable happened. The red spider shivered a little, and its aura became gentle."]},{"number":121,"title":"Chapter 121: Upgrading to Legend","paragraphs":["When Wen Yu walked out of Lin Yuan’s pavilion, she might have a pale complexion and was still sickly in appearance, but her eyes emitted a different light. It wasn’t as bright as the lustrous stars, but it was a kind of determination of being acknowledged.","She was holding tightly to a very small amber-colored bottle and was just clamping on it tightly. The afternoon sun was burning like fire, and even though it was deep into autumn, it still gave warmth to the body.","Wen Yu walked on the stone pavement and looked at the bottle in her hands. Her eyes suddenly turned red. A tear dropped on the stone pavement with a ‘drip’ sound, which produced a watermark. The watermark was quickly evaporated by the proud afternoon sun, and even the tears in Wen Yu’s eyes turned into mist.","The bottle she was holding tightly contained a drop of Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar. It was the Radiant Moon Palace’s exclusive product, and it was always precious.","Even the spirit attendants nurtured by the Radiant Moon Palace would only be able to obtain one drop when they were selected as spirit attendants. It helped to cleanse the impurities within their bodies and increase their potential.","The Radiant Moon Palace might seem like a peaceful place, but the competition between spirit attendants never stopped. A moment of impulse and kindness had allowed Wen Yu to see the world’s harsh reality during this year.","With this drop of Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar in her hand, she would be able to cleanse her body’s impurities again and heal her injured roots. Therefore, once she drank this drop of Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar, she would be able to remove the burden.","At that moment, Wen Yu wasn’t just grateful for this drop of Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar. It was because the uncertain path she had chosen had now been proven to be correct. At least, someone had acknowledged this path, and she wasn’t just a kind-hearted fool.","To sacrifice one’s future to do a good deed might sound nice, but Wen Yu might not do it again. Even if she was going to do so, she would weigh out the options with the benefits and losses. After a close encounter with the harsh reality, it allowed Wen Yu to know when she should be using her kindness.","Lin Yuan didn’t wish to see an originally kind-hearted person turning to the darkness at the end. At least, this drop of Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar would allow a kind-hearted young girl to retain that injured kindness, keeping it at the bottom of her heart.","...","When the Mother of Bloodbath saw that Lin Yuan was preparing to enhance feys, it flashed and went outside of the pavilion. It laid on the pavilion’s roof motionlessly as though it was going into a deep sleep.","When a Creation Master enhanced feys, it would easily distract the Creation Master if someone was around. Thus, when Creation Masters wanted to enhance feys, they would choose to be in the breeding room where no one would disturb them.","When there was a contest between Creation Masters, apart from comparing their capabilities, they would also compare their mental attributes and resistance to disturbances. When a Creation Master was preparing a concoction, the sound of a slight distraction might waste all of the spiritual ingredients and might even affect the fey from evolving to the next grade or upgrading its quality.","Lin Yuan returned to the pavilion and took out the spiritual ingredients he had obtained from the Radiant Moon Palace’s vault. He checked them carefully, and when there wasn’t any problem, he placed them on the table.","This matter involved the upgrading of his feys’ quality, so Lin Yuan had to be cautious. He first soaked in the spring water to clean off the dust on his body before changing into a set of clean clothes. He was preparing to upgrade the qualities for the Jasmine Lily, Chimey, Genius, the Spirit-Gather Goldfish, and the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly.","Lin Yuan never had the chance to upgrade a fey’s quality from Epic to Legend, so he didn’t know the difficulty level. Although he imagined that it wasn’t going to be easy, he would finally experience it.","He now had a total of seven feys. However, Morbius’ quality couldn’t be upgraded with normal methods as the quality of the spirit-locked feys would upgrade it. Red Thorn would also have to upgrade its quality by the consumption of flesh.","As such, Lin Yuan could only upgrade the quality of the Jasmine Lily, Chimey, Genius, Spirit-Gather Goldfish, and Blue Flash Purple Butterfly. Lin Yuan pondered for a moment. Since he was going to go into seclusion and upgrade the quality of all five feys, he simply chose the Jasmine Lily as the first fey.","Lin Yuan prepared a purple sand pot[1] before pouring the Revival Soil inside. He then took out two Mahogany Tree Cores, which were superior among the other Mahogany Tree Cores. While looking at the dark red Mahogany Tree Cores, Lin Yuan couldn’t help touching them a little.","The Mahogany Tree Cores were filled with tree bark patterns. They were tree cores from Mahogany Pines, and for each year of age, the tree core would have an additional pattern. Hence, when Lin Yuan looked at these Mahogany Tree Cores, he knew that they came from two, at least, 100-year-old Mahogany Pines.","Lin Yuan took out a crystal bowl before crushing and grinding them carefully. He then poured the Mahogany Tree Cores’ powder into the Revival Soil and stirred them up meticulously. Immediately after, Lin Yuan planted his Bronze X/Epic Jasmine Lily into the mixture.","The Jasmine Lily quickly extended its roots into the mixture before starting to absorb the nutrients. The Jasmine Lily was lush and plump as a succulent, while the flower was translucent and limpid, emitting a light fragrance.","As it got closer to the core of the flower, the color would look more like jade. If one took a casual glance, they would feel as though there was a good-looking jade at the center of the Jasmine Lily’s flower.","Since the Jasmine Lily was taking root, Lin Yuan started to pour in the Grasswood Fountain Water slowly. Once the soil mixture was moist enough, he stopped pouring more Grasswood Fountain Water and circulated his spiritual power to enhance the Jasmine Lily.","Every time the Jasmine Lily absorbed the Grasswood Fountain Water in the soil mixture, the soil mixture would dry up, and Lin Yuan would pour in more Grasswood Fountain Water. As the Jasmine Lily absorbed the energy within the mixture of Revival Soil, Mahogany Tree Cores, and Grasswood Fountain Water, it would become greener.","Lin Yuan enhanced the Jasmine Lily for a few hours before checking on its condition. He felt that it was truly a huge task to upgrade the Jasmine Lily’s quality to Legend. Thus, he entered the Spirit Lock spatial zone to enhance the Jasmine Lily under an environment with more concentrated spirit qi.","Time elapsed quickly. Apart from having his meals and five hours of sleep, Lin Yuan would spend the rest of the time enhancing the Jasmine Lily.","Five days later, apart from a small portion of Revival Soil left, the two Mahogany Tree Cores’ powder and one liter of Grasswood Fountain Water had been used up by Lin Yuan. The Jasmine Lily had already stopped absorbing the purple sand pot’s energy, and Lin Yuan realized that its quality was now Legend.","Lin Yuan let out a deep breath and wiped the sweat off his forehead. After upgrading the Jasmine Lily’s quality from Epic to Legend, Lin Yuan was now more certain. He knew that it would take around five days to enhance a Bronze fey from Epic to Legend within the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","[1] It is actually the Yixing ware"]},{"number":122,"title":"Chapter 122: Evolving to Fantasy Breed","paragraphs":["Lin Yuan was currently using his fingers to rub his temples while he was in deep thought. For the past five days, he had been sleeping for only five hours a day on average. The rest of the time would be basically used to enhance the Jasmine Lily, and it was truly exhausting for Lin Yuan. During the enhancement, Lin Yuan would need to constantly circulate the spiritual power within his body.","In order to be able to circulate spiritual power like this, Lin Yuan would need at least five hours of sleep to compensate for the exhaustion. Of course, this was because of the bowl of Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar had consumed previously as it had cleansed the impurities in his body. If Lin Yuan tried to enhance such a fey before consuming the bowl of Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar, his body wouldn’t have been able to take it.","While contemplating, Lin Yuan suddenly stood up. He found someone to bring over a Silver/Epic fey for him to enhance within the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","Lin Yuan realized that it was truly difficult for him to enhance a Silver/Epic fey to Legend right now. He spent the past two days enhancing the Silver/Epic fey. After checking on the Silver/Epic fey’s condition, Lin Yuan discovered that all his hard work for the past two days was all for naught. He was inadequate in enhancing the Silver/Epic fey to Legend quality.","After a rough calculation, if Lin Yuan wanted to enhance a Silver/Epic fey to Legend quality, he would need to go through a sleepless process for over two months in the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","The current situation allowed Lin Yuan to know that he was completely different from other Creation Masters. It would be easier for other Creation Masters to enhance a fey’s quality from Epic to Legend if the fey’s grade was higher, but it was the opposite for Lin Yuan.","For Lin Yuan, the lower the grade of the fey, the easier it was for him to enhance the quality from Epic to Legend. Given Lin Yuan’s current strength, he was unable to increase a Silver/Epic fey’s quality to Legend.","If this matter was made known outside, it would overturn the perspective and knowledge of other Creation Masters. If Lin Yuan were to put a Bronze/Legend fey on an auction, it would probably cause an instant uproar in the Radiance Federation. All the major factions in the Radiance Federation would most probably be competing for it frenziedly.","After the experiment, Lin Yuan asked for someone to bring the Silver/Epic Needle-Tailed Squirrel away. He then went to look for the Moon Empress in the inner palace to inform her that he was planning to enter seclusion.","Subsequently, Lin Yuan entered seclusion at the pavilion. He used over 20 days to enhance Genius, Chimey, the Spirit-Gather Goldfish, and the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly from Bronze/Epic to Bronze/Legend.","After rounding up the number of days, he took a total of one month to finally upgrade his five contracted feys from Epic to Legend quality.","Lin Yuan was extremely exhausted now. During the last month, apart from his basic body functions’ maintenance and recovery, he would enhance the feys’ qualities. Therefore, he felt very fatigued. However, the joy of seeing his contracted feys upgrading from Epic to Legend quality was truly indescribable.","Lin Yuan looked at the evolved states of Genius, Chimey, the Spirit-Gather Goldfish, and the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly. Their quality might be Legend, but their appearances didn’t undergo many changes. Nevertheless, their spirits and vitality were evidently enhanced.","Genius’ fur had become even softer, while its memory was even better.","Chimey’s feathers had even more obvious cloud patterns, and its exclusive skill, Clear Sky’s scorching trait, was more intense. Its voice was even more pleasant to the ears now and its singing ability way better.","However, the current Chimey didn’t know that its disappearance for over a month had caused its fans to go completely insane. Chimey was a phenomenon-class host, and there was a GIF blocking the screen. Its singing voice had intoxicated plenty of people. Many even speculated that Chimey was actually an absolute beauty who was trying to rely on her talent to earn a living.","The Radiance Hundred’s Sequence #87, Lord Ranger, was a fanatic supporter. When he won a battle against his opponent on the Celestial Stairway, he even publicly expressed that he loved listening to Chimey’s sounds. Consequently, that allowed Chimey to become even more famous.","Chimey, a new star that had risen up to the sky, had suddenly vanished without a trace, for an entire month at that. Plenty of forum topics on the Star Web focused on this incident, and there were all sorts of speculations too. Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess’s disappearance had already become a popular topic among the Radiance Federation’s entertainment news.","The Spirit-Gather Goldfish was now swimming and giving off a special prowess. This kind of prowess was similar to what Long Tao’s Sea King Cretaceous Dragon gave off. However, the Spirit-Gather Goldfish’s prowess was still rather faint. It was a kind of dragon prowess that was unique to the dragon-species feys.","The Blue Flash Purple Butterfly’s scale powder was now lighter and finer, making it easier to spread further. When the floating scale powder reflected light, it would look as though there was a light purple-based rainbow trailing behind the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly, making it exceptionally beautiful.","Lin Yuan stretched his body and immediately lay down on his bed for a good long sleep.","This sleep took up an entire day, and it compensated for all the hard work previously, allowing his body to return to its best and most lively state.","...","Lin Yuan was going to begin fusing the Jasmine Lily with the Willpower Rune, allowing it to evolve into a Fantasy Breed.","He concentrated and summoned one of the three Willpower Runes from the spiritual spatial zone. This Willpower Rune was the one that he had comprehended after observing the green mountain. A fire had scorched all its greenery, yet after several months of fine rain, plants had started growing again.","In Lin Yuan’s opinion, instead of saying that the rain gave life, it was better to say that plants had tenacious vitality. A wildfire wouldn’t be able to burn everything, while the spring’s wind would bring back life again. Perhaps it was due to the remaining roots within the soil that would conduct a praising of life after several months, allowing for greenery to be reborn.","Lin Yuan looked at the green mountain-shaped Willpower Rune and shot it toward his Bronze X/Legend Jasmine Lily.","In an instant, the Jasmine Lily’s flower flickered. It was filled with desire as it embraced the Willpower Rune, allowing it to instantly fuse with the Jasmine Lily.","The willpower of how a green mountain would never change its color and that all living things would be reborn allowed the Jasmine Lily to emit a jade-colored light.","The Jasmine Lily’s originally short branches suddenly shrunk and vanished. More flowers popped out, and in just a moment, and the Jasmine Lily resembled an emerald green bouquet now. The flowers were all squeezed together and looked like they were forming a small mountain shape. The unique Jasmine Lily’s fragrance was now even more concentrated.","Lin Yuan gasped with surprise.","The Jasmine Lily actually developed bunches!","When succulent plants were growing and evolving, there was a very strong instability, and it was very rare for mutations to occur. Growing in bunches was actually a kind of fundamental mutation for succulents. Once it happened, the succulent plant would give up a portion of evolution potential. It would firm down on the gene model to evolve toward a flawless gene model.","Due to Morbius’ Spirit Lock, the Jasmine Lily only had one ability—Heal. This meant that the Jasmine Lily had given up on the possibility of having more abilities and focused on enhancing Heal!"]},{"number":123,"title":"Chapter 123: A Healing Ability Can Actually Be A Control Ability","paragraphs":["Succulents could not control a mutation, such as developing bunches. Most succulents with a contract with humans did not prefer a mutation like this.","Although most feys had stronger abilities in the later stages, there would rarely be such anomalies like the Blue Flash Butterfly.","However, things were different, as Lin Yuan’s Jasmine Lily could only use one ability.","After forming bunches, each of the Jasmine Lily flowers could release healing energy. This was akin to the Jasmine Lily healing multiple targets. Each flower was equivalent to an increase in healing.","Just as Lin Yuan thought the Jasmine Lily was about to complete its Fantasy Breed evolution, its round petals suddenly turned into a long, irregular shape.","Soon, the bottom layer of the Jasmine Lily and those flowers grew into an irregular shape. Only the largest flower of the Jasmine Lily was left on top without experiencing any changes.","Lin Yuan could not help but cry out in surprise at this sudden change.","Unexpectedly, after forming bunches, a rare fasciation in succulents actually occurred!","Fasciation was the most amorphous abnormal mutation in succulents. It caused the plant itself to have amorphous development and growth.","At the same time, fasciation was one of the most precious mutations of succulents.","Lin Yuan had never heard of a fasciated Jasmine Lily because it would only occur in succulent feys when they were evolving into Fantasy Breeds. Nobody would choose to evolve a Jasmine Lily, one of the most basic feys, into a Fantasy Breed. As such, Lin Yuan’s fasciated Jasmine Lily might be the only one in the world.","After fasciation, the Jasmine Lily’s bottom petals grew layer by layer and destroyed the original structure of the flower. Thus, the emerald green in the middle of the Jasmine Lily spread out to all parts of the leaves.","At another glance, it seemed like a lingering emerald mist, just like the feeling of the mist from the best jades.","The Jasmine Lily flower at the very top that had not experienced any changes became as big as a bowl.","The Jasmine Lily was only truly evolving into a Fantasy Breed at this moment.","After the Jasmine Lily had evolved into a Fantasy Breed, Lin Yuan used Jasmine Lily’s Heal ability on himself immediately. He felt that he was lost in a trance for three seconds while the surging vitality was injecting into his body.","As a result, he suddenly had a feeling as though he had collapsed on a big soft bed when he was the most tired. It was just like how he wanted to laze in bed in the early morning and could not be woken up.","Lin Yuan believed that he was strong-willed, but it was still very hard for him to recover from this sense of extreme happiness.","When he completely came back to his senses, an idea arose in his head as he looked at the Jasmine Lily.","Its Heal ability was clearly a healing-type ability, but it now seemed to be able to be used as a control-type ability. The happiness and sense of being lost in a trance due to the Heal ability’s comfortable feeling were actually a kind of unexpected control.","After some experiments, Lin Yuan finally discovered the source of this sense of happiness.","When only that Jasmine Lily flower that had not undergone fasciation was used to heal, it would just heal injuries swiftly. There would not be the feeling of happiness of having one’s vitality replenished.","However, when the irregular fasciated flowers were used to heal, that feeling of happiness would be born.","It seemed that the fasciation had mutated the Jasmine Lily’s Heal ability.","When Lin Yuan looked at the exclusive skill that had appeared when the Jasmine Lily evolved into a Fantasy Breed, he could not help but stare blankly at the Jasmine Lily in his hands.","[Normal Spirit Lock]:","Jasmine Lily: Bronze (10/10), Fantasy I","Ability – [Heal]: Rapidly recovers external injuries and gradually recovers vitality.","Exclusive Skill:","[Recovery Imprint]: Accumulate the healing energy that is released by the Jasmine Lily during normal times. The contractor can activate the imprint to release the accumulated healing energy.","[Severed Limbs Growth]: Comprehend the arcana of plant growth. Even if one has severed limbs, the rich vitality can continue to grow slowly.","What kind of great product have I created?","This exclusive skill of the Fantasy Breeds could allow them to use their surging vitality to activate the muscle cells’ memory factor and thus achieve the ability for severed limbs to regrow.","Of course, these severed limbs referred to hands and feet, and even arms and thighs. Without a head, one would certainly die even if the gods arrived, unless he laughed his head off!","Now that he had his first Fantasy Breed fey, Lin Yuan would first evolve the Jasmine Lily. He had actually wondered how hard it would be to evolve the Jasmine Lily from Bronze to Gold.","While he was evolving it, Lin Yuan realized it was simply difficult to upgrade the grade of a Fantasy Breed fey.","After spending a month in seclusion, he then evolved the Jasmine Lily to Silver with difficulty.","He now seemed to have suddenly understood why feys that evolved into Fantasy Breeds early on had greater potential.","There was a conservation of energy. After a month of spirit qi injection, a Fantasy Breed would evolve from Bronze X to Silver and go through a door that would be broken at a touch before it evolved into a Fantasy Breed.","Since the spirit qi would not disappear out of thin air, the Fantasy Breed Jasmine Lily had absorbed a huge amount of spirit qi.","The foundation laid by this huge amount of spirit qi was naturally much stronger than the feys that evolved into Fantasy Breeds after reaching Bronze.","During this period, Lin Yuan had been in seclusion, evolving his fey in the Spirit Lock spatial zone all day, which suffocated him. There was more to life than it met the eye, like poetry and faraway places.","During these two months, Lin Yuan had the capital to step into the world. It was time for him to take a look at the world. Only when he took a look at the world would he then know how to live as splendid as the summer flowers. As such, Lin Yuan decided to visit the Endless Forest outside the Royal Capital for wild harvesting.","The feys Creation Masters enhanced were not all hand-reared. Some rarer feys were collected from wild harvesting.","Creation Masters would attract the feys by mixing spiritual ingredients and use the spirit qi in the spiritual ingredients to make the wild feys approach humans. After enhancing them, they would sell them.","Lin Yuan did not have to go through such trouble. He only needed to channel spirit qi and place his palm toward the wild feys. This pure spirit qi could soon allow the wild feys to have a favorable impression of him.","Lin Yuan was going to open his own store in the Royal Capital. Although he had yet to do so, it was of utmost importance to gather some rare feys in advance. He could not always pick near-death feys with damaged roots. Not only would it be hard to find such feys, but he also had no way to heal them now, even if he found high-grade feys.","In addition, there was a Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus and a recovering Cinnabar Osmanthus Haworthia in the Spirit Lock spatial zone’s Pure Land of Bliss.","The 40-square-meter Pure Land of Bliss in the Spirit Lock spatial zone would not be big enough for him to accommodate some other feys with damaged roots. Moreover, Lin Yuan was still waiting for the Cinnabar Osmanthus Haworthia fruit, which he urgently needed, to enhance his spiritual power.","After finishing up, Lin Yuan was ready to go. He planned to return to the Royal Capital after the wild harvesting and establish the store first."]},{"number":124,"title":"Chapter 124: Not Even in The Sin Cleansing Pool","paragraphs":["The red afterglow in the rosy-tinted sky at the Royal Capital was especially conspicuous. It made the sky look especially tall and vast.","The evening arrived.","Since Lin Yuan had decided to set off and did not intend to live on the Leaning Moon Mountain for a long time, he simply went to the Radiant Moon Palace to bid goodbye to his Master, the Moon Empress.","He then left the pavilion when the Mother of Bloodbath opened its eyes on the roof and jumped onto the leaf-shaped fey storage box on his chest.","It continued to lie motionless as it gained insight into the Law Rune.","When he reached the Radiant Moon Palace’s inner palace, and the Moon Empress saw Lin Yuan come, her eyes lit up as she asked, “You’ve been in seclusion for two months. Have you gained anything?”","Lin Yuan touched the back of his head and smiled brightly, revealing his white teeth and a youthful aura.","“I did gain from this seclusion.”","For Lin Yuan, raising his five feys from Epic to Legend and getting his first Fantasy Breed fey during his seclusion, they were considered huge and important harvests.","Upon hearing that, the Moon Empress nodded with a smile. She had always appreciated Lin Yuan’s character, but she did not expect he would be so hardworking in his cultivation.","Nowadays, few youths would spend over two months in seclusion without going out.","Ever since the Moon Empress had taken Lin Yuan as her disciple, she had not asked him about his progress as a Creation Master and spirit qi professional, besides teaching him the appropriate knowledge. She felt that one should mainly rely on one’s own self-consciousness for cultivation.","On the other hand, she also did not want to pressure him, so she never asked him about it.","Since the Moon Empress had not asked, Lin Yuan had never told her about his progress either.","Regardless of whether he had three Willpower Runes before or the fact that the Jasmine Lily that had evolved into a Fantasy Breed at Bronze, the Moon Empress was his Master. If she asked him about it, he would naturally tell her without hiding anything.","However, she did not ask him about it. As he was an introvert, he would not take the initiative to tell her.","Lin Yuan knew his own capabilities. These were his means and not something to show off. If other people had Lin Yuan’s skills, they would probably have made it known. He had always been afraid that if he showed himself too much, the saying ‘An outstanding person will attract jealousy and criticism’ would apply in his case.","But now, with the Moon Empress as his Master, Lin Yuan did not need to worry about these. No matter how strong the wind would be, with the Moon Empress, a tall and straight little tree like Lin Yuan would not be affected at all.","Moreover, the Suzerain/Myth Breed Mother of Bloodbath was following him. If anybody dared to do anything to Lin Yuan, they would have to worry about themselves first.","After a few moments of small talk, Lin Yuan told the Moon Empress why he was there.","Upon hearing his words, she raised her hand and handed him a dark-brown beetle-shaped accessory with a pin on the back. It could be worn.","At a glance, Lin Yuan recognized that the beetle-shaped accessory was a Diamond fey storage box. This beetle-shaped fey storage box was dark brown with some dark-green patterns on it and looked strange. It was far from looking as nice as the previous leaf-shaped Diamond fey storage box.","Lin Yuan took this strange beetle-shaped Diamond fey storage box and heard the Moon Empress say, “This Diamond fey storage box contains all the wealth that Cheng Wu had accumulated over the years as a pinnacle Class 4 Creation Master. He had attacked you before, so take the things in this fey storage box as something to help you recover from the shock.”","Lin Yuan looked at the Moon Empress’ deeply concerned gaze and did not reject her. He put away this Diamond beetle-shaped fey storage box. When he was doing so, he took a look at the Diamond fey storage box.","He found that instead of some unknown spiritual ingredients, a huge amount of Radiance dollars was inside.","Lin Yuan had been using the Star Web Card to transfer money, so although he knew what the Radiance dollars looked like, he had never used them.","When he looked inside the Diamond fey storage box, he saw bottle cap-sized Radiance dollars like amber buttons piled up like a little mountain.","Lin Yuan was shocked at the sight. He did not know how many Radiance dollars were inside, but the wealth of a pinnacle Class 4 Creation Master was really not to be underestimated.","After sitting for a while, when Lin Yuan was ready to bid goodbye, he heard the Moon Empress say softly, “You still have a long road ahead of you, and the world is very vast. It’s up to you to fly to the highest, farthest, and vastest place. Remember, no matter what happens, I will always be your support.”","Upon hearing that, a feeling of being cared for surfaced at the bottom of his heart. Lin Yuan was used to being independent, but this feeling made him cherish it.","After respectfully performing a disciple’s salute, he returned to his pavilion and was prepared to leave first thing in the morning.","He was still thinking about where he should open his store and how much space to buy. Thanks to Cheng Wu’s wealth in this Diamond fey storage box, Lin Yuan had more options to open his store without worrying about the expenses.","As a Creation Master, although he had great capabilities to make money, he lacked the capital. He could do whatever he wanted now without being restrained now that he had a capital.","...","After Lin Yuan left, Cold Moon went forward and saw that the Moon Empress was watching Lin Yuan leave, so she asked, “Are you worried about Lin Yuan?”","The Moon Empress shook her head and poured a cup of tea before she sipped a mouthful and replied, “I’m not worried. I’m just proud and a little reluctant to see my own disciple wanting to explore the world.”","Upon hearing that, Cold Moon said softly, “Didn’t you exchange all of Cheng Wu’s accumulated wealth into equivalent Radiance dollars so that he will have the capital to explore the world? You have gone through a lot of trouble.”","The Moon Empress shook her head and did not continue to speak further. After she had taken in a disciple, she then understood the true responsibility as a teacher.","The continuation of life and passing down of knowledge were never as simple as through words.","Although they were unrelated by blood, they had reached the degree of kinship through the master-disciple relationship.","At that moment, the sounds of footsteps came from outside. Mystic Moon walked in and bowed before saying, “Moon Empress, Cheng Wu has been suffering in the Sin Cleansing Pool for two months and has just died. The Spirit Guards’ Chief Guard Ye and Iron Prison asked you what they should do next.”","The Moon Empress stood up and was about to go to the breeding room when she answered in a clear, cold voice, “He’s dead, so what is there to be done? Let them handle it by themselves. After my moonlight hit him, he was capable of lasting two months in the Sin Cleansing Pool. How could I let him off when he wanted to harm my disciple? Not even if he’s alive in the Sin Cleansing Pool.”"]},{"number":125,"title":"Chapter 125: Guild Alliance and the S Tournament","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","The next morning, Lin Yuan went down the Leaning Moon Mountain early and traveled light. He had stored all the things into the Diamond fey storage box on his chest, and it had to be said that this fey storage box was pretty convenient.","Last night, Lin Yuan sent a message to Liu Jie, telling him that he did not need to worry about choosing a store anymore. He would pick a bigger store that was situated well, as he no longer needed to worry about money.","When he got down the Leaning Moon Mountain, Lin Yuan had an obvious purpose.","He called for a Speed-Hoofed Donkey Car and headed to the Guild Alliance.","This Guild Alliance was not an official organization like the Creation Master Association and the other lifestyle-class spirit qi occupation guilds. The Guild Alliance was an alliance of countless guild clubs in the Radiance Federation that relied on the Combat-Class Spirit Qi Occupation Guild.","Lin Yuan was going to register and get authenticated in this Guild Alliance.","After registering in the Guild Alliance, he could join the guild club teams and form a temporary team if he wanted to go wild harvesting. He could even receive and issue missions in the Guild Alliance.","If the Star Web was the second world of the Radiance Federation’s citizens and had the second world industry, the Guild Alliance would be where most combat-class spirit qi professionals lived, worked, and trained in the real world.","One could get a lot of commissions by completing the missions.","If a boss issued a mission, one could also get the spiritual ingredients or feys one needed as soon as possible with adequate remuneration.","Many Creation Masters who needed special spiritual ingredients would also issue a mission with rewards at the Guild Alliance. Some well-known guild club teams would accept the missions for those with high rewards.","Of course, most of the time, the feys for the Guild Alliance’s mission reward were basically rare ones.","If one wanted to evolve a precious fey or enhance the fey’s grade, they would need to find a Creation Master.","If there would be any place where Creation Masters would be most respected and most popular, that would certainly be the Guild Alliance.","In the Guild Alliance’s casual teams, most of the combat-class spirit qi professionals were at lower levels, and those without outstanding qualities might work hard for a year or two to enhance the fey’s quality or grade.","Most of the true talents or stronger spirit qi professionals had joined a guild club. If a talented person wanted to be chosen by a powerful guild club, the best way would be to fight until the 80th floor and above in the Star Web Tower or even up to the Celestial Stairway.","This was because the powerful guild clubs would choose and accept new people at the Star Tower.","The Radiance Federation admired battle skills. All year round, there were various tournaments for all sorts of guild club teams.","However, the most standard and famous ones had to be included. Every year, the Guild Alliance would work together with the Radiance Federation to hold a tournament of the entire federation’s guild teams.","It was known as the S Tournament.","The S Tournament was considered a tournament for the young ones, as the contestants could not exceed 30 years old. It was almost the same as the members’ age limit in the Radiance Federation’s Radiance Hundred Sequence.","Some truly powerful guild clubs would take part in the S Tournament, and their main teams would more or less have members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","The members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence were the most dazzling star players in the S Tournament. The main teams of some guild clubs were even all made up of the members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","Each guild could only send one team with five members.","Each team must take part in various knockout matches, group matches, and qualification matches to make it to the next round.","16 teams would eventually be chosen to compete on the Star Web with the Radiance Federation citizens watching before finally being ranked.","Even though these 16 teams would be ranked, the top three teams would be divided into the champion and runners-up, all of whom would receive different levels of rewards and unparalleled glory.","However, only the champions would be remembered.","After all, there was a saying—’The second place is the first loser’.","There was no limit in learning, so everyone could contend against one another. However, in combat, the strong and the weak could be differentiated at a glance.","Lin Yuan had arrived at the entrance of the Guild Alliance and got off the Speed-Hoofed Donkey Car. He looked at the lively and prosperous scene before him and touched the back of his head.","The Guild Alliance was the liveliest place in the Royal Capital, which seemed like the case now.","Lin Yuan entered the Guild Alliance and realized the people at the side were looking at him.","One of the Guild Alliance’s receptionists warmly greeted him and looked at him with a burning gaze.","Lin Yuan soon found out the reason. It turned out that these people were looking at the Class 2 Creation Master crest on his chest. It seemed that Creation Masters were conspicuous wherever they went.","At that moment, the Guild Alliance receptionist asked respectfully, “Class 2 Creation Master, did you come to the Guild Alliance to issue a mission or find a guild club squad?”","Lin Yuan quickly shook his head and answered, “I’m here for the first time, and I intend to register and get authenticated.”","Upon hearing that, the receptionist beamed with joy and quickly replied, “Please follow me to the VIP reception room to get those done, sir.”","Then, the receptionist hurriedly led the way.","The receptionist was overjoyed. Although Creation Masters would issue missions at the Guild Alliance, it would only require them to have an identity authentication, so few Creation Masters would choose to register in the Guild Alliance.","The purpose of registering at the Guild Alliance was to be able to receive missions. If Creation Masters wanted to earn money, make a concoction of spiritual ingredients, or cultivate feys, they would not need to take up missions at the Guild Alliance.","If any receptionists in the Guild Alliance could receive a Creation Master and let them register there, they would receive a good commission. This commission was almost as much as the receptionist’s monthly salary, so Lin Yuan’s registration was splendid news to the receptionist.","When Lin Yuan entered the VIP lounge, he unobtrusively took off the Class 2 Creation Master crest on his chest.","At the same time, he summoned Genius for Tool Transformation.","There were two forms of Genius’ Tool Transformation—glasses or masks.","Lin Yuan chose the mask form this time.","Genius transformed into a silver mask with a light pattern that perfectly fit on his face.","Lin Yuan’s aura completely changed when he wore the mask. He looked like a cheerful boy before, but he looked very composed after wearing the mask with black spirit qi clothes.","Soon, he finished what he needed to do in the Guild Alliance.","Lin Yuan only needed to bind himself to the other Star Web Card that he had obtained when he became a Class 2 Creation Master, which was something pretty simple.","Then, he bound his Creation Master identity with the ‘Purchase With No Loss’ Star Web store.","At the same time, he also transferred his account for climbing the Star Tower to the other Star Web Card."]},{"number":126,"title":"Chapter 126: You Cannot","paragraphs":["From this moment on, Lin Yuan possessed two identities in the Star Web and the Radiance Federation. One identity was a prodigy Class 2 Creation Master, Lin Yuan. The other identity was ‘Mr. Black’ that fought in the Star Tower. ‘Black’ was the name that Lin Yuan had just given to his other identity.","Lin Yuan’s actions had basically split up his statuses as a Creation Master and a combat-class spirit qi professional. After finishing the registration and authentication, Lin Yuan saw that the attendant was still going to follow him. He shook his hand and said, “I can continue myself. You can attend to others.”","After speaking, Lin Yuan headed for the mission area. Seeing that Lin Yuan had left, the attendant muttered. “Such a young Class 2 Creation Master is actually a healing-type spirit qi professional too. Such a combination is truly going to make someone jealous to death!”","That’s right. Lin Yuan registered, ‘Mr. Black’, his spirit qi professional identity, as a Healer.","Lin Yuan arrived at the mission area and was preparing to look for a team that was heading for the Endless Forest. As a result, he realized that all of the teams were looking for healing-type spirit qi professionals.","He could hear plenty of people hawking loudly in the rather noisy mission area.","“Improvised team. Searching for basic spiritual ingredients, Moist Moss. We have two power offense-type spirit qi professionals, one defense-type spirit qi professional, one support-type spirit qi professional, and we are waiting for one healing-type spirit qi professional.”","“Triple Fire Guild Club. Three club teams are working together to capture a Gold youngling of the Rapid Shadow Lynx. 14 members waiting for one! We lack a healing-type spirit qi professional! As long as you come, you are the boss!”","“Cedar Grass Guild Club. The team is heading to the Endless Forest to capture 10 Silver Black Back Mountain Boars. Let’s earn great money since boar meat is on the rise. Four members waiting for one healing-type spirit qi professional. Please heal my father and mother and quickly join the team. After joining the team, you can take 30% of the team’s profits.”","Lin Yuan raised his brows silently.","Healing-type spirit qi professionals are truly popular.","Lin Yuan might have already known that healing-type spirit qi professionals were rare, as the Radiance Federation estimated that there would only be a single individual that was compatible with healing-type feys among every 100 spirit qi professionals. After learning of this statistical value, Lin Yuan had also been lamenting at the rarity of healing-type spirit qi professionals.","However, when Lin Yuan was in the Guild Alliance’s mission area and saw how every team was seeking a healing-type spirit qi professional, the rarity of healing-type spirit qi professionals was finally proven. Healing-type spirit qi professionals were simply treated as bosses in every single team.","In order to harvest anything great in the Endless Forest, one must enter its depths. It was obvious that the Cedar Grass Guild Club’s team wouldn’t go deep into the Endless Forest since they were capturing Silver Black Back Mountain Boars. After all, they could be found in the outer regions of the Endless Forest.","Recently, a Class 2 Dimensional Rift had opened above the Radiance Federation’s largest pig farm. The dimensional rift was extremely close to the pig farm, and nearly all of the lifeforms that emerged from the dimensional rift would drop directly into the pig farm.","The pig farm had pig-species feys by the number of tens of millions, yet the dimensional lifeforms had instantly eaten them up.","Ultimately, the situation got under control, and the dimensional lifeforms that emerged were also killed. However, the largest pig farm of the Radiance Federation lost tens of millions of pig-species feys. This, in turn, caused an instant shortage, directly increasing the price of pork by several times.","Therefore, all sorts of spirit qi professionals formed small teams to hunt for pigs and boars in the wild. These pigs and boars were mainly captured for reproduction, and only those rare old pig-species feys that couldn’t reproduce would be used as meat. After all, an old pig’s flesh would taste nicer.","In the mission area, there were plenty of solo spirit qi professionals that were searching for teams. As solo spirit qi professionals that would regularly join various teams for adventures in the wild, most of them had carefree and easygoing personalities.","A burly man, who was also searching for a mission, took the initiative to speak with Lin Yuan in a friendly tone as he saw Lin Yuan standing there. “Young Brother, instead of waiting for a mission here, why don’t you take the initiative to speak with some smaller guild club’s teams that require members?”","Lin Yuan turned around to see a burly man looking at him with a straightforward and candid face. According to what the burly man said, Lin Yuan understood that those guild clubs’ teams were much more popular than improvised teams.","From the looks of it, those improvised teams did seem to have a harder time recruiting spirit qi professionals than the guild club teams. Most of the guild club teams were only waiting for one healing-type spirit qi professional.","Most of the improvised teams had given up on getting a healing-type spirit qi professional but were still unable to form their five-men team.","Upon seeing Lin Yuan nod, the burly man laughed heartily. “This is your first time looking for a team and mission, right?”","Lin Yuan was rather curious as to why this burly man was able to see that it was his first time taking a mission.","Could it be that my mask really looks like a newcomer?","“Why are you so certain that this is my first mission? I might be a veteran.”","The burly man pointed at Lin Yuan’s spirit qi clothes and said with a tinge of envy, “Who would wear such spirit qi clothes for an adventure? If the clothes get torn, a single mission’s reward won’t be enough to compensate for your clothes. Young Brother, it seems like your background isn’t bad. Do you need a veteran to guide you? If you need one, I can do it!”","Lin Yuan finally knew where the problem was, but after hearing the burly man saying he could do it, Lin Yuan suddenly felt a chill in his back. “No, you cannot,” he blurted out.","When the burly man heard Lin Yuan’s response, he shrugged and didn’t really mind. Immediately after, Lin Yuan looked at a nearby guild club team and pointed. “Isn’t there someone wearing spirit qi clothes for an adventure too?”","When the burly man heard Lin Yuan’s question, he patted on his chain armor. “This is the attire for an adventure. That person is wearing spirit qi clothes because he is a healing-type spirit qi professional and the boss of the team.”","Lin Yuan reached for the back of his head and looked at the burly man. “How do you know I am not a healing-type spirit qi professional?”","The burly man rolled his eyes and said, “If you were a healing-type spirit qi professional, would you be here looking for a team? The Guild Alliance’s attendant would have attended to you and helped you to look for a team based on your objective.”","Lin Yuan suddenly recalled about the attendant that had been following him and was hesitant to speak. It turned out that the attendant had been trying to help him contact a team.","When the burly man saw that Lin Yuan didn’t continue speaking, he laughed heartily and patted on Lin Yuan’s shoulder in a friendly manner. “When a newcomer is looking for a team, it is best to look for one that isn’t going to fight and is harvesting fundamental spiritual ingredients. It will familiarize you with the wilderness. Recklessly accepting a mission that requires combat to capture feys might just get you injured and become a burden for the team unless you are really a healing-type spirit qi professional. That way, the team members would do their best to protect you.”","The burly man was certain that Lin Yuan was a newcomer, so he said that in a rather serious tone.","These sounded logical, and Lin Yuan naturally understood. But to be informed by a stranger, he still expressed his gratitude. When the burly man saw that Lin Yuan had registered the information, he wanted to encourage Lin Yuan again. But at this moment, the clamor and noise in the mission area suddenly softened."]},{"number":127,"title":"Chapter 127: Spitting Turtledove","paragraphs":["When the noise softened, Lin Yuan and the burly man immediately looked around. Lin Yuan saw a team wearing white and red, with a flying eagle on the clothes. The team members were all youths that were slightly more than 20 years old.","The four were all wearing the same attire, and it should be the team uniform of a certain guild club. One of the members, a tall and skinny man, walked to the mission area and yelled, “The train heading for Endless Forest is about to depart, veterans are leading the team, and we are in urgent need of a healing-type spirit qi professional. As long as you come, you will be my little precious. I will make you experience the most enjoyable ride—”","Before the man could finish shouting, a blonde-haired lady patted on his back so hard that the skinny man coughed.","The young blonde-haired lady glared at the skinny man and barked, “Zhang Xiaobai, can’t you be serious!? You are really making this lady angry to death, uh!”","The skinny man looked at the blonde-haired lady and suddenly exclaimed, “Xin Ying, you actually said ‘uh’!”","As a result of his words, Zhang Xiaobai received the blonde-haired lady’s heavy fist, causing him to become utterly obedient.","The blonde-haired lady then shouted, “Extreme Guild Club’s S Tournament reserve team is heading for the Endless Forest’s depths. We are gathering the venom of the Gold Jade Unicorn Ice Snake. We are in urgent need of a healing-type spirit qi professional. The healing-type spirit qi professional must not be lower than C-rank and possess a healing-type fey that is not lower than Silver.”","When the lady’s statement ended, a commotion broke out as this team’s reputation was obviously rather high.","All of a sudden, Lin Yuan heard the burly man clicking his tongue and cheering along as though he was in a fervent state. “Tsk, tsk, tsk, they are indeed worthy of being a B-level guild club and reserve team of the S Tournament team. Young Sister Xin Ying is getting prettier too.”","Lin Yuan was rather speechless as it seemed like this burly uncle was a fan chasing a celebrity. However, Lin Yuan didn’t know whether this burly uncle was a fan of the Extreme Guild Club’s team or the Young Sister Xin Ying that he had mentioned.","Lin Yuan couldn’t help but pat on the burly man’s shoulder and ask, “Where did this team come from?”","The burly man looked at Lin Yuan with disbelief and wide eyes. “You don’t even know this team? Even if you don’t know this team, you should know of the Extreme Guild Club, right?”","Lin Yuan still shook his head, and the burly man immediately let out a gasp, blowing the mustache by his mouth. “Kid, don’t mess with me. You don’t even know the B-level Extreme Guild Club!? Do you not have a Star Web Card, or have you not logged into the Star Web before!?”","Lin Yuan was rather speechless after getting criticized by the burly man.","I do log into the Star Web, but I have been enhancing feys recently and don’t have time to bother about things other than the enhancement of feys.","Lin Yuan might not know about the Extreme Guild Club, but he knew what a B-level guild club was. Lin Yuan understood why this four-men team would be so popular now.","The S Tournament was the top-class team tournament among the Radiance Federation’s young generation. The Radiance Hundred was a ranking of individuals, and they were ranked according to their sequence numbers.","However, the S Tournament was a five-men team tournament, and when fighting in teams, it wasn’t just a comparison of strength—teamwork would be compared too. Therefore, it was much more exciting than solo contests.","For the Radiance Hundred Sequence members fighting in S Tournament’s teams, their performance might affect their sequence rankings in the Radiance Hundred.","In the Radiance Federation, there were only 16 recognized A-level guild clubs. The 16 A-level guild clubs would be ranked every year, as they were determined by the 16 teams that were qualified to enter the S Tournament.","As for the rest of the guild clubs that had the strength to qualify, they would be recognized as B-level guild clubs. There were plenty of B-level guild clubs that had become A-level guild clubs before, but they declined due to their failure in the S Tournament.","As for the squad here, they were the reserve team for the Extreme Guild Club’s S Tournament team. If, due to some special reasons, any of the S Tournament team members couldn’t participate, these reserved members would be replacing the main members.","Thus, these four members were all considered famous among the young generation.","Seeing the burly man’s intense response when Lin Yuan didn’t know about the Extreme Guild Club, it proved that the S Tournament was an extremely popular topic in the Radiance Federation.","This world didn’t have any of the so-called actors or actresses, and even those singers in the Star Web would be part of the minority.","This world’s most popular people were the youths who participated in the S Tournament. The team members, who were part of the Radiance Hundred Sequence, were giants among the celebrities.","This team fitted Lin Yuan’s requirement to harvest in the depths of the Endless Forest. Simultaneously, Lin Yuan fitted the requirements of this team.","Just as Lin Yuan was preparing to walk over and apply to join the team, a healing-type spirit qi professional was already walking toward the four-men team. When Lin Yuan saw someone ahead of him and walking toward the Extreme Guild Club’s squad at that, he stopped moving.","The healing-type spirit qi professional then summoned his fey in front of the four-men squad. It was a rather ugly and strange-looking bird, which didn’t have many feathers. Instead, it was covered in wrinkly skin. The grayish-black skin had some orange spots on its back.","Lin Yuan used True Data to check on the fey’s attributes.","[Fey Name]: Spitting Turtledove","[Fey Species]: Columbidae order/Streptopelia genus","[Fey Grade]: Bronze (10/10)","[Fey Type]: Flying","[Fey Quality]: Elite","Abilities:","[Sticky Saliva]: The secreted saliva is very sticky and can prevent wounds from bleeding and gradually recover external injuries.","[Pungent Saliva]: The secreted saliva is pungent and can reduce wounds’ pain while uplifting the mind.","Exclusive Skill:","[Excessive Secretion]: The Spitting Turtledove salivary glands are very developed and can produce great amounts of saliva.","Most of the time, healing-type feys would be plant-species feys. A bird-species healing-type fey was rather uncommon among the healing-type feys. However, it didn’t mean that uncommon healing-type feys would be expensive in the market. Take this Spitting Turtledove, for example. It was very cheap as its abilities were simply too disgusting.","When this Spitting Turtledove was summoned, Zhang Xiaobai looked at the bald and ugly turtledove and couldn’t help singing:","“Old Indian turtle doves have short legs and little hair, they can live without water for days.","Their brains are a little funny as they are more upset than anyone when their prey dies[1].”","After listening to this song, Lin Yuan couldn’t help but get shocked!","[1] A song by Jay Chou"]},{"number":128,"title":"Chapter 128: Sudden Change in Attitude","paragraphs":["Lin Yuan was simply too familiar with the song that the skinny Zhang Xiaobai sang.","This song was from Jay Chou, a superstar singer in his previous life.","Before he had transmigrated, Lin Yuan had always been an avid fan of Jay Chou and had almost listened to all of his songs. Even if he could not remember the lyrics or did not know how to sing the songs, he could hum them out.","He loved this Ancient Indian Turtledove song and remembered the lyrics clearly.","When he had been working and tending to feys in the small store in Redbud City’s Xia Region, he would hum to this song when he had nothing to do.","But how did Zhang Xiaobai know how to sing this song?","After Zhang Xiaobai sang two lines of the song, many surrounding people searching for members actually applauded.","“Zhang Xiaobai, you sing the Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess’s song quite well! It has a bit of that feeling!”","“Hey, you’re worthy of being the Extreme Guild Club’s Zhang Xiaobai. You’ve indeed shown your talents again.”","“The Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess has not shown up for over two months. I wonder what she’s been busy with that she left so many fans behind. I’m willing to use the happiness of my previous hundreds of ex-boyfriends to exchange for her early return.”","“Have you guys seen the previous Star Web interview? I heard that Lord Ranger is the first on the charts instead of the Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess. Ever since her disappearance, he has been pulling a long face and did not say much during the Star Web interview. He put the host in a very awkward position.”","When Lin Yuan heard the interspersed discussion among the surrounding applause, he frowned even more.","Who is this Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess?","Contracted feys with greater wisdom could sense the changes in the contractor’s thoughts and emotions.","Presently, Chimey was happily eating the Platinum Celery Vine leaves in the Spirit Lock spatial zone. It would always fly high every time and then swoop down to tear off a small piece of it with its beak before swallowing it.","Chimey would eat and have fun. It would fly to the side of the spirit pool to drink a few mouthfuls of water from time to time.","However, when Chimey sensed Lin Yuan’s emotions and thoughts, it did not eat the Platinum Celery Vine or drink the water from the spirit pool anymore. It landed honestly on the table and shrunk its neck.","Due to Lin Yuan’s thoughts, Chimey, which had been indulging in eating the Platinum Celery Vine, recalled that it had deserted its live-streaming career for over two months.","Chimey flew up and arrived on the Pure Land of Bliss’s white sand before using its wings to fan away the fine white sand. The Star Web account card that Chimey used for live-streaming was buried in the fine white sand. When it cranked its head and looked at the account card, it recalled that it was time for live-streaming.","Just as Zhang Xiaobai was enjoying the surrounding applause, he happened to see Xin Ying clenching her fists at him. As a result, he shouted to his surroundings sternly, “Everyone, be kind and stop applauding, or this woman is going to take my life away.”","After the other surrounding adventurers broke out in a peal of laughter, they started to search for teammates.","Lin Yuan stroked his chin as he looked at the Spitting Turtledove.","Although the way this Spitting Turtledove healed was a little gross, both its Sticky Saliva and Pungent Saliva had a pretty good effect. One could effectively stop bleeding and heal external injuries, while the other could effectively toughen one’s mind and ignore the pain caused by external injuries in a battle. Combined with its exclusive skill, Excessive Secretion, they greatly enhanced the Spitting Turtledove’s healing abilities.","As a healing-type fey, the Spitting Turtledove was still considered having a good exclusive skill that could be compatible with abilities. However, this Spitting Turtledove was only at Bronze X. Despite being close to Silver, its healing ability was far worse in comparison. Evidently, this healing-type spirit qi professional could not meet the Extreme Guild Club’s four-man team’s requirements.","At that moment, Lin Yuan heard the burly man beside him start dissing.","“The orange spots on the back of this Spitting Turtledove are not even fully formed, so it’s clearly not at Silver and can’t meet the requirements. Yet, he still wants to apply to join the team. If Xin Ying allows him to do so, he’ll hold the team back.”","Lin Yuan could hear that this burly man was defending the Extreme Guild Club’s four-man team. He was indeed a professional fan.","Not far away, the blond-haired Xin Ying turned her head to the left and realized that Zhang Xiaobai was frowning at the surrounding adventurers. Then, while she was turning to her right, her hair hit Zhang Xiaobai’s head, causing him to not be able to frown in time. He grimaced in pain and rubbed his cheeks.","Xin Ying looked at her other two teammates and asked, “Tan Ran, Lu Pinru, what do you guys think?”","The man called Tan Ran had chestnut hair, natural curls and revealed an innocent smile.","The girl called Lu Pinru had short, ear-length hair. She was carrying a super-huge rectangular wooden object on her back, which was nearly twice her height and looked a little strange.","Lin Yuan looked over and could not help but feel that this girl called Lu Pinru might be carrying around her closet.","Lu Pinru looked at the healing-type spirit qi professional that had applied to join the team and said, “We are going to enter the depths of the Endless Forest and collect the venom of the Jade Unicorn Ice Snake. Although the Jade Unicorn Ice Snake is a Gold fey, there might be Platinum feys in its habitat. He certainly won’t be able to provide us enough healing if we bring him along.”","The curly-haired Tan Ran also said sternly, “When he was channeling spiritual power when summoning the fey, I sensed the fluctuation of his spiritual power. He should be at pinnacle D-rank, not far from C-rank. Therefore, I reject the idea of him joining the team.”","Even though Tan Ran spoke seriously, he seemed like a cute little dog wheedling thanks to his cute appearance.","After Xin Ying listened to her teammates’ opinions, she turned her head to the healing-type spirit qi professional and expressed her disapproval.","The healing-type spirit qi professional was not at all annoyed to see that he was rejected but only a little disappointed. However, he took out a book with a smile.","“I knew I wouldn’t be able to act with you guys. But since we almost became teammates, can I get an autograph?”","Lin Yuan could not help but feel dumbfounded. This healing-type spirit qi professional had been aware that he would not be able to join the team. He simply wanted to find an excuse to ask for an autograph as a fan of these people.","The few people of the Extreme Guild Club graciously took the book and signed their names on it.","At that moment, the burly man beside Lin Yuan started to cry out, “I also want Xin Ying’s autograph.”","Just after he said this, his expression suddenly changed, and he added while grimacing in pain, “The Extreme Guild Club’s reserve team for the S Tournament is really something! Other teams treat a healing-type spirit qi professional as a boss, but they’re picky. This is infuriating. I’ve almost forgotten what it was like to be healed by a healing-type spirit qi professional last time.”","Lin Yuan looked at the burly man. The latter’s sudden change in attitude made Lin Yuan find him really strong."]},{"number":129,"title":"Chapter 129: Officially Joining","paragraphs":["This burly man had inadvertently come up with a unique talent!","He had just been defending the Extreme Guild Club’s team and disapproving of the healing-type spirit qi professional joining the team.","When the burly man saw Lin Yuan’s expression, he was not even embarrassed. He touched his nose and said with a laugh, “You need to bootlick and make sarcastic remarks when you need to. This is what a professional fan should be like. You’re still too young.”","Lin Yuan felt that this burly man had quite a lot of unique talents. It was a pity that he had come out to adventure.","The healing-type spirit qi professional, who had been rejected, soon found a team and was treated like a boss.","The Extreme Guild Club’s team continued searching for a healing-type spirit qi professional to recruit.","When Lin Yuan saw this, he went forward.","At that moment, the burly man at Lin Yuan’s side wanted to tell him that if he did not get into the team, the two of them could form a team instead. The burly man would treat it as though he was leading a newcomer.","However, he realized that Lin Yuan was heading to the Extreme Guild Club’s team. As a result, he could not help but open his mouth wide immediately.","“F*ck! Heartless! This kid won’t happen to be a healing-type spirit qi professional, right?”","Lin Yuan greatly appreciated the Extreme Guild Club’s team’s approach just now.","The most important thing of a team formation was communication and respecting each other, just like how the blonde-haired girl called Xin Ying would listen to and respect her teammates’ opinions.","Her other teammates also adhered to the team’s bottom line of recruiting teammates.","Other combat-class spirit qi professionals were required to do their best to protect the healing-type spirit qi professionals in the field battles, provided that the healing-type spirit qi professional could keep up with healing the team.","They should not receive protection just because they could not fight.","Therefore, there was a mutual relationship between the teammates. If a healing-type spirit qi professional could not keep up with healing the team, the other people would naturally not treat them like a boss either.","Adventuring in the wild was not a child’s play. If a healing-type spirit qi professional could not keep up with healing the team, they would cause the combat-type spirit qi professionals to sustain fresh injuries before their old injuries were healed.","This would create a vicious cycle, and the team would eventually crumble.","If a combat-type spirit qi professional was compared to a kinetic energy machine, then a healing-type spirit qi professional would be the one constantly repairing the machine and refueling it.","Thus, everyone would want to form a team with a qualified healing-type spirit qi professional who could heal the team when out in the wild.","Healing-type spirit qi professionals were so highly sought after because they were irreplaceable and not due to their scarcity.","The Extreme Guild Club’s four people were all sitting down on the chairs in the mission area to rest.","Only Zhang Xiaobai was there, looking at the ceiling of the Guild Alliance’s mission area and humming a song, seemingly thinking about life.","It was difficult for a small team to find a suitable healing-type spirit qi professional. They would usually have to wait for a day or two to find a suitable one.","Even if a four-man team of the Extreme Guild Club wanted to find a suitable healing-type spirit qi professional, it might have to wait a few hours. Therefore, the four of them did not think that another healing-type spirit qi professional would come so quickly after they rejected one that could not meet their requirements.","When Xin Ying saw Lin Yuan approaching, she habitually said, “I’m sorry. We don’t usually sign autographs outside the S Tournament.”","Xin Ying was not surprised that Lin Yuan was wearing a mask. Many adventurers wore masks—some of them because their faces had been wounded in some dangerous missions. They would usually wear a metal maskIn in order not to affect their teammates.","Lin Yuan stood there, cleared his throat, and said, “I’m a healing-type spirit qi professional who meets your requirements. I’m here to apply to join the team.”","Xin Ying found it a little unexpected, but she then looked at him seriously. The man in front of her exuded an indescribable aura, which surprised her. Without taking into consideration his masked appearance, his aura gave her the feeling that he was a cheerful youth.","Before Xin Ying could speak in time, Zhang Xiaobai wowed and stood up. “We don’t have to wait anymore. The most annoying part of a mission is to wait here for a healing-type spirit qi professional. I waited so long that I felt drowsy.”","Xin Ying rolled her eyes at Zhang Xiaobai and stood up.","Then Tan Ran and Lu Pinru, who were sitting at the side, also stood up and looked at Lin Yuan as they nodded slightly to greet him.","Xin Ying said, “Our mission this time is to enter into the depths of the Endless Forest and collect the venom of the Jade Unicorn Ice Snake that we need, so we cannot share it with you. However, we’ll allocate ten units of venom for the five of us, and you can take three. Based on the price of the venom, we can convert and give you Radiance dollars. See if you can accept this.”","Lin Yuan did not care about the Jade Unicorn Ice Snake venom, a precious spiritual ingredient that was extremely hard to store and easy to deteriorate.","Thus, the fresher the Jade Unicorn Ice Snake venom, the more precious it would be. It was a kind of spiritual ingredient that helped evolve poisonous feys. Since Lin Yuan had no use for it, it would be better if he could exchange it for Radiance dollars.","Lin Yuan wanted to go to the Endless Forest for wild harvesting, so he deliberately explained his goal. “I will do wild harvesting when I encounter any precious feys. If there is no problem with that, I will join the team.”","Lin Yuan’s words caused the four members to widen their eyes on the spot.","Zhang Xiaobai asked first, “Brother, you’re not a Creation Master, right?”","Generally speaking, only Creation Masters would want to do wild harvesting in the wild.","They could kill feys and obtain spiritual ingredients, but they could not gather the feys in one piece. Wild feys were fierce. Although most of the wild feys would not attack humans first, if humans wanted to capture them and do wild harvesting, they would inevitably counterattack. Therefore, only Creation Masters could make the wild feys to have a favorable impression on them and be collected obediently.","Since Zhang Xiaobai asked, Lin Yuan nodded without hiding anything. He could not hide the fact that he would do wild harvesting from the other members if they were to enter the depths of the Endless Forest. He might even need their help, so he was frank about it.","Upon seeing Lin Yuan nod, the eyes of Xin Ying, Tan Ran, and Lu Pinru lit up.","Zhang Xiaobai was elated and said exaggeratedly, “We’ve picked up a treasure this time! I didn’t expect to find a healing-type spirit qi professional who is also a Creation Master. With a Creation Master assisting us in the wild, this mission will be much smoother.”"]},{"number":130,"title":"Chapter 130: I’ve Been Superior Since a Young Age","paragraphs":["The most fearful thing about adventuring in the wild was encountering perilous situations. The combat-class spirit qi professionals’ feys might damage their roots, something that healing-type spirit qi professionals could not help with. Only a Creation Master could heal them.","Even though only a Class 2 Creation Master could fully heal a fey with damaged roots, a Class 1 Creation Master could only take measures immediately. That could also ease the feys with damaged roots, so not much of their combat power would be weakened due to it. They could continue on their journey until they returned to the city and found a Class 2 Creation Master to heal their feys.","It was not hard for Creation Masters to do wild harvesting, so there was naturally no reason to reject Lin Yuan.","Xin Ying replied with a nod, “In that case, there is no problem at all. Since you’re a Creation Master, you’ll be of great help to the team. I’ll raise your remuneration from 30% to 35%, but before this, I want to verify your healing ability.”","Naturally, Lin Yuan would not refuse Xin Ying’s suggestion, as this was a responsibility toward all her teammates from a certain aspect.","At that moment, Zhang Xiaobai started yelling, “F*ck! Heartless! Xin Ying, you’re not going to test it on me again, right?”","Xin Ying looked at Zhang Xiaobai as though he were a fool and nodded. “Who else would it be besides you?”","Zhang Xiaobai looked around and spat out his tongue as he resigned to his fate.","He was the only defense-type spirit qi professional on the team. Xin Ying and Tan Ran were power offense-type spirit qi professionals, while Lu Pinru was a support-type spirit qi professional. He was still the most suitable one to test Lin Yuan’s healing ability, after all.","Tan Ran, who had not been talking much, suddenly stepped forward and said seriously, “I can also try it. I’ll test the healing ability on behalf of Big Brother Zhang.”","Upon seeing this, Zhang Xiaobai hurriedly walked to Xin Ying’s side and said, “I’ll do it. Your body isn’t strong. Why do you have to try?”","Zhang Xiaobai, who could imagine Xin Ying beating himself up, could not help but gnash his teeth and look at her before saying, “Do it lightly.”","Xin Ying clenched her fist, and a sudden surge of energy rushed to her hand, creating a golden flare on her fist.","Lin Yuan sensed that this energy’s attribute was metal and speculated that she should have a metal-type fey.","Xin Ying had attached the energy of her contracted metal-type fey to herself. However, a contractor using one’s own fey’s ability like this was much weaker than summoning the fey itself to do so.","She looked at her fist and then at Zhang Xiaobai before she went through her backpack on the seat. “Should I hit you with my katar, so you’ll sustain more serious injuries? You can test the healing ability better that way.”","Zhang Xiaobai covered his face and groaned. “What kind of horrible life am I living? Xin Ying, let me tell you, you won’t be able to get married like this.”","While Xin Ying raised her fist and smashed it toward Zhang Xiaobai’s chest, Lin Yuan could clearly feel she had withheld her force.","When her fist smashed on Zhang Xiaobai’s chest, it sent him flying three meters away. He struggled for a while before getting up as he put his hand on his chest with a pale face.","Zhang Xiaobai was about to take a deep breath when Xin Ying said, “I will be able to get married. If I can’t, I’ll look for you. I’ve beaten you, so you’ll have to be responsible for me.”","Zhang Xiaobai was taking a deep breath when he choked and coughed as he put his hand on his chest.","After coughing for a long time, he responded, “I’m coughing so badly. It seems that I have internal bleeding.” Then, he looked at Lin Yuan. “Brother, I’m depending on you. If you can’t heal me, I will have been beaten up in vain.”","As soon as Lin Yuan raised his hand, a beam of serene emerald green luster enveloped Zhang Xiaobai. When this emerald green flare circled Zhang Xiaobai, Lin Yuan stopped his actions and withdrew his hand.","After Zhang Xiaobai felt his body condition, he patted his chest, where he had been hit, and said, “I’m completely healed. Brother, you’re really something. Your healing ability is at Silver.”","Actually, when Xin Ying had made her move earlier, she had particularly controlled her force to the limit of what a Silver healing ability could heal.","Zhang Xiaobai felt his body condition and was sure that Lin Yuan’s casual healing ability was at the level of mid-stage Silver.","He was very pleased with Lin Yuan’s ability. The healing ability of his summoned feys would at least be at pinnacle Silver. When such a powerful healing-type spirit qi professional was adventuring in the wild, he would undoubtedly give the whole team a peace of mind.","After some tests, Lin Yuan was considered a part of the team.","Zhang Xiaobai smacked his lips and said, “We have formed our team. Let’s invite him to a meal so that we can get to know each other. After lunch, we’ll head toward the Endless Forest.”","When he arrived at the eating area, Zhang Xiaobai used his Star Web Card to connect to this restaurant’s private room radio.","After fiddling for a long time, he finally found a channel and said to everyone as though he was offering some treasure, “Guys, listen. This channel is interesting.”","Soon, Lin Yuan heard the contents of the channel Zhang Xiaobai had found.","“On the night of September 4, a jobless Mr. Wang invited his online friend Mr. Zhou to his rented house to have a drink. During that period, Mr. Wang lamented that there were too many rich people and suggested they should go out and earn some money, to which Mr. Zhou agreed. The surveillance cameras on Jianghe Road showed that they set up their breakfast stall at 5:16 a.m. on September 5.”","Zhang Xiaobai laughed.","“At 5:26 a.m., a black van stopped in front of the stall, and a few robust men got off the vehicle. They walked toward Mr. Zhou and ordered four bowls of egg noodles with fried dough fritters.”","Zhang Xiaobai laughed.","“At 5:28 a.m., Mr. Wang pulled out a sharp kitchen knife under the breakfast stall and cut scallions while they were chatting.”","Zhang Xiaobai laughed.","Then, he realized that nobody was laughing, and they were looking at him instead. He could not help but grin and cautiously ask, “Not funny?”","Xin Ying felt that her fists needed Zhang Xiaobai to stop them from itching.","Ever since Lu Pinru had entered the private room, she had asked for a basin of water from the service staff and had always been wiping her closet.","She calmly glanced at Zhang Xiaobai and sighed helplessly. “Zhang Xiaobai, when will you be decent?”","Zhang Xiaobai felt like he had been greatly insulted. “I’ve been superior since a young age, so how do you expect me to be decent?”","Then, he glanced at Tan Ran, who had not spoken much.","Tan Ran looked at Zhang Xiaobai’s encouraging gaze, gnashed his teeth, clapped, and said with a chuckle, “It’s so funny! You’re too awesome, Brother Zhang.”"]},{"number":131,"title":"Chapter 131: Cracked Sky","paragraphs":["As Lin Yuan watched the members’ interactions, he noticed that the team had a genuinely great relationship. Along the way, Lin Yuan still remembered how Lu Pingru secretly told him, “Xin Ying and Zhang Xiaobai are actually a couple.”","Lin Yuan was truly shocked. There was no way to see any love as it was nothing but torture and oppression. The relationship between Xin Ying and Zhang Xiaobai was simply Xin Ying torturing Zhang Xiaobai.","The meal was quickly served, and Lin Yuan simply took off his mask. After all, there wasn’t a way to eat a meal without removing the mask. When Lin Yuan removed the mask, Genius quickly canceled its Tool Transformation state and turned back into a two-tailed, white kitty.","Genius snuggled in Lin Yuan’s embrace and let out two meows before saying in a soft voice, “Yuan, I wish to eat together with you.”","Genius’ soft voice was obviously rather whiny. When Lin Yuan heard that whiny voice, he knew that Genius was throwing a small tantrum.","Ever since Lin Yuan had enhanced Chimey, Genius, Blackie, and the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly to Legend quality during these two months, he had been enhancing the Jasmine Lily, evolving the Fantasy Breed Jasmine Lily from Bronze X to Silver.","But these two months had really been so busy that Lin Yuan’s sleeping time had to be created forcefully. Genius was able to see how hard-working Lin Yuan had been for this period of time, so it hadn’t been pestering Lin Yuan and simply accompanied him quietly.","When Lin Yuan was enhancing a fey, Genius would side by Lin Yuan’s side while quietly wagging its two small tails.","As compared to how Lin Yuan would spare time to play with Genius every day, this period of time had truly been a suffering one for Genius.","Just as Lin Yuan was going to get a bowl and take some food or Genius, it quickly used its small paw to push on Lin Yuan’s face before it continued to speak in a soft voice. “No, Genius wants Yuan to feed me personally. Otherwise, I won’t eat.”","Lin Yuan couldn’t help smiling as each time Genius threw a tantrum, he couldn’t do anything but raise his hands to surrender.","When Lin Yuan used his chopsticks to pick a piece of braised meat for Genius, he looked up and saw that the Extreme Guild Club’s four members were looking at him.","In fact, when Lin Yuan took down his mask, his four teammates were already consciously looking at him.","At the Guild Alliance, the Extreme Guild Club’s four members didn’t think much when Lin Yuan was wearing a mask. Now that they were out as teammates, they were naturally curious about the face behind Lin Yuan’s mask.","The moment Lin Yuan removed his mask, it gave the four teammates an impression that Lin Yuan was a sunshine and neat youth. However, when Lin Yuan smiled at Genius, the four teammates felt it was truly breathtaking.","When Lin Yuan saw his four teammates looking at him with dumbfounded faces, he suddenly laughed. “Do you not recognize me after I take off my mask?”","Zhang Xiaobai let out some strange cries before he looked at Lin Yuan intently. He then looked at Tan Ran before looking at his own reflection on the plate.","He then said with a grave face, “Alright, then. I admit that Lin Yuan is the most good-looking. But I am second place, and Tan Ran is third place.”","Lu Pinru rolled her eyes ruthlessly. As expected, Zhang Xiaobai might look serious, but the words he spouted were definitely not serious.","Xin Ying felt her fist getting itchy as she picked up a bun and stuffed it into Zhang Xiaobai’s mouth. “Hurry up and eat a bun. I want to see if this bun can shut your mouth.”","The four teammates might be stunned by Lin Yuan’s looks, but what really shocked them was Lin Yuan’s age. Previously, Xin Ying had already felt a youth’s aura coming from Lin Yuan’s body, but she didn’t expect him to actually be so young.","Tan Ran might have a baby face and look young, but he was already 22 years old. However, Lin Yuan was an authentic youth. Furthermore, this youth was able to release a Silver healing ability without summoning his fey, and to be a Creation Master at such a young age showed how great his talent was.","Since the start of the meal, Tan Ran had been looking at Genius with a tilted head. Genius was using its small paws to eat the meat that Lin Yuan fed to it. When Genius saw Tan Ran looking at it, Genius quickly ate the meat in its paws before licking its small paws.","Genius took a few glances at Tan Ran and felt that it was still the cutest. It then pounced into Lin Yuan’s embrace and requested to be petted.","Tan Ran was looking at Lin Yuan with extreme envy as he said in a gloomy tone, “Kitties are the cutest. But why is my fey compatibility not fated with any cuteness?”","When Zhang Xiaobai heard Tan Ran’s words, he nearly choked on the bun in his mouth. When recalling Tan Ran’s fey compatibility, Zhang Xiaobai quickly shook his head.","Your fey compatibility is more than just not fated with cuteness!","The meal was quickly finished, and the casual conversation over the table had brought them closer. Lin Yuan was now more familiar with the four members of the Extreme Guild Club. They were all young and had similar interests. They might not be close friends, but they became regular friends rather easily.","...","The extreme north of the Endless Forest was the land of bitter cold, and the extreme south was the muddy swamps. Therefore, the Endless Forest was extremely extensive. A large patch of trees were all connected, forming a paradise for the wild feys.","The Endless Forest was connected to 13 major cities of the Radiance Federation, and they were at the borders of the Endless Forest. Presently, Lin Yuan and the Extreme Guild Club members were heading for Ascending Dragon City that was closest to the Royal Capital.","At the borders of Ascending Dragon City was Millstone Town. It was closest to the Jade Unicorn Ice Snake’s habitat, which the Extreme Guild Club members wanted to go. Therefore, it was most suitable to set off from Millstone Town.","Millstone Town might be a town within the Ascending Dragon City’s influence, but after reaching the place, Lin Yuan realized that it wasn’t even a third of the size of Xia Region. Furthermore, Millstone Town was rather far away from Ascending Dragon City and other regions. Even a Bronze flying fey would need a period of time to travel across the distance.","The situation was actually due to the formation of Millstone Town. In the beginning, Millstone Town had been a place where many merchants would sell supplies because it was at the border of Endless Forest. It had slowly turned into a steady gathering place, and after dozens of years of development, many adventurers resided here, gradually forming Millstone Town.","Millstone Town was just like an adventurer town embedded at the border of the Endless Forest and Ascending Dragon City.","Lin Yuan stood on the street of Millstone Town and looked at the town that wasn’t very clear due to the setting sun. After hearing all the hawking and shouting, and conversations between adventurers, Lin Yuan couldn’t help but lament. “Even in remote mountains and rivers, traces of humans could still be found.”","Lin Yuan and his four teammates were walking on the main street as they prepared to buy some supplies.","However, in the background of this peaceful time, none of the people in Millstone Town, including Lin Yuan’s group, was aware that a crack had appeared on the horizon. Behind the crack was a hidden dark red wave..."]},{"number":132,"title":"Chapter 132: Alien Insect’s Descent","paragraphs":["During autumn, the sky would turn dark much faster than summer. Ascending Dragon City wasn’t like Redbud City, where all four seasons were filled with gloomy rain and would be stuffy even during autumn. But for Ascending Dragon City’s autumn, the cool winds would be extremely comfortable, but after getting blown for a prolonged period of time, a person would feel the chill within their bodies. It was especially so at night when the winds blew across Millstone Town at night; everyone would involuntarily wish they had an additional layer of clothing.","The lamps by the streets of Millstone Town had lit up, and the stalls under the illumination of the light looked to be even more lively than daytime. There were no signs of influence due to the cold autumn. All sorts of food stalls and fruit stalls were opened up, their business booming.","The aroma of barbecue skewers was so prominent when walking through the streets, and it was the aroma that enticed the gluttonous worm within everyone’s stomach. The fruits’ refreshing sweetness was also able to lift a person’s mood.","Xin Ying looked at the sky and said, “Let’s stay in Millstone Town for tonight. Pinru and I will prepare the daily necessities for this mission. Tan Ran will go and book rooms in a guest house.”","Xin Ying frowned when she looked at Zhang Xiaobai and said, “Zhang Xiaobai, you will buy... Forget it, Zhang Xiaobai, you may move around as you please.”","She then looked at Lin Yuan and said, “Lin Yuan, you can also shop around as you like. We’ll gather back here in one hour and meet up at the guest house that Tan Ran found. We will depart tomorrow morning.”","It was obvious that this wasn’t Xin Ying’s first time at Millstone Town, and she knew the place very well. Just a few instructions were enough to fix the itinerary for everyone.","When Zhang Xiaobai heard that he didn’t have to do anything, he was rather happy, but he had a sudden change in response. “Wasn’t I included when purchasing daily necessities last time? Why aren’t I required this time? Xin Ying, are you shunning me!?”","Zhang Xiaobai looked at Xin Ying with a righteous expression before he instantly received Xin Ying’s heavy fist.","Lu Pinru rolled her eyes. “Zhang Xiaobai, when you were told to buy daily necessities last time, what did you buy? You bought 50 roasted chickens and came back with nothing else. You nearly agitated Big Sister Ying to death. This time, you better be obedient and go eat some barbecue. It is enough as long as you don’t create trouble.”","Zhang Xiaobai held his stomach, partly because it was rather painful as he was just punched by Xin Ying, partly because he was feeling wronged by what Lu Pinru said. However, after he heard that he could eat some barbecue, he immediately let out a delighted ‘pfff’.","Seeing that Xin Ying was turning restless, Zhang Xiaobai quickly yelled, “I am not going to be mischievous this time!”","Lin Yuan and the Extreme Guild Club’s quartet started to split up.","Just as Lin Yuan was preparing to find a random stall, Zhang Xiaobai pulled him aside and said in a secretive voice, “Lin Yuan, do you want to eat barbecue with me? That stall is very good.”","Zhang Xiaobai then pointed at a place that wasn’t far behind him.","Lin Yuan wasn’t hungry yet. He took a glance at the barbecue stall and the fruit stall beside him and replied, “I am not hungry yet. You can go ahead. I will buy some fruits here.”","Zhang Xiaobai patted on Lin Yuan’s shoulder and said, “Then just wait here for around ten minutes. I will come and look for you after buying the barbecue.”","After speaking, Zhang Xiaobai started running to the barbecue stall and shouted with a stretched neck, “Boss, give me 30 kidney skewers. I want them super-duper spicy.”","Lin Yuan had already prepared his own supplies as it was very important to stock up supplies in order to go for an adventure. Since Lin Yuan decided to venture out, he was naturally fully prepared for all situations.","The Moon Empress had given Lin Yuan two Diamond fey storage boxes. The leaf-shaped fey storage box had all sorts of dimensional lifeforms’ flesh, so Lin Yuan didn’t touch them.","As for Cheng Wu’s dark brown, beetle-shaped fey storage box, Lin Yuan had tidied up the Radiance dollars that took up half the space inside and emptied out a corner. That corner was used to store a large amount of water and some convenience food to curb hunger.","When adventuring in the wilderness, the lack of food could be solved by killing a wild fey and making a fire to do a simple barbecue. However, it was hard to survive without water in the wilderness.","Those experienced adventurers would know that water in the wild must not be drunk casually unless it was a large water body with living fish or the mountain’s spring water. Otherwise, drinking water casually might cause diarrhea, fever, or even get inflicted with poison. Such conditions might be even more fatal than a fey’s attack.","Lin Yuan took two steps forward to the stall beside him. Seeing that the fruits were all very fresh, he had the idea to store some in the Diamond fey storage box.","Just as Lin Yuan was picking the fruits, he heard a middle-aged woman’s voice. “Good baby, quickly pick a sugar figurine[1] and let the old uncle help you make one.”","Lin Yuan looked at the stall beside, which was selling sweets. They sold sugar figurines and cotton candy.","The little boy who was being carried by the woman then asked the old man, making sugar figurines, shyly, “Old uncle, I wish to have a sweet sugar figurine. Could you make me a fat yellow duck?”","The old man chuckled with a benevolent smile and said, “This old uncle is the best at making fat yellow ducks. I will make one for you quickly.”","The old man grabbed a handful of malt sugar with proficiency, and after a short moment, a cute and fat yellow duck was made. He then brushed on some sugary coating, giving life to the fat yellow duck.","The little boy received the fat yellow duck with excitement and smiled happily as though there were stars in his eyes.","Just as the woman was about to leave with the little boy in her arms, the little boy then said with an innocent tone, “Mommy, mommy, I want cotton candy.”","The woman pinched the little boy’s cheek helplessly and pointed at the sugar figurine before saying, “You have yet to finish the sugar figurine in your hand. Why do you want cotton candy too?”","The little boy was very persistent as he immediately kissed the woman on the cheek. The woman immediately smiled after getting kissed by her own baby and immediately paid money for the cotton candy.","The cotton candy was very easy to make, and it took just two minutes for the old man to make a huge cotton candy ball that was like a white blanket.","The little boy received the cotton candy and said to the fat yellow duck, “Ducky, with the cotton candy as your blanket, you will not feel cold at night.”","The child’s words were filled with innocence, and it was probable that this sugar figurine duck might not feel cold with the cotton candy blanket even during winter.","After Lin Yuan stored the fruits in the beetle-shaped fey storage box, the sky looked like a shattered mirror as a dark red luster leaked out of the shattered night sky. There was a distortion energy wave that ripped open a huge gap in the night sky. Soon enough, a rift was formed in the sky by the dark red energy.","As soon as the rift was formed, large quantities of alien insects instantly surged out of the rift!","[1] Actually called sugar people, and it is a traditional Chinese form of folk art using hot, liquid sugar to create three-dimensional figures"]},{"number":133,"title":"Chapter 133: This Punch Is Strong Enough","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","When Lin Yuan saw this strange energy rift, his brain felt as if it was going to explode. He had seen this strange energy rift back in the Xia Region.","Wasn’t it a dimensional rift?","Alien insects frantically rushed out of this opened dimensional rift, and all sorts of alien insects fell from the sky before falling into pieces.","But as layer after layer of alien insect corpses laid down and formed a thick layer of insect corpses, there were no casualties among the newly fallen alien insects when they fell on them.","Soon, a sea of alien insects suddenly gathered secretly in the night under the dimensional rift.","All sorts of alien insects cried in unison, creating an ear-piercing and disordered sound of insects. Then, these alien insects gorged their sacrificed companions’ flesh below them and seemed to be waiting for something.","The dimensional rift had suddenly opened widely at the Endless Forest border, and the sea of insects had gathered only two or three meters away from Millstone Town.","This was almost akin to the dimensional rift opening at the gates of Millstone Town.","This dimensional rift that had suddenly opened in the night sky revealed its hideous claws and teeth, just like a devil choosing people to devour.","Millstone Town, which was directly connected to this sudden change, started to panic.","At that moment, Zhang Xiaobai dashed at his side. He was holding 30 kidney skewers, which could not be held in one hand, so he held 15 in each hand.","Zhang Xiaobai might be experienced eating Millstone Town’s kidney skewers. Those 30 kidney skewers could satisfy his appetite.","He ran to Lin Yuan with a very grave expression, glanced at the kidney skewers in his hands, and threw them on the ground. “Lin Yuan, we’ll gather at the earlier location. With such a big change of events, they should have rushed over immediately.”","Zhang Xiaobai rarely looked so grave. He looked at Lin Yuan and wanted to say something, but did not in the end. Instead, he only reached out to pat Lin Yuan’s shoulder.","Lin Yuan and Zhang Xiaobai ran toward the location previously agreed with Xin Ying, Lu Pinru, and Tan Ran.","After arriving at the location, Lin Yuan found Xin Ying and Lu Pinru standing there with ugly and anxious expressions.","When Xin Ying saw Lin Yuan and Zhang Xiaobai, she shouted, “Based on the disorderly insect sounds, this opened dimensional rift must be linked to the dimension with alien insects. However, I don’t know if it’s a Class 1 Insect Dimensional Rift or a Pinnacle Class 1 Insect Dimensional Rift.”","Lin Yuan had also done a lot of research on this aspect. If the alien insect dimensional rift reached Class 2, the sounds of the alien insects alone could cause dizziness and blurred vision to people under such proximity.","Therefore, this opened alien insect dimensional rift could only be Class 1. However, there was a vast difference between an ordinary Class 1 alien insect dimensional rift and a pinnacle Class 1 dimensional rift.","At that moment, Tan Ran dashed to their side while panting.","The five-member team officially assembled. Xin Ying regained her calmness and said as she looked at Lin Yuan, “Due to the sudden dimensional rift in Millstone Town, our mission of finding the Jade Unicorn Ice Snake venom in the Endless Forest is suspended. You can go to the Royal Capital’s Guild Alliance to collect the deposit we put up as the compensation for a sudden suspension of a mission.”","Zhang Xiaobai held back until his face turned red. Despite wanting to say something and looking at Lin Yuan and then Xin Ying, he still did not say what he wanted to, even if his face turned red.","Lu Pinru and Tan Ran were frank, but it was as though they had a vague expectation as they looked at Lin Yuan.","At the same time, Lu Pinru took down the closet, which was the height of two people, that she was carrying on her back.","Tan Ran also opened the backpack he was carrying and wore a forehead protector. He pushed his naturally curly hair to the back of his head and revealed his forehead. It was clear that Lu Pinru and Tan Ran were ready for battle at this point.","Lin Yuan could see the intention of the quartet. They wanted to stay in Millstone Town and help the town defend against the insect tide invasion.","At that moment, Lin Yuan could not help but think of the little boy that had bought a fat yellow duck sugar figurine earlier.","He also recalled that when Chu Ci was young and was eating sugar figurines, she would always throw a tantrum about wanting a sugar figurine in the shape of an Elite Black Back Mountain Boar.","It was as though the taste of pork could be felt.","Those distant memories appeared before his eyes.","What was happiness?","When one was hungry, rice would be one’s happiness. It was enough if one could eat to one’s fill.","When one was thirsty, water would be one’s happiness. It was enough if one could drink to one’s fill.","When one was poor, money would be one’s happiness. It was enough if one had sufficient money.","Happiness might be one thing when one was young, and one would feel happy when one had something.","When one grew up, happiness might be one goal, and one would feel happy when one achieved that.","A few months ago, Lin Yuan had been a struggling man on the line of happiness, and he had been neither healthy nor had enough food or clothes.","But now, he had bigger life goals than other people.","In Lin Yuan’s opinion, rather than saying it was because of his reincarnation, him forming a contract with Morbius, or being able to channel spirit qi to enhance feys, it was because he had been born in the Radiance Federation.","Although Lin Yuan had grown up unwilling to accept others’ help, he had unknowingly accepted too many favors.","From time to time, Auntie Zhang and Uncle Wang would take care of his daily life and wonder whether he could live well. Before Chu Ci had a contracted fey, Teacher Bao had wanted to buy one for her with his own money. And there was also his dutiful teacher, the Moon Empress.","When Lin Yuan saw the battle intent in the quartet’s eyes, it seemed as if he suddenly understood the meaning of radiance.","Radiance was a legacy, a mission, and a kind of belief.","Lin Yuan frowned as he looked at them. “Do you think that the four of you are the only ones who want to stay? In my opinion, our temporary squad can’t be disbanded, not at least until we get through this insect tide.”","Xin Ying, Lu Pinru, and Tan Ran looked at Lin Yuan with their eyes lit up.","If they were kind to Lin Yuan before, then it was because they had formed a temporary squad. But now, they were looking at Lin Yuan in approval. This kind of recognition had nothing to do with his strength. Rather, it was a kind of soul-level recognition.","Zhang Xiaobai’s face turned red from holding back his words. He laughed and punched Lin Yuan. “Lin Yuan, you’re worthy of being a good brother of mine.”","Lin Yuan almost took a step back from Zhang Xiaobai’s punch on his shoulder.","Zhang Xiaobai was worthy of someone boorish who had to eat 30 kidney skewers for each meal. He was indeed boorish.","Lin Yuan also punched back on Zhang Xiaobai’s shoulder. “I’ll focus on healing you during the battle later.”","Zhang Xiaobai took a step back from Lin Yuan’s punch and replied with a laugh, “This punch is strong enough. That’s satisfying!”","Zhang Xiaobai and Lin Yuan were not good at expressing their affection. Hitting each other with a punch was sometimes the way males expressed their friendship.","Lin Yuan looked at the dimensional rift and said sternly, “We won’t be able to stop this insect tide with just a few of us. We’ll follow the stream of people toward the location where Millstone Town’s adventurers gather.”","Xin Ying quickly responded, “There is a Guild Alliance branch in Millstone Town. The stream of people is heading there. We’ll head there now.”","Lin Yuan was running with the quartet to the Millstone Town’s Guild Alliance branch when he heard a strange yet pleasant female voice. It belonged to none other than the Mother of Bloodbath, which had been silent before."]},{"number":134,"title":"Chapter 134: A New Dormant Red Thorn","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","The Mother of Bloodbath’s voice suddenly rang in Lin Yuan’s ears, causing him to feel more at ease. “Kid, as your Path Protector, I’ll only care about your life and not anything other than that. However, you’re considered courageous for wanting to fight against the insect tide under the dimensional rift.”","The Mother of Bloodbath suddenly became silent for two seconds before a strange female voice sounded again. “However, this Pinnacle Class 1 Dimensional Rift is no joke to you right now. If you can get through it and defend against the insect tide, I’ll give you the source-type item from this dimensional rift as a reward.”","When Lin Yuan heard the Mother of Bloodbath’s words, he frowned.","Although Lin Yuan knew that this alien insect dimensional rift was Class 1, he was unsure whether it was just an ordinary or a pinnacle Class 1.","Now that the Mother of Bloodbath had said that it was a pinnacle Class 1 dimensional rift, the grade of this dimensional rift could be determined.","Lin Yuan’s heart tightened.","A Class 3 alien insect would appear from a pinnacle Class 1 dimensional rift as the swarm leader.","The combat power of a Class 3 alien insect was comparable to that of a Gold fey, which also meant that the insect tide in Millstone Town would have at least one Class 3 alien insect with a combat power comparable to a Gold fey.","This was utterly bad news for the five-member team and Millstone Town.","The alien insect dimensional rift was known as the most dangerous dimensional rift due to the countless alien insects gushing out of it, just like a raging tide.","The sea of insects would turn any place barren wherever they went.","In a battle, they could kill spirit qi professionals and feys alive.","However, the pinnacle Class 1 alien insect dimensional rift was not just simply a sea of insects for Millstone Town.","This was because a pinnacle Class 1 dimensional rift’s Class 3 alien insect was akin to the power of a sharp knife for Millstone Town.","Lin Yuan asked the Mother of Bloodbath softly, “Mother of Bloodbath, if we can’t stop this insect tide, can you step in to defend Millstone Town?”","Mother of Bloodbath’s voice sounded again. “I’m an arachnid fey, not a human like you guys. I am only your Path Protector and will only save you before you get buried in the sea of insects.”","Then, the Mother of Bloodbath stopped talking.","Lin Yuan’s question was buried by the autumn wind that whistled past his cheeks as he ran in the cool night.","He now did not even think about the so-called source-type lifeform reward. Instead, he clenched his fists and measured his power.","This battle would be the touchstone after the Jasmine Lily had evolved into a Fantasy Breed.","The alien insects that spewed out of the pinnacle Class 1 alien insect dimensional rift were mainly low-grade alien insects comparable to Normal feys or lower than that.","Such alien insects accounted for more than 80% of the insect tide. The remaining 19% or more were just alien insects similar to Elite feys.","Among the higher-grade alien insects that accounted for less than the remaining 0.001%, the Class 1 alien insects that were like Bronze feys made up most of this percentage.","Although this 0.001% seemed little, it was really terrifying given the numbers of the sea of alien insects.","Lin Yuan could not help but think of Red Thorn, which had evolved into Bronze.","However, when Red Thorn was evolving into Bronze, it had to grow new tissues and organs due to its exclusive skill.","After eating an enormous amount of flesh from dimensional lifeforms, Red Thorn had fallen into a deep slumber, storing up for the growth of its organs that would allow its combat system to be rebuilt.","Red Thorn had been sleeping for a long time, and Lin Yuan wondered when it would awaken.","If Red Thorn awakened, its newly awakened exclusive skill would simply be a weapon for mass destruction to the alien insect tide.","When Lin Yuan and the quartet reached Millstone Town’s Guild Alliance branch, they realized that many spirit qi professionals had gathered there.","Based on their attire, most of these spirit qi professionals were some aborigines living in Millstone Town. Some came from other places to explore Millstone Town, and now they still chose to stay there.","At that moment, a steward-like person clad in a body of chain armor shouted, “Check the combat-class spirit qi professionals who came to the Guild Alliance branch.” While he said that, sweat broke out on his forehead, and he looked unusually grave.","Soon, an old man stepped forward. “Sir! 1,325 registered spirit qi professionals in Millstone Town also settled down here. 215 of them had gone out, leaving 1,110 spirit qi professionals here!”","While the old man spoke, he looked at the combat-class spirit qi professionals gathered at the side, most of whom had settled in Millstone Town.","In times of crisis, as a defender of Millstone Town—although the old man was so old that it would be strenuous for him to fight in a battle—seeing all the combat-class spirit qi professionals in Millstone Town present to fight against the catastrophe, a proud feeling, and uplifting power arose in his heart.","This cohesive force was unique to Millstone Town. If every spirit qi professional was like a small tinder, the thousand of people gathered would have been a strong bonfire.","The steward-like man clad in chain armor was the president of the Millstone Town’s Guild Alliance branch.","There was a hint of pride on his anxious face, but then he had a bitter smile.","As the Millstone Town’s Guild Alliance branch president, how could he not know the limit of Millstone Town?","Among these more than 1,000 combat-class spirit qi professionals, most of them had Bronze feys, while only a few dozen of them had Silver feys. Only one of them had a Gold fey.","In a small town like Millstone Town, such combat power was considered great as compared to other similar towns.","However, in the face of this sudden opening of the Class 1 alien insect dimensional rift and the approaching insect tide, it was clearly too much.","At that moment, a voice deeper than the old man’s shouted, “We’re foreign spirit qi professionals who came to Millstone Town to provide healing and prepared to explore the Endless Forest. After summing it up, we have 113 foreign spirit qi professionals present, 87 with Bronze feys, and 25 with Silver feys. I have a Gold fey.”","The middle-aged burly man’s words made the president of the Millstone Town’s Guild Alliance branch feel more at ease. However, this middle-aged man then made his expression turn uglier.","“Among us 113 people, we only have one healing-type spirit qi professional who has a Bronze Spitting Turtledove. How many healing-type spirit qi professionals are there in Millstone Town?”","The president’s face was covered with worry.","Healing-type spirit qi professionals were too valuable and in high demand everywhere. Therefore, few healing-type spirit qi professionals would stay in a small place like Millstone Town to develop.","In Millstone Town, with thousands of people, there were only five healing-type spirit qi professionals who were responsible for healing the thousands of people in the town.","However, only four healing-type spirit qi professionals had Bronze feys, while the other one only had an Elite fey.","Upon hearing him say the Spitting Turtledove, Lin Yuan subconsciously glanced at the crowd.","He surprisingly found the healing-type spirit qi professional who had previously been rejected in his application to join the four-member squad of the Extreme Guild Club.","Lin Yuan knew that such healing-type feys like the Spitting Turtledoves were relatively rare compared to other healing-type feys. They also had disgusting abilities that few would use.","It was indeed a small world.","Just as the president of Millstone Town’s Guild Alliance branch looked worried, he heard a pleasant male voice. “To prevent world destruction and protect world peace, carrying out love and true—”","Before he could finish, a blonde-haired, valiant woman raised her hand and gave the tall and thin young man a heavy punch before she yelled tenderly, “Zhang Xiaobai, don’t speak at this moment!”","Then, Xin Ying took two steps forward and said calmly and firmly, “We’re a five-member squad with two power offense-type spirit qi professionals, one defense-type spirit qi professional, one support-type spirit qi professional, and one healing-type spirit qi professional. Please let us join the battle.”"]},{"number":135,"title":"Chapter 135: Five People Going to The Battle","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Xin Ying’s words made both the middle-aged man who had spoken before and the president of the Millstone Town’s Guild Alliance branch look relieved.","They quickly nodded in greeting to the five people, including Lin Yuan.","At that moment, several shouts of surprise suddenly sounded. “Wow! Aren’t these the four people from the Guild Alliance’s Extreme Guild Club S Tournament reserve team!? They’re actually here! It’s great that they’re here!”","“At this time, the Extreme Guild Club team would be a really powerful reinforcement with them joining in.”","Then, a clamor suppressed the previous voice. “You’re in Millstone Town too, my idols! We are really too destined!” The healing-type spirit qi professional with the Spitting Turtledove spoke as he was running toward them.","Even if it was a reserve team in the S Tournament, they had an excellent reputation everywhere they went.","Presently, the spirit qi professionals had recognized Xin Ying, Zhang Xiaobai, and the others.","In addition to proving to be youths with great potential, they could also prove their strength.","As soon as the five people, including Lin Yuan, appeared, everyone there got excited.","Since Lin Yuan had always been wearing the mask Genius had transformed into, he seemed like a background character.","As Lin Yuan looked at the excited crowd, he said to the quartet, “Report your strengths to boost their morale.”","Morale was obviously the most important thing during the insect tide invasion in a while, especially since they would go through a defensive battle.","In this lifetime, even though Lin Yuan had never read any books on the art of war, he knew the importance of morale to a battle based on all kinds of hearing and observations in his previous lifetime.","The team then understood Lin Yuan’s purpose.","“Xin Ying, a power offense-type spirit qi professional with a Gold fey.”","“Zhang Xiaobai, a defense-type spirit qi professional with a Gold fey.”","“Tan Ran, a power offense-type spirit qi professional with a Gold fey.”","“Lu Pinru, a support-type spirit qi professional with a Silver fey.”","“Black, a healing-type spirit qi professional with a Silver fey.”","Previously, the crowd was still focused on the quartet. But when Lin Yuan revealed that he was a healing-type spirit qi professional and had a Silver fey, their eyes all focused on him instead.","A Silver healing-type spirit qi professional was an important strategic resource in a battle. With a healing-type spirit qi professional, who had a Silver fey standing behind, it was akin to having solid protection behind while they were fighting for their lives in a battle. What would be more exciting than this?","The other people present and the quartet stared at Lin Yuan blankly.","Zhang Xiaobai almost blurted out. Brother, are you still Lin Yuan? You’re rather fair and not tanned1.","Lin Yuan blinked at the quartet and pointed at the mask on his face.","They looked at Lin Yuan’s non-stop blinking eyes behind the mask and soon understood what he meant.","When they recalled that Lin Yuan was a Creation Master at a young age and healing-type spirit qi professional with a Silver healing-type fey, they guessed that his identity was not simple. Black might be Lin Yuan’s identity outside.","Lin Yuan had become friends with them using his actual name, which made the quartet feel his sincerity.","At that moment, as the representative of the spirit qi professionals in the town, the president of the Millstone Town’s Guild Alliance branch quickly took two steps forward. He brought Lin Yuan and the other four members to the front of all the spirit qi professionals and said, “All of you are young elites. I thank all of you for staying in Millstone Town. You’re a coordinated squad and the one with the strongest combat power present. It’s better that you guys command the fight against the insect tide.”","Millstone Town’s Guild Alliance branch president was considered to be the person whose words carried the most weight.","The people guarding the town were getting on in years and barely could fight, so the battle arrangements depended on the president of the Millstone Town’s Guild Alliance branch.","At present, he was delegating authority because there could be no two commanding voices in a defensive battle, or it would weaken the team’s cohesion.","The president delegated his authority so that there would only be one commanding voice later.","On the other hand, he simply had too much pressure due to the fight against the insect tide. He believed that his qualifications and brainpower could barely withstand such pressure. Therefore, he might as well push this responsibility to the best of the younger generation, while he would fight with all his might in the battle as a pure combat-class spirit qi professional.","Lin Yuan, Xin Ying, Zhang Xiaobai, Lu Pinru, and Tan Ran looked at each other. Then, they nodded gravely, and Xin Ying said, “Which one of you has a small flying fey to observe what scale this dimensional rift really is and whether it’s an ordinary Class 1 insect tide? If we can find out what kind of Class 3 alien insect leads this Class 1 insect tide, we can be prepared in advance and target them effectively!”","After she said those words, the feedback she received made her expression turn ugly.","It was not that these people present did not have flying feys. Rather, their flying feys were either too large or did not have high wisdom. Thus, they could not complete the scouting work and effectively bring back the information.","Xin Ying knew that the four members of her team did not have such scouting flying feys. This was because support-type spirit qi professionals usually equipped scouting flying feys. However, Lu Pinru’s situation was special. She did not have such scouting flying feys.","This was not Xin Ying’s first time encountering an insect tide. Previously, she had taken part in the Extreme Guild Club’s insect tide trials. Because of that, Xin Ying had heard that the sounds of insects from the ordinary Class 1 dimensional rift’s insect tide were more ear-piercing than she had an impression on.","Upon seeing that, Lin Yuan activated his spiritual energy and summoned Chimey, which had recently been in the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","When Chimey was summoned, it was still confused. It was about to stand on Lin Yuan’s ear and get closer. But when it saw Lin Yuan’s grave expression, it became well-behaved as well.","Chimey had actually been live-streaming in the Spirit Lock spatial zone, and the return of the long-lost Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess had surprised the fans.","Many fans had flocked to the live-streaming room to witness the return of the Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess.","Lord Ranger, who had been the top contributing fan, had even frantically donated 10,000 Radiance dollars.","After live-streaming for a while, the fans encouraged Chimey to compete with other live steamers, but it still had not figured out how to.","The dimensional rift had caused abnormal dimensional fluctuations that it could not log in with its Star Web Card, so Chimey naturally got off the live-streaming.","At that moment, Chimey could not help but miss Genius.","Without Genius as its manager and helping with the operation, Chimey felt it was hard putting on a GIF in front of the computer screen.","Chimey thought that when Genius was around, it would compete with the other live-streamers. It would spare them for now. At that moment, it would let them know the power of the Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess.","When Lin Yuan summoned Chimey, the surrounding people glanced over.","Although Chimey was a Silver fey, since its quality was Legend, it looked quite better than most Silver feys.","Furthermore, it was in sky blue with obvious cloud patterns on its wings that contained mysteriousness and elegance. Coupled with Chimey’s agileness, the people knew that this small flying fey had good wisdom.","The quartet looked at Lin Yuan differently. He had actually given them a surprise at such a moment.","It was crucial to have flying feys to scout the insect tide, as their side was already vulnerable. If the weak side could not grasp the upper hand, there would really be little chance of resisting the insect tide invasion.","Lin Yuan immediately issued an order to Chimey, telling it to fly outside Millstone Town and observe the insect tide’s situation. If possible, it could also check out the species of the Class 3 alien insect."]},{"number":136,"title":"Chapter 136: Wearing Pinru’s Clothes","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Actually, Chimey wasn’t adept at scouting from high altitudes as it couldn’t recognize Class 3 alien insects nor call out their names. However, as long as Chimey described the Class 3 alien insect’s appearance, most of the people there would be able to identify it.","After all, understanding various dimensional lifeforms from the dimensional rifts was a compulsory lesson for each citizen of the Radiance Federation.","It was rare for Chimey to see Lin Yuan so solemn, so it was particularly serious too. It immediately flapped its wings and flew out of the Guild Alliance’s sub-branch in Millstone Town. It flew toward the dark red dimensional rift under the darkness.","Presently, Lu Pinru had already unloaded the two wardrobes that were the height of two humans. She was now rapidly circulating her spiritual power. The two wardrobes suddenly opened up when Lu Pinru circulated her spiritual power.","It was now that Lin Yuan finally got to know what Lu Pinru’s contracted fey was and why she was constantly carrying two huge wardrobes behind her. The wardrobes were filled with plenty of silk racks, and there were three 3-inch-long light yellow silkworms within.","The moment Lu Pinru circulated her spirit qi, the three silkworms rapidly spat out silk and weaved spirit qi silk clothes on the silk racks. The silk clothes weren’t ordinary ones as they were weaved with energy.","The three silkworms were spitting silk at extreme speed, and it took just a short moment to finish weaving an entire set of silk clothes on the racks. Subsequently, Lu Pinru took down the energy-weaved silk clothes.","Lin Yuan was looking at the three identical silkworms and using True Data to check on them.","[Fey Name]: Glowing Silkworm Weaver","[Fey Species]: Silkworm gene/Cocoon worm species","[Fey Grade]: Silver (8/10)","[Fey Type]: Wood","[Fey Quality]: Flawless","Abilities:","[Silk Spit]: Rapidly spit out a large amount of disheveled silk to protect itself.","[Light Body Silk Clothing]: Spit out energy silk to weave silk clothing that allowed the wearer’s body to feel lighter and faster.","[Firm Armor Silk Clothing]: Spit out energy silk, using large amounts of energy silk to weave silk clothing that could effectively guard against physical attacks.","Exclusive Skill:","[Tough Silk]: Silk has resilience and toughness. It can greatly enhance durability and reduce wear and tear when using the silk products.","When using True Data, Lin Yuan was surprised to find out that these three Glowing Silkworm Weavers didn’t just have the same abilities—they also had the same exclusive skill, Tough Silk.","Putting aside the rarity of the exclusive skill, Tough Silk, or the great abilities that the Glowing Silkworm Weavers possessed, the real difficulty was to have three Glowing Silkworm Weavers with the same exact abilities and exclusive skills.","When feys evolved, they would obtain exclusive skills of a huge myriad. A single Glowing Silkworm Weaver could have up to 1,000 different exclusive skills, and when they evolved to the next grade, the abilities weren’t fixed either.","The three Glowing Silkworm Weavers had the same exclusive skills and abilities to rapidly produce energy silk clothing. Lu Pinru wasn’t like other support-type spirit qi professionals who would use control abilities to weaken and restrict the enemies. She had sacrificed her individual combat ability to provide full support to her teammates.","Zhang Xiaobai received Lu Pinru’s energy silk clothes and gave the first set to Lin Yuan. “Black, wear this Firm Armor Silk Clothing first. It can help you resist some physical attack. Pinru’s clothes are very comfortable!”","Lin Yuan didn’t reserve himself. As a healing-type spirit qi professional, when he was healing a teammate, it was best that his teammates wouldn’t have to be distracted in order to protect him.","After wearing this Firm Armor Silk Clothing, Lin Yuan’s body had a layer of silk that was fused with energy. It was light and comfortable.","As Lu Pinru went all out to exhaust her spiritual power, she quickly produced over a dozen Firm Armor Silk Clothing. After giving them to the few healing-type spirit qi professionals, the remaining clothes were distributed to the spirit qi professionals with Gold feys.","By the time the Firm Armor Silk Clothings were completed, Lu Pinru’s complexion was abnormally pale. She quickly took out a spiritual ingredient that could replenish her spirit qi and chewed it twice before saying, “Let me rest for five minutes, and I will continue weaving Firm Armor Silk Clothings.”","The healing-type spirit qi professionals would wear the Firm Armor Silk Clothings Lu Pinru weaved, but spirit qi professionals with Gold feys would choose their feys to wear them instead. The Firm Armor Silk Clothing was made by fusing energy and silk, so there wasn’t a fixed shape. Even a large-sized fey could expand the Firm Armor Silk Clothing and equip it.","Lin Yuan was able to see the obvious expectations on the faces of the spirit qi professionals who witnessed Lu Pinru’s ability. He was completely able to understand why these spirit qi professionals desired the Firm Armor Silk Clothings, even though they were already prepared to die in order to protect Millstone Town. Everyone simply wanted to have an additional layer of protection, even if this layer of protection could only protect them from a few attacks of Class 1 or Class 2 alien insects before getting damaged.","Lin Yuan responded immediately and summoned his Bronze/Legend Spirit-Gather Goldfish from Morbius’ Spirit Lock spatial zone. This was the first time Lin Yuan summoned Blackie into the outside world.","Blackie was originally inviting the female Five Fortune Ranchu to play and eat Butterfly Shells. When Lin Yuan summoned it, it habitually flourished its tail. Half of Blackie’s body was now in the shape of a black peony after flourishing its tail. It was now waiting solemnly for Lin Yuan’s command.","When Lin Yuan summoned Blackie, the Spirit-Gather Goldfish didn’t release any trace of spirit qi due to its exclusive skill, Spirit Qi Imprint. However, its faint dragon prowess already told everyone present that Blackie was a dragon-species fey. After awakening the dragon-species bloodline, the Blackie wasn’t just a fey—it was a luxury item that only wealthy people would possess.","“Blackie, use Spirit Injection on Lu Pinru and help her recover her spirit qi.”","When Lin Yuan commanded Blackie to use Spirit Injection, he completely forgot his own codename was called Black too. Blackie immediately spat out pure spirit qi from its mouth and injected it into Lu Pinru’s body.","The Spirit-Gather Goldfish might only be bronze-grade, but having awakened the dragon-species bloodline while its quality was at Legend, its Spirit Injection’s effects were extremely potent.","While Lu Pinru was showing a surprised expression, her spiritual power and spirit qi were rapidly getting replenished. The Extreme Guild Club’s quartet didn’t expect Lin Yuan to bring such a pleasant surprise during the battle preparation.","Spirit Injection was a spirit qi recovery ability that was hard to come by because the fey that possessed this ability would have other abilities that were almost useless. Therefore, such feys weren’t suitable for contracts. However, it was an ability that was extremely crucial, be it on the battlefield or in tournaments.","Lu Pinru could feel her spirit qi getting rapidly replenished. When her spirit qi was almost fully replenished, she continued to produce the Firm Armor Silk Clothings. Among the Glowing Silkworm Weavers’ weaving abilities, the Firm Armor Silk Clothing was certainly more useful.","Zhang Xiaobai distributed Lu Pinru’s silk clothes and shouted, “Humans and feys can wear Pinru’s clothes. Please, don’t forget the wardrobe before wearing the clothes.”","Zhang Xiaobai might not sound serious still, but his eyes were filled with overwhelming battle intent and determination. Xin Ying was also boosting everyone’s morale before the battle.","The healing-type spirit qi professional who had the Spitting Turtledove was currently pressing down on his Spitting Turtledove’s head and said, “Drink a little more water. If you don’t have enough saliva later, you will not be able to eat your favorite Gray Beetles anymore.”","When the Spitting Turtledove heard that it couldn’t eat the Gray Beetles anymore, it disregarded its life and continued gulping down the third bucket of water. Earlier on, the Spitting Turtledove had already emptied two buckets of water.","Lin Yuan concentrated his eyes as Chimey had already scouted the situation and was flying back. He could feel the panic in Chimey’s heart when it was flying."]},{"number":137,"title":"Chapter 137: Heart-Penetrating Ironline","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Once Chimey flew in front of Lin Yuan, he immediately communicated with Chimey. After a short communication and feeling what Chimey had seen, Lin Yuan’s face behind the mask looked terrifyingly gloomy.","Lin Yuan already knew that this alien insect dimensional rift was a pinnacle Class 1 one, through the Mother of Bloodbath. However, by seeing the scene through Chimey, Lin Yuan could feel the endless numbers of alien insects gathering under the dimensional rift. There were all sorts and types of alien insects packed up together, and it looked like they were piling on top of each other.","Had Chimey not experienced Cheng Wu and Cheng Rui’s assault and gone through life and death, it would have been overwhelmed when it saw so many alien insects.","Of course, the massive numbers of this insect tide wasn’t the reason why Lin Yuan had a gloomy expression. The most important reason was that Chimey had seen three Class 3 alien insects.","Class 3 alien insect, Acid Tapeworm.","Class 3 alien insect, Spiky Beetle.","There was another one, but it was a Class 3 alien insect that was halfway out of the dimensional rift.","The Acid Tapeworm looked just like a green neon lamp under the night sky and was abnormally eye-catching. The Acid Tapeworm’s skin was just like a translucent and durable membrane, and it was filled with green glowing acid that was extremely corrosive. When it spat out the corrosive acid, the flesh would be instantly carbonized once it made contact with flesh.","The Class 3 alien insect, Spiky Beetle, was just like an iron tortoise with horrifyingly thick armor. The massive body possessed power that could raise things that were several times heavier than its body. When the Spiky Beetle smashed with its spiked armor, it would be able to penetrate city walls.","Of course, there were individuals here who had Gold feys that could battle with Class 3 alien insects, so Lin Yuan wasn’t really worried about these two Class 3 alien insects. The most important Class 3 alien insect was one that Chimey saw when it was still emerging from the dimensional rift. It was a slender black line.","The black line was the reason why Lin Yuan frowned. This third Class 3 alien insect that only revealed half its body was an invisible killer, the Heart-Penetrating Ironline.","Under normal circumstances, the Heart-Penetrating Ironline wouldn’t reveal its original body and would be hiding within the bodies of other alien insects. From an alien insect that didn’t have any grade or a Class 3 alien insect, any of the alien insects could be the host for the Heart-Penetrating Ironline.","The Heart-Penetrating Ironline would control the host’s movement, and it would grab the opportunity to suddenly emerge. It would use its slender iron-line-like body to penetrate the heart of its target. It was considered an invisible assassin on the battlefield.","With the Class 3 Heart-Penetrating Ironline around, each spirit qi professional would need to be 120% concentrated. If the Heart-Penetrating Ironline found a gap and suddenly attacked, it would penetrate the heart. There was no method to cure or save the victim.","The heart was the core of the blood’s movement, and if the heart was shattered, the entire body’s blood would stop flowing, instantly losing vitality.","No matter how great a healing-type spirit qi professional was, it was impossible to rescue a life with a shattered or penetrated heart.","When everyone noticed that Lin Yuan wasn’t talking after gathering intel, their morale that was originally boosted by Xin Ying had fallen a little. However, Lin Yuan had to tell everyone of the Heart-Penetrating Ironline’s presence. If they weren’t cautious in advance, the Heart-Penetrating Ironline would be able to launch its sneak attack. It was highly possible that they might lose a Gold combatant. Even a Gold defense-type fey wouldn’t possibly be able to defend against an all-out attack from the Heart-Penetrating Ironline.","“Acid Tapeworm, Spiky Beetle...” Lin Yuan paused for a moment before he said with a deep voice, “And also the Heart-Penetrating Ironline. This dimensional rift is a pinnacle Class 1.”","Since Lin Yuan took responsibility for the reconnaissance, he felt that he shouldn’t withhold any information. It might affect morale, but it wasn’t enough to win the battle with just empty morale.","When the alien insect dimensional rift opened, it was already a fight to life and death. Both sides had a huge difference in combat power, and if they couldn’t even have the most accurate and factual information, then the result would be them getting wiped out. All of the non-combatants in Millstone Town would become food for the alien insects, and Millstone Town would become a meat paradise for the alien insects.","Lin Yuan’s words made everyone silent—only the silly Spitting Turtledove was still gulping down the third bucket of water. In order to eat Gray Beetles, it wasn’t willing to give up even if it was choking.","All of a sudden, Zhang Xiaobai let out an inappropriate peal of laughter. Immediately after, he gripped his fist and stepped forward. “It doesn’t matter if this alien insect dimensional rift is a normal Class 1 or a pinnacle Class 1. We are not trying to slaughter the insect tide. We are just going to endure until reinforcement arrives.”","Zhang Xiaobai wasn’t certain if Ascending Dragon City would notice the opening of this dimensional rift, however, someone had to step out and boost the morale for everyone.","Xiao Ying looked at Zhang Xiaobai with a little extra. This obviously inappropriate person is always surprisingly reliable during crucial moments.","After hearing Zhang Xiaobai’s statement, everyone stayed silent for a moment until some unknown person yelled out, “Since we have stayed behind, then we don’t have to be afraid of death! It is just an insect tide. I am great at enduring!”","“There is nothing to be afraid of. Even if I am not from Millstone Town, I cannot allow my own race to be killed by alien insects! Fight! Fight! Fight!”","Gradually—it was unknown if it was because of extreme fear or a certain indestructible faith that was passed down—everyone had a sudden boost of morale.","A dazzling spot of light that supported the morale was fused with the boost of morale from everyone, and it was shining brightly. A radiant spirit was rising up within the Millstone Town’s Guild Alliance. A grand spirit was produced invisibly under the night sky, and it was enough to contest with this dimensional rift.","The heaven’s dome in the night sky was like a silent reporter. When the sword aura drew across thousands of miles, the sword light would lit up all nineteen states1.","The faith and grand spirit at this moment was something that many people would eulogize, but it would be carved into the memories for eternity.","As the radiant light gathered, the energy was enough to penetrate the sky.","As Lin Yuan felt that grand spirit, he involuntarily wanted to laugh heartily toward the sky. However, he quickly withdrew his mind and reverted to his most composed state at this crucial moment.","“The alien insects might start moving at any time. We cannot allow the alien insects to enter Millstone Town. Therefore, our only choice is to meet the alien insects outside Millstone Town.”","Millstone Town didn’t just have spirit qi professionals. There were also ordinary people, and they were all helpless. If they were to face the insect tide, they would instantly become food for the insect tide.","Furthermore, once the alien insects entered Millstone Town, they would be receiving attacks from all directions, and it was impossible to defend against the alien insects from all directions. They would have to break formation due to the alien insects’ attacks, and everyone would be overwhelmed by the insect tide, turning into food for them.","Millstone Town’s city wall was built between two mountains, connecting them. Because it was very close to the Endless Forest, the city walls were built to be very thick.","To fight outside Millstone Town and rely on this city wall was the best choice to resist this insect tide.","Lu Pinru was still constantly producing Firm Armor Silk Clothing. Even with Blackie replenishing her spirit qi through Spirit Injection, her spirit qi was still exhausted.","After extracting all the spiritual power and spirit qi from herself and working hard with the coordination of her three Glowing Silkworm Weavers, almost every spirit qi professional with Silver feys had a set of Firm Armor Silk Clothing.","Lu Pinru was currently pale like a white sheet, and sweat was rolling down her cheeks. She wiped off the sweat on her cheeks and stood up to carry the two large wardrobes before she took big steps forward.","Lin Yuan and the quartet of the Extreme Guild Club led the way while the spirit qi professionals that were residing in Millstone Town followed behind, along with the adventuring spirit qi professionals that actually wanted to venture into the Endless Forest.","Over 1,000 individuals that disregarded death had started to form up formations under the city wall of Millstone Town. Dozens of Firm Armor Silk Clothing were glowing, and when buried in the insect noises, the silk clothing was giving off a trace of stern feeling.","Just as everyone formed up the formations, Lin Yuan suddenly felt the atmosphere tensing up. He took a deep breath and could see low-grade alien insects rushing over from the source of the insect noises.","Everyone could feel the ground underneath their legs constantly shaking. Lin Yuan looked far away and could see countless yellowish-green, reddish-brown, and different spots of light under the night sky. They looked just like spin drifts from the ocean and were surging over at astonishing speed.","Behind each spot of light was a dashing alien insect.","When facing this ferocious insect tide, everyone circulated their spiritual power to summon their feys.","The battle was about to begin!"]},{"number":138,"title":"Chapter 138: Cat Transformation","paragraphs":["Under the night, the surging insect tide brought up a fishy smell, a smell that only belonged to the alien insects.","The wind brought by the insect tide spread this smell to the people in Millstone Town.","Zhang Xiaobai could not help but say, “Wow, this is so smelly! Thank goodness I didn’t eat the skewers earlier, or I would have thrown up now.”","As he said that, he instructed his two feys. One of his fey was a mediocre defense-type fey, the Gale Mussel. It could provide other feys with a Gale Shield and had a solid physical defense. Due to its speed, the gale could cause powerful cuts through the wind blades.","His other fey was a bit peculiar. It was a fey the height of a human, which was reasonably common, but it was an uncommon Bloody Leech. How much blood did this Gold Bloody Leech usually need to absorb to be full?","Zhang Xiaobai constantly instructed the Gale Mussel to provide a Gale Shield to this Gold Bloody Leech. Then, he gave this Bloody Leech the five layers of the Firm Armor Silk Clothing from Pinru’s closet.","“I will be at the front line later. My fey has a strong attraction to the alien insects. My Gale Shield will cut the alien insects to death. Little mussel, don’t slack on the shields later, or I won’t feed you salt. I’ll let you become a freshwater mussel.”","Zhang Xiaobai had returned to his former improper self, but his words were very reliable.","Upon seeing the change in him, Xin Ying felt she had nowhere to place her fists.","At that moment, Lin Yuan and the quartet had taken over issuing commands.","The Gold fey Xin Ying had summoned was just a big, pure golden cat with a metallic luster that was slender and elegant. The big cat was more than a meter long with very sharp claws.","Xin Ying yelled, “Cat Transformation.”","Golden flames ignited on this big golden cat, and it quickly pounced toward Xin Ying before fusing into her body like a shadow.","Then, Xin Ying’s entire aura changed.","The black pupils in her red phoenix eyes[1] turned into golden slit pupils. These slit pupils solely belonged to cat-species feys and were the same as the big golden cat’s. Sharp claws emerged from Xin Ying’s hands as golden soft cat fur grew on her. Two golden cat ears also grew on her head.","Lin Yuan sighed when he saw Xin Ying’s transformation.","It was true that someone in the reserve team for the S Tournament would have an outstanding fey.","The exclusive skill that Xin Ying’s fey had awakened at Bronze was actually the rare Transformation Possession skill. This exclusive skill was like Tool Transformation, as it rarely appeared.","However, Transformation Possession and Tool Transformation were different. There was no weak Transformation Possession, unlike the latter, which was reliant on luck.","If one was lucky, a bike would turn into a motorbike. Otherwise, even a pair of skateboarding shoes would become open-toed.","With a fey that had Transformation Possession, a spirit qi professional was akin to having the fey’s combat abilities. A large part of the cat-species feys’ combat power was beast instincts, which Xin Ying had undertaken perfectly.","Xin Ying raised one hand, and golden flames arose on her sharp claws, looking very resplendent under the night sky.","“We have too few people and high-grade combatants, so those with Gold feys will attack at the periphery later. Those with Silver and Bronze feys will form two rows alternatively. If those at the front line can’t hold on, move to the back, and let the healing-type spirit qi professionals heal you. Those behind them will immediately take over.”","Then, Xin Ying rapidly flashed past everyone, creating an arc scratched by her claws on the ground.","“In a moment, with this line as the boundary, we’ll use the alien insect corpses as a solid line of defense.”","Lin Yuan soon understood what Xin Ying meant. She wanted to kill the alien insects along this line, where their corpses would pile up along. They only needed to leave a gap in those corpses that would keep piling up high in order to defend well.","Of course, this defense was only limited to the alien insects.","The constant opening of the alien insect dimensional rift gave the Radiance Federation’s Fey Researchers more chances to constantly analyze the alien insects and eventually come up with several ways to fight them.","Rather than saying the alien insects were intelligent beings, they were a race willing to devour everything in order to keep evolving.","Low-grade alien insects were not very intelligent and were almost in a state of confusion. They only acted according to instinct. Even with the high-grade alien insects commanding, when faced with the temptation of many alien insect flesh, the low-grade alien insects would probably devour this un-struggling flesh.","Of course, even the high-grade alien insects could not restrain their obsession for evolution. This obsession was inscribed in the bones and souls of the dimensional lifeforms, like the alien insects.","The alien insect evolution came entirely from devouring flesh and absorbing the energy from the flesh.","Xin Ying’s line could even stop the Class 3 alien insects and let them gorge on the corpses.","It was because of such instincts that the people in Millstone Town could use it as a sharp sword against the alien insects.","These alien insects’ cruel instinct to evolve by devouring was one of the reasons that made them terrifying.","All alien insects with grades would probably have experienced a lot of battles on the other side of the dimensional rift and cruelly devoured their companions. Therefore, almost every alien insect with grades was an experienced executioner.","The alien insects were going to attack Millstone Town because their echolocation had helped them find out which place contained the most lives that they could devour. When facing the vast and empty periphery of the Endless Forest, there was undoubtedly the most flesh energy in Millstone Town. This was why the insect tide would flock to Millstone Town.","Lin Yuan turned his head to look at the healing-type spirit qi professionals behind him and exclaimed, “Healing-type spirit qi professionals, regardless of whether you’re Bronze or Elite, go to the back. Find an opportunity at the back to heal the injured combat-class spirit qi professionals. It’s enough for me at the front line. My fey can heal all.”","A cheer rang out in the Millstone Town. Lin Yuan’s words once again increased their morale at this critical moment.","Multi-target healing would mean that Lin Yuan could heal multiple targets at the same time and provide more chances for the people present to receive his healing.","[1] Eyes where the inner corners are slanted down while the outer corners are slanted up."]},{"number":139,"title":"Chapter 139: Hippopotamus Affinity?","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Lin Yuan knew that it was inevitable for people to get injured and sacrificed in the battle to defend Millstone Town and fight against the insect tide. However, he could only allocate the other healing-type spirit qi professionals to the rear while he healed the front line.","As such, he could ensure the survival of those healing-type spirit qi professionals that could not defend themselves—only by ensuring their survival could the people receive more healing.","Given his capabilities, Lin Yuan was confident that he could do a good job healing the front line. Actually, this was because his Jasmine Lily was a Fantasy Breed. Otherwise, he would not dare to be so bold.","Even if there would be sacrifices in the battle, Lin Yuan would also do his best to maintain the sacrifices at the minimum within his ability.","The insect tide was a breath away, and all the feys had taken their positions, ready to meet their enemies.","Lin Yuan finally got to know why even though Tan Ran loved cute feline feys, Zhang Xiaobai had said that the former was not fated with cute feys in this lifetime.","Two of Tan Ran’s five-meter-long and three-meter-tall huge feys stood there. One was a Gold Lava Hippopotamus, while the other was a Silver Gluttony Hippopotamus.","When Lin Yuan looked at Tan Ran, who had natural curls, a cute face, and smooth skin, a guess arose in his heart.","Is Tan Ran’s affinity for feys more inclined toward hippopotamus feys?","This was simply a discrepancy in cuteness!","When Zhang Xiaobai saw that the insect tide had rushed to less than 100 meters before him and would reach him in a few seconds, he and his Bloody Leech immediately stood in the very front.","Accompanied by a flash of sword light, Zhang Xiaobai cut his wrist, causing fresh blood to drop on the Bloody Leech right away. He then yelled, “Little Red, use Oily Plasma.”","The Bloody Leech’s body quickly secreted a layer of lustrous dark-red plasma, which was as sticky as oil.","Oily Plasma was actually an ability to defend against damage caused by sharp weapons and heavy blows.","Before the sharp weapons could cut the Bloody Leech, the Oily Plasma would slide away the sharp blades. And when there was a heavy blow, this layer of Oily Plasma could also serve as a cushioning role.","It was just that he now used this Oily Plasma as a tool to attract the alien insects.","The actual world was no game. Defense-type spirit qi professionals did not have taunting abilities, which only existed in games. Nonetheless, the Oily Plasma ability was just like a taunting ability to the alien insects.","The Oily Plasma emitted a thick stench of blood with a mixture of oil and blood that stimulated the alien insects nearby when diffused into the night sky.","The alien insects that smelled this stench of oil and blood rapidly rushed toward the Bloody Leech right away.","Zhang Xiaobai had taken advantage of the alien insects’ weakness. When the bloody smell attracted the alien insects, they crashed into the Gale Shield around the Bloody Leech.","A dozen layers of Gale Shields had covered the Bloody Leech’s body. The gale circulated rapidly on this Gale Shield’s surface and stirred the gradeless alien insects into smithereens.","Although many alien insects approached wave after wave, these dozen Gale Shield layers did not suffer any damage. Instead, they ran out of energy and dissipated when the Gale Shield turned the alien insects into smithereens.","Many low-grade alien insect corpses on both sides of the Gale Shield built up half of the fortification on this side.","The alien insect corpses on both sides were three meters high, with only a gap between where the Bloody Leech stood.","Upon seeing that the fortification on this side almost built up, Zhang Xiaobai immediately led the Bloody Leech to retreat. Then, he moved to another side of the battlefield to help build the fortification and fight against the insect swarm’s fierce attacks.","Zhang Xiaobai handed over the fortifications to the spirit qi professionals led by Millstone Town’s Guild Alliance’s branch president to guard.","On the other side, Tan Ran’s Gold Lava Hippopotamus used its Gold ability, Melting Mantle.","The land in front of the Gold Lava Hippopotamus suddenly churned, and the black land slowly turned red. It emitted a scorching heat and crimson blaze.","The land within this range turned into slow-flowing lava that melted and cremated many alien insects.","At the side, the Gluttony Hippopotamus bit those alien insects that stepped on their companions’ corpses to come over and chewed and swallowed them.","The alien insects’ blood contained strong acidic toxicity, which was nothing to the Gluttony Hippopotamus.","When Lin Yuan looked at the Gluttony Hippopotamus’ data information, he realized that its exclusive skill was interesting.","[Fey Name]: Gluttony Hippopotamus","[Fey Species]: Hippopotamidae/Hairless Horse","[Fey Grade]: Silver (7/10)","[Fey Type]: Water","[Fey Quality]: Flawless","Abilities:","[Tooth Stab]: Continuous stab with its five-inch-long sharp teeth.","[Hunger Eating]: The Gluttony Hippopotamuses are always hungry and will always crush and rapidly eat the target.","[Fasting Bomb]: The Gluttony Hippopotamuses stop eating and spew out all the accumulated energy, causing an explosion of energy.","Exclusive Skill:","[Harmful Food Purification]: The Gluttony Hippopotamuses will purify all the toxic and harmful components out of its body with the special jaw glands.","The Gluttony Hippopotamus was executing its exclusive skill and filtering out the acidic toxicity from the alien insects’ blood before it spat it out to the insect swarm. The purified acid sprayed on the alien insects’ hard shells and caused their bodies to corrode and soften.","In the process of running, the alien insects with softened shells were cut into pieces by their companions’ shells at the side, leaving their corpses with no bones left.","Xin Ying quickly hunted and killed the nearby alien insects with grades.","Regardless of Class 1 alien insects that were equivalent to Bronze feys or Class 2 alien insects that were equivalent to Silver feys, Xin Ying leaped up, and her sharp claws soon killed these alien insects.","The dead Class 1 and Class 2 alien insects were left in the swarm of mostly Normal alien insects, which immediately caused turmoil. Those low-grade alien insects madly snatched the high-grade alien insect flesh, and it was for this reason that the advance of the insect swarm was greatly reduced.","Lin Yuan’s Spirit-Gather Goldfish was still incessantly replenishing Lu Pinru’s spiritual power, while Lu Pinru was still producing the Firm Armor Silk Clothing.","Chimey was guarding by Lin Yuan’s side as the latter was standing behind Tan Ran. It would kill those alien insects that crossed Tan Ran’s line of defense with its Sound Thrust.","At that moment, Lin Yuan summoned his Jasmine Lily."]},{"number":140,"title":"Chapter 140: The Insect’s Butthole","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","When the Jasmine Lily was summoned, its emerald-green fasciated flowers were mottled with a jade-like color, as though emitting an emerald green mist.","The light mist rose from the jade-green color, causing the normal flower on the top to look extraordinary.","In the process of evolving into a Fantasy Breed, not only had Lin Yuan’s Jasmine Lily developed bunches, but it had also undergone fasciation.","Not even an ordinary Creation Master could recognize that Lin Yuan had summoned a Jasmine Lily.","When the quartet and many combat-class spirit qi professionals saw Lin Yuan summon his Jasmine Lily, they could feel that this fey was quite extraordinary. However, nobody entertained the idea of it being a Fantasy Breed, as they had never heard of a Silver Fantasy Breed.","Despite that, Lin Yuan could not help but feel somewhat awkward when he used his Jasmine Lily’s Heal ability.","If he used the Jasmine Lily’s fasciated flowers to heal, the healing effect would indeed be much stronger.","However, the feeling of happiness the fascinated parts caused while healing was fatal to the combat-class spirit qi professionals in the midst of battle. If such a feeling of happiness enveloped them and they got indulged in it, the approaching alien insects would rip them apart.","Thus, Lin Yuan could only use the Jasmine Lily’s topmost flower that had yet to undergo fasciation to heal the front line.","Xin Ying had killed high-grade alien insects among the insect tide, and inevitably, the other alien insects snuck up on her and injured her.","But every time Xin Ying got injured, she realized that there would always be a beam of green light shining on her. The surging vitality in the green light could heal her wounds by just circulating her once.","While Zhang Xiaobai’s Bloody Leech was resisting against many alien insects, its Oily Plasma seemed to have faded because of the alien insects’ attacks.","Under the sea of insect attacks, it was inevitable to be injured by the low-grade alien insects’ spikes and sharp teeth.","At that moment, there were many fine wounds on the Bloody Leech, and the tissue fluid oozing out of the wounds almost drenched its body.","Just as Zhang Xiaobai felt that the Bloody Leech could not hold on any longer, a beam of green light shone on its body. The green light rapidly helped the Bloody Leech to replenish its vitality and healed its wounds.","These beams of green light always brought hope filled with vitality when the front line combat-class spirit qi professionals were having the hardest time. Regardless of Lin Yuan’s control of the healing amount or the timing of his healing, those on the front line felt a peace of mind.","If it were not for the fact that they had no way to make a move when defending against the insect tide, the people Lin Yuan had healed would probably want to give a thumbs-up to him.","Although Lin Yuan was actually healing other spirit qi professionals for the first time during this perilous insect tide, he acted calmly and unhurriedly without panicking.","Each time, the topmost Jasmine Lily flower would emit eight healing beams, which was the best Lin Yuan had experimented with. Otherwise, too many healing beams would not allow him to achieve the perfect healing effect.","If he released too many healing beams, it would cause a healing overflow. Under such a situation where healing was lacking, any healing overflow was an intolerable mistake.","Lin Yuan then followed the eight healing beams’ frequency to heal the people on the front line.","From time to time, he would turn around to help ease the burden of those healing-type spirit qi professionals at the back.","Whenever there were combat-class spirit qi professionals in the back who were seriously injured and had to retreat from the battle, Lin Yuan would use the Jasmine Lily’s fasciated flowers to heal them.","But every time he healed them, these combat-class spirit qi professionals would uncontrollably make strange sounds, which made the battle against the insect tide seem somewhat bizarre.","Zhang Xiaobai pursed his lips, and when he heard these strange sounds, he could not help but mutter, “Are they really so happy to be wounded by alien insects? Why can’t I feel it whenever I get beaten up by Xin Ying? If this is happiness, then how is Xin Ying different from the alien insects?”","Upon hearing Zhang Xiaobai’s words, Xin Ying, who was killing the alien insects with grades, felt the fire in her heart igniting. Despite killing the alien insects with strong intensity, her exhausted body and her speed got better right away.","After Cat Transformation, Xin Ying constantly scratched with her sharp claws and killed the alien insects more effectively than before.","Lin Yuan found that among the healing-type spirit qi professionals, the person with the Spitting Turtledove had really made a big difference. Despite its gross abilities, the Spitting Turtledove’s Sticky Saliva could effectively stop bleeding. Basically, the combat-class spirit qi professionals who had gone to the back and moved back up to the front line all almost had the Spitting Turtledove’s sticky saliva.","With its contractor forcing it, the Spitting Turtledove frantically spat its saliva. It felt very regretful now. If it had known earlier that it would have to spit so much saliva, it would have drunk one more bucket of water, even if not for the delicious Gray Beetles.","If the Spitting Turtledove could speak, it would probably have jumped and shouted, “I really don’t have a drop of saliva left.”","After just less than 20 minutes, a defensive line formed by the alien insects’ flesh had basically been built.","At that moment, a violent crashing sound rang from the solid defensive line.","A few dark spikes pierced through this defense line of alien insect flesh pile, creating an opening due to the impact.","With a body full of spikes, a huge black beetle was rapidly eating the alien insect flesh on the line of defense that had been knocked apart. This black beetle was one of the three Class 3 alien insects. It was a Class 3 Spiky Beetle.","The Class 3 alien insect finally appeared among the insect tide.","Alien insects were indeed greedy, and such greed referred to their desire for flesh. Naturally, the Class 3 Spiky Beetle was not an exception.","The Spiky Beetle was the most excited. Given the enormous amount of insect corpses accumulated there, the Spiky Beetle could not help but quickly enjoy this gourmet feast.","Xin Ying’s expression turned bitter. She circulated the spirit qi in her body, and a golden feline fey shadow appeared behind her.","She shot a glance at Tan Ran and Zhang Xiaobai. They looked at each other and immediately worked together to command their feys to attack and attract the Spiky Beetle’s attention.","The Spiky Beetle hissed upon seeing the Bloody Leech and Lava Hippopotamus. Upon sensing the power within the Bloody Leech and the Lava Hippopotamus did not lose to itself, it charged toward them.","Its shell with sharp spikes that carried a tremendous force was the Spiky Beetle’s best means of attack. The spikes’ penetration power, coupled with the tremendous force, allowed them to pierce through steel plates with the same thickness as the spikes. The burst of power due to the spikes’ tremendous force was truly terrifying.","At that moment, Xin Ying condensed the golden feline shadow behind her into her claws. She sneak-attacked the Spiky Beetle with all her power and hit its most vulnerable area—its butthole!"]},{"number":141,"title":"Chapter 141: The Sea of Flowers Eating The Insects","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Xin Ying managed to strike the Spiky Beetle.","The golden feline shadow hidden in her claw blades exploded when it hit the Spiky Beetle’s weak spot and entered the insect’s butthole.","This strike containing Xin Ying’s full force exploded in the Spiky Beetle’s body.","Despite being a Class 3 alien insect, the Spiky Beetle had suffered a full blow at its weak spot by Xin Ying, a B-rank power offense-type spirit qi professional with a Gold fey.","Although it was still struggling, it was obviously the Spiky Beetle’s last resistance before its death. Soon, the Spiky Beetle lost its life and lay motionless.","Zhang Xiaobai immediately commanded his Bloody Leech to drain the Spiky Beetle’s blood.","The Bloody Leech could quickly replenish its lost stamina during the battle by draining blood.","The defense line formed by the alien insect corpses was mostly thanks to Zhang Xiaobai and the Bloody Leech. Without the Bloody Leech using its Oily Plasma to attract the insects, the fortification could not have been constructed so quickly.","At this point, everyone had been fighting hard for nearly an hour, causing their stamina to reach rock bottom.","However, they still carried on fighting, relying on nothing more than the faith and protection in their hearts, as well as the desire to live.","Zhang Xiaobai’s Bloody Leech drained the Spiky Beetle’s blood. Its acidic blood made the Bloody Leech suffer serious injuries, but it recovered its stamina pretty well.","Then, Zhang Xiaobai commanded the Bloody Leech to fill the Spiky Beetle on the fortification where the Spiky Beetle had previously crashed into.","The Spiky Beetle’s shell faced outward, and its spikes pierced through the low-grade alien insects that crashed into it, just like candied hawthorn sticks.","It seemed that the Spiky Beetle had contributed a lot to the fortification.","Under the dome of the night, the battle ensued.","Lin Yuan could completely sense that everyone had little stamina left. Not only had the front line defense become a bit strenuous, but those combat-class spirit qi professionals with Bronze and Silver feys behind also rotated at a much faster pace than before. Before their fresh injuries could heal, they had to take over. Due to their unhealed fresh injuries adding onto their old injuries, everyone could barely hold on any longer.","Healing-type spirit qi professionals were rare, including those with Bronze feys, like the Spitting Turtledove. These healing-type spirit qi professionals had already exhausted the spirit qi in their bodies.","At that moment, Lin Yuan suddenly received an intimate greeting that came from his spiritual spatial zone.","Red Thorn had awakened from its evolution, and a look of surprise appeared on Lin Yuan’s face. It had awakened at the right time!","Lin Yuan summoned Red Thorn without hesitation.","A strange plant that was nearly two meters tall appeared in his hand. A huge sphere grew in the middle of the plant, with the folds on the sphere covered with sharp teeth. Each sharp tooth was a bloody mouth when opened. Red Thorn’s Mouth of Relinquish had become more powerful after evolving to Bronze.","Large but layered flesh-like flowers grew above the Mouth of Relinquish. The flowers were covered with folds and carried a strange aroma. Strong acids from all sorts of dimensional lifeforms’ flesh that Red Thorn had digested and extracted filled the digestive cavity. Not only could the acid help the Mouth of Relinquish with digestion, but it could also be spat out by the large rose-shaped flowers growing on the digestive cavity.","The first 18 vines that had grown previously could now reach seven or eight meters long. They were the thickness of a wrist, and the barbs that grew on them also had many irregular serrations. The outer new vines were the thickness of a thumb.","Not only did they have barbs on top, but these barbs were also hollow.","While stabbing into the target, the acid in Red Thorn’s digestive cavity could also be injected.","Red Thorn was more like a killing machine than when it had been at Elite. However, this was not why Lin Yuan was confident in Red Thorn. Rather, it was because of the new layers of flesh-like flowers on the Mouth of Relinquish.","This was an organ that had grown based on the new exclusive skill when Red Thorn had evolved to Bronze—the spore cavity.","Lin Yuan yelled, “All the combat-class spirit qi professionals at the front line, retreat backward! Protect the combat-class spirit qi professionals at the back! Those with Gold feys focus on killing the alien insects.”","Despite not knowing why Lin Yuan had given such an order, their instinctive trust in Lin Yuan made them retreat at the same time, including the quartet.","Red Thorn had not seen Lin Yuan for a long time. The smooth vine with no sharp barbs that Red Thorn had evolved particularly for Lin Yuan wrapped around his wrist, expressing the affection of Red Thorn, which did not have high wisdom.","Lin Yuan held this smooth vine and said, “Red Thorn, release the spores to your heart’s content and devour all the alien insects that you can.”","Red Thorn conveyed its joy when it sensed the alien insect corpses everywhere and the countless alien insects not far away.","In the simple-minded Red Thorn’s opinion, these alien insects were the food that Lin Yuan had sent it after its awakening.","The spore cavity on the Mouth of Relinquish shook. Each of the spores released from the layered flesh-like petals flew to the alien insect corpses and quickly took root. In just a few seconds, the Red Thorn’s spores drained the alien insect corpses’ energy.","A shrunken version of the Red Thorn with only a digestive cavity with several vines grew as a result.","Rhizomes grew out of these spores’ child ramets and quickly joined in tandem, passing energy to each other.","A few of the closest ones to Red Thorn were rooted on the alien insect corpses’ fortification line, and the strongest ramets were connected to all the new child ramets grown from the spores.","These few strong ramets placed their roots on top of Red Thorn’s roots and passed on the energy that the child ramets were draining from the sea of insects.","While the crowd was defending for more than an hour, the child ramets rapidly drained the insect corpses.","Red Thorn was constantly releasing spores and producing new child ramets.","The child ramets that had previously grown were also becoming more robust from a height of 30 centimeters to nearly 2 meters tall. The rose-shaped flowers of the digestive cavity could swallow most of the alien insects when it swirled open.","Each child ramet had a digestive cavity with large and delicate red rose-like flowers.","Under this night sky, snaking vines with sharp barbs were hidden in the growing sea of flowers.","This scene was beautiful yet strange and magnificent.","While this sea of flowers was rapidly digesting the alien insect corpses, it started to sweep up the alien insects.","Most of the alien insects were gradeless or even Normal. Such alien insects were the best soil for these child ramets to absorb nutrients.","The sea of flowers spread toward the sea of alien insects, regarding them as the most sumptuous dinner.","The Millstone Town people, including the quartet, looked dumbfounded at the magnificent sea of flowers’ sudden appearance. When they looked at Lin Yuan and Red Thorn’s ortet, they could not help but swallow.","The vines danced, and the sea of insects trudged among the flowers."]},{"number":142,"title":"Chapter 142: The Battle Between the Sea of Flowers and the Insect Tide","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Under the approaching early morning’s sky, the chill of the late autumn crept up and constantly produced water vapor in the air, forming vague, cold fog.","When everyone looked at this sea of flowers colliding with the endless insect tide and killing them to its heart’s content, they felt a tightness in their throats.","However, the Millstone Town people suddenly felt ease in their tense feelings.","At the very least, the sea of flowers was now in a stalemate with the insect tide, giving all of them the chance to breathe at last.","When the Extreme Guild Club’s quartet looked at Red Thorn’s ortet beside Lin Yuan and then at him, they could not help but feel that he was simply a person full of surprises.","At every critical moment—be it the previous scouting, his fey having the ability to restore spiritual power, or the fact that he could keep up healing the front line—Lin Yuan could always come forward.","And now, when everyone was nearly unable to hold on anymore, he summoned a strange plant lifeform and controlled the insect tide’s pace.","Xin Ying detected Red Thorn’s ortet beside Lin Yuan’s hand. She could sense that this two-meter-tall, strange plant that she had never heard of was not very powerful. Its battle prowess was merely at Bronze.","However, this plant lifeform’s ability was simply too powerful. It seemed as if it was born to suppress this insect tide.","Xin Ying had taken part in the S Tournament before, so she had more thoughts on this. When she looked at the Normal child ramets in the sea of flowers and the Elite ramets beside the ortet, she deeply felt that Lin Yuan’s plant lifeform was terrifying.","If its grade reached Diamond, then what kind of killing power would the Platinum ramets and countless Gold child ramets possess?","If this was the case, wouldn’t it alone be able to suppress a Class 3 insect tide?","Lin Yuan did not know what Xin Ying was thinking, or else, he would have smiled bitterly.","It was difficult on him now, as his spiritual power was being consumed while the Red Thorn was constantly releasing spores from the Mouth of Relinquish’s topmost flesh-like petals.","Before Lin Yuan could not bear with it, he quietly activated the Spirit Qi Imprint on his back.","The Spirit Qi Imprint’s spiritual power was continuously supporting Red Thorn’s constant release of spores, allowing the sea of flowers to become more magnificent. It was all thanks to Blackie’s exclusive skill. Otherwise, even if Red Thorn had such a capability, Lin Yuan’s body’s spiritual power could not last.","Another point was that the Red Thorn’s spores needed to grow into child ramets. If the child ramets wanted to grow, they would need an enormous amount of flesh energy. Thanks to everyone killing these alien insects, Red Thorn’s released spores could quickly form into a sea of flowers.","However, Xin Ying was right. If Red Thorn was truly at Diamond, and with the premise of a large number of insect corpses and sufficient spirit qi in Lin Yuan’s body, the sea of flowers could really resist a Class 3 insect tide alone.","Xin Ying looked at Lin Yuan’s outstanding figure by the sea of flowers and knew that his future was promising. Then, her eyes focused as she looked at everyone behind her. “Those who still can kill the alien insects, follow me!”","She had noticed that this sea of flowers could control the insects below Normal and be in a stalemate with Normal ones. If it encountered Elite ones and they struggled—even though the child ramets’ barbed vines could pierce the Elite insects’ shells and release strong corrosive blood—they could easily break the child ramets’ vines and even crush them.","Therefore, the sea of flowers was not very effective against Elite alien insects. Nonetheless, the Elite alien insects could still perish under the child ramets’ concentrated attacks.","Naturally, the sea of flowers could deal no damage to Class 2 insects, comparable to Silver feys. They rampaged through the sea of flowers and soon destroyed it.","Xin Ying, Zhang Xiaobai, Tan Ran, and two other spirit qi professionals with Gold feys did their best to kill all the Class 2 alien insects in the sea of flowers. When they encountered some Class 1 insects, they would kill them to reduce the pressure on Red Thorn and allow it to spit out more spores, enhancing the sea of flowers.","It was also akin to saving Lin Yuan’s spiritual power consumption.","In fact, the sea of flowers’ damage degree could only be considered minor for the situation at hand. There were simply too many Normal, and below, insects, which were also the child ramets’ potential source of nutrients.","Some of the earliest child ramets had grown close to one meter tall. Despite almost reaching a ramet’s degree, the child ramets’ combat power was close to an Elite.","Such child ramets did not even need to use the vines to attack the Normal insects. Instead, they could just spiral open the flower on the corrosive cavity and reveal the sharp teeth inside before easily devouring them.","A large amount of acid in the corrosive cavity could also quickly digest the devoured insects, turning them into energy. Part of the energy would be given to Red Thorn’s ortet. The child ramets would absorb the remaining energy themselves, which would then turn them even stronger.","At the same time, Red Thorn’s ortet still constantly released spores that continued to spread the sea of flowers’ dominance. These spores would also rapidly replenish the sea of flowers’ damaged parts.","Because the child ramets’ rhizomes were all interconnected, even if the sea of flowers killed lesser alien insects, the nutrition would be shared based on these rhizomes.","If they encountered some insects that wreaked havoc in the sea of flowers, Red Thorn would quickly mobilize energy. It would channel energy to numerous child ramets near that rampaging alien insect. These child ramets would rapidly absorb the ortet’s energy and grow into Elite ramets.","Red Thorn had reached Bronze, so its ramets were Elite.","Numerous ramets would besiege the Class 1 alien insects and devour them to offset the consumed energy.","The stalemate between the sea of flowers and the insect tide was because the former had the upper hand. The sea of flowers’ nutrients came from the insect tide, but the latter could not replenish any nutrients from the former.","Nonetheless, there were too many insects. Even if the sea of flowers devoured all the present insects, many more were approaching like an endless stream.","The sea of flowers’ vines danced, and the alien insects hissed. The stalemate had lasted for nearly an hour, and in the crowd’s eyes, it was the most beautiful outcome.","This was because such a stalemate could allow the injured ones and their feys to recuperate. The injured combat-class spirit qi professionals and feys were still waiting for the healing-type spirit qi professionals to heal them.","Lin Yuan’s Spirit-Gather Goldfish no longer used Spirit Injection on Lu Pinru. Instead, it replenished the healing-type spirit qi professionals’ exhausted spiritual power.","As a result, the healing-type spirit qi professionals had enough spirit qi to unleash their abilities and heal the combatants who were alternating between old and new injuries."]},{"number":143,"title":"Chapter 143: Lin Yuan’s Solo Kill","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","After another half an hour of stalemate, a green luminescent insect suddenly appeared at the sea of flowers’ edge. This huge alien insect was the second Class 3 alien insect, the Acid Tapeworm.","When everyone saw the Acid Tapeworm appear, they were relieved but had grave expressions.","While killing the Class 1 and Class 2 alien insects, the combat-class spirit qi professionals with Gold feys needed to focus and carefully observe their surroundings. This was because they did not know in which insect’s body the hidden killer, Class 3 Heart-Penetrating Ironline, was. It might launch a sudden attack at any time.","Since the Acid Tapeworm appeared, only the Class 3 Heart-Penetrating Ironline was left.","Everyone retreated to their defensive positions, prepared to deal with the Acid Tapeworm in unison.","The Acid Tapeworm’s defensive power was not strong, not even comparable to a Class 1 insect. Nonetheless, it was terrifying due to the green acidic corrosive liquid in its body that would even corrode sand and soil when spewed out.","Even if a Gold fey got into contact with a little of this acid, a huge chunk of its flesh would be corroded. If it was covered in more acid, its roots would be damaged.","Just as Xin Ying, Zhang Xiaobai, Tan Ran, the Millstone Town’s Guild Alliance branch president, and a middle-aged foreign man were prepared to attack the Acid Tapeworm, Red Thorn suddenly became excited.","Lin Yuan soon understood why he sensed Red Thorn’s sudden excitement and intense emotion waves. Red Thorn had probably spotted its favorite delicacy.","The leaf-shaped Diamond fey storage box that the Moon Empress had given Lin Yuan contained a huge amount of dimensional lifeform flesh.","After devouring the flesh of different kinds of dimensional lifeforms, Red Thorn slowly became picky.","Based on Lin Yuan’s observation, Red Thorn preferred eating the dimensional lifeforms’ flesh that contained a lot of acid in their blood. Naturally, alien insect flesh contained the strongest acidity.","The carcass of an Acid Tapeworm was in the Diamond leaf-shaped fey storage box all along, and Red Thorn had been drooling over its Class 3 flesh. However, Lin Yuan had not allowed Red Thorn to eat it.","This was because Red Thorn had been at Elite previously. If it ate this Class 3 Acid Tapeworm, it would likely be unable to digest it and would instead be injured by the Acid Tapeworm’s strong acidity.","Now that Red Thorn had seen the Acid Tapeworm, its vine wrapped around Lin Yuan’s wrist shook. It was like a puppy wagging its tail pitifully to plead its master when it saw something delicious.","Lin Yuan nodded as he looked at the Acid Tapeworm at the edge of the sea of flowers.","When Red Thorn had been at Elite, Lin Yuan would at most feed it the flesh of Silver dimensional lifeforms. Now that it had reached Bronze, it should be fine for it to eat some Gold dimensional lifeforms’ flesh.","Red Thorn’s roots, which had been rooted to the ground, suddenly erupted with surging energy. This energy fluctuation made Lin Yuan sense a layer of airwaves forming in the ground underneath his feet.","This energy was what the child ramets had drained from a huge amount of alien insect flesh.","At that moment, Red Thorn redirected that energy to the child ramets near the Acid Tapeworm, and they rapidly grew into 1.5-meter-tall ramets. These ramets had the ability of pinnacle Elite feys, which was the limit of Red Thorn’s ramets.","The nearly 100 ramets close to the Acid Tapeworm waved their barbed vines at it.","When the Acid Tapeworm sensed the attack and was about to spit out acid, Lin Yuan raised his hand, used the Spirit Qi Imprint’s spiritual power, and unleashed his Blue Flash Purple Butterfly’s ability, Silence Scale Powder.","The Silence Scale Powder landed and attached on the Acid Tapeworm, effectively stopping it from spitting out acid.","In fact, the Silence Scale Powder would not affect the Acid Tapeworm when it spat out acid, as it did not need to communicate with the spirit qi in the world. It was just releasing the acid from its body.","However, the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly’s exclusive skill, Scale Powder Halo, made a vast difference. The light pollution—caused by the scale powder reflecting the Acid Tapeworm’s body’s greenish light—made it dizzy.","What Lin Yuan wanted was the Scale Powder Halo to cause brief dizziness.","Just as the Acid Tapeworm was dizzy, the pinnacle Elite ramets wrapped it, and the vines’ barbs pierced into its weak epidermis.","The vines were soon firmly fixed on the Acid Tapeworm and dragged it from the edge to within the sea of flowers.","Red Thorn’s pinnacle Elite ramets tore apart the Acid Tapeworm’s weak translucent epidermis, causing a huge amount of green acid to spray out and land on the child ramets in the sea of flowers.","The child ramets below Normal were instantly corroded and withered when the acid touched them, while the Normal child ramets did not last long before they turned yellow and gradually corroded completely.","However, the Elite ramets could bear this powerful corrosive acid.","Red Thorn had drained a huge amount of alien insect flesh, so it had significant resistance to the acid in the alien insect blood.","The potent digestive fluids in Red Thorn’s body were a result of devouring highly acidic dimensional lifeforms’ flesh.","The Elite ramets swirled open the rose-shaped flowers on the corrosive cavity and revealed the sharp teeth inside.","The sharp teeth immediately bit through the Acid Tapeworm’s epidermis. At the same time, the corrosive cavity penetrated its body and rapidly drained the Acid Tapeworm’s acid in huge amounts. Then, they transferred all the energy to the ortet.","While the ramets were devouring the Acid Tapeworm’s acid, the ortet’s Mouth of Relinquish became a little more acidic due to the energy the ramets provided.","Thanks to Lin Yuan’s Silence Scale Powder and Red Thorn’s attacks, this Class 3 Acid Tapeworm perished.","Its death could be attributed to three factors—Lin Yuan’s unexpected use of Silence Scale Powder, the sea of flowers being spread out to attack, and the Acid Tapeworm having a weak spot.","Naturally, Lin Yuan’s actions astonished everyone. It was a Class 3 alien insect, comparable to a Gold fey, after all.","Tan Ran could not help but mumble, “Lin Yuan is a legendary social elite, right?”","Upon hearing Tan Ran’s words, Zhang Xiaobai scratched his head and asked, “Tan Ran, what’s a social elite?”","Xin Ying looked at Zhang Xiaobai’s silly look and rolled her eyes before explaining, “You don’t know what a social elite is? They’re the ones who are left after gathering everyone in society, compressing, extracting, filtering them, and repeating it many times.”","Xin Ying’s explanation dumbfounded Zhang Xiaobai. “Isn’t that a... scum?”"]},{"number":144,"title":"Chapter 144: Severed Arm","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","It was unknown whether Zhang Xiaobai’s mind was truly creative, or he was purposely trying to make everyone light-hearted. In any case, everyone under the Millstone Town’s city walls had their tension relieved. Apart from Xin Ying, the rest of the people were laughing heartily. However, Xin Ying could only feel that her fist was getting itchy again.","At that moment, there was a sudden change of events.","Zhang Xiaobai originally commanded his Silver Gale Mussel to shoot out its basic ability, Forceful Wind Blade, to kill a Class 1 alien insect that was destroying things within the sea of flowers.","When the Forceful Wind Blade cleaved the Class 1 alien insect, it should have split the alien insect into two. However, the Forceful Wind Blade felt as though it had slashed on a metal plate, and there was a clear metallic clash.","At that moment, a two-meter long black iron line suddenly shot out of the Class 1 alien insect’s body and rushed straight for Zhang Xiaobai’s heart.","Zhang Xiaobai wasn’t considered far from the Class 1 alien insect and was less than 15 meters away. The Heart-Penetrating Ironline took just a blink of the eye to cover the distance.","Back when Lin Yuan heard the ‘clang’ sound, he knew that it wasn’t good. He consciously commanded Red Thorn to grow a huge quantity of Elite ramets in front of Zhang Xiaobai.","Unfortunately, the produced Elite ramets were immediately penetrated by the Heart-Penetrating Ironline and couldn’t stop its straight-line thrust.","Within a distance of 15 meters, Red Thorn had produced six Elite ramets. Each of the Elite ramets had a bowl-sized hole in their corrosive cavity, and it was an injury made by the Heart-Penetrating Ironline.","However, when the Heart-Penetrating Ironline paused for a moment due to Lin Yuan’s defense, Zhang Xiaobai was able to react. Xin Ying had also reacted by pouncing over.","Due to shock and anger, Xin Ying used nearly all of her strength to pounce over and released all the power with her claws. The sharp claws instantly cleaved on the Heart-Penetrating Ironline, and there was a metallic clash.","It was fortunate that Xin Ying’s all-out attack was able to shift the Heart-Penetrating Ironline’s attack trajectory. It was originally targeting Zhang Xiaobai’s heart, but its direction had slightly changed now. Surprisingly, the Heart-Penetrating Ironline forcefully twisted its body to change direction and still pierced toward Zhang Xiaobai.","But when Zhang Xiaobai dodged, the Heart-Penetrating Ironline didn’t manage to accurately pierce through Zhang Xiaobai’s heart. Instead, it pierced through Zhang Xiaobai’s shoulder bone.","When the Heart-Penetrating Ironline pierced through the shoulder bone, it twisted gently, and its ironline body gathered together. This brief contact had caused Zhang Xiaobai’s entire arm to drop onto the ground.","“Zhang Xiaobai!”","“Big Brother Xiaobai! Your arm!”","“Zhang Xiaobai!!”","This sudden change of events stunned everyone. Had it not been for Lin Yuan and Xin Ying’s fast reactions, Zhang Xiaobai’s heart would have been penetrated by the Heart-Penetrating Ironline, and he would be a lifeless corpse now.","However, even if Lin Yuan and Xin Ying had reacted fast enough, Zhang Xiaobai still couldn’t keep his arm. In fact, Zhang Xiaobai didn’t just lose his arm—the severed part started from the scapula.","Zhang Xiaobai was now in such pain that he was ghastly pale and drenched in a cold sweat. His other arm was still holding his wound tightly, but fresh blood was still spraying out in large amounts.","Ten fingers weren’t even able to cover the entire shoulder, let alone an entire arm. The pain was so intense that Zhang Xiaobai’s vision turned black, and he nearly collapsed. However, before Zhang Xiaobai’s vision could black out, another intense pain made Zhang Xiaobai’s body shiver. It felt as though he didn’t even have the strength to cover his wound.","Xin Ying, who was always aggressive, knelt on the ground lifelessly after seeing Zhang Xiaobai suddenly losing an arm. She didn’t even blink her eyes as tears started to drip down constantly.","The moment Zhang Xiaobai lost his arm, Xin Ying knew that his life was done for. Even if they were able to survive this insect tide, Zhang Xiaobai’s arm would never be able to recover.","The core of the Extreme Guild Club’s S Tournament official team was the Radiance Hundred Sequence #18, White Devil.","Xin Ying knew that even White Devil wouldn’t be able to regrow severed limbs. Healing-type spirit qi professionals were already rare in the Radiance Federation, and there were just a few high-ranked healing-type spirit qi professionals. Even if the Extreme Guild Club was able to invite a king-class healing-type professional, they still might not regrow Zhang Xiaobai’s severed arm.","Those who could be considered king-class experts were those that possessed at least one Fantasy Breed, and they were also A-rank spirit qi professionals. Only such experts could be known as king-class experts.","A king-class expert was no longer determined by just a spirit qi professional rank or fey’s strength—it was the combination of both factors. There were plenty of spirit qi professionals who were A-rank but didn’t possess Fantasy Breed feys. Therefore, they weren’t considered to be king-class experts.","As for those heavenly prodigies, like the members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence, they possessed Fantasy Breed feys, but their spirit qi professional rank wasn’t at A-rank yet. Therefore, they weren’t considered king-class experts either.","King-class experts were considered the top few experts in the Radiance Federation, and such experts weren’t that easy to invite. In addition, the rarest kind of king-class experts were healing-type ones.","In the Radiance Federation, the ratio of combat-class spirit qi professionals and healing-type spirit qi professionals was always 150:1. The ratio wasn’t as exaggerated among the king-class individuals, but the number of king-class healing-type experts was still less than 1/20 of king-class combat-class experts.","As for White Devil, a core member of the Extreme Guild Club’s S Tournament official team, according to her true combat strength, she might not even be top 30. White Devil was Sequence #18 of the Radiance Hundred because she was a healing-type spirit qi professional, so her strategic significance was far beyond her combat significance.","Moreover, even if a king-class healer was invited, each king-class healer possessed different types of Fantasy Breed feys. Each of those healing-type Fantasy Breed feys would have different abilities and exclusive skills, so the healing methods were different too.","Some king-class healers were adept at eliminating poison, and some others were adept at healing mental damage. But in the Radiance Federation, Xin Ying had never heard of a king-class healer with a Fantasy Breed that could regrow a person’s limbs.","Furthermore, even if there was such a king-class healer, and if the Extreme Guild Club was able to pay such a huge price, would they really be able to invite such a king-class healer?","Tan Ran and Lu Pinru were now attacking the injured Heart-Penetrating Ironline, which was smashed by Xin Ying’s all-out attack. However, Tan Ran and Lu Pinru were still looking at Zhang Xiaobai with eyes of unspeakable concern.","All of a sudden, Tan Ran yelled furiously, “Lava Hippopotamus, use Lava Bomb!”","A scorching lava sphere was shot out of the Lava Hippopotamus’ mouth and smashed onto the already injured Heart-Penetrating Ironline. It instantly burned the Heart-Penetrating Ironline and turned it into charcoal.","Tan Ran’s voice carried a sobbing sound, while Lu Pinru’s eyes were reddened.","Zhang Xiaobai was in such pain that his teeth were chattering. He was watching Xin Ying kneeling down and crying for him. He put in great effort to let out a simple smile. “Xin Ying, my arm is severed now. In the future, I will be a cripple. Are you willing to take care of me?”"]},{"number":145,"title":"Chapter 145: Miracle at Millstone Town","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Zhang Xiaobai originally wanted to tease Xin Ying and stop her crying, but he didn’t expect Xin Ying to actually cry even more intensively.","Zhang Xiaobai was shocked and immediately said, “Don’t, don’t, don’t cry. I don’t need you to take care of me! Look at how afraid you are!”","Xin Ying stood up and disregarded everything to rush over and hug Zhang Xiaobai. Xin Ying’s actions gave Zhang Xiaobai so much pain that he was grimacing.","All of a sudden, Zhang Xiaobai heard Xin Ying saying softly, “I will take care of you for life! In fact, my Star Web Card’s password has been your birthday since a long time ago!”","The pain had already numbed Zhang Xiaobai, and when accompanied by the loss of blood, he couldn’t continue standing anymore. Had it not been for Xin Ying supporting him, he would have collapsed on the ground.","But after hearing Xin Ying’s gentle voice, Zhang Xiaobai’s originally pale face had a little color of blood. He felt as though his arm wasn’t in as much pain anymore.","The Millstone Town’s Guild Alliance branch president stood by the side and didn’t know what he should say. A young elite from the S tournament reserve team of a B-level guild club was going to be crippled for the rest of his life just because he protected Millstone Town from the dimensional rift that had suddenly opened.","Plenty of spirit qi professionals who had fought alongside Zhang Xiaobai had red eyes too. Everyone started killing alien insects at a speed that was more than two times the original, pouring all of their respect and worry into the insect tide.","Lin Yuan took a deep breath and stopped supplying spiritual power to Red Thorn. The flesh-like flower above Red Thorn’s Mouth of Relinquish stopped releasing new spores.","Lin Yuan looked at the thriving sea of flowers. It was already enough to repel the alien insects. A huge quantity of child ramets had consumed the alien insect flesh and had already evolved into Elite ramets.","Given the massive numbers of Elite ramets, there wasn’t a need for more spores to enlarge the size of the sea of flowers as this insect tide had already lost all of its Class 3 alien insects.","Lin Yuan could feel that his Spirit Qi Imprint was already reaching the bottom, and he took another glance at the people that were in battle. He then looked at Zhang Xiaobai and his severed arm.","Without any hesitation, Lin Yuan took a deep breath and activated Jasmine Lily’s exclusive skill, which he had never activated before, Recovery Imprint. All of a sudden, the totem pattern of a Jasmine Lily appeared on Lin Yuan’s forehead once he activated Recovery Imprint.","The Jasmine Lily totem was radiating bright light on Lin Yuan’s forehead. The massive healing energy from the Recovery Imprint was channeled into the Fantasy Breed Jasmine Lily. All of a sudden, the Jasmine Lily burst out with a flourishing light of recovery.","Lin Yuan used up all of his remaining spirit qi within the Spirit Qi Imprint. The top flower of the Jasmine Lily sprayed out with healing green light, releasing the massive amount of healing energy that was accumulated in the Recovery Imprint.","The green spots of light that were formed by Heal were transmitted to each spirit qi professional on the field.","Everyone on the battlefield was already severely exhausted, be it in stamina or energy. They were now immersed in the healing green light and were having a nice and comfortable dream.","The light’s green spots weren’t bright nor resplendent, but the mild light was filled with exuberant vitality. They were just like the fireflies that would fly out with the breeze during February.","The fireflies were swirling and dancing in the wind. Each and every spirit qi professional was engrossed in their sweet dreams, giving all of the injured and exhausted spirit qi professionals the most comfortable treatment. Even if they were severely injured, their injuries would be quickly recovered when the healing spots of light flowed down. Even their mental state would be at the prime.","At this moment, Lin Yuan controlled the Jasmine Lily’s topmost flower to shoot out a green light that was as thick as a thumb.","The green light was like a spiritual snake that dove into Zhang Xiaobai’s body, instantly relieving his pain significantly. When nourished by this surging vitality, Zhang Xiaobai felt as though all his weakness and fatigue were wiped away.","All of a sudden, Zhang Xiaobai felt an extremely itchy feeling from the area of his severed arm. He turned to look and widened his eyes as he realized his arm was regrowing.","Everyone, including Xin Ying, was shocked by this miraculous event that happened in front of their eyes. This was all credited to the Jasmine Lily’s exclusive skill that had been awakened when evolving into a Fantasy Breed—Severed Limbs Growth.","Lin Yuan knew that the Jasmine Lily’s exclusive skill, Severed Limbs Growth, could regrow severed limbs, but he didn’t think that regrowing a single severed arm would actually use up so much healing energy and spirit qi.","Once Zhang Xiaobai’s arm was completely regrown, Lin Yuan realized that all of the healing energy that had been accumulated in the Recovery Imprint for a few months was all used up. In addition, Lin Yuan’s spirit qi was also completely exhausted. Had it not been for Red Thorn’s vine still holding onto his wrist, Lin Yuan wouldn’t have been able to continue standing.","At that moment, there was a dawn of light at the horizon of the grey night sky. The sudden emergence of the dawn’s radiance outlined the silhouette of the distant mountains. It eliminated the cold air of the autumn night, and at the same time, a corner of darkness had been taken away.","When the light of dawn illuminated the youth wearing the silver mask, it made the youth look rather weak as his spirit qi was exhausted. The youth’s figure set off a contrast with the huge sea of flowers and the insect tide that was still trying to push back the sea of flowers. This light of dawn elongated the youth’s figure and also lit up a miracle under the heavenly dome of Millstone Town.","This youth created this miracle, but the miracle belonged to him and all the spirit qi professionals that were fighting outside of Millstone Town. At the same time, this miracle belonged to the Radiance.","This miracle made everyone in Millstone Town look at this silver-masked youth with flabbergasted eyes. Their eyes were filled with amazement, gratitude, respect, and an unconcealed fanaticism.","The boundless sea of flowers and thousands of life-saving green light spots were engraved into the minds of all the spirit qi professionals in Millstone Town.","Zhang Xiaobai suddenly rushed toward Lin Yuan and yelled, “Black! You are really my lucky star!”","Zhang Xiaobai was definitely the person with the most excited and surging emotions.","When Zhang Xiaobai’s arm was severed, he had already helplessly accepted the reality. However, he didn’t expect that Lin Yuan would allow his arm to regrow, and it was definitely a favor of giving another life. This was definitely a miracle for Zhang Xiaobai that rescued the second half of his life.","When Zhang Xiaobai rushed over, Red Thorn immediately assumed a defensive stance, but Lin Yuan quickly stopped it.","Just as Lin Yuan thought he was going to receive the impact from Zhang Xiaobai’s bear hug, he didn’t expect the three other members of the Extreme Guild Club to rush over too.","Xin Ying’s eyes were tearing up, but she was smiling with an abnormally radiant expression. After seeing Zhang Xiaobai’s regrown arm, droplets of salty tears rolled down the bridge of her nose. They weren’t tears of sorrow, but tears of joy.","The trio and Zhang Xiaobai could already see that Lin Yuan’s spirit qi was exhausted, and he was struggling to stand.","Therefore, Zhang Xiaobai, Xin Ying, Lu Pinru, and Tan Ran hugged Lin Yuan from all four directions so that Lin Yuan didn’t have to support his body alone.","This hug was particularly warm in the chilly autumn’s dawn.","This was a hug from comrade-in-arms that experienced life and death together."]},{"number":146,"title":"Chapter 146: The Puzzled Handsome Young Man","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","The Millstone Town people felt the joy brought by surviving the calamity and this hearty victory.","The insect tide that was constantly pouring into the sea of flowers was no longer a threat to the town.","Given the sea of flowers’ numerous Elite ramets, the alien insects served to act as flower fertilizer and nutrition to them.","In addition, the Millstone Town people were now in their best condition thanks to Lin Yuan’s Fantasy Breed Jasmine Lily.","Even if those Class 1 and Class 2 alien insects struggled in the sea of flowers, they were soon killed in an orderly manner.","Just as they had stabilized the insect tide, a little red spider lying on the leaf-shaped Diamond fey storage box on Lin Yuan’s chest jumped, as though it was one with the fey storage box. It jumped into the pinnacle Class 1 alien insect dimensional rift.","When the Mother of Bloodbath leaped toward the pinnacle Class 1 alien insect dimensional rift, it looked at Lin Yuan and sent a voice transmission. “Not bad, kid. You’re worthy of being the Moon Empress’s disciple. Since you held off the insect tide, I’m going to get you the source-type item in this dimensional rift as my reward to you.”","The Mother of Bloodbath had actually previously made preparations to save Lin Yuan in the sea of insects when it devoured all the people.","After all, in the Mother of Bloodbath’s opinion, the insect tide from such a pinnacle Class 1 alien insect dimensional rift was simply not something that these thousand or so uncoordinated people could resist against.","As Lin Yuan’s Path Protector, the Mother of Bloodbath wanted to let him understand through this matter that, no matter what, he should not easily get himself involved in such perilous situations.","This was also the way of its survival, engraved in its bones as a fey. Feys lived in nature and faced all kinds of threats all the time at a young age. They might lose their lives if they were not careful.","Life was the root of everything. Without one’s life, how could they bother about anything else?","How would Lin Yuan not know the principle of ‘A wise man foresees danger and hides himself’?","But sometimes, some beliefs must be adhered to.","Moreover, Lin Yuan knew that he still had a Path Protector like the Mother of Bloodbath as his trump card. In fact, the Mother of Bloodbath’s prediction had not been wrong, but it had not taken a variable like Lin Yuan into consideration. Lin Yuan had taught the Mother of Bloodbath, a Suzerain/Myth I fey, a lesson.","The Mother of Bloodbath had seen that Lin Yuan’s Red Thorn was a Bronze lifeform grown from a Source Seed, while that healing-type fey that had healed everyone was a Silver/Fantasy Breed fey.","However, the Mother of Bloodbath did not attribute the success of everything to Lin Yuan. It speculated that it was a trump card that the Moon Empress had given to her disciple.","It had never thought that even the Moon Empress was unclear of Lin Yuan’s strength. This was entirely because Lin Yuan relied on his own ability and grew up step by step.","When the Mother of Bloodbath headed to the pinnacle Class 1 alien insect dimensional rift, Lin Yuan was finally relieved. He quickly let Blackie release its skill, Spirit Injection, on him. After that, Lin Yuan finally got rid of the feeling of powerlessness that his spiritual power’s exhaustion brought.","At that moment, Zhang Xiaobai laughed and patted Lin Yuan’s shoulder before he said, “It’s now dawn. Several hours have passed since this dimensional rift opened. Even if Millstone Town is located at the border, the Ascending Dragon City should have noticed it. Therefore, the Ascending Dragon Guards will come here to bring this pinnacle Class 1 alien insect dimensional rift to an end.”","Tan Ran also let out a deep breath and said, “We can finally remove this burden.”","Xin Ying looked at Zhang Xiaobai, who had a strange smile and looked improper, and felt her fist itching again. She swung her fist hard at him, causing him to rub his stomach in grievance and say, “Hey, you said you’d take care of me previously! Say it! Say it! When did you change your Star Web Card’s password to my birthday? How come I didn’t know?”","Xin Ying did not expect Zhang Xiaobai to shout out her private words just like that. Furious, she swung her fist hard and mastered a deadly rhythm. As a result, Zhang Xiaobai shouted for help. While Xin Ying swung her fist hard, her face was secretly flushing.","Tan Ran could not help but say, “Big Brother Xiaobai, you are always messing with Sister Xin. Do you like the feeling of pain and pleasure?”","When Lu Pinru heard Tan Ran’s words, she felt somewhat helpless. It seemed that she could not let Tan Ran surf the Star Web with Zhang Xiaobai or read that strange book anymore.","Unexpectedly, she made a rare joke. “Tan Ran, if you want to experience the feeling of pain and pleasure, I can lock you in my closet.”","Tan Ran was puzzled.","Lin Yuan also revealed a handsome young man’s puzzled expression.","Zhang Xiaobai was rubbing his stomach when he heard Lu Pinru’s words. “Lu Pinru, you can’t hide liking someone!” he shouted.","Lu Pinru was puzzled.","“Because your future husband will still find you, even if you hide in the closet.”","Lu Pinru, Tan Ran, and Lin Yuan were puzzled.","Xin Ying rolled her eyes at Zhang Xiaobai. “It seems that I hit you lightly just now. Zhang Xiaobai, don’t run away if you can!”","Lu Pinru wiped the beads of sweat on her forehead that she could not wipe during the battle and said to Lin Yuan, “It was all thanks to you this time, Black! If it wasn’t for you, none of us would have survived.”","She sounded very solemn as she looked at the Millstone Town people, who were showing smiles on their faces as the sea of flowers was blocking the insect tide.","She was very glad that Lin Yuan had applied to form a temporary squad with them, and they had accepted him as well.","At that moment, the pinnacle Class 1 dimensional rift, where alien insects were constantly falling from, suddenly distorted and returned to normal, as though the sky had broken like a mirror.","That dark-red pinnacle Class 1 dimensional rift completely vanished, as if it had never appeared.","Before this dimensional rift disappeared, a small red spider, which was about one centimeter in size and carved like a crystal, appeared on Lin Yuan’s leaf-shaped Diamond fey storage box.","The Mother of Bloodbath’s strange yet very pleasant voice sounded, but it seemed to contain a hint of disdain. “You’ve really hit the jackpot with the source-type item inside the pinnacle Class 1 alien insect dimensional rift. There’s actually such a compatible source-type item. This item is not for you, but that Source Seed plant of yours.”","The Mother of Bloodbath babbled and sounded so sour, as though she had eaten a cartload of limes.","Lin Yuan chuckled. He would simply welcome any praises to an uber-lucky person like him! It just felt too awesome!"]},{"number":147,"title":"Chapter 147: Quality Upgrade","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Dimensional rifts had undoubtedly all sorts of source-type items. The source-type items had no exact strength or weakness in terms of ability. They were either compatible or incompatible, and sometimes, it was even up to how one would use them in the future.","It was just like the Source Seed that Lin Yuan had produced Red Thorn from. The Radiance Federation’s Scholars had once identified Source Seeds as one of the most useless source-type items. But in Lin Yuan’s hands, Red Thorn had perfectly stopped the pinnacle Class 1 insect tide based on its exclusive skill.","There were too many types of source-type items, and it had only been over 100 years since the Radiance Federation’s Spirit Qi Awakening.","Although many dimensional rifts had opened, there were still a huge amount of source-type items that remained unique to this day.","Each spirit qi professional had a different route to pairing with and choosing their feys. Therefore, it was very much a matter of luck to find the right one among the random source-type items in the dimensional rifts.","The feys’ contracts all depended on the spirit qi professional’s spiritual energy, but not the Source Seed. Although everyone’s spiritual energy differed, there was a limit to their spiritual energy. The contract of a Source Seed might likely not occupy their spiritual energy. This was undoubtedly akin to having an extra contracted fey spot.","A source-type item that did not occupy one’s spiritual energy was an excellent choice for Lin Yuan, whose spiritual energy was almost completely occupied by Morbius. However, a Source Seed that did not occupy one’s spiritual energy might also have more demanding requirements. For example, Cheng Rui’s Spine Gu would require a spine and harm the contractor’s roots.","Source-type items were so precious that they rarely circulated even in Star Web’s Treasure Pavilion. This was because even if any source-type items were not applicable, most experts with source-type items would choose to keep them and not sell them easily.","Besides going into the dimensional rifts to obtain the source-type items, they could only be obtained by exchanging with the Radiance Federation’s merits.","Most of the transactions between individuals for source-type items were through bartering—exchanging it with another source-type item.","It was difficult to go into a dimensional rift and obtain the source-type items.","When the pinnacle Class 1 alien insect dimensional rift opened, although only three Class 3 alien insects had descended because of the rift’s energy, there were many Class 3 alien insects in a pinnacle Class 1 alien insect dimensional rift. The sea of insects inside would keep pouring out of the rift, mostly because they had been squeezed out by the other alien insects inside.","One could imagine how perilous it was inside such a dimensional rift.","Only a Suzerain/Legend I fey like the Mother of Bloodbath could easily obtain a source-type item from a pinnacle Class 1 dimensional rift.","Otherwise, even a king-class expert would at least need to form a squad to take down the world inside the dimensional rift and obtain the source-type item.","Lin Yuan did not bother to check out exactly what the source-type item the Mother of Bloodbath had taken from the rift or why it had said it was suitable for Red Thorn.","Instead, he stored the source-type item, which looked like a translucent thumb-sized insect egg, in the Diamond fey storage box. Lin Yuan thought that this was not a good time to study this newly-acquired source-type item.","At that moment, many sharp chirping sounds from large avian feys came from the sky.","Soon, these sharp chirping sounds approached.","Lin Yuan looked over and recognized that the hundreds of avian feys were Gold Blade-Winged Feathered Eagles.","On the back of each Gold Blade-Winged Feathered Eagle stood a spirit qi professional with armor engraved with dragon-species fey patterns.","These people who suddenly arrived on the Blade-Winged Feathered Eagles were none other than the Ascending Dragon Guards from the Ascending Dragon City under the famous city lord.","The pinnacle Class 1 dimensional rift had vanished from the sky, as though no new alien insects would appear.","The remaining alien insects were swallowed by the sea of flowers and could no longer be healed, just like stagnant water.","Soon, these alien insects were more or less gone.","When the Ascending Dragon Guards saw that the sea of flowers had devoured the insect tide in Millstone Town, they could not help but widen their mouths one by one.","In particular, the Ascending Dragon Guards’ leader felt that the scene before him was surreal.","But when he saw the intact Millstone Town, he could not help but start laughing.","His peals of laughter were full of joy, with his worries dissipated.","When the Ascending Dragon Guards had received news that a pinnacle Class 1 dimensional rift had opened outside Millstone Town, they had immediately gathered two large teams and headed to the town without a moment’s delay.","Their only wish on the way there was for their Gold Blade-Winged Feathered Eagles to fly faster.","A pinnacle Class 1 dimensional rift was no joke at all. They had thought that Millstone Town might have become a paradise for the alien insects. However, when they finally arrived, they realized that it was intact and had managed to protect itself.","The Ascending Dragon Guards were somewhat curious about where the pinnacle Class 1 dimensional rift had gone. If they had not seen the traces of battle outside Millstone Town, they would probably not believe that a pinnacle Class 1 dimensional rift had opened there.","However, the Ascending Dragon Guards did not really care much about these. After all, their goal was to save Millstone Town. The other departments of the Ascending Dragon City would settle the matters afterward.","The Ascending Dragon Guards’ leader looked at the situation at hand and could not help but touch his big bald head.","They probably had to return without success as that strange sea of flowers had nearly devoured all the insect tide.","Lin Yuan would undoubtedly benefit the most from this dimensional rift. Not only had he obtained a source-type item from it, but his Red Thorn’s child ramets and ramets had nearly devoured this insect tide, and hence gave Red Thorn a huge amount of flesh energy, allowing its quality to upgrade.","Lin Yuan had always been suppressing Red Thorn’s grade and let it upgrade its quality first.","After devouring the vast amounts of flesh energy, Red Thorn had jumped from Normal to Elite and Flawless.","Upon seeing that the Ascending Dragon City’s Ascending Dragon Guards had taken over the situation outside Millstone Town, Lin Yuan knew that Red Thorn’s sea of flowers Red was no longer needed.","He then ordered Red Thorn to deal with the child ramets and ramets.","Upon receiving Lin Yuan’s order, Red Thorn’s roots danced and siphoned all the energy from the child ramets and ramets.","Many Normal child ramets and Elite ramets instantly withered, and they transferred all their energy to Red Thorn’s body through the connected root system.","Red Thorn trembled violently before this withering sea of flowers, and Lin Yuan could clearly feel that it had grown much stronger than before. Its Mouth of Relinquish had become even bigger, and the barbs on its vines had become sharper and longer. Red Thorn had evolved from Flawless to Epic.","The pinnacle Class 1 dimensional rift’s insects had nearly all become sacrifices to the Red Thorn’s Mouth of Relinquish.","Thanks to the insects frantically presenting themselves, Red Thorn’s quality underwent a transformation!"]},{"number":148,"title":"Chapter 148: He Had Always Been Unfettered","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Lin Yuan had always been frustrated about upgrading Red Thorn’s quality, but he did not expect this insect tide to solve his problem.","Now that Red Thorn had reached Epic, it could only devour dimensional lifeforms’ flesh and work hard to accumulate if it were to reach Legend.","Although time passed without a trace, time could solve many problems.","Xin Ying suddenly said to Lin Yuan softly, “The Ascending Dragon City’s Ascending Dragon Guards have taken charge of the situation and will be responsible for the Millstone Town people. Let’s leave now. Otherwise, when Ascending Dragon City’s reporters arrive here and find us for an interview, we won’t be able to leave within a day or two.” She suddenly paused and did not continue, as she knew that it was a slip of her tongue.","If a person who had resisted against the pinnacle Class 1 insect tide alone and protected a small town were to accept the Star Web’s interview, they would undoubtedly become famous and gain widespread attention.","Xin Ying never cared about this because in such a situation, even though guarding Millstone Town was an unwise choice—it was a splendid choice.","In her opinion, if one wanted to be famous, they had to improve their strength and fight it out in the S Tournament.","Even though Xin Ying, who knew the world’s ways, had long recognized Lin Yuan as her friend, she felt awkward because she had unintentionally helped Lin Yuan grab the attention.","Zhang Xiaobai did not think like this. He put his arms around Lin Yuan’s shoulders and said, “Hahaha! We should just go quickly! Otherwise, we won’t be able to leave a while later!”","Xin Ying wanted to pull Zhang Xiaobai, but Lin Yuan said softly, “The Endless Forest is up ahead. Let’s hit the road! Wasn’t our original plan to set out early in the morning to collect the Jade Unicorn Ice Snake venom?”","Lin Yuan’s words were faint yet contained an indescribable refreshment and straightforwardness. He had never been a person who cared about fame and fortune.","On the contrary, after living two lives, Lin Yuan looked at everything dialectically and focused on things he truly cared about.","In a world where strength was highly respected—although fame and fortune could not be equated with strength—having strength was akin to having fame and fortune.","If strength were to be compared to flowers, while fame and fortune as butterflies, then the butterflies would naturally come when the flowers bloomed.","The Radiance Hundred Sequence was Lin Yuan’s next best choice. A real man’s choice was to speak with strength.","Lin Yuan looked at the blazing sun that arrived with the dawn. The warm light emanating from the blazing sun seemed to be more conspicuous than it had been at noon.","At that moment, there was a subtle spiritual fluctuation on Lin Yuan’s body that not even Zhang Xiaobai, who had his hands on Lin Yuan’s shoulder, felt.","The Mother of Bloodbath lying in the leaf-shaped fey storage box moved gently and felt even more jealous. “This kid is really uber lucky. He has comprehended a Willpower Rune after sensing my Law Rune!”","However, the Mother of Bloodbath thought about it and felt that since Lin Yuan already had a Fantasy Breed Jasmine Lily, this Willpower Rune should be his second one.","The Mother of Bloodbath believed that Lin Yuan had comprehended this Willpower Rune because when it became his Path Protector, it had allowed him to sense the energy in the Law Rune.","Naturally, it had something to do with him sensing the Mother of Bloodbath’s Law Rune back then, but if it knew that Lin Yuan had comprehended the fourth Willpower Rune, it would have been so jealous that its name would become the Mother of Jealousy.","The clearest light of the morning sun seemed to have risen in Lin Yuan’s eyes, and a twilight-like Willpower Rune appeared in his spiritual world.","When Lin Yuan comprehended this rune, he thought that it was perfect for Chimey.","Lin Yuan looked at the gradually rising morning sun, and his face behind the mask suddenly revealed a smile that no one saw but was enough to overshadow the blazing sun.","He was a youth that had always been taking fragmented footsteps with sooty air while in a weak state—stumbling, standing, and running.","Whether it was seeking survival at his lowest point in life or being calm at his highest point, he had never forgotten the epiphany in his heart.","The warm light had dispersed the last bit of sooty air in his fragmented footsteps.","And he, as someone who had lived two lives, had always been unfettered.","When Xin Ying, Zhang Xiaobai, Lu Pinru, and Tan Ran heard Lin Yuan’s refreshing and straightforward words, they could not help but wear a smile on their faces.","Those with favorable impressions of each other would become friends after interactions. After experiencing life and death together, they were comrades. Since their interests were completely similar in such a situation, they were bosom friends.","Zhang Xiaobai gave Lin Yuan a thumbs-up and said, “Lin Yuan, you were so cool when you said that.”","Lin Yuan could not help but laugh upon seeing Zhang Xiaobai’s actions and strange expressions.","Was it cool? Maybe!","Actually, those who were themselves were the coolest at any moment!","Lu Pinru rolled her eyes at Zhang Xiaobai. “Can you stop showing the results of you learning weird facial expressions in cram school!” Xin Ying felt helpless as she looked at Zhang Xiaobai.","After last year’s S Tournament, they had a month of vacation, and she had wanted to go on a vacation together as a team. However, Zhang Xiaobai had gone to enroll in classes teaching weird facial expressions, wanting to learn a specialty.","Zhang Xiaobai felt grieved and pursed his lips before saying, “Is it wrong to learn a specialty?”","Lin Yuan could not help but ask, “Is there such a thing as learning weird facial expressions as a specialty?”","Zhang Xiaobai felt even more grieved and blinked his eyes. “I’ve got a certificate in that!”","Lin Yuan and the Extreme Guild Club’s quartet quietly left Millstone Town and headed to the Endless Forest, where the morning rays were shining at.","Actually, they did not know that the people present had taken their departure seriously.","One of them had guarded Millstone Town under the pinnacle Class 1 insect tide and healed everyone during the most critical moment.","In the eyes of everyone, Lin Yuan’s grace of saving them had made it difficult for the people outside Millstone Town, who had experienced the killings, to take their eyes off Lin Yuan.","When Lin Yuan and the quartet left, the Ascending Dragon Guards’ leader, the Millstone Town’s Guild Alliance branch president, and everyone in Millstone Town stood there quietly, gazing sincerely as they watched their heroes leave.","This was the heroes’ choice. Heroes would always help those in need but leave so easily, unwilling to leave their names behind.","The Millstone Town’s Guild Alliance branch president felt that the morning sun was particularly bright during dawn. For some reason, be it the bright sun shining on his eyes or his aroused feelings, tears streamed down his face as he softly spat out the words—”Outstanding youths.”","Upon hearing that, the bald man leading the Ascending Dragon Guards looked in the direction where Lin Yuan and the others had left with a solemn expression and said while bowing, “They’re more than outstanding youths. This is the spirit and backbone of radiance.”"]},{"number":149,"title":"Chapter 149: Come, Keyboard! The Birth of Ancestor Peace Berserker!","paragraphs":["The mountains and waters were in serenity, while the birds, beasts, fish, and insects were all resting. As they were walking in the Endless Forest, Lin Yuan felt that the air he could smell was particularly refreshing.","It was refreshing not because of the spirit qi concentration but the fragrance from the plants and soil that pervaded the Endless Forest’s air.","At that moment, Lin Yuan noticed a thumb-sized dragonfly that was only a birch, close to 20 centimeters in height. The dragonfly was completely red, and its wings were light green. From this dragonfly’s appearance, Lin Yuan could guess that it was a Normal Mist Flame Dragonfly that had just been born.","The Mist Flame Dragonfly was an extremely rare fey with great potential. Along the way, Lin Yuan had encountered plenty of Normal and Elite feys, but the Mist Flame Dragonfly had the best aptitude among them all.","A fey’s aptitude didn’t indicate its grade, but instead the potential during the evolution process. The Mist Flame Dragonfly was a dual-type fey that had great potential in both wind and fire. If it underwent a spiritual mutation, it would be considered rather powerful among the offense-type feys that could use the wind and fire energy.","Wind could enhance fire, so wind was always fire’s best companion.","Since Lin Yuan spotted this Mist Flame Dragonfly that had a great aptitude, he naturally wasn’t going to miss out on it.","He carefully approached the Mist Flame Dragonfly. When his palm was still a certain distance away, he quickly circulated his spirit qi and allowed the Mist Flame Dragonfly to feel the pure spirit qi that was coming out of his palm.","Lin Yuan only released pure spirit qi for a split moment. The Mist Flame Dragonfly immediately flew over because it felt the split moment of spirit qi release. At that moment, the Mist Flame Dragonfly was already obediently standing on Lin Yuan’s fingertip. It wasn’t afraid of humans, and it was actually flapping its wings gently, as though it was appealing to Lin Yuan to release more spirit qi.","This scene stunned the Extreme Guild Club’s quartet. They had seen other Creation Masters harvesting in the wild, but none of them had such an easy time to develop a good relationship with wild feys.","Zhang Xiaobai suddenly muttered, “Is a handsome appearance able to make feys have a favorable impression of you? If that’s the case, all of Endless Forest’s feys should be surrounding me!”","Xin Ying couldn’t help holding her forehead. Even though it was very satisfying to hit Zhang Xiaobai, it was rather tiring to always do so. Therefore, Xin Ying took a katar out of her bag and equipped it. Zhang Xiaobai became obedient instantly.","Meanwhile, Lin Yuan stored this Normal Mist Flame Dragonfly in the fey storage box.","The group continued on their way and walked for a few hours until it was noon.","Lin Yuan had already caught several feys with potential in the wild. If he nurtured them, he would be able to nurture some of the powerful feys that were hard to obtain.","During lunch, everyone sat on the ground and ate the rations that Lu Pinru had prepared. While Zhang Xiaobai was eating, he was chattering, “I should have bought a few dozen kidneys in the morning. It would definitely be satisfying and delicious to eat them right now!”","Xin Ying glared at Zhang Xiaobai and waved the katar on her hand. He immediately rephrased. “I mean that I would have energy after eating all the kidneys. Otherwise, how would I be able to stand in front of all of you and block the damage?”","Lu Pinru involuntarily rolled her eyes at Zhang Xiaobai and said, “You are just a gluttonous freak. You are cheap!”","Zhang Xiaobai wasn’t going to take such criticisms. “Is the kidney not fattening enough? Is the kidney not delicious enough?! Why can’t I be gluttonous over it!?”","Lin Yuan had removed his mask when they entered the Endless Forest and was enjoying the rations now. When he noticed that everyone was almost done with the rations, he flipped his hand and brought out the fruits that he had bought and stored within the leaf-shaped fey storage box.","Upon seeing the fruits, Zhang Xiaobai immediately chucked the rations to the side and started munching on the fruits. The slightly sour but sweet flesh of the fruit in his mouth made Zhang Xiaobai think, What satisfaction! My life is at the pinnacle!","When adventuring in the wild with a Creation Master, the team’s chances of getting attacked by wild feys were greatly reduced. Lin Yuan and the Extreme Guild Club’s quartet had been attacked a few times earlier, but with Xin Ying and Tan Ran as the main attackers, Zhang Xiaobai as the main defense, Lu Pinru as support, and Lin Yuan as the healer, the battles were quickly ended.","At the same time, Lin Yuan and the Extreme Guild Club’s quartet had obtained plenty of fresh spiritual ingredients.","As they were treading through the Endless Forest, Zhang Xiaobai had a sudden flash of inspiration and asked everyone with a mysterious face, “‘Women giving birth...’ Give me a saying!”","Xin Ying, Lu Pinru, and Tan Ran couldn’t be bothered to respond. Therefore, Zhang Xiaobai quickly turned to look at Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan looked at Zhang Xiaobai’s expectant eyes and pondered before saying, “Wishing for death more than to live.”","Zhang Xiaobai seemed as though he already expected Lin Yuan’s answer. He laughed heartily and said, “It should be spitting blood.”","Lin Yuan also revealed a handsomely puzzled expression. He didn’t have many friends in this life as he had been struggling to survive previously, so he didn’t have many chances to make friends, either.","Lin Yuan had always felt that the friendship between gentlemen would be indifferent but pure like water. Nonetheless, after many interactions with Zhang Xiaobai, he felt that such silly conversations actually made Lin Yuan feel it was particularly interesting.","The collection of the Jade Unicorn Ice Snake’s venom was easy for Lin Yuan and the Extreme Guild Club’s quartet. At the same time, Lin Yuan had also discovered a few fish in the cold pond the Jade Unicorn Ice Snake resided.","When Lin Yuan saw the small fish, he immediately recognized the species. He didn’t think that such a place would have such great feys. Lin Yuan was planning to nurture these few fish carefully after bringing them back.","Lin Yuan quickly placed the few fish in a vessel filled with the pond’s water and carefully stored it inside the Diamond fey storage box.","Lin Yuan’s harvest was also considered to have officially ended now. He might not have gathered a large number of feys, but each of them was considered exquisite, especially the three fish in the cold pond—they were considered superior.","On the way back, Lin Yuan wasn’t planning to return to the Royal Capital along with the Extreme Guild Club’s quartet. Before returning to the Royal Capital, Lin Yuan was planning to visit Chu Ci in Redbud City’s Redbud Intermediate Spirit Qi Academy.","At the same time, the Normal Earth Powder Butterfly that had hatched from the cocoon had already evolved into a Bronze Vajra Butterfly. He was going to give it to Chu Ci for her second contracted fey. Also, Lin Yuan had reserved the Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar for Chu Ci.","Lin Yuan was planning for Chu Ci to consume the nectar as it was able to refine her body constitution and cleanse the impurities. It was better for Chu Ci to consume it as early as possible.","Lin Yuan and the quartet exchanged contact information and arranged to have a small gathering once they all returned to the Royal Capital. As such, Lin Yuan and the quartet parted ways at Ascending Dragon City.","Immediately after, Lin Yuan spent a huge amount of Radiance dollars to call for a Platinum Divine Travel Black Swallow. This fey had the fastest speed among all avian transportation feys in the Radiance Federation, so its ‘Divine Travel’ name was truly fitting.","Lin Yuan had called for the Divine Travel Black Swallow because Ascending Dragon City and Redbud City were too far apart. Back then, even Ling Xiao’s Fantasy Breed Blue Jade Pegasus had taken several days just to fly from Redbud City to the Royal Capital.","If Lin Yuan were to ride on a Silver fey and fly from Ascending Dragon City to Redbud City, by the time he arrived, Chu Ci would have already ended her school term, which was over two months from now.","Lin Yuan, who was riding on the Divine Travel Black Swallow, still didn’t know that his identity, Black, had already become famous in the Star Web. He might not have accepted any interviews from Star Web reporters, but all of Millstone Town’s combatants could attest to Black’s prowess.","The Star Web reporters that had arrived after the incident had roughly sketched Black’s image and abilities. Millstone Town’s combatants had provided the description, of course.","Previously, no one had actually thought that Black’s fey was a Fantasy Breed. After all, a Silver/Fantasy Breed was too shocking. However, after research and discussions among the Star Web reporters and Class 3 Scholars that were also contacted—along with the description of how Black’s Silver healing-type fey was able to regrow limbs—they finally concluded that Black’s healing-type fey was a Silver/Fantasy Breed.","The Radiance Federation was a nation that worshiped heroes. Thus, Black’s status started to become famous on the Star Web. There was even a dedicated forum and fan club on the Star Web.","The Star Web forum and fan club for Black was created by none other than the healing-type spirit qi professional who possessed the Bronze Spitting Turtledove. In addition, almost everyone from Millstone Town, including the Guild Alliance branch president, had joined Black’s forum and fan club.","There were also plenty of people that joined because of Black’s achievements, strengthening Black’s forum and fan club significantly. Of course, there were plenty of jealous people too.","Liu Lang, the healer with the Bronze Spitting Turtledove, was currently flaming back at the Star Web haters. When someone tried to criticize his idol and savior, Black, it really infuriated Liu Lang.","A prodigious hero like Black is someone you can criticize?","Liu Lang couldn’t help cursing. “These haters are really disgusting. They swallow their pride and don’t dare to humiliate others in reality, but they are not holding back in the Star Web. Casually ridiculing others without any regard. For such haters, I, Liu Lang, shall not be courteous!”","Liu Lang had a stern expression as he chanted:","Heaven doesn’t give birth to me, the Keyboard Warrior!","My flaming skills are as great as the long night!","Pinnacle of the immortal realm, and looking down at the mortal realm!","With my keyboard, there is heaven!","I am suppressing the enemies for the Keyboard God!","Who would dare to say they are invincible in this world?","Who would dare to say they would never be defeated!?","The keyboard has materialized into my heart!","The keyboard of heaven is arriving!","Receiving no replies after a waterfall of typed words!","I will wait until the Yin and Yang cross over!","I will take down the clear sky with my demonic keyboard!","The world shall turn into a keyboard! Come, keyboard!","Because Liu Lang’s Star Web name was ‘Ancestor Peace’, after his amazing ‘poem’, his name had also become famous and was given the title of—”Ancestor Peace Berserker”."]},{"number":150,"title":"Chapter 150: Acid Corrosion Queen Bee","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Lin Yuan sat on the back of the Divine Travel Black Swallow and couldn’t help criticizing. It would be fine if it wasn’t comfortable to ride on the Divine Travel Black Swallow—the crucial thing was because it was hard on the butt.","The Divine Travel Black Swallow was rather small, and its body very light. Most of the feathers were gathered on the wings, so its back only had a thin layer of woolen feathers.","In fact, the Divine Travel Black Swallow wasn’t suitable for riding because it was too fast. There were plenty of avian feys that were suitable for transportation in the Radiance Federation. The Divine Travel Black Swallow might not be a comfortable means of transportation, but it was definitely the most popular avian fey.","The distance between the Radiance Federation’s major cities was too far, and if time could be saved during travel, a little discomfort could be overlooked.","Actually, before Lin Yuan ordered for the Divine Travel Black Swallow for transportation, he had also looked through other Platinum avian feys. Among them, the most expensive and comfortable avian fey would be the Orchid Fragrance Swan.","The Orchid Fragrance Swan’s appearance was exquisite. Its slender neck and wide wings looked very graceful. The white feathers that had slight pink gave off a romantic feeling. At the same time, the Orchid Fragrance Swan’s body had plenty of Goose-Feathered Orchids that were particularly pleasant to smell.","The Goose-Feathered Orchids had the fragrance of orchids and a refreshingly sweet fruit smell. Once a person could smell it, they would feel refreshed and also elegant. At the same time, the Goose-Feathered Orchids were also a type of Platinum spiritual ingredient that had extreme value. It was also the main ingredient for a high-quality perfume that was very popular among female spirit qi professionals.","The Orchid Fragrance Swan’s pinkish feathers were very smooth, and it felt as though the hand was sliding into a huge patch of silk.","Although the Platinum Orchid Fragrance Swan was so comfortable and elegant, when a spirit qi professional was going to travel for a long distance, they wouldn’t ride on the Orchid Fragrance Swan no matter how wealthy they were. The Orchid Fragrance Swan’s flying speed was truly too slow, and it was even slower than some of the Silver feys that were great at flying.","Therefore, the Orchid Fragrance Swan was normally the best choice when wealthy spirit qi professionals got married and they were going to have a honeymoon. If someone was to ride on the Orchid Fragrance Swan to attend to urgent matters, the matter might have already been resolved itself by the time the Orchid Fragrance Swan arrived.","Lin Yuan rode on the back of the Divine Travel Black Swallow and adjusted his body. After all, he would need a few days to travel from Ascending Dragon City to Redbud City.","As such, Lin Yuan checked on the source-type lifeform that the Mother of Bloodbath had retrieved from the pinnacle Class 1 alien insect dimensional rift. It looked like a thumb-sized and translucent insect egg. Lin Yuan took the insect egg-like source-type lifeform out of the leaf-shaped fey storage box.","When Lin Yuan used True Data to check on this source-type lifeform, it was really an insect egg. Lin Yuan only realized why the Mother of Bloodbath would say that this insect egg was extremely suitable for Red Thorn and that it was a great deal for him.","This translucent insect egg was an Acid Corrosion Queen Bee that was in its egg form. As a source-type lifeform, the contracting requirements for the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee were extremely harsh.","The Acid Corrosion Queen Bee was a kind of parasitic source-type lifeform, and it could only survive by living as a parasite in other feys or source-type lifeforms. At the same time, the body of the fey or source-type lifeform would need to have an extremely acidic environment because the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee could only thrive in such extremely acidic environments.","The Acid Corrosion Queen Bee would normally live inside the fey or source-type lifeform’s body while harvesting large amounts of acid as nutrition and maintaining its life. Therefore, it was right to say that there weren’t many feys and source-type lifeforms that were suitable for it to live as a parasite.","After hatching from the egg, the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee would immediately build its hive under the acidic environment. While building the hive, the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee would also absorb large amounts of acid and energy from the host. After building the hive, the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee would form a contract with its host and protect the host from then on. The Acid Corrosion Queen Bee would treat the host as its only god and listen to all their commands.","Lin Yuan was speechless as this Acid Corrosion Queen Bee was truly a perfect match for Red Thorn. Most of the feys and source-type lifeforms would only have powerful acidic parts in their digestive system. Since the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee was going to build its hive, all those smaller-sized feys and source-type lifeforms would need to be eliminated.","But even if that was the case, those animal-type feys and lifeforms with powerful acid wouldn’t be suitable to host the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee. Once the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee constructed its hive in its stomach area, which was also the digestive area, if the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee consumed a large amount of acid and energy, the host would definitely suffer damage to their roots.","But it was different for Red Thorn, as it had the perfect conditions for the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee. When Red Thorn evolved to Bronze/Epic, its Mouth of Relinquish was now a blood-and-flesh smelting furnace. Large quantities of alien insects would be easily digested. Lin Yuan wouldn’t dare to say that Red Thorn’s acid would be stronger than the alien insects’ acidic juices, but it was already enough to corrode sand.","Such powerful acid was a really great aid for the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s growth. Furthermore, the large amount of energy and acid required for the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee to construct its hive wouldn’t be a problem for Red Thorn.","Red Thorn’s Mouth of Relinquish contained powerful digestive capability, and its body had over a dozen digestive cavities that were mainly used to store surplus acid. If the Mouth of Relinquish required any acid replenishment, the digestive cavities would just cycle the stored acid to the Mouth of Relinquish.","Due to the massive number of consumed alien insects in Red Thorn’s body and the massive amount of acid contained within the alien insect’s blood, Red Thorn had an overflowing amount of digestive fluid. Therefore, when there was a need to spray out a massive amount of acid fluid, the digestive cavities would always be able to supply.","Presently, Red Thorn was only required to reserve one of the digestive cavities for the ortet. If the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee required more energy, Red Thorn would just need to consume more dimensional lifeforms’ blood and flesh.","Another advantage for Lin Yuan was that the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s contract didn’t require him to use any of his remaining spiritual energy. As a parasite inside Red Thorn’s body, the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee would only form a contract with Red Thorn, allowing Red Thorn to command the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee casually.","Due to Red Thorn and Lin Yuan’s bloodline connection, when Red Thorn commanded the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee, it was the same as Lin Yuan commanding the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee. However, due to the parasite and host relationship, the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee wouldn’t have a contract with Lin Yuan. Therefore, Lin Yuan wasn’t able to provide any Willpower Rune for the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee.","If the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee was to evolve into a Fantasy Breed, it could only reach the pinnacle of Diamond, like a wild fey. Once the quality reached Legend, the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee would need to comprehend its own Willpower Rune.","However, it was fortunate that Lin Yuan couldn’t enhance the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee. As such, it wasn’t difficult for the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee to reach the Legend quality.","As for whether the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee was able to comprehend a Willpower Rune and become a Fantasy Breed, it would be up to the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s aptitude as a source-type lifeform."]},{"number":151,"title":"Chapter 151: Advantage of Rapid Evolution","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","As a fey that had grown up freely in the wild, the most difficult thing was to raise its quality.","There were even quite a few feys that grew up freely in the wild. However, they were only Elite when they reached Platinum and Flawless when they reached Diamond.","It took a long process to raise the wild feys’ quality, but they might be able to do so if they encountered fortuitous opportunities.","This was why Creation Masters could use all sorts of spiritual ingredients to concoct spirit elixirs to attract the wild feys. The spirit elixirs contained pure spirit qi that was a dream for the wild feys.","All lifeforms wanted to evolve and raise their quality. This instinct to constantly evolve was the cornerstone of the great poetry of life formed by the evolution of thousands of species in the history of life. The instinct for the desire to evolve had long been engraved in the soul of every fey since birth.","Therefore, only the Creation Masters with the ability to evolve feys and raise their grade and quality were especially favored by the wild feys.","Although the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee was a source-type lifeform and not really a true fey, it was destined to tread this hard path. Fortunately, it would easily dissolve this hardship thanks to Lin Yuan.","When the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee reached Bronze, it could be raised to Legend with Lin Yuan’s help.","Given the increase of Lin Yuan’s spirit qi rank and his Creation Master ability, it would only be a matter of time before the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee reached pinnacle Diamond. Thus, there was only one thing difficult for the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee, which was how to comprehend the Willpower Rune.","This was actually what Lin Yuan would like to see.","Since the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee did not fuse the Willpower Rune to evolve into a Fantasy Breed at Bronze, like Lin Yuan’s other feys in order to maximize their potential, Lin Yuan could keep upgrading it with no worries.","It was also easier for him to upgrade the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee if it did not evolve into a Fantasy Breed.","This undoubtedly made up for Lin Yuan’s current lack of combat power.","Given Lin Yuan’s ability as a C-rank spirit qi professional, it was easy to enhance a source-type lifeform like the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee to Gold.","The Gold/Legend source-type Acid Corrosion Queen Bee was not inferior to some pinnacle Gold feys that had yet to reach Legend.","It had already given Lin Yuan the qualification to fight in the Radiance Hundred Sequence and the combat power to become the Radiance Federation’s top youth.","The Acid Corrosion Queen Bee was more like a tool for Red Thorn, which only needed to provide a corrosive cavity to the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee in order for the queen bee to treat Red Thorn as its god and serve it.","The highly acidic digestive fluids and energy were not a big deal to Red Thorn.","The leaf-shaped fey storage box that the Moon Empress had given to Lin Yuan contained enough dimensional lifeforms’ flesh to feed Red Thorn to Platinum.","The energy needed to feed the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee was just a drop in the ocean compared to the energy from the dimensional lifeforms’ flesh in the leaf-shaped Diamond fey storage box.","Red Thorn’s greatest problem was that it was good at quickly unfolding the situation and starting a war of attrition. It belonged to a powerful group-attacking method.","The Gold Acid Corrosion Queen Bee perfectly made up for Red Thorn’s lack of lethality toward a single target.","Red Thorn’s vines had lethality and control power, which would undoubtedly give the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee more opportunities to strike.","Red Thorn also had no obvious shortcomings after cooperating with the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee to make up for its flaw in single-target combat.","Only then would Red Thorn be considered a truly terrifying killing machine.","As the vines danced in the spread-out sea of flowers, there was a hidden powerful source-type lifeform, the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee. It could perfectly cooperate with Red Thorn to sneak-attack and kill some powerful single enemies.","Lin Yuan put the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s insect egg back in the Diamond fey storage box.","It was undoubtedly unsuitable to summon Red Thorn on the Divine Travel Black Swallow’s back. Thus, it was also impossible for the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s eggs to hatch.","Lin Yuan had originally wanted to simply go to the Endless Forest for wild harvesting. But along the way, he had met Zhang Xiaobai, Xin Ying, Lu Pinru, and Tan Ran, and even experienced a battle in Millstone Town.","At the same time, he had comprehended the Twilight Willpower Rune from the sunrise that had risen after the battle, gathered many feys with great potential, and had gained quite a lot along the way. If not for meeting Chu Ci now, he even had the desire to enter seclusion.","This was because Lin Yuan could probably only transform what he had gained into actual power through one or two months of seclusion.","As Chimey did not have a suitable Willpower Rune previously, it had been stuck at Bronze/Legend.","It could now evolve into a Fantasy Breed with the suitable Twilight Willpower Rune.","Lin Yuan could not help but look forward to the changes that would happen after Chimey evolved into a Fantasy Breed with the Twilight Willpower Rune. He also wondered what exclusive skill it would learn.","A fey would undergo a life-changing transformation when it became a Fantasy Breed.","Based on the Jasmine Lily’s evolution into a Fantasy Breed alone, it was clear what kind of boost a fey would have after evolving into a Fantasy Breed.","Lin Yuan finally understood why so many experts loved to enter seclusion. During seclusion, they could calm their minds in a relatively undisturbed environment and become stronger and sort themselves out as they wished. At the same time, they could also decide what path to take next during seclusion.","Lin Yuan had been sitting on the Divine Travel Black Swallow these days.","As he looked down at the mountains and land under the glow, he felt that they were majestic.","The battle in Millstone Town had really strained Lin Yuan’s mind. The relaxation he had for the past few days had allowed him to feel refreshed.","After the Divine Travel Black Swallow sent Lin Yuan into Redbud City and saw him confirm his order on Star Web, it flew away.","He had spent 3 Radiance dollars riding the Platinum Divine Travel Black Swallow, causing him to have the idea of cultivating avian transportation feys.","In the Radiance Federation, it was possible to privately cultivate such feys.","Ordinary spirit qi professionals would need a contract with the transportation feys before they were allowed to register in the Radiance Federation. Only these registered transportation feys were eligible for driving certificates.","However, Creation Masters were the only exceptions. They could directly apply for a fey’s driving certification in the Creation Master Association without forming a contract with the fey, provided that they had the Creation Master Association’s verification that the Creation Masters themselves independently cultivated their avian feys.","Actually, the Radiance Federation was strict in this area because it was afraid that the avian feys would lose control in flight and result in some accidents.","There were many different kinds of avian feys that individuals could ride on. These feys would usually not have very low grades.","However, such avian feys would cause extreme destruction if they lost control. Besides hurting the pilot, they might also harm innocent people, which would cause many unnecessary disputes."]},{"number":152,"title":"Chapter 152: Plan to Forge an Iron Bucket Sister","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","In fact, the Radiance Federation’s avian feys were pretty expensive, especially those rare ones that could transport people. That was because avian feys were not only a means of transportation, but they were also regarded as a kind of luxury item to show one’s status in the Radiance Federation.","Lin Yuan was walking on Redbud City’s streets and looking at the thriving city at noon. Unexpectedly, he discovered that he shared a special connection with Redbud City, as his state of mind would be different whenever he came to this city.","The first time he had come to Redbud City was when he had hurriedly brought her Bronze Sharp Iron Horn Bull to Chu Ci. At that time, Lin Yuan had just regained his ability to sense spirit qi and discovered his ability as a Creation Master.","He had an infinite vision of his future because, in his opinion, he had started to erect his life goals again at that time.","The second time was when he had passed the Creation Master’s test, becoming a Class 2 Creation Master. At that point, Lin Yuan had confidence that he was on the right path.","And now, he had come to Redbud City for the third time.","After experiencing a life-and-death battle, he had a clear view of this world. Lin Yuan had long been firm about the path he wanted to take in the future.","Then, he suddenly heard a hawking voice. “Cornbread, 1 Federation dollar for four!”","Lin Yuan could not help but reveal a cheerful smile. Every time he came here, he would always see this stall selling cornbread. It was really fate.","He walked up and spent 1 Federation dollar on buying four loaves of cornbreads. Then, he bit on one of them.","After eating high-grade spiritual ingredients for so many months in the Radiant Moon Palace, Lin Yuan realized that he had become much pickier than before. He found it hard to eat the cornbread that he found delicious a few months ago.","It was a bittersweet memory, but Lin Yuan felt that it should be a sweet memory when he swallowed this chunk of cornbread. In his opinion, his former strong self was a sweet memory.","Lin Yuan had cleansed away all the impurities in his body thanks to the Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar and allowed himself to be perfectly optimized toward his own genetic model. After that, his excellent temperament had become extraordinary.","His cheerful youthful aura gave off a kind of indescribable carefreeness and attracted many people’s attention along the way.","Lin Yuan had been a precious pearl that was shimmering slightly before. He had gone down his memory lane and had long been an unparalleled handsome young man.","Before Lin Yuan went to the Redbud Intermediate Spirit Qi Academy, where Chu Ci was, he made a special trip to the store to buy some fruits. Among these fresh fruits were also some unique to Ascending Dragon City and Millstone Town that could not be bought in Redbud City.","Lin Yuan was going to give these fruits to Teacher Bao. He would always remember those who had once helped him or Chu Ci when he had been weak.","When Lin Yuan arrived at Redbud Intermediate Spirit Qi Academy’s entrance, he dialed Chu Ci’s number. Soon, Chu Ci answered the phone.","“Lin Yuan, why are you calling me at this time? I’ve just finished my training class! You don’t know how strong this Sharp Iron Horn Bull is! Those seniors can’t even beat me!” Chu Ci quickly spoke when she picked up Lin Yuan’s call.","Lin Yuan could not help but touch the back of his head. He was skeptical whether Chu Ci had forgotten she was a defense-type spirit qi professional.","Chu Ci was simply taking the Sharp Iron Horn Bull as an offense-type fey and actually competing with the seniors during the training class. What if those seniors hurt her?","Despite Lin Yuan’s carefreeness, he could not help but worry about his only kin in this world.","Upon noticing Lin Yuan’s silence, Chu Ci immediately knew what the problem was. “Aren’t I trying to improve myself as soon as possible? Brother, you’re a Creation Master now. If I don’t work harder, won’t I be pulled further and further away from you?”","When Chu Ci called him ‘brother’, he immediately knew that things were not that simple. Chu Ci should have sustained injuries during the training. Otherwise, given their dependence on each other for so many years, Chu Ci would always call him Lin Yuan. As such, there was nothing good when she called him ‘brother’.","Lin Yuan hurriedly replied, “I’ve arrived at the school entrance. Where are you? I’ll go over and find you.”","Chu Ci was first happy, but after she looked at the teacher healing her, she could not help but stuck out her tongue.","Just then, her teacher said, “Chu Ci, you have fractured your arm. My fey can only heal external injuries, so you might need to nurse your broken bones for a while.”","When the teacher spoke, Chu Ci wanted to cover the phone, but Lin Yuan still heard that she had fractured her arm.","Chu Ci could not help but feel guilty. Whenever Lin Yuan called her, he would always tell her to take care of herself, and she would tell him not to worry. Unfortunately, he found out about her injury this time.","Chu Ci’s training regime was very harsh. She would usually be in the training ground practicing combat skills with her seniors, which inadvertently caused minor and major injuries to her. Nonetheless, the healing teacher could always treat her, but it was the first time she had a bone fracture.","“Brother, hold on. I’ll go find you, but you might have to accompany me to buy some spiritual ingredients to treat fractures.”","Chu Ci glanced at her arm—that she did not dare to exert any force on—and knew that she could not conceal such an injury even if she wanted to.","Lin Yuan was somewhat frustrated now, as Chu Ci had always been stable since young. How had she sustained injuries just because of a rough defense-type fey like the Sharp Iron Horn Bull?","Lin Yuan had always wanted to forge Chu Ci into an iron bucket that nobody could break, but he would always put aside this thought.","Now, he felt the need to have this thought again in order to prevent Chu Ci from being injured again. It was necessary to forge her into an iron bucket.","The Earth Powder Butterly’s cocoon in Lin Yuan’s Spirit Lock spatial zone had hatched. He had turned the Normal Earth Powder Butterly inside into a Bronze Vajra Butterfly.","Before the Earth Powder Butterly evolved into a Vajra Butterfly, Lin Yuan had already upgraded it from Elite to Epic. Therefore, there were three kinds of exclusive skills for the Bronze Vajra Butterfly.","Two of these exclusive skills were not considered good, so Lin Yuan had given up on them.","The third exclusive skill, Counterattack Tremor, had overjoyed Lin Yuan. This exclusive skill could allow Chu Ci to defend against an opponent’s attack while rebounding a portion of the damage back in the form of an energy tremor.","For the Vajra Butterfly’s Elite ability, Vajra Shield, it would fly around the target while condensing a strong transparent Vajra Shield on the target.","This was the prototype of an iron bucket in Lin Yuan’s mind.","The Vajra Butterfly’s exclusive skill, Counterattack Tremor, would allow Chu Ci to strengthen her defense while also possessing some means to counterattack.","In Lin Yuan’s opinion, this should be the choice of a defense-type spirit qi professional.","In contrast to the Vajra Butterfly, the Sharp Iron Horn Bull was simply a fake defense-type fey.","After some discussion with Chu Ci, Lin Yuan had chosen the Vajra Butterfly. If the Vajra Butterfly was cultivated properly, it could evolve into a Jadeite Butterfly when it was at Gold.","The Jadeite Butterfly had a reputation of being the top shield among the Gold defense-type feys. This meant that the hardness of the shield released by the Jadeite Butterfly was recognized as the top among the Gold defense-type feys.","However, if he wanted to cultivate the Vajra Butterfly into a Jadeite Butterfly, he would need a huge amount of resources and extremely pure spirit qi.","Presently, Lin Yuan only had the Radiance dollars from Cheng Wu’s beetle-shaped Diamond fey storage box, so he did not need to worry about resources.","Creation Masters might not be able to obtain extremely pure spirit qi, but for Lin Yuan, it could not be any simpler. He only needed to channel the spiritual power in his body. Thus, Lin Yuan was confident of evolving Chu Ci’s Vajra Butterfly into a Jadeite Butterfly at Gold.","Nevertheless, he would have to consider at length about the Jadeite Butterfly evolving into the legendary Tourmaline Emperor Butterfly.","At that point, Lin Yuan had come up with a plan to forge his sister into an iron bucket.","Stack the thickest armor!","Even if she took the most vicious beating, she also had to counterattack with the greatest injury!","And not get injured at all!","This was what a mature older brother should do!","Lessons were still ongoing in the Redbud Intermediate Spirit Qi Academy, so few people were in front of the school.","At the entrance, a young girl’s nervous head revealed itself. The young girl saw the cheerful young boy standing at the entrance and immediately smiled happily. Just as she wanted to rush over, she suddenly thought of something.","She quickly revealed a pitiful smile and said sweetly, “Brother, I haven’t seen you for so long. I missed you!”"]},{"number":153,"title":"Chapter 153: Ice in a Jade Kettle","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Lin Yuan was still a bit angry that Chu Ci, a defense-type spirit qi professional, had actually injured herself in a battle with her seniors, causing her to fracture her arm.","If she wanted to practice her combat skills, she could have just gone to climb the Star Tower and fight.","Lin Yuan had not seen Chu Ci for a few months. When he saw her, he vented out the yearning he had been suppressing.","When Lin Yuan had suffered Cheng Wu’s sneak attack and was on the brink of death, all he could think of was Chu Ci, his only kin. As her older brother, if Lin Yuan really died, Chu Ci would have nobody to rely on.","Upon seeing Chu Ci’s pitiful face, her big, clear eyes, as well as her calling him in a sweet tone, Lin Yuan knew that she was using the same trick. However, he could do nothing about it. His anger due to his worry dissipated.","Lin Yuan was a carefree person. When facing his only kin, Chu Ci, the double standard was inevitable.","If other defense-type spirit qi professionals like Chu Ci fought with their seniors and worked hard to improve their offensive skills, Lin Yuan would certainly give them a thumbs-up and praise them immediately.","After all, the Star Web’s combat training techniques were less practical than actual combat, which was also why the school’s live combat classes were not on Star Web.","In Lin Yuan’s opinion, it was unrealistic to not get injured in actual combat. Nevertheless, when it concerned Chu Ci, he did not think so.","The moment he saw Chu Ci walking over with her hands, which would hurt even when she walked, hanging at her sides, Lin Yuan started feeling distressed and activated the Silver Fantasy Breed Jasmine Lily’s Heal ability.","A beam of green light filled with vitality shone on Chu Ci’s injured left arm. As the green light flowed, Chu Ci felt an indescribable comfort surrounding her arm.","A moment later, Chu Ci realized that her arm did not hurt anymore. She tried moving her arm and said in surprise, “Lin Yuan, when did you become a healing-type spirit qi professional?”","Chu Ci previously only knew that Lin Yuan had the talents to become a Creation Master, but she did not expect him to be a healing-type spirit qi professional as well.","She hurriedly ran to Lin Yuan’s side and happily observed Lin Yuan’s hand that had cast the healing energy.","Chu Ci usually missed Lin Yuan the most when she was learning in school, and after she knew that his body had recovered, her worries were gone. She was happy on his behalf, whether he was a Creation Master or a spirit qi professional, but she valued his health the most.","It was just like how Lin Yuan worried about her injury.","In Chu Ci’s heart, Lin Yuan was a giant that had always been protecting her. The word ‘older brother’ would always be the most sacred and powerful in her heart.","Chu Ci only had a vague impression of her parents, as she was still young when they had gone to fend off against the dimensional rift, not to ever return.","Therefore, even when Lin Yuan was physically weak, he still managed the fey store. No matter how hard it was, he still clenched his teeth to support his family and her education.","Whenever something good happened to Lin Yuan, Chu Ci would be happier than when something ten times better happened to her—such dependence for over ten years was indescribable.","Although it was late autumn in Redbud City, it was still hot, but there was some wind. This autumn wind blew a strand of Chu Rui’s hair apart and made one stand of her foolish hair stand up, which Lin Yuan hurriedly pressed down.","Chu Ci had relatively hard hair from a young age. Every autumn, some strands of foolish hair would always stand up when the wind blew. And every time Lin Yuan saw it, he would skillfully press them down.","“Do you still have any classes today?”","Chu Ci replied after thinking for a while, “I’m supposed to have live combat classes in the afternoon, but since I’ve fractured my arm, I should be resting in my dorm.”","Lin Yuan handed the fruits he was carrying to Chu Ci and said, “Then I’ll accompany you to ask for leave from Teacher Bao.”","Even though Chu Ci could rest in the dorm and did not need to go to the live combat class in the afternoon due to her fracture, her arm was now healed. Thus, it was necessary to inform Chu Ci’s homeroom teacher. After all, Lin Yuan believed that they should adhere to the school rules.","Lin Yuan wanted to give the fruits to Teacher Bao as well.","Soon, they arrived at Teacher Bao’s office, knocked on the door, and went in. Lin Yuan saw Teacher Bao sitting at his desk and writing something.","After taking a closer look, he realized that the thick book was actually a lesson plan.","Teacher Bao was a Spiritual Ingredient Analyst teacher and taught theoretical knowledge.","Lin Yuan saw the thick book of lesson plans that Teacher Bao was writing and knew that he had made a lot of efforts to make it easier for the students he taught to understand the lesson.","When Teacher Bao saw Lin Yuan beside Chu Rui, he obviously froze for a moment and looked carefully before confirming Lin Yuan’s identity.","Chu Ci and Lin Yuan had been together for over ten years. No matter how one looked at it, they were the closest to each other.","Although Lin Yuan’s temperament had changed greatly, Chu Ci did not feel there was any difference. This was because Lin Yuan was the best in every way in her heart.","However, Teacher Bao had only met Lin Yuan twice and was a little afraid to recognize him. The young man in front of him was cheerful and handsome with a distinguished temperament. It was not too much to say that he was outstanding.","After confirming Lin Yuan’s identity, he nodded and said in a solemn tone as he looked at Chu Ci’s hand, “Chu Ci has exceptional talent. She became a C-rank spirit qi professional last week, but she has suffered a severe arm fracture. You have to pay attention to that. If you can prepare some spiritual ingredients to speed up the healing process, coupled with the school doctor’s treatment, you can enhance her recovery speed.”","If Chu Ci’s fracture could be healed earlier, she could train as early as possible and not waste her excellent talent. It was very important for spirit qi professionals to have a foundation at a young age.","Chu Ci raised her hands and said to Teacher Bao with a smile, “Teacher Bao, my brother has healed my hand.”","She did not think there was anything wrong with her words, but Teacher Bao could not help but look at Lin Yuan in surprise.","Teacher Bao did not expect that Lin Yuan would be a healing-type spirit qi professional with such potent healing abilities that could heal bone injuries.","He had always been a serious person, but when he saw Chu Ci’s hand had healed, he could not help but wear a smile on his face. The smile on his wrinkled face made his serious face look a bit more benevolent.","Lin Yuan told Teacher Bao his purpose for coming, so Teacher Bao waved his hand and allowed Chu Ci to take leave.","Before leaving, Lin Yuan asked Chu Ci to place the fruits on Teacher Bao’s desk. However, before Lin Yuan could say anything, Teacher Bao handed the fruits back and said, “As her guardian, you picked Chu Ci up and still bought fruits. Take them away. I have to write lesson plans.”","Then, he continued writing up the lesson plans.","Lin Yuan did not mention leaving the fruits for Teacher Bao. Instead, he left the office with Chu Ci.","There were always some of the most honorable people in this world who taught and educated others without expecting anything in return.","As the saying went, “Silvery hair sets off against the sun and moon, and loyalty and passion irrigate the new flowers.”","Teacher Bao had probably forgotten about the help he had given to Chu Ci in the past. Although Teacher Bao was not very strong and was just an ordinary person among the masses, he always did things like ice in a jade kettle1, shining with the light of greatness."]},{"number":154,"title":"Chapter 154: Our Daughter Has Grown Up","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Lin Yuan and Chu Ci were already walking on the Redbud Intermediate Spirit Qi Academy’s campus and about to leave the academy. Since classes had ended, the campus was filled with laughter and noises.","At that moment, Lin Yuan suddenly heard the two classmates beside them say, “What’s the loneliest thing you’ve ever heard?”","Another classmate opened his mouth without even thinking about it and answered, “Being the only one who hasn’t handed in your homework.”","Then, he asked, “Do you know what extreme sports are?”","The student that had asked previously was obviously an expert and replied instantly, “While the teacher is collecting our homework, you copy the other classmates’ homework to make up for your own.”","Lin Yuan frowned when he heard that. These two students were really witty. Fortunately, he never had to worry about Chu Ci’s studies.","Chu Ci, who was walking beside Lin Yuan, had never stopped smiling and was apparently in an excellent mood.","Lin Yuan looked at Chu Ci and said, “You’re really something! You’ve become a C-rank spirit qi professional, but why didn’t you tell me in the call? Had Teacher Bao not told me, how long were you going to hide it from me?”","Chu Ci stuck out her tongue before she then wrinkled her nose and replied, “I was going to tell you personally when you would visit me, but Teacher Bao leaked it out instead!”","Besides giving herself a peace of mind regarding her own progress, the happiest thing was probably to share with Lin Yuan so that her closest kin could share in the joy of her own improvement.","Lin Yuan was actually surprised. Although he knew that Chu Ci had exceptional talents, he did not expect her to become a C-rank spirit qi professional from a D-rank in such a short time of cultivation.","He knew that he was different. Upgrading a spirit qi professional’s rank relied on enhancing feys, so there was no need to compare himself with Chu Ci.","However, the Radiance Hundred Sequence’s top talents, like Sequence #3 Overflowing Sea, Long Tao, were currently only pinnacle B-rank spirit qi professionals. It was very difficult for them to reach A-rank.","Chu Ci was only 15 years old. When Long Tao was at that age, he might not have been able to break through to C-rank.","Just then, Chu Ci said softly, “Lin Yuan, I seem to have comprehended a Willpower Rune after breaking through to a C-rank spirit qi professional.”","After saying that, Chu Ci circulated her spiritual energy. A Willpower Rune with a dark metallic luster flew out of her spiritual mind and circled her.","Lin Yuan’s surprise had yet to be dissipated, and he did not expect Chu Ci to bring him another surprise again.","Since Chu Ci had already comprehended a Willpower Rune at the age of 15 meant that she could now possess a Fantasy Breed fey.","Although there was no absolute boundary between the grade of a spirit qi professional and their contracted fey, they were closely related.","For example, D-rank spirit qi professionals could only command Bronze feys, C-rank spirit qi professionals could only command Gold feys, B-rank spirit qi professionals could command Platinum feys, while A-rank spirit qi professionals could command Diamond feys.","For feys to reach Suzerain, their contractors needed to reach S-rank.","If the spirit qi professionals could not reach the standard and raised their feys’ grade, they might likely cause a very embarrassing situation.","For example, their spiritual energy would not be able to withstand the load and collapse.","As spirit qi professionals raised their ranks, their spiritual energy and the spirit qi in their bodies would also increase. If they had a few contracted feys, their spiritual energy would barely be able to reach the standard without collapse.","Nonetheless, their bodies’ spiritual power certainly could not keep up with the consumption needed for the feys to release their skills. Hence, it had always been a big no-no for spirit qi professionals whose ranks were not up to standard to rashly find a Creation Master to raise the grades of their feys.","Chu Ci was currently a C-rank spirit qi professional and could handle Gold feys. Her Willpower Rune contained a metallic, oppressive feeling, and it was evidently suitable for the Sharp Iron Horn Bull.","At that moment, Lin Yuan suddenly heard a pleasant yet strange voice. “Lin Yuan, your sister really has amazing talents! She will have a boundless future when she grows over time!”","Even if the Mother of Bloodbath was experienced and knowledgeable, it could not help but sigh at Chu Ci’s talent.","After seeing that Chu Ci possessed a Willpower Rune, Lin Yuan said seriously to her, “Call Teacher Bao later and ask for ten days’ leave.”","Lin Yuan said nothing, but Chu Ci asked nothing either. She just called Teacher Bao.","Upon hearing that Chu Ci was taking a leave of absence, he thought that something had happened to her hand, so he just approved of her leave without hesitation.","Lin Yuan’s envisioned plan of forging his sister into an iron bucket was just at the planning stage. But due to her talents, he had to implement this plan now.","Chu Ci was done with the phone call, so Lin Yuan reached out to touch her head before saying, “Chu Ci, you can now be called a powerful spirit qi professional.”","When Chu Ci had a Fantasy Breed fey, she could indeed afford to be called powerful.","Apart from needing a Willpower Rune, it was hard to evolve Bronze Fantasy Breed feys to Legend. Most Creation Masters could not do so.","Feys also had talents. Those with exceptional talent could also reach a high quality without the Creation Masters’ help. However, such feys were always rare.","Lin Yuan did not know what rank of Creation Masters could evolve a Bronze fey into Legend.","An ordinary Class 4 Creation Master clearly could not do so, and Lin Yuan did not know if pinnacle Class 4 Creation Masters could succeed with that.","However, it was not a problem for him to raise the feys into Legend at Bronze.","As a C-rank spirit qi professional, Lin Yuan only needed five days to enhance the feys in the Spirit Lock spatial zone and evolve them from Bronze to Legend.","In the past, it was indeed difficult for Chu Ci to have a Fantasy Breed at Bronze, as she needed to have a Willpower Rune. However, she had one now.","Lin Yuan had asked Chu Ci to take ten days off because he wanted to improve her capabilities.","Upon seeing Lin Yuan’s serious expression, as if he was thinking about something, Chu Ci said softly to him, “Lin Yuan, I didn’t tell anyone that I comprehend a Willpower Rune.”","Lin Yuan laughed. The saying, “Poor children matured early.”, was indeed right.","Lin Yuan, who had lived two lifetimes, naturally knew the principle of “An outstanding tree would definitely be blown down by the wind.”","Chu Ci, who had grown up in a tough environment, also understood this fact.","Lin Yuan was very pleased with Chu Ci’s cautiousness. At the same time, he looked firmly at her and said, “It’s good to hide your abilities, but you don’t have to do that now. You can show your talents to the fullest.”","The moment he learned that Chu Ci had comprehended a Willpower Rune, he had decided that he would let his Master, the Moon Empress, know about Chu Ci’s talent.","Lin Yuan could afford all of Chu Ci’s future feys and resources.","However, what he needed was to make sure that Chu Ci, who had such extraordinary potential, could show her talents in front of everyone, and nobody would do anything to her because they were jealous.","Although Lin Yuan had always wanted to explore the world single-handedly, he knew that from the moment he had gone through the ceremonial rites to have the Moon Empress as his Master, the Moon Empress had become his teacher and his kin with no blood relations.","The Moon Empress, one of the Class 5 Creation Masters in the Radiance Federation, would always support him.","With her around, Chu Ci’s safety would not be a problem.","As Lin Yuan looked at Chu Ci, he could not help but feel proud. His heart was filled with pride!","My younger sister actually has exceptional talents, so why should she hide? She should be shining among the crowd!","At the same time, Lin Yuan’s gaze also became increasingly determined. Given his current improvement speed, in just two years, he would be able to protect Chu Ci.","As Lin Yuan looked at Chu Ci, he suddenly had a feeling as if his daughter had grown up."]},{"number":155,"title":"Chapter 155: Fantasy Breed Choice","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Since he had decided to improve Chu Ci’s capabilities, Lin Yuan did not delay at all. After Lin Yuan and Chu Ci went to have a meal, they headed to Redbud City’s Creation Master Association.","Lin Yuan had previously completed the Class 2 Creation Master’s test in Redbud City’s Creation Master Association.","This time, Lin Yuan met Elder Ning first. He realized that Elder Ning was still nurturing that Spiral-Toothed Shark.","As compared to two months ago, the Spiral-Toothed Shark had become much bigger and was more robust. This was an omen that the Spiral-Toothed Shark was about to return to its ancestry line.","It seemed that Elder Ning’s desire to activate a trace of the Megalodon’s bloodline in the Spiral-Toothed Shark’s body was really likely to come true.","After meeting Elder Ning, Lin Yuan rented a breeding room in the Creation Master Association as a Class 2 Creation Master. Then, he prepared some fresh fruits rich in spirit qi, which would be his meals.","In the next few days, Lin Yuan wanted to improve Chu Ci’s rank.","Although Chu Ci had been attending school in Redbud City for some time, it was still her first time in the Creation Master Association.","As a member of the Radiance Federation, even though Chu Ci was not really clear about the various aspects of how Creation Masters evolved feys, she was aware of the Creation Masters’ status in the Radiance Federation.","The fact that Lin Yuan had become a Creation Master made her proud. Lin Yuan’s expectation for Chu Ci was the same as her expectation for him. It was just that she wished for him to be healthy.","Nevertheless, they were proud of the other when any of them made any achievements.","Lin Yuan took the Vajra Butterfly out of the leaf-shaped Diamond fey storage box in the breeding room.","[Fey Name]: Vajra Butterfly","[Fey Species]: Nymphalidae/Heliconius","[Fey Grade]: Bronze (10/10)","[Fey Type]: Metal","[Fey Quality]: Epic","Abilities:","[Wing Block]: Congeal hard metal on its wings for blocking.","[Steel Pattern Shield]: Quickly attaches to the target and condenses a solid metal, transparent, all-around shield that can follow the target’s movement.","Exclusive Skill:","[Counterattack Tremor]: When attacked, it will rebound a portion of the damage from physical attacks or magic attacks, in the form of an energy tremor.","When he looked at this Vajra Butterfly, particularly its exclusive skills, Lin Yuan was very satisfied and said to Chu Ci, “This Vajra Butterfly suits you. It can take up the duties you have as a defense-type spirit qi professional.”","After the Vajra Butterfly’s appearance, Chu Ci only saw a butterfly the size of an adult’s fist fluttering around her. The butterfly’s wings shone with a dark metallic luster, carrying many metallic patterns.","While fluttering, the Vajra Butterfly flew to Chu Ci’s side with Lin Yuan’s gesture. Chu Ci reached out, and it immediately landed on her hand. She played with the Vajra Butterfly for a while before forming a contract with it.","Chu Ci was naturally very clear of her duties as a defense-type spirit qi professional. In a squad, a defense-type spirit qi professional had to cooperate with the teammates and fulfill the duties of defending her comrades.","Although the Sharp Iron Horn Bull was a defense-type fey, it was undoubtedly more of a combat-class fey. Its Sacrifice ability was also only effective toward Chu Ci.","Chu Ci currently had a contract with only the Sharp Iron Horn Bull, so she was unqualified to form a squad with other people as a defense-type spirit qi professional.","With the Vajra Butterfly’s addition, however, it was clearly different.","After Chu Ci formed a contract with the Vajra Butterfly, Lin Yuan let her summon the Sharp Iron Horn Bull. When the Sharp Iron Horn Bull appeared, it made a ‘mooing’ sound. It gently rubbed against Chu Ci’s hands, still worried about the injury she had sustained previously in the battle. The Sharp Iron Horn Bull was apparently very attached to her.","Then, it saw Lin Yuan and turned to Chu Ci. Only with her gesture did it then walk to his side. It shook its head at Lin Yuan as a greeting.","Apparently, the Sharp Iron Horn Bull still remembered Lin Yuan. Even though it remembered that Lin Yuan had saved it at that time, after it had become Chu Ci’s contracted fey, it only listened to her words. Feys had spirituality, and they always chose one person until the end.","Seeing the Sharp Iron Horn Bull’s state, Lin Yuan knew that it had been nurtured well. Its evolution from Bronze I to Bronze IV was undoubtedly fast without the help of a Creation Master.","In addition, the Sharp Iron Horn Bull’s body was much stronger than before, with richer metallic luster on its body. The horn on its head was also sharper.","It was evident that the Sharp Iron Horn Bull usually ate a lot of metals to have such a wonderful development.","However, Chu Ci now was faced with a choice, as she had comprehended the Willpower Rune that contained a strong sense of metal.","The Willpower Rune was very suitable for both the Sharp Iron Horn Bull and the Vajra Butterfly that she had just formed a contract with.","Under such circumstances, as a contractor, Chu Ci had to make a choice.","Lin Yuan knew that the choice would be difficult at this point, but Chu Ci had to choose because there was only one Willpower Rune.","“Chu Ci, your Willpower Rune is suitable for both the Vajra Butterfly and the Sharp Iron Horn Bull. Which fey do you have in mind to evolve into a Fantasy Breed?”","“Fantasy Breed?” Chu Ci asked back in surprise, somewhat baffled.","Why did Lin Yuan suddenly mention the Fantasy Breed? And he even asked me to choose between the Sharp Iron Horn Bull and Vajra Butterfly to evolve into a Fantasy Breed?","Although Fantasy Breeds were not a piece of common knowledge, there was knowledge of it in Chu Ci’s course.","Naturally, she knew that she needed to raise a fey to Legend before evolving into a Fantasy Breed.","She looked at Lin Yuan in a daze. Don’t tell me he can evolve a fey to Legend?","Lin Yuan reached out and scratched her nose, making her come back to her senses. “Silly girl. When have I ever lied to you? Your choice this time concerns your future development, so you have to choose carefully.”","Chu Ci had unconditional trust in Lin Yuan, so she carefully pondered over the question he had asked her and weighed the Willpower Rune’s usage in her mind. After some contemplation, she said firmly, “I choose the Sharp Iron Horn Bull.”","Lin Yuan sighed as he personally hoped that she would choose the Vajra Butterfly. This was because if the Vajra Butterfly evolved into a Fantasy Breed, it could protect Chu Ci so that she almost would not be subjected to the danger of an arm fracture like today.","After all, as a very powerful defense-type fey, when the Vajra Butterfly evolved into a Fantasy Breed and awakened its second exclusive skill, its defensive ability would only become stronger.","Even though Lin Yuan wanted to forge an iron bucket sister, Chu Ci was independent as a spirit qi professional. She had the right to choose her future path.","As her older brother, Lin Yuan would only intervene in major problems and could only guide her on the choice of her path.","At that moment, Lin Yuan asked very carefully once again, “Have you really decided it’ll be the Sharp Iron Horn Bull?”","Willpower Runes had always been unattainable. Although Chu Ci had obtained one, nobody knew when she would have another one.","Thus, all the spirit qi professionals were very cautious about the feys for the Willpower Rune. Once they chose a certain fey to fuse with the Willpower Rune, their combat style and combat system would likely change with this choice.","Chu Ci nodded without hesitation, her eyes shining brightly. “Lin Yuan, I’m sure!”","Chu Ci had her own goal. She wanted to pass the Redbud Hundred selection, get into the top ten, and represent Redbud City to compete in the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","She had her considerations. If she chose the Vajra Butterfly, even though her defense capability could be improved, her combat ability would undoubtedly be weaker than choosing the Sharp Iron Horn Bull.","The individual capabilities were undoubtedly more valued than team capabilities in the Redbud Hundred’s selection or the Radiance Hundred Sequence’s competition.","Thus, if she wanted to get into the top ten of the Redbud Hundred and be qualified to join the Radiance Hundred Sequence’s competition, it would be more suitable for her to evolve the Sharp Iron Horn Bull into a Fantasy Breed.","At the same time, Chu Ci had long since adapted to the combat style with the Sharp Iron Horn Bull, which was her first fey.","Actually, Chu Ci, a 15-year-old girl, also had her own ambition. She wanted to stand on the Radiance Hundred Sequence through her own efforts.","Although Lin Yuan had always been protecting her, she also wanted to be fully-fledged and able to protect him. This was the warm ambition of a young girl.","After Chu Ci truly decided, Lin Yuan started to prepare for the Sharp Iron Horn Bull’s evolution."]},{"number":156,"title":"Chapter 156: Legend Sharp Iron Horn Bull","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Lin Yuan was more compatible with healing-type feys, support-type feys, and plant-type feys.","As healing support, he had nurtured the source-type fey, Red Thorn, into a combat-class fey with output.","Based on Red Thorn’s evolution into its current state, it was evident how Lin Yuan was obsessed with output.","However, Lin Yuan did not expect his younger sister Chu Ci to be the same as him. As a defense-type spirit qi professional, she manipulated a big iron bull and was immersed in output.","Indeed, family members did have a similar way of thinking.","It would take Lin Yuan over five days to evolve the Bronze Sharp Iron Horn Bull to Legend.","In the past five days or so, Lin Yuan alone was enough to evolve the Sharp Iron Horn Bull in the breeding room. At that moment, the bell rang.","When Creation Masters were usually nurturing feys in the breeding room, nobody would disturb them.","Lin Yuan knew Elder Ning had come. When he came to visit Chu Ci, he only wanted to send her the Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar and the Vajra Butterfly he had nurtured for her to form a contract with. However, he did not expect that Chu Ci would comprehend a Willpower Rune.","The Sharp Iron Horn Bull would need some spiritual ingredients to evolve into Legend. Lin Yuan had not prepared the spiritual ingredients beforehand, as it had been beyond his expectations.","Therefore, when he met Elder Ning earlier, Lin Yuan had asked him to see if any spiritual ingredients in the Creation Master Association’s material room could evolve the Sharp Iron Horn Bull.","Lin Yuan opened the door and saw Elder Ning standing there with Ning Xuejun, who had taken part in the Creation Master’s test in the Creation Master Association. Ning Xuejun was Elder Ning’s granddaughter.","At that moment, she was holding a Bronze fey storage box.","When Ning Xuejun saw Lin Yuan, she nodded and greeted him, while a hint of surprise appeared in her eyes.","Lin Yuan had left a deep impression on her as few people like him had scored perfect marks in all three knowledge spirit qi occupations’ Rank 1 exam.","Seeing Lin Yuan again, Ning Xuejun was surprised that, as compared to before, his temperament seemed to have changed a lot.","Elder Ning looked at Lin Yuan and said with a laugh, “Little Yuan, I’ve prepared all the spiritual ingredients you’ve asked for.”","Lin Yuan was now finally relieved. At the very least, he did not have to waste time collecting the spiritual ingredients needed to evolve the Sharp Iron Horn Bull into Legend. He touched the back of his head and smiled cheerfully. “Elder Ning, I’m sorry to trouble you.”","The Bronze Sharp Iron Horn Bull needed a huge amount of ferromanganese ores and metal essences to evolve to Legend. These two were not very rare spiritual ingredients.","The metal essences were the crystals left behind after a mixture of many metals was forged at a high temperature, while the ferromanganese ores were dark-blue sheet metal in the deep earth.","The ferromanganese ore was particularly hard. If one touched it, their fingers would feel a stinging sensation from the sharpness of the metal.","The metal essences and the ferromanganese ores were two kinds of spiritual ingredients, of which 250 kilograms of metal essences and 1,000 kilograms of ferromanganese ores were needed.","The metal essences’ price was about 2 Radiance dollars/500g, while the ferromanganese ores cost nearly 8 Radiance dollars/500g.","In the past, Lin Yuan could not take out this amount of nearly 20,000 Radiance dollars. But ever since he obtained Cheng Wu’s beetle-shaped fey storage box and the mountain of Radiance dollars in it, his hands were no longer tied. If he needed spiritual ingredients to nurture a fey, he could just buy them now.","Ning Xuejun handed the Bronze fey storage box to Lin Yuan and looked at Chu Ci, who was beside him. At a glance, she knew that Chu Ci was Lin Yuan’s younger sister, even if they had completely different temperaments.","Lin Yuan was the cheerful kind, allowing people to feel comfortable. On the other hand, Chu Ci was quiet and had a trace of coldness. Although she was smiling, she seemed to have a faint sense of detachment to everything besides Lin Yuan.","Despite their different temperaments, they had similar eyebrows. With a glance at their eyebrows, it was clear that they were siblings.","Ning Xuejun kindly reached out her hand and greeted Chu Ci, who was startled but revealed a faint smile and shook hands with her.","Upon seeing that, Elder Ning looked at Chu Ci and said with a laugh, “Little Yuan, you can’t take care of this little girl now that you’re going to nurture the fey inside. Why don’t I bring her out and let my granddaughter accompany her to stroll around?”","Lin Yuan had been thinking that he could not allow Chu Ci to stay bored in the breeding room while he was nurturing the fey. He needed to concentrate on nurturing the fey for five days. However, he could not bear to throw Chu Ci aside. He still felt more at ease, allowing Chu Ci to be with Elder Ning and Ning Xuejun.","Chu Ci turned to look at Lin Yuan. After he nodded, she followed Elder Ning and Ning Xuejun out of Lin Yuan’s breeding room, leaving only Lin Yuan inside.","Lin Yuan also took the metal essences and ferromanganese ores out of the Bronze fey storage box that Ning Xuejun had given him. Then, he touched the Sharp Iron Horn Bull’s horns and said, “Metal lump, eat these metal essences and ferromanganese ores, and I’ll upgrade your quality.”","Although the Sharp Iron Horn Bull was not as intelligent as Chimey, it could still understand Lin Yuan’s words. After understanding what Lin Yuan meant, the Sharp Iron Horn Bull immediately snorted and gobbled up all the metal essences and ferromanganese ores Lin Yuan had put on the ground.","Although these metal essences were 250 kilograms, and the ferromanganese ores were 1,000 kilograms, which all sounded a lot, both were very dense and unusually heavy. Therefore, they actually looked small in size.","Just as the Sharp Iron Horn Bull was happily eating the metal essences and the ferromanganese ores, Lin Yuan gently smiled as he looked at it.","In Lin Yuan’s opinion, the seriously injured Elite/Epic Sharp Rock Bull back then had been a great bargain, as it was an extremely good fey.","Now that Lin Yuan had money, he could easily buy a lot of defense-type feys that were more outstanding than the Elite/Epic Sharp Rock Bull.","Fortunately, it had comprehended the Sacrifice ability at Elite that allowed it to be above most of the defense-type feys.","Back then, when Lin Yuan’s body had recovered and could sense the spirit qi, he did not have the time to accumulate resources. Thus, it had been really hard for him to prepare a defense-type fey for Chu Ci.","As an older brother, Lin Yuan also did not have a guilty conscience. At that time, he had said, “I may not give you the best, but this is the best I can give you now.”","The Sharp Iron Horn Bull had transformed greatly due to its Sacrifice ability. It was now about to go through its second metamorphosis in life, which was also an extremely important ascension in Chu Ci’s life.","Every cell of the Sharp Iron Horn Bull’s body quickly absorbed the pure spiritual power that Lin Yuan channeled in its body.","The Sharp Iron Horn Bull’s cells seemed to have been activated by this pure spiritual power and showed a hungry state, scrambling to absorb the energy in the metal essences and ferromanganese in its stomach.","Time flew by, and Lin Yuan basically rested little these five days.","At that moment, the Sharp Iron Horn Bull suddenly started ‘mooing’.","The Sharp Iron Horn Bull that was nearly three meters in size had soared to three and a half meters, becoming even stronger. Its horns became even sharper as they flashed with a metallic luster. The Bronze Sharp Iron Horn Bull finally reached Legend.","Next, Chu Ci had to fuse the Willpower Rune with the Sharp Iron Horn Bull to evolve it into a Fantasy Breed."]},{"number":157,"title":"Chapter 157: The Rising Masstone in the Greenish-Black Halo","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","At noon, Chu Ci and Ning Xuejun returned after eating out together. For the past few days, after getting along with Chu Ci, Ning Xuejun always felt that she was repeatedly refreshing her senses.","At first, Ning Xuejun had felt that Chu Ci was indifferent and detached from everything apart from Lin Yuan. But after interacting with her, Ning Xuejun realized that was not the case. She did not feel that faint sense of detachment either.","Ning Xuejun finally understood that the sense of detachment actually originated from her character of not wanting to bother about anything that did not concern her, as well as a hint of shyness.","Elder Ning had been researching on how to nurture the Spiral-Toothed Shark, as usual, these days. Therefore, Ning Xuejun was always with Chu Ci, regardless of whether they were eating or resting, and they gradually became friends.","“Chu Ci, we’re not going to this place to eat tomorrow. Why do they have to put so much garlic in their cold dishes! I still have to attend to some newcomers for the Creation Master’s test in the afternoon!” Ning Xuejun pouted.","Upon hearing what Ning Xuejun said, Chu Ci took a piece of watermelon-flavored hard candy out of her pocket. It had a very refreshing watermelon flavor and could cover up the strong garlic smell in the mouth.","Chu Ci had always had the habit of putting a piece of hard candy in her pocket, as Lin Yuan used to get dizzy from time to time due to his weak body or him having low blood sugar because of the daily labor of maintaining a small store. She would give the hard candy to Lin Yuan when he was feeling dizzy.","Even though Lin Yuan’s body was now healthy again, Chu Ci still maintained her habit of nearly ten years.","When Ning Xuejun saw Chu Ci hand her the hard candy, her eyes lit up, and she put it in her mouth before saying exaggeratedly, “Chu Ci, the watermelon-flavored hard candy tastes so good! It’s much better than chocolate.”","Two spirit qi professionals were sitting in the hall on the first floor of the Creation Master Association. They seemed to be women in their 20s and were dressed very beautifully. They should have made an appointment with a Creation Master to nurture their feys.","At that moment, Chu Ci suddenly heard the long-haired female spirit qi professional say, “Last night, my best friend complained tearfully to me that her boyfriend of eight years cheated on her.”","The other short-haired female spirit qi professional was clearly interested and responded, “For what reason? Why did he cheat on her? Eight years are so long that they should even already have kids!”","The long-haired female spirit qi professional was fiddling with the decorations on her spirit qi clothes and said with great contempt, “There are no good men.”","The other spirit qi professional hurriedly replied, “Yes, I think so too! Otherwise, I wouldn’t have always been single.”","Just after she finished speaking, the long-haired female spirit qi professional next to her said with a sigh, “Eight whole years of relationship! Surprisingly, he couldn’t resist a single seduction from me.”","Ning Xuejun coughed after listening to this conversation, almost choking on the watermelon-flavored hard candy in her mouth.","Chu Ci revealed a strange look and could not help but think in her heart, Is this the world of adults? It’s just too scary! Luckily, I’m just a kid.","In the afternoon, Ning Xuejun received the newcomers who came to take the Creation Master test.","On the other hand, Chu Ci was in Ning Xuejun’s office watching the videos of defense-type spirit qi professionals fighting in the S Tournament on Star Web, hoping to learn their defense techniques. Just at this moment, she received Lin Yuan’s call.","When she entered his breeding room, she saw that her contracted Sharp Iron Horn Bull was much stronger than before, be it in size or the sharpness of its horns.","Lin Yuan was feeding some spiritual metal ingredients to the Sharp Iron Horn Bull so that it could accumulate more energy to prepare to evolve into a Fantasy Breed.","Lin Yuan stood up upon seeing Chu Ci come in and said, “Chu Ci, your Sharp Iron Horn Bull is now at Legend. Fuse the Willpower Rune that you’ve comprehended with it, and it’ll be able to evolve into a Fantasy Breed.”","Chu Ci looked at the Sharp Iron Horn Bull, surprised at its significant changes over five days. Although she knew what Creation Masters could do, she had never seen or felt that in school.","The Sharp Iron Horn Bull was rubbing its cheek affectionately against Chu Ci’s palm.","While Chu Ci was surprised at the Sharp Iron Horn Bull’s change, she also felt happy with its growth brought about by its quality upgrade.","The splendor and magnificence of life laid in development and evolution. Each development and evolution of a fey was a small epitome of the greatness of life.","Lin Yuan raised his brow at Chu Ci’s astonished look and said with a smile, “Only when you fuse the Willpower Rune with the Sharp Iron Horn Bull will it truly go through metamorphosis. Chu Ci, how did you come into contact with and comprehend the Willpower Rune? This is very important, as it will affect your exclusive skill.”","Chu Ci stuck out her tongue and carefully glanced at Lin Yuan before answering in embarrassment, “It was when I fought against the seniors, and the Sharp Iron Horn Bull was knocked down repeatedly, but it still got up and charged forward. Because of this, I felt its steel-like willpower and comprehended the Willpower Rune.”","Lin Yuan held his forehead. What else could he say? Chu Ci had gotten her Willpower Rune out of roughness!","Had his plan to forge his sister into an iron bucket been botched at this point?","Lin Yuan looked at Chu Ci’s cautious expression and rubbed the hair on her head before saying, “I’ll be behind you on your path, so just proudly stride forward!”","Chu Ci smiled brightly and nodded. Then, she said silently in her heart, Brother, I also want to tell you that I can stand behind you. Even if I can’t protect you, I think I can help you and fight side by side with you!","She summoned the Willpower Rune from the spiritual spatial zone. When she had summoned it outside previously, it had flashed past, so Lin Yuan had not had the chance to carefully feel it.","But now, this greenish-black Willpower Rune brought out unyielding willpower and a rich metallic feeling that made Lin Yuan feel moved. Through this Willpower Rune, he could see how hardworking a 15-year-old girl and her Bronze Sharp Iron Horn Bull had been.","Chu Ci fused this greenish-black Willpower Rune with the Sharp Iron Horn Bull, causing an intense mooing sound to resound in the breeding room.","It was not as calm as when the Jasmine Lily had evolved into a Fantasy Breed.","In the rich metal halo, the Sharp Iron Horn Bull’s body trembled violently, clearly enduring the pain. Suddenly, the metal halo flourished, and a pure masstone rose from the greenish-black halo.","At that moment, Lin Yuan and Chu Ci realized that the horns on its head and the sharp sword-like horn on its forehead instantly melted. Then, its body was enveloped in the sudden bloom of the metal halo."]},{"number":158,"title":"Chapter 158: Everything Is For Being Rougher","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Chu Ci witnessed its horns suddenly melt, and the metal halo envelop its body. When she heard the Sharp Iron Horn Bull’s painful mooing, she could not help but be greatly anxious, her mind somewhat shaken.","At that moment, Lin Yuan said, “The Sharp Iron Horn Bull will undergo an all-round change when it evolves into a Fantasy Breed. Since its metamorphosis is based on its genetic model, the pain is inevitable when it reshapes its body.”","Lin Yuan’s words put Chu Ci at ease, even though the Sharp Iron Horn Bull was mooing painfully.","Chu Ci felt an indescribable heartache for this companion, which she had spent a long time with.","This greenish-black metal halo was unusually thick, but a ball of pure masstone rose from it and flowed in the metal halo before a kind of obsidian-like luster emerged. Gradually, the obsidian-like luster replaced the greenish-black metal halo. Then, there was a mooing sound that even shook the breeding room.","This obsidian-like luster became restless before condensing, and the Sharp Iron Horn Bull’s eyes absorbed all of it.","At that moment, along with Chu Ci’s cry of surprise, the Fantasy Breed Sharp Iron Horn Bull finally revealed its appearance.","If the Sharp Iron Horn Bull had sharp horns with heavy armor before, then its body was currently condensed with the strong aesthetics of a battle all over that was hidden behind the surging steel-like willpower, with a determination to go forward.","The Sharp Iron Horn Bull’s greenish-black body turned black, which was not just pure black. Rather, it was an obsidian-like flare where all sorts of colors would emerge from a beam of light.","When Lin Yuan looked at the Sharp Iron Horn Bull, he suddenly realized that it suddenly had aesthetics after evolving into a Fantasy Breed. It actually was in a five-colored black color.","But it must be said that the Sharp Iron Horn Bull’s obsidian-like body, combined with the smooth metal lines’ aesthetics, made it shed its bulkiness.","Based on just its gaze now, it seemed to be a domineering and determined beast.","The Sharp Iron Horn Bull’s melted horns did not grow and left two black holes there.","With the Sharp Iron Horn Bull’s intent, the metal element that spurt out of the holes would form all sorts of horns on its head.","After its complete evolution, it trotted to Chu Ci’s side and fondly rubbed her hands with its head.","In the past, the Sharp Iron Horn Bull had to be very careful every time it came into contact with her, as its sharp horns would cut her hand upon contact.","After evolving into a Fantasy Breed, the Sharp Iron Horn Bull no longer needed to worry about hurting Chu Ci. This was because its horn had elementalized and would condense based on its intent during a battle.","In Lin Yuan’s opinion, the elementalized horns were much stronger than its previous horns.","The Fantasy Breed Sharp Iron Horn Bull’s horns were much sharper and harder than before, but its elementalized horns’ strength did not lie in the hardness and sharpness. Rather, it was in its ability to change its form, length, and orientation at will.","The Sharp Iron Horn Bull had to adjust its horns’ angle to achieve maximum damage or defense against the target when charging.","Presently, as it charged toward a target’s weak spot, it could control its elementalized sharp horns and condense them into all sorts of forms, so fast that it was difficult to dodge.","It was like when the sharp horns of the Sharp Iron Horn Bull and other horned feys clashed together.","While the Sharp Iron Horn Bull used its elementalized horns to block, it could also instantly condense a sharp black horn to penetrate the target’s eyes or even pierce through the skull and brain.","Chu Ci was feeling the changes in the Sharp Iron Horn Bull when her eyes gleamed, full of surprise.","Lin Yuan used Morbius’s True Data ability to start checking the Sharp Iron Horn Bull’s true data.","[Fey Name]: Obsidian Iron Wild Bull","[Spirit-Lifeform Species]: Horned species/Bull species","[Fey Grade]: Bronze (10/10)","[Fey Type]: Metal","[Fey Quality]:: Fantasy I","Abilities:","[Iron Horn]: Enhance the metallic properties on the nose horn. Disregard injuries and smash into the enemy with full strength.","[Sacrifice]: When the contractor is injured, automatically split the damage with the contractor. If the contractor is injured, it will feed the contractor with its vitality.","Exclusive Skill:","[Pain Absorption]: When receiving damage, absorb a portion of the damage and turn it into vitality.","[Annihilation Gaze]: Domineering battle consciousness and war fervor drive its instinctive footsteps. The Obsidian Iron Wild Bull instantly transforms all the damage taken in a battle into a mental impact on the opponent.","Lin Yuan frowned at the true data. The Sharp Iron Horn Bull should now be called the Obsidian Iron Wild Bull.","Lin Yuan’s eyes lit up when he saw that the exclusive skill after the Sharp Iron Horn Bull had become a Fantasy Breed Obsidian Iron Wild Bull.","This rough fey was really something!","After the Sharp Iron Horn Bull evolved into a Fantasy Breed Obsidian Iron Wild Bull, it was getting farther and farther away from the trajectory of a defense-type fey.","But when observing the Obsidian Iron Wild Bull’s abilities, Lin Yuan discovered that its abilities had been upgraded after becoming a Fantasy Breed.","Its basic abilities had better penetration than before. The biggest change was its Sacrifice ability it had learned at Elite. While this rare ability could share the contractor’s damage, it now could feed its vitality to the contractor.","This made Lin Yuan look at the Obsidian Iron Wild Bull in a new light.","It seemed that as a defense-type fey, not only did the Obsidian Iron Wild Bull want to become a combat-class fey, but it also wanted to be a healing-type fey.","What a greedy bull!","In a team, defense-type spirit qi professionals were responsible for taking up the defense and needed to be healed by healing-type spirit qi professionals.","However, not only could the Sacrifice ability be used as a shield for the fey to get injured instead of the contractor, but it could also be used as a large mobile blood bag.","Combined with the exclusive skill, Pain Absorption, it had learned at Bronze, it could absorb part of the damage and turn it into vitality. It could directly raise the Obsidian Iron Wild Bull’s endurance.","Given its excellent healing system and the exclusive skill it had learned after becoming a Fantasy Breed, the Obsidian Iron Wild Bull had turned into the sharpest sword.","Nobody knew how much damage it would take in a battle.","After being attacked, the Obsidian Iron Wild Bull could absorb part of the damage and replenish its vitality. If the opponent could not kill it in one strike, it would be no different than an unkillable cockroach.","Based on its Annihilation Gaze, if the Obsidian Iron Wild Bull unleashed a mental attack through its eyes from all the damage it took during the battle, then the feys or spirit qi professionals hit by it would likely become fools or even die.","Lin Yuan found that the Obsidian Iron Wild Bull was simply a defense-type fey that could attack and heal, but all these were for the sake of being a rougher fey.","Lin Yuan recorded the Obsidian Iron Wild Bull in his little notebook and blamed Chu Ci’s roughness on it.","However, he then realized that the Obsidian Iron Wild Bull’s rare Sacrifice ability and the Vajra Butterfly seemed to be able to help him with his plan of turning his sister into an iron bucket.","Would you be afraid of an iron bucket who could counterattack and replenish her vitality?","But Lin Yuan felt that his previous plan needed to be modified again. Just as Chu Ci looked at him, another refined version of his plan arose in his heart."]},{"number":159,"title":"Chapter 159: Spirit Food Pavilion","paragraphs":["In Lin Yuan’s opinion, with the Fantasy Breed Obsidian Iron Wild Bull and the Bronze/Legend Vajra Butterfly, Chu Ci should have few worthy opponents among her peers and in the Redbud Intermediate Spirit Qi Academy. At the same time, its Annihilation Gaze gave it a proper means of attack.","It did not only have a basic attack like inflicting damage with its horns.","Now, it could attack on a mental level.","I’ll hit you if you hit me, and I’ll do the same if you hit me again!","But if you hit me after I replenish my vitality with Pain Absorption, watch me use my Annihilation Gaze!","An iron bucket was not scary, but one full of thorns and with automatic recovery was!","However, Chu Ci’s combat style was more inclined toward an individual, rather than taking up the defensive duties in a team. Therefore, Lin Yuan would have to focus on team defense in his future choice of feys for her. This was because a true defense-type spirit qi professional could not be separated from the team.","“Lin Yuan, this little iron block is so strong now after becoming a Fantasy Breed! I can sense its power has increased over five times than before!”","Lin Yuan’s eyebrows jumped. Was it really appropriate to call such a rough Obsidian Iron Wild Bull a little iron block?","“Not only has its strength improved, but it has also experienced a complete change in other aspects. When you go to the live combat class and fight with the senior who injured your arm, you’ll know.”","Upon hearing that, Chu Ci’s eyes lit up, and she said, “Then I’ll wait until I try it when I go to the live combat class! Senior Zhao Liang is the Year 3 training class representative. I can get some credits if I can beat him.”","Lin Yuan snorted lightly and thought, If Zhao Liang, that Year 3 class representative of the live combat class, fights against the Fantasy Breed Obsidian Iron Wild Bull, it will certainly give him a good time!","As one needed to fight freely to truly achieve the purpose of real training, even if the live combat class teacher was watching, it was inevitable to get injured. Although Lin Yuan knew he could not blame Senior Zhao Liang for Chu Ci’s injury, she was his younger sister! Also, he always had a double standard when it came to her!","Chu Ci sent food over to Lin Yuan daily these few days. When she sent him his three meals, she realized that he would only eat one meal, which was before his daily rest. Also, Lin Yuan had been enhancing her fey.","Even though Chu Ci had watched Lin Yuan suffer ever since she was young, she inevitably felt heartbroken seeing him like that.","It was now afternoon, but Lin Yuan had yet to eat, so Chu Ci said, “Lin Yuan, let’s go eat outside!”","Chu Ci wanted to say they would go to eat his favorite food. Even though she rarely strolled around in Redbud City, her classmates would inevitably talk about it, so she unintentionally also noted some places.","When she thought about it, she realized that Lin Yuan never seemed to have expressed any food he loved or hated in particular from a young age.","Every time she picked up two more chopsticks of dishes, he would rarely take those dishes to eat and leave them all for her.","When the two of them had been depending on each other in the past, he would ensure two dishes for every meal, no matter how hard it was, even though each dish’s serving was so pathetic that it would be gone in with just picking them with the chopsticks once or twice.","Lin Yuan had always been caring for her. She remembered little childhood sufferings, but every scene in her memory was the sweetness of relying on each other.","Fortunately, Lin Yuan also felt hungry at this point. He had been focused on raising the fey’s quality earlier and hence did not feel hungry.","Now that Chu Ci had evolved the Obsidian Iron Wild Bull into a Fantasy Breed, he had completed the goal of renting the breeding room in the Creation Master Association.","When Chu Ci said they would go out and eat, Lin Yuan really felt that his stomach was empty, even though it did not grumble.","“Let’s go. We’ll bid goodbye to Elder Ning, and I’ll bring you to eat your favorite seafood.”","Chu Ci revealed a bright smile. He would always think about what she loved to eat first.","When Lin Yuan and Chu Ci arrived at Elder Ning’s office, they realized he was not there. Lin Yuan thought that he should be nurturing the Spiral-Toothed Shark in the breeding room.","He then brought Chu Ci to the hall on the first floor and found Ning Xuejun, who was receiving newcomers in the hall at the moment.","Ning Xuejun was sitting on a chair, waiting for the newcomers taking the Creation Master test to come out. Lin Yuan went forward and said, “Sister Xuejun, I’m done with the breeding room. Thank you for taking care of Chu Ci for the past few days. We’ll be leaving. Please tell Elder Ning on our behalf.”","Ning Xuejun nodded with a smile and replied, “No problem. He said the Spiral-Toothed Shark would be evolving in the next few days, so his mind is in the breeding room.”","Ning Xuejun then made a calling gesture to Chu Ci, who immediately returned the same gesture and revealed a bright smile.","Lin Yuan felt warm at that sight. Other girls of Chu Ci’s age were well-protected and made good friends.","Ever since Chu Ci started attending school, he had never heard her talk about friends. It now seemed that Chu Ci and Ning Xuejun had gotten along and become friends, which made him feel at ease.","Lin Yuan had never wanted Chu Ci to be too mature but hoped that she could enjoy her childhood to the fullest. For so many years, this was the reason Lin Yuan had worked so hard. Otherwise, he would not have insisted on Chu Ci attending school.","After leaving the Redbud City’s Creation Master Association, Lin Yuan brought Chu Ci to the Spirit Food Pavilion not far away.","The Spirit Food Pavilion was an organization similar to Ostrich Logistics. It was just that the Ostrich Logistics did logistics while the Spirit Food Pavilion opened restaurants.","The Spirit Food Pavilion had opened restaurants in all the 32 major cities in the Radiance Federation. It made all the meals with various spiritual ingredients.","It also had all sorts of famous, excellent wine, which was very popular in the Radiance Federation.","There were no delicacies cooked with the ingredients from Normal and Elite feys.","Bronze was the lowest grade of the ingredients, and some signature dishes even had Platinum ingredients.","However, the price of meals made of Platinum ingredients was astronomical. Few of those people who were not rich could afford to pay the price.","Lin Yuan had brought Chu Ci here because the seafood was very delicious and famous in the entire Radiance Federation. On the other hand, she was now studying at the Redbud Intermediate Spirit Qi Academy and had to train every day.","Since this was a precious prime time in Chu Ci’s life, Lin Yuan intended to give her long-term custom-made set meals with spiritual ingredients from the Spirit Food Pavilion, and the Spirit Food Pavilion would deliver her daily three meals.","Although there was not much effect eating food with nutritious spiritual ingredients for a few days, it was different when accumulated.","When Lin Yuan walked to the Spirit Food Pavilion entrance, he saw a young couple arguing.","“Jiang Yan, let’s break up! You’re simply eating too much!”","The girl slammed her fists on the boy’s head. “My name is Zhang Yan!”","The boy was stunned. “Which Zhang[1]?”","The girl gave him another slam. “It’s Zh-ang[2], Zhang! You ordered one plate of chicken wings, and I only ate all four of them! How am I eating too much!”","At that moment, Lin Yuan suddenly heard someone call him from behind. He turned around and found an acquaintance.","[1] The Zhang here is written as 章.","[2] The Zhang here is written as 张."]},{"number":160,"title":"Chapter 160: Little Frog Findings Its Mother","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","When Lin Yuan turned around, he found the person calling him was Ling Wu, who had brought him to meet Ling Xiao in Redbud City.","Ling Wu quickly took two steps forward and said, “Lord Lin Yuan, are you here to eat at the Spirit Food Pavilion?”","Lin Yuan nodded and did not have the strength to criticize how Ling Wu addressed him. He smiled and looked at Chu Ci before answering, “I’m here to have a meal with my sister.”","Ling Wu looked at Chu Ci and could not help but feel his heart thumping. As Ling Xiao’s subordinate officer, even though Ling Wu did not know why Ling Xiao had brought Lin Yuan to the Royal Capital, based on Ling Xiao’s attitude toward Lin Yuan, he knew that Lin Yuan had an extraordinary background.","Thus, he hurriedly said, “Lord Lin Yuan, your sister is a Redbud Intermediate Spirit Qi Academy student? At noon, the principal will also be present in the private room on the Spirit Food Pavilion’s third floor. Why don’t both of you go there?”","Lin Yuan shook his head. “I’ll just have a good meal with my sister, so I won’t be going.”","Upon hearing that, Ling Wu nodded and did not speak further. He took his leave and went into the Spirit Food Pavilion.","Chu Ci looked at Lin Yuan and said, “Lord Lin Yuan?”","Lin Yuan looked at her and replied, “Lordess Chu Ci, please speak your mind.”","Chu Ci was a little shocked. Based on Ling Wu’s words, although she knew that Lin Yuan was very formidable, she did not expect him to be doing so well.","Nonetheless, she was not too surprised. When she had seen Lin Yuan talking to Elder Ning in the Creation Master Association, she had already been surprised.","Even if Ling Wu was City Lordess Ling Xiao’s subordinate officer, he was incomparable to Elder Ning, the Creation Master Association’s Vice President.","Lin Yuan had rejected Ling Wu because, in his opinion, Chu Ci just needed to rely on her own talent and strength.","Earning respect with strength would earn one dignity.","It was just like when Cheng Rui was conferred as the top Creation Master of the younger generation and named as ‘Tribunal Sun’ when he was at Class 2.","Perhaps, those who were not within the Creation Masters’ circle would feel envious. Still, based on Long Tao’s attitude toward Cheng Rui, Lin Yuan knew that Cheng Rui, who had earned the title of being a genius by fame alone and not strength, was nothing more than a clown in the eyes of the true geniuses.","After all, in a world where martial arts were respected, strength was the foundation of everything.","Lin Yuan hoped that Chu Ci could later embark on a path full of splendor.","Everyone had free will, but in the end, the only answer was the righteous way of life.","When they entered the Spirit Food Pavilion, they saw the decorations inside had ancient elegance. Deep mellow zither music played, just like Rain Pattering on the Banana Leaves1. The zither sound was tranquil and gave people a comfortable feeling of shunning the world.","Even though Lin Yuan had lived two lives, he also had to sigh.","The Spirit Food Pavilion had almost reached the point of being impeccable from its exquisite decoration alone.","Lin Yuan and Chu Ci did not go to the private room upstairs. Instead, they sat down in the hall where there were many diners around them.","Although eating in the bustling hall was not as quiet as in the private room, there was the fragrance of food.","Lin Yuan pushed the menu to Chu Ci, who looked at the prices and pushed it back to him. She said, “Lin Yuan, this place is really too expensive! Why don’t we go to another place? The barbecued fish place you took me to last time was super delicious.”","Lin Yuan rubbed the hair on her head and handed the menu back. “I have money now. I can afford whatever you like.”","Chu Ci took a very long time but only ordered two seafood stew made with Bronze ingredients.","Lin Yuan took the menu and ordered several dishes made from Silver ingredients according to Chu Ci’s liking.","Although the Steamed Fish with Chilli Pepper was made with Silver ingredients, the chili peppers were Gold ingredients.","Chu Ci looked at Lin Yuan worriedly, afraid that he would overspend on this meal and cause him to be money-tight afterward.","He could understand her thoughts. After all, they had been frugal for over ten years. However, he wanted to change her way of thinking. They had to be frugal when they had no money, but now that he had money, it would be a waste not to spend it.","At that moment, the dishes they ordered were served one by one. While the service staff was serving them, they heard a little girl around five or six years old at a nearby table ask, “Mom, if the little frog doesn’t return home, will its mother be worried?”","The middle-aged woman at her side was clearly her mother. She was taking the braised bullfrog dish when the little girl asked that question, causing her hands to freeze in the air. She felt awkward and did not know how to answer her.","Then, the service staff who served Lin Yuan hurriedly went forward to relieve the situation and said, “It won’t. They’re all here.”","Lin Yuan was drinking the seafood stew and nearly choked by the shrimp inside. This answer that destroyed one’s naivety was simply outstanding!","He could see that Chu Ci was happily eating this meal made from spiritual ingredients. Upon sensing how she was, he also ate a lot more than before.","Even though it was Lin Yuan’s first time at the Spirit Food Pavilion, he always felt that the taste was familiar, as though he had tasted them in the past.","After the meal, Lin Yuan booked two months of set meals made from Silver spiritual ingredients for Chu Ci. Given Chu Ci’s current rank, she was most suited to eat such food.","After that, he brought her to the Treasure Pavilion in Redbud City and bought a huge batch of metal spiritual ingredients and energy nectar that the Fantasy Breed Obsidian Iron Wild Bull and Vajra Butterly needed to regularly eat, respectively.","After this purchase, Lin Yuan found that if he used a low-grade fey storage box to store so many spiritual ingredients, it would be inconvenient for Chu Ci. Thus, he ordered a custom Diamond fey storage box from Ostrich Logistics for her.","Although Lin Yuan knew that it was very expensive, he did not expect such an outrageous price. If not for Cheng Wu’s Radiance dollars, he really could not afford the Diamond fey storage box.","Lin Yuan deliberately did not evolve the Obsidian Iron Wild Bull into Silver because Bronze Fantasy Breed feys were more reflective of their talents.","Since Chu Ci was going to pursue the route of a genius, then she would have to go until the end!","Lin Yuan had accomplished his goal of coming to meet Chu Ci. Then, he discreetly gave the bottle of Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar to Chu Ci and said, “Chu Ci, this Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar can cleanse the impurities in your body and raise your potential. Drink all of it, and you can cleanse all the impurities in your body at once.”","Seeing Lin Yuan speak so solemnly, Chu Ci remembered his words. Even though she did not know what the Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar was, it must be something extraordinary if it could cleanse the impurities in the body and raise her potential.","Ever since Lin Yuan had left last time, Chu Ci had applied for the school’s single dormitory so that she could have enough private space to better improve her strength. When she returned to the dorm, she would first drink all the Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar.","After sending Chu Ci back to school, Lin Yuan went to meet City Lordess Ling Xiao. She and Elder Ning were considered experts who had helped Lin Yuan, so he respected them both very much.","Before he left Redbud City after doing that, he called his master, the Moon Empress."]},{"number":161,"title":"Chapter 161: Congratulations! It Hasn’t Been Healed!","paragraphs":["In the Radiant Moon Palace’s breeding room, the Moon Empress was concocting with spiritual ingredients. With her natural movements, she completed a bottle of light-purple concoction.","The Moon Empress shook her hand, and the light-purple concoction turned into an aromatic mist that enveloped a Diamond/Epic lotus fey in the lotus pond. This fey quickly absorbed the light-purple aromatic mist, and in a moment, it evolved into Diamond/Legend.","But when doing so, most of the aromatic mist was used up. What was left spread out and was absorbed by the other lotus feys in the lotus pond.","At that moment, the Moon Empress’s cell phone, which she had not used for a long time, on the table rang.","If she wanted to meet anyone, she could just summon them. If anyone wanted to meet her, they had to see whether they were worthy enough to do so.","The Moon Empress did not save many numbers in her cell phone besides those exceptional experts from the Radiance Federation. Of course, there were exceptions, such as Lin Yuan.","The Moon Empress looked at her cell phone, and a gentle smile crept on her cold face when she saw the caller ID. She answered the call. “Lin Yuan, it’s been a while since you came to see me at the Radiant Moon Palace.”","Lin Yuan hurriedly replied, “Master, I went to the Endless Forest for wild harvesting some time ago. I’m now in Redbud City again. I’ll go visit you when I go to the Royal Capital.”","He did not tell her about the dimensional rift outside Millstone Town and the battle that had ensued, as he was afraid she would worry.","Although he said nothing, the Moon Empress had long known about it since it was such a big thing that involved Lin Yuan.","Upon finding out, the Moon Empress marveled at Lin Yuan’s strength. She had always known that he had exceptional talents as a Creation Master, but she did not expect him to be such a powerful combat-class spirit qi professional.","While she was proud of Lin Yuan, she could not help but feel that she had neglected her duties.","The Moon Empress was not worried about Lin Yuan’s safety, as the Mother of Bloodbath was his Path Protector. It could take Lin Yuan away in one piece from even a Class 3 dimensional rift.","After chatting with the Moon Empress for a while, Lin Yuan stated his purpose of calling her. “Master, I would like to ask you a favor.”","Upon hearing that, the Moon Empress nearly giggled in joy. During that period, she had been worried to death. What should she do when her independent disciple did not rely on her, his master?","As a result, the Moon Empress, who rarely went onto Star Web, even searched for posts there but did not find any answers.","She then anonymously posted a post for help, but the answer she had received made her so angry that she almost crushed her phone.","If Cold Moon had not found out that the Moon Empress was angry and had taken the initiative to crush the cell phone on her behalf, the Moon Empress would have crushed it instead.","Now that the Moon Empress heard Lin Yuan had something he needed her help with, the sense of accomplishment as his master arose in her heart.","“Tell me, what do you need my help with?” The Moon Empress said very generously because there was nothing in the world she could not do.","Afterward, Lin Yuan told her about Chu Ci’s situation and his thoughts.","Upon hearing that, the Moon Empress could not help but hold her forehead. She had been happy for nothing. Her disciple sought her help not because he was in trouble but because of his sister.","Nonetheless, the Moon Empress replied very solemnly, “Lin Yuan, don’t worry. I’ll ask Cold Moon to get this done.”","After hanging up the phone, Lin Yuan then ordered a Platinum Divine Travel Black Swallow on Star Web and rode it to the Royal Capital.","When he returned to the Royal Capital, he first confirmed his store location.","During this period, Liu Jie had searched for quite a few locations and had sent Lin Yuan the details of each place.","After narrowing them down, Lin Yuan then realized two places were quite good. One of them was where he had gone for an appointment but had been attacked by Cheng Wu, while the other was an excellent location in the Royal Capital’s bustling area.","Lin Yuan needed to choose between the two locations—the well-located bustling area where it was easy to set up the store or the huge one with the nice scenery located in the remote suburbs. However, he still needed to see the places before choosing one.","After he confirmed his store location in the Royal Capital, he would enter a long period of seclusion inside. Firstly, he had to fuse Chimey with the Twilight Willpower Rune and evolve it into a Fantasy Breed. He would then put the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee in Red Thorn’s corrosive cavity and let it hatch. After that, he would evolve the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee into Gold.","Given his strength, Lin Yuan had the possibility of climbing to the 100th floor of the Star Tower and ascending to the Celestial Stairway.","If he were to be fighting and raising his rank in the Celestial Stairway, he could most likely be matched with the Radiance Alliance’s young pinnacle experts.","Lin Yuan had always kept Liu Jie’s Insect Queen in the Pure Land of Bliss. In these few months, the Insect Queen, which had been in imminent danger, had more or less recovered. As long as he spent a few days healing it, it could completely recover. At that time, Liu Jie could restore the Heart of Insect Swarm’s strength, which ranked Sequence #39 in the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","...","Liu Jie, who was helping Lin Yuan find the locations for his store in the Royal Capital, was standing there in a confrontation.","“Liu Jie, you’re becoming worse! You used to be a member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence, yet you’re actually working as a retainer for a Class 2 Creation Master.”","A man with a pair of peach blossom eyes[1] shouted at Liu Jie. His tone seemed to have a fit of indescribable anger.","But before he could finish his words, a thick voice sounded from the side, stopping the man with the peach blossom eyes from speaking further.","The man with the thick voice turned to Liu Jie and said, “Liu Jie, Bai Hao has a temper like this. When he learned that you were injured, he looked around the entire world for you, but you disappeared without a word.”","Bai Hao snorted and turned away from Liu Jie.","Liu Jie did not expect that he would meet his former teammates. Before Liu Jie had gotten injured, Liu Jie, Bai Hao, and Wang Fan would always go out to train and do missions.","However, after Liu Jie had gotten injured and learned that he could not recover, he felt downhearted and left the Royal Capital.","He had bidden goodbye to his identity of Heart of Insect Swarm, the former Sequence #39 in the Radiance Hundred Sequence, and had become an ordinary down-and-out adventurer.","Upon hearing Bai Hao’s words, Liu Jie, who always had a good temper, frowned and responded in a low voice, “I work for him not because he’s a Creation Master of a certain class or his strength.”","He lowered his head to look at the Class 2 Creation Master crest on his chest and felt that it was particularly hot.","Two months ago, a youth had given him hope for a new lease of life while he was desperate and down, allowing him to once again find his value, his dream, his persistence, and the meaning of his life.","Therefore, Liu Jie had sworn an oath with the Willpower Rune to dedicate his future life as a retainer knight.","However, Liu Jie’s words made Bai Hao tremble. He clenched his teeth and looked at Liu Jie before asking, “Has your Insect Queen been healed?”","When Liu Jie shook his head, Bai Hao clapped. “Congratulations! It hasn’t been healed.”","Bai Hao then left with Wang Fan, who wanted to say something. Wang Fan sighed as he looked at Bai Hao and did not say what he wanted to.","Bai Hao turned around to look at Wang Fan and asked very seriously, “Wang Fan, how much money do you have?”","Wang Fan took out his Star Web Card and handed it to him. “I should have over 20,000,000 Radiance dollars in it.”","Bai Hao took Wang Fan’s Star Web Card and replied, “I’ve saved some money in the past two years, so I have 32,000,000 Radiance dollars in my Star Web Card. Counting yours in, we have over 50,000,000 Radiance dollars. Let’s see if we can get Liu Jie’s Insect Queen healed!”","Wang Fan had long known about Bai Hao’s temper and said helplessly, “You never speak properly. You have a sharp tongue but a soft heart. Have you never thought that you would hurt Liu Jie when you clapped your hands?”","Bai Hao immediately went silent and only said after some time, “He hurt me first. He left without saying a word and did not treat me as a brother.”","Wang Fan was speechless for a moment and did not speak.","When Liu Jie had been in trouble, the three of them had just pooled their money together to buy spiritual ingredients for Bai Hao to evolve his fey.","Liu Jie had lost his capabilities and had pooled all his savings in his Star Web Card for Bai Hao, so the latter did not know how Liu Jie had been getting along all these years.","At that moment, Bai Hao said, “Before Liu Jie’s Insect Queen is healed, I won’t spend a single penny. I’ll save them for its treatment.” He then let out a strange cry. “Ugh! I can’t reward the Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess anymore during this period. I don’t know if I can maintain my spot of being the top contributing fan.”","Wang Fan rolled his eyes. Bai Hao was becoming more and more like a child. He watched the Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess’s live-streaming on Star Web daily and even rewarded it. He was really hopeless.","[1] Alluring eyes like the shape of a peach blossom petal."]},{"number":162,"title":"Chapter 162: Heart of Insect Swarm","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Lin Yuan sat on the Divine Travel Black Swallow’s back and endured the discomfort on his butt. He could not help but have the idea of nurturing an avian transportation fey.","Given his spiritual energy, although he could still contract with a Normal/Normal fey that would not use much of his spiritual energy, he clearly would not leave his contracted fey spot for an avian transportation fey.","Lin Yuan was a Creation Master. If he nurtured an avian fey from a young age, even if he did not form a contract with it or could not command it to fight well, there would be no problem using it for transportation.","Before leaving Redbud City, he entered the Spirit Lock spatial zone once again. He found that in the past few months, the Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus within had produced young new leaves.","Although the Cinnabar Osmanthus Haworthia, which he cared most about, still looked withered, he was surprised to find that it had extended its roots and grown on the Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus’s trunk. This clearly meant that the Cinnabar Osmanthus Haworthia was starting to recover.","If he could evolve the Gold Cinnabar Osmanthus Haworthia into Platinum after it was healed, then it could produce one to three fruits. Lin Yuan could also grow his spiritual energy by eating those fruits.","As he looked at the mountains and white clouds while on the Divine Travel Black Swallow’s back, even though he felt his heart and mind open up after looking at them for so long, he did not feel that the mountains and white clouds were hard to come by.","Lin Yuan had nothing to do, so he took the Insect Queen, which had been recovering from its damaged roots, out of the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","This journey would take a few days. Lin Yuan thought that he might as well completely heal its damaged roots before he met Liu Jie.","Actually, he could heal it all thanks to the fact that Liu Jie’s contracted source-type lifeform was the Insect Queen.","If it were other feys or source-type lifeforms at Platinum, Lin Yuan could not heal them.","The Insect Queen was a kind of special source-type lifeform. It needed a huge amount of spiritual energy based on its contract alone, and the contractor could not form a contract with other source-type lifeforms or feys. This was why Liu Jie only had one contracted fey, the source-type Insect Queen.","Once its roots were damaged, then Liu Jie did not have any other feys to use.","If other spirit qi professionals had feys with damaged roots and could not be healed, they could nurture other feys. Although a fey would greatly affect one’s talent if they could not use it, the contractor would not end up in a down-and-out state.","On the other hand, it also showed the Insect Queen’s power.","Liu Jie had long comprehended a Willpower Rune, but his Insect Queen was stuck at Epic, unable to upgrade to Legend. Therefore, even with the Willpower Rune, Liu Jie still could not evolve it into a Fantasy Breed.","Nonetheless, he was still ranked Sequence #39 in the Radiance Hundred Sequence, despite having the Insect Queen as his only fey.","Before the Insect Queen’s roots got damaged, Liu Jie had spent a lot of resources visiting Creation Masters everywhere to improve its quality. However, no Creation Masters could upgrade his fey from Epic to Legend. This was because all spirit fluids concocted with spiritual ingredients were not as helpful as the pure spirit qi for the Insect Queen.","The Insect Queen was a kind of lifeform that required extremely high pure spirit qi. In an extremely pure spirit qi environment, even if it was on the verge of death, it could absorb the highly pure spirit qi and activate the powerful self-repair function in its body to restore its damaged roots or even raise its quality.","Without pure spirit qi, no matter how powerful the spirit fluids concocted by Creation Masters were, it could not do so. This was also why after Liu Jie had gotten seriously injured when he guarded the Cold Frost City alone and held off the dimensional lifeforms for half an hour, the Bamboo Monarch, one of the Class 5 Creation Masters, had helped him. However, he still could not heal the Insect Queen’s damaged roots.","That was because the Bamboo Monarch had used all sorts of spiritual ingredients to produce spirit qi. Although there were various medicinal properties that could restore the damaged roots, they were not very useful for the Insect Queen. The best recovery medicine for the Insect Queen was pure spirit qi.","Despite the pure spirit qi in the spirit fluid that the Bamboo Monarch had prepared, it was not pure enough for the Insect Queen to activate its body’s self-repair function.","But it was different when Lin Yuan used his spiritual power to channel spirit qi into the Insect Queen’s body. He did not channel pure spirit qi. Instead, he purified the spirit qi in the world into pure spirit qi through his body before injecting it into the fey’s body.","To put it bluntly, Lin Yuan was a porter of spirit qi. He could make the spirit qi very pure while moving it.","At that moment, a purple flesh cocoon appeared in Lin Yuan’s hand. He channeled the spiritual power in his body and injected a huge amount of pure spirit qi into the Insect Queen’s body with his hands.","This purple flesh cocoon was thumping like a heart, absorbing the pure spirit qi from Lin Yuan like a bottomless pit, with an unusual joyfulness.","Lin Yuan suddenly opened his eyes wide in surprise after two days! He found that the Insect Queen had healed its damaged roots and evolved from Epic to Legend.","In other words, if Liu Jie fused his Willpower Rune with it, the Insect Queen would immediately become a Fantasy Breed. At that time, even if Liu Jie had completely wasted these two years, it was not a loss compared to the Insect Queen evolving into a Fantasy Breed.","It could even be said that after these two years of silence, Liu Jie, who would return with a Platinum Fantasy Breed Insect Queen, could be considered soaring into the sky like a phoenix’s nirvana.","Lin Yuan used Morbius’ True Data to check the Insect Queen.","[Fey Name]: Insect Queen","[Fey Species]: Bombycidae/Queen Insect","[Fey Grade]: Platinum (4/10)","[Fey Type]: Source/Spiritual","[Fey Quality]: Legend","Abilities:","[Bayonet Beetles]: The small beetles have black armor and six legs as sharp as blades.","[Shield Ladybugs]: The large ladybugs have thick armor. Their hard shells can resist physical and energy damage.","[Plasma Caterpillars]: The medium-sized caterpillars have a huge amount of plasma in their bodies that can cause paralysis and high electric shock damage.","[Lightning Gathering Moths]: The small moths can quickly gather lightning. A large number of them can gather a super-strong lightning cannon.","Exclusive Skill:","[Blast Recovery]: The Insect Queen can choose to explode the insects it produces and recover some energy contained in their bodies.","Lin Yuan finally understood why Liu Jie only had a Platinum Insect Queen two years ago.","Liu Jie was ranked as Sequence #39 in the Radiance Hundred Sequence and was known as ‘Heart of Insect Swarm’."]},{"number":163,"title":"Chapter 163: Complementing Combination","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","The Insect Queen had a very special method to obtain abilities. Unlike other feys and source-type lifeforms, which would obtain a corresponding ability when they progress in grade, the Insect Queen would obtain its abilities when it progressed to the next grade and consumed an insect-species fey. The insect-species fey’s genetic model would be engraved in the Insect Queen’s body. The Insect Queen would then absorb the genetic model and make its ability.","During combat, the Insect Queen could use up the energy in its body to rapidly reproduce the genetic model, producing the insect-species fey itself.","Take Liu Jie’s Gold Insect Queen’s abilities, Bayonet Beetle, Plasma Caterpillar, Lighting Gathering Moth, and Shield Ladybug. These four insect-species feys’ genetic models were all embedded within the Insect Queen’s body.","Lin Yuan could see that Liu Jie had put in a great amount of effort in the nurturing of the Insect Queen, especially in terms of the combination and choices of abilities.","When choosing each of the insect-species fey for the Insect Queen’s ability combination, Liu Jie didn’t pick those insect-species feys with extreme individual strength. Instead, he chose those with genetic models that were easy to replicate. At the same time, the insect-species feys with simple genetic models would have a qualitative change in strength as their numbers increased.","Take the Bayonet Beetles as an example. The Insect Queen was able to produce 100 of them quickly due to their simple genetic model. When a group of Bayonet Beetles crawled on the other feys’ bodies, it would feel like an execution of thousands of slashes due to their six blade-like legs.","The Shield Ladybug was a fey that was extremely adept at defense, and when in defense, it would open up an insect shield on its back. When a few of the Shield Ladybugs opened up their insect shields simultaneously, it would form a firm insect-armored wall. It was normally used to defend the Plasma Caterpillars that were adept at energy attacks but weak in defense.","The Plasma Caterpillars’ plasma wasn’t just extremely lethal, as they also had a paralysis effect. After getting paralyzed, the Bayonet Beetles would then attack relentlessly.","As for the Gold ability, it was the Lightning Gathering Moths. It was an insect-species fey that could fly in an agile manner while expending very little energy. The lightning attack from a single Lightning Gathering Moth wasn’t powerful. However, when an eclipse of Lightning Gathering Moths gathered lighting elements, they could blast out a destructive lightning cannon to create immense damage.","Furthermore, the Plasma Caterpillars’ plasma could also help the Lightning Gathering Moths gather lightning elements rapidly. It would greatly reduce the loading time required for the group of Lightning Gathering Moths to prepare the lightning cannon.","One had to admit that Liu Jie’s contracted Insect Queen was already a combatant with a comprehensive battle style.","Even though the Insect Queen was a Platinum fey and had yet to consume any insect-species fey for its Platinum ability, its current abilities already had an extremely good combination.","The Insect Queen was able to reproduce all sorts of insect-species fey combinations to battle, as though it was controlling an insect horde during a war.","When used along with the Insect Queen’s exclusive skill, Blast Recovery, it would be able to effectively reduce the Insect Queen’s energy consumption. Those severely injured insects could be used to self-destruct and regain plenty of energy, allowing the Insect Queen to reproduce new insects.","On the other hand, Blast Recovery could also scale up with the numbers. A single Bayonet Beetle might not be lethal or wouldn’t create great damage if it self-destructed alone. However, when many Bayonet Beetles exploded simultaneously, it would be enough to deal severe injuries and even threaten the enemy’s life.","A Platinum defense-type fey might be able to resist the explosion, but if a wound was blasted open, it would become a nightmare when other Bayonet Beetles crawled inside.","Lin Yuan was involuntarily amazed by the strength of this source-type lifeform, Insect Queen.","In Lin Yuan’s opinion, if any fey received a proper and effective nurturing, it might not be the strongest, but it would certainly be useful during battle. However, this idea could only be possible for Lin Yuan’s ability to channel spirit qi and help feys to evolve.","There was still close to an entire day of journey before reaching the Royal Capital, so Lin Yuan took a fey that he had captured in the Endless Forest out of the leaf-shaped fey storage box. It was a Normal, snake-species fey, the Green Bamboo Snake.","The small Green Bamboo Snake was extremely fast and adept at using its venomous fangs to deal damage. It was considered a rather good assassin, offense-type fey.","Lin Yuan started to channel his spiritual power after bringing out the Green Bamboo Snake, allowing large amounts of pure spirit qi to pour into the snake and enhance it.","Soon enough, Lin Yuan enhanced the Green Bamboo Snake to Bronze/Epic. Lin Yuan then stored this Green Bamboo Snake back into the leaf-shaped fey storage box.","If Lin Yuan wanted to open a fey shop, he would need to produce superior feys to build its reputation. For all spirit qi professionals, what could make them more insane than a Bronze fey with high quality?","A higher graded fey might be precious, and Lin Yuan might still be able to tame a Gold fey right now, but he would need to use a lot of effort and time. Enhancing a fey to platinum-grade was currently impossible for Lin Yuan. Furthermore, when the fey was at Bronze, the higher its quality, the more expensive it was.","A Bronze fey would be particularly cheap when its quality was Normal or Elite. However, once the Bronze fey had Flawless quality, the price would be more than most of the low-quality Silver feys. That was because Bronze feys with higher quality would have a higher chance of being enhanced to the Legend quality in the future. They just had to fuse a Willpower Rune with the fey to obtain a Fantasy Breed by then.","A Bronze/Epic fey was already the highest quality of Bronze feys in the market right now. Whenever a Bronze/Epic fey appeared in the Rare Lifeform Pavilion, it would be auctioned out for an astronomical price.","When a spirit qi professional formed a contract with a fey, they would always reserve some spiritual energy and wouldn’t use all the spiritual energy on the fey contract. One reason was due to the large number of resources required to nurture feys. Only a rare few individuals were able to afford the resources, even if they were from prestigious families.","Instead of pouring resources into five feys, why not gather the resources to nurture one main fey and two complementing feys? Also, the reserved spiritual energy would be used after comprehending a Willpower Rune.","Many spirit qi professionals would choose to form a contract with another low-grade fey and nurture them from the beginning. Because the faster a low-grade fey became a Fantasy Breed, the higher its potential would be.","Therefore, those who strived for these low-grade and high-quality feys were mostly experts who comprehended Willpower Runes but didn’t have high-quality and low-grade feys. Or some of the prestigious families wished to prepare a low-grade and high-quality fey for an exceptional junior of the family, allowing the junior to have a greater head start.","Thus, whenever a Bronze/Epic fey appeared, it would attract plenty of disputes. If Lin Yuan were to release a Bronze/Legend fey, the entire Radiance Federation might be shocked and would cause an intense contest between the major factions.","Lin Yuan wasn’t planning to release any Bronze/Legend fey, at least not for now.","To upgrade a Bronze fey to Legend quality would need at least five days. For now, Lin Yuan felt that the most important thing was for him to increase his spirit qi professional rank.","Only by increasing his spirit qi professional rank would he be able to enhance stronger feys and his strength would also improve along.","After Lin Yuan enhanced the Green Bamboo Snake, he didn’t enhance other feys. He closed his eyes to rest on the back of the Divine Travel Black Swallow.","When Lin Yuan woke up, it was already noon, and the Divine Travel Black Swallow had just arrived at the Royal Capital.","After alighting the Divine Travel Black Swallow, Lin Yuan felt half his butt was numb.","He gave Liu Jie a call first and fixed the time for their meeting in the afternoon. Subsequently, he went to the Leaning Moon Mountain and headed for the Radiant Moon Palace.","At the entrance of the Radiant Moon Palace, Lin Yuan saw the silver-robed Mystic Moon."]},{"number":164,"title":"Chapter 164: Picking a Spirit Attendant","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Mystic Moon was sweeping up the Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia’s fallen leaves at the Radiant Moon Palace entrance. Lin Yuan walked over and said, “Senior Mystic Moon, it has been a long time.”","Mystic Moon was originally very happy to see Lin Yuan but was shocked by Lin Yuan’s greeting. Mystic Moon immediately took a step forward and bowed. “Young Lord, you must not! I cannot afford to be called senior by the Young Lord!”","Mystic Moon’s voice was already clear, and his personality was particularly calm. Ηowever, a single greeting of a senior from Lin Yuan actually stirred him up.","Lin Yuan shook his head helplessly. Cold Moon had also said the same time, and Lin Yuan felt rather uncomfortable.","Lin Yuan then saw Mystic Moon handing over a bottle. Lin Yuan received it and realized it was filled with Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar. The bottle was huge, and if the nectar was poured out, it would probably fill up four or five bowls.","Lin Yuan raised his brows and looked at Mystic Moon with a confused expression.","“Previously, I mentioned that I would treat the Young Lord to the Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar, but I had to go for a mission. Now that the Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia flowers are fully developed in deep autumn, I have harvested them personally to make this bottle of Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar. After making it, I smelled it and felt that it was better than Cold Moon’s nectar.”","While speaking, Mystic Moon let out a bright smile.","Cold Moon had already set off for Redbud City. Had she been around now, she would have mercilessly exposed Mystic Moon. In order to personally make this bottle of Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar, Mystic Moon had wasted countless Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia flowers.","While Mystic Moon was letting out a bright smile, the Moon Empress’ voice echoed behind him. When the Moon Empress detected that Lin Yuan had arrived, she immediately came to the Radiant Moon Palace entrance.","As a result, when she saw Mystic Moon handing over a Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar bottle to Lin Yuan, she was so angry that she nearly choked.","“Mystic Moon, go to the Chef Supreme and help This Empress collect a Spirit Savory Pig.”","When Mystic Moon heard the Moon Empress’ voice, he quickly turned around and bowed. “Yes, Moon Empress. I shall go immediately.”","At this moment, Mystic Moon saw that the Moon Empress was holding a crystal bottle that was at least three times bigger than his bottle. It might be called a crystal bottle, but it was actually like a small barrel, and it was filled to the brim with Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar. He noticed that the Moon Empress was grinding her teeth while looking at him, and it felt as though her eyes were shooting a barrage of black dragon bullets.","Mystic Moon was confused at first, but when he looked at the Moon Empress’ eyes, he immediately found out what was happening. He silently felt that it wasn’t good as he was standing right in front of a gun barrel. He quickly turned around and left in a hurry to help the Moon Empress collect that Spirit Savory Pig from the Chef Supreme.","When Lin Yuan saw the Moon Empress, he quickly greeted her. The Moon Empress carried out a face-changing act and turned gentle. She then handed over the crystal bottle that was at least three times bigger than Mystic Moon’s bottle.","“Master personally made this Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar. I have added plenty of Lotus Heart Dew, and it is much better than Mystic Moon’s nectar.”","The Moon Empress had already recorded a punishment for Mystic Moon in her heart. My disciple hasn’t visited the Radiant Moon Palace for half a month, and you actually dare to give something This Empress’ disciple in front of me? Furthermore, you actually gave the same type of gift. Are you trying to infuriate This Empress to death!? Can you give this Empress a chance to show my good side in front of my disciple?!","Lin Yuan didn’t reject the bottle of Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar given by his master. It wasn’t because Lin Yuan wanted to rely on the Moon Empress, but he had already treated the Moon Empress as a blood-relative.","A gift from the elder must not be rejected!","This was a sign of respect and filial piety.","However, it was unknown how much Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia flowers were used to produce so much nectar. When Lin Yuan looked at the two Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassias at the Radiant Moon Palace entrance, he noticed that one of them didn’t have any more flowers, while the other didn’t have many flowers left either. There was only a thin layer of flowers left behind that were still on the branches.","Lin Yuan and the Moon Empress arrived at the Radiant Moon Palace’s inner palace to conduct a question and answer session that they hadn’t done for a long time. Lin Yuan had asked everything he didn’t understand during this period of time, while the Moon Empress answered all the questions.","The Moon Empress’ answers were very concise, and it was so clear that Lin Yuan was able to achieve speedy enlightenment. At the same time, the Moon Empress had also imparted some new knowledge to Lin Yuan in an inquiry method.","This time, the question and answer session lasted much longer, allowing Lin Yuan to receive a huge input of knowledge. During this session, the Moon Empress was also able to feel Lin Yuan’s improvement.","After the questions ended, the Moon Empress poured a cup of flower tea to Lin Yuan and asked, “Are you going to be developing in the Royal Capital for the next period of time?”","Lin Yuan nodded. “I wish to open a shop in the Royal Capital and increase my capability as a Creation Master. At the same time, I will prepare to compete for the Radiance Hundred Sequence.”","After hearing Lin Yuan’s response, the Moon Empress revealed a bright smile as she was very happy that Lin Yuan was going to stay in the Royal Capital. That was because Lin Yuan wouldn’t be going to places like Millstone Town or Redbud City, not visiting the Radiant Moon Palace for half a month again.","Presently, she was a master, as well as a senior. She finally understood why the Bamboo Monarch and the Chef Supreme would always be filled with emotions when mentioning their disciples.","It was the same for the Moon Empress now as she was now smiling much more than before as compared to the number of smiles she had in a year. She was also proud and happy to see her disciple growing.","“Since you wish to open a shop, how can you not have an assistant? Later on, pick a spirit attendant from the Radiant Moon Palace to be your assistant. She can help you to attend to the plants that are nurtured in the shop too.”","Which of the spirit attendants in the Radiant Moon Palace wasn’t a prodigy among Creation Masters? Most of them were so young and already had the capability of a Class 1 Creation Master. Some of the more talented ones were even Class 2 Creation Masters. For such prodigies to attend to plants, wouldn’t it be a waste of talent?","Any of the spirit attendants in the Radiant Moon Palace could open up a shop in the Royal Capital, and after a few years of development, their shop’s reputation would surely be great. However, if a spirit attendant was attending to the shop, it would certainly save Lin Yuan plenty of trouble.","The Moon Empress said to Cai Cha, who was brewing the tea, “Ask all of the spirit attendants to gather at the main palace. Let Lin Yuan pick his own assistant.”","Cai Cha immediately responded and carried out the task given by the Moon Empress. Over ten spirit attendants wearing light yellow robes were standing in the main palace in just a short moment.","Each of the spirit attendants had a kind of indescribable expectation. When they heard the news from Cai Cha, all of the spirit attendants wished they could become Lin Yuan’s assistant.","Lin Yuan was the Moon Empress’ disciple, and seeing how long Lin Yuan had been staying in the Radiant Moon Palace and how the Moon Empress treated him, it was obvious that Moon Empress treated her disciple with great importance. Even the two Moon Envoys, Cold Moon and Mystic Moon, would greet Lin Yuan respectfully as Young Lord.","The moment Lin Yuan became the Moon Empress’ disciple, he was already seated firmly on the Radiant Moon Palace’s second chair. If they could become Lin Yuan’s assistant, their status would be entirely different and might even be above the tea attendant sisters. In fact, they might even have comparable status with Cold Moon and Mystic Moon.","These spirit attendants were all young ladies, and it was obvious that most of them took the effort to put on some exquisite make-up before coming.","Wen Yu was currently holding a small amber bottle, but it was already empty. All of a sudden, Wen Yu heard a voice that made her frown.","“You are a sickly person, so why are you standing at the front? Hurry up and stand at the back.”","Wen Yu lifted her head and saw that it was none other than Jin Qi who was speaking to her.","“I am just standing in place according to our ranking exam last year. Is there a problem?”","Jin Qi immediately sneered in response. “One month later will be this year’s spirit attendants ranking exam. As a sickly person, you will definitely fail. Why do you still have the face to stand at the front?”","Wen Yu’s roots had already been healed after consuming the Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar, and her original talent had already been restored. In fact, the drop of Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar had actually allowed Wen Yu’s aptitude to improve further.","However, Wen Yu hadn’t informed any of these girls, who she had been treating as sisters in the past. During this period of suffering, Wen Yu had understood that these people weren’t even her friends, and it wasn’t worth it for her to invest any emotions.","Wen Yu was always indifferent and didn’t wish to compete, so she simply stood at the back. However, Wen Yu felt that the small amber bottle in her hand was actually boiling up."]},{"number":165,"title":"Chapter 165: Why Did She Grow a Mouth?","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Wen Yu was clenching that small amber bottle tightly and had unspeakable gratitude. She knew that it was that small drop of Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar in the bottle that had completely changed her fate.","Without the drop of nectar Lin Yuan had given her, Wen Yu knew that she was destined to be eliminated during the spirit attendant’s ranking exam, and she would need to give up her position as a spirit attendant. But with Lin Yuan’s drop of nectar, she was at least able to keep her position as a spirit attendant.","She might not be able to get ranked at the top, but even if she was at the bottom, as long as she could stay in the Radiant Moon Palace as a spirit attendant, she would still be able to climb up the rankings.","Furthermore, this drop of Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar had actually improved her constitution significantly.","All of the spirit attendants had similar talents, but Wen Yu’s improvement in strength was affected due to her damaged roots. Now that her aptitude was better, she would be able to catch up with other spirit attendants’ progress in just a matter of time.","When Wen Yu was walking toward the back, she took a glance at Jin Qi and realized that she was smiling. Thus, she looked at the entrance that was connected to the inner palace. Her face was beaming, and her eyes were filled with indescribable expectations.","Wen Yu couldn’t help sighing.","Ever since Jin Qi had learned that the Moon Empress had accepted a disciple that was around the same age as her, she had been filled with inappropriate thoughts. Wen Yu had reminded her, but in return, Wen Yu had received Jin Qi’s anger.","Wen Yu didn’t care if other spirit attendants would be picked, but Jin Qi would definitely not be picked—even though she was no. 2 among the spirit attendants—because their conversation that night had been brought to Lin Yuan’s ears by the autumn wind.","Just as Wen Yu walked to the back of all the spirit attendants, Jin Qi suddenly said to the spirit attendant standing in front of her, “Pan Yue! Why do you have a withered flower on your head?”","The spirit attendant called Pan Yue quickly removed the red flower on her head and took a look at it. It might not be withered, but it was rather listless. Pan Yue then quickly hid the red flower in her sleeve and said with frustration, “I have looked through many flowers, but you plucked all of them. You still dare to say it is withered, such shamelessness.”","When Jin Qi looked at Pan Yue, she felt much better. Pan Yue might be better looking than her, but it was only when she was quiet. Whenever Pan Yue spoke, everything would be torn apart. Why did a beautiful girl like her have to grow a mouth?","How could such an ignorant girl be picked?","Jin Qi was filled with confidence in herself. In terms of strength, she might only be ranked no. 2, but in terms of speech, Pan Yue would never be able to compare with her. Once Pan Yue started speaking, she would lose.","At that moment, two figures appeared at the entrance connected to the inner palace.","There was a woman wearing moon-colored robes with a cold expression and graceful bearing.","There was a handsome, sunshine youth with a faint smile. Anyone who saw him would feel that he was particularly amiable.","As the two figures walked into the Radiant Moon Palace’s main palace, all of the spirit attendants bowed in unison. “Greetings to the Moon Empress, greeting to Lord Lin Yuan.”","The spirit attendants might all be bending down, but they knew that they would be like carps leaping into the dragon gate and would never be the same again if they were picked. Therefore, when they were all looking at the ground, they were all nervous and filled with expectations.","Perhaps when Lin Yuan was making a choice, he would be picking someone randomly, and it was indifferent. However, to these spirit attendants, it was truly considered the greatest fated opportunities of their life.","The Moon Empress turned to look at Lin Yuan and said lightly, “Lin Yuan, pick one yourself. If you feel that one spirit attendant isn’t enough, then pick two.”","The Moon Empress’ words made all the spirit attendants delighted, but the youth immediately responded, “Master, one is enough.”","Lin Yuan only wanted to open one shop, so one spirit attendant was already enough. He didn’t feel it was necessary to have an additional spirit attendant.","When all the spirit attendants lifted their heads, they had varying expressions, but all of them had a sincere expectation.","When Lin Yuan glanced at all the spirit attendants, he realized that the only spirit attendant he was familiar with and had spoken with was only Wen Yu. He had quite a good impression of Wen Yu, so he simply pointed at Wen Yu.","Wen Yu was standing at a position farthest from Lin Yuan, and when he appeared, she was clutching onto the amber bottle with increasing strength. It would be false if Wen Yu said that she wasn’t nervous, and it would be even more pretentious if she said she didn’t wish for Lin Yuan to pick her. However, at the same time, Wen Yu wished to say thank you to Lin Yuan personally.","In Wen Yu’s heart, the person she was most grateful to was the Moon Empress, who had established her life. But now, there was another person, and it was Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan had rescued her shattered life, which was already established, allowing her shattered life to become settled again.","When Wen Yu saw Lin Yuan pointing at her, she felt as though all of her strength had vanished. Her mind was in chaos, as there was pleasant surprise, excitement, and also disbelief.","However, there was more of an indescribable peace of mind. If she was able to become Lin Yuan’s assistant, she wouldn’t have to say thank you to Lin Yuan. Instead, she could use her actions as an assistant to repay the favor to Lin Yuan.","When the Moon Empress saw Lin Yuan pointing at Wen Yu, she said, “The one that is picked can stay behind. The rest of the spirit attendants will go back to their respective tasks.”","The spirit attendants looked rather bewildered as none of them imagined that Wen Yu would be picked. The most astonished person was none other than Jin Qi.","Jin Qi had always been very confident in herself, but she knew that she might not be picked. Nonetheless, she never ever expected that Wen Yu would be picked. At this moment, Jin Qi knew that she wasn’t even qualified to be jealous.","The instant Wen Yu became Lin Yuan’s assistant, Jin Qi, and Wen Yu’s status had a drastic difference. If Wen Yu wished to take revenge on her, she could just find a reason for Jin Qi to be dismissed from the Radiant Moon Palace. All of her expectations and fantasies had turned gray now.","Just as Ji Qi was going to walk out of the Radiant Moon Palace with a disappointed expression, she heard a cracking voice that echoed in her ears. “If you find too many excuses for yourself and if it continues, anyone will become depressed.”","When hearing this statement, Jin Qi turned around to see a calm Pan Yue. Before Jin Qi could get angry, she couldn’t help asking, after seeing Pan Yue’s face that wasn’t disappointed at all, “Are you not disappointed at all?”","Pan Yue rolled her eyes and giggled. “What is there to be disappointed about? As long as I can go onto the Star Web to see those energetic young people, my life is fulfilled.”","Jin Qi felt even worse after hearing Pan Yue’s strange peal of laughter.","The Moon Empress gave some comments after Lin Yuan picked Wen Yu and returned to the inner palace.","The Moon Empress knew everything that happened within her Radiant Moon Palace, but she had never meddled in Wen Yu’s affairs before.","For any place with people, it would be a martial world, and the martial world was a place of contest. It was already so for places with ordinary people, let alone the Radiant Moon Palace where all the spirit attendants were prodigies.","The contest between spirit attendants was just like the calm water on the surface—there were raging undercurrents.","But it was because of this reason that true pillars were able to be filtered out from all of these prodigies."]},{"number":166,"title":"Chapter 166: Why Can Frogs Fly?","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","After Lin Yuan had lunch with the Moon Empress, he took Wen Yu down the Leaning Moon Mountain and was prepared to head toward the agreed place with Liu Jie.","Lin Yuan was fiddling with his cell phone, ready to book an avian fey. It was indeed hard for him to travel without an avian fey.","When Wen Yu secretly glanced at Lin Yuan fiddling with his cell phone, her eyes lit up. She then said softly, “Young Lord, I have ready-made avian feys here. You don’t need to book them from Star Web.”","She channeled her spiritual energy and summoned a four-meter-long bird with a wingspan of six meters.","Lin Yuan felt that the large bird looked rather beautiful. It was covered in white feathers with a faint luster that looked like scattered sunlight.","He used True Data to check it and discovered that this large bird was a Silver Sunlight Egret. Ardea feys were relatively rare among the avian feys, but they also had high potential, growing up mostly with extraordinary combat power.","However, Sunlight Egrets were a surprise among them. They were a kind of feys with limited attack abilities. Their bodies’ scattered sunlight could soothe one’s mind, and most abilities they comprehended were to better increase their speed.","It could be said that Sunlight Egrets were very outstanding avian transportation feys. They were occasionally sold and even bought at high prices.","Due to their size, when they were at Bronze, they could grow to two meters with a four-meter-long wingspan. They could grow to four meters with a six-meter-long wingspan when they reached Silver, just like Wen Yu’s Sunlight Egret.","Few Silver avian feys could grow that big. If they reached Gold, Sunlight Egrets could carry dozens of people on their backs. Also, they had an elegant posture and looked graceful when they flapped their wings, so they were considered luxurious avian transportation feys.","Lin Yuan did not expect that Wen Yu would make a contract with such a fey. Ordinary Creation Masters would not usually contract with a Sunlight Egret, even if they nurtured one, as they could command their nurtured avian transportation feys without a contract.","After all, the Sunlight Egrets’ greatest advantage was their high visuals, fast speed, and specialization in transportation. Nonetheless, they almost had no combat ability, so it would be a waste if they became a contracted fey.","When Wen Yu saw Lin Yuan observing her Sunlight Egret, she said, “Young Lord, this Sunlight Egret was my first fey when I became a spirit attendant. I don’t like fighting. I only want to become a good Creation Master, so most of my contracted feys are not good in combat.”","Lin Yuan nodded. Everyone had their own right to decide the path they wanted to take, just like Wen Yu, who did not choose to take the path of a combat-class spirit qi professional.","Instead, she chose to devote all her energy to becoming a Creation Master, so she had faster growth compared to other Creation Masters, who had divided attention.","Wen Yu did not have a competitive nature. If she had a stronger personality, the other spirit attendants in the Radiant Moon Palace would not have bullied her.","When Lin Yuan saw that the Sunlight Egret was already Flawless at Silver, he could see that Wen Yu’s Creation Master talent was superb.","“Let’s go then. I’ve long heard that Sunlight Egrets are very comfortable avian feys. I’ve never ridden on one before.” Lin Yuan revealed a cheerful smile. He was willing to ride on anything besides the Divine Travel Black Swallow. He did not want to experience the discomfort on his butt again.","Upon seeing Lin Yuan’s smile, an excited emotion immediately flashed in Wen Yu’s eyes. She felt indescribably happy that she could help him.","When Wen Yu had chosen this Sunlight Egret as her first contracted fey, many spirit attendants had laughed at her. They had chosen some combat feys to nurture.","Although Wen Yu’s compatibility with feys was not as good as those of combat-class spirit qi professionals, her compatibility with avian feys was also considered good. Many of those feys were even good at combat.","However, besides her Sunlight Egret, her two other contracted feys were only helpful to Creation Masters.","Nevertheless, Wen Yu felt that she had made an excellent decision to contract and carefully nurture the Sunlight Egret.","Lin Yuan silently thought, It’s so comfortable sitting on the Sunlight Egret’s back.","He wondered how much more comfortable the Sunlight Egret was to the Divine Travel Black Swallow.","Lin Yuan took out his cell phone on the Sunlight Egret’s back and went to the forum he would always visit back when he could not feel the world’s spirit qi. He had not been on this forum for nearly three months.","As a result, he found that he had a lot of unread messages on it, most of which came from the foolish online friend who claimed that she had been bitten by a Ghost Shadow Bristled Spider.","Lin Yuan looked through the records and realized that this online friend was trying to ‘battle’ with him!","I’m Not Lin Yuan: “Weren’t you bitten by a Ghost Shadow Bristled Spider? How come you’re still so spirited? Don’t you get tired of greeting me steadily three times a day?”","I Hate Spiders the Most: “I don’t. You previously talked bad about me. You have to apologize. Otherwise, you will be bitten by Ghost Shadow Bristled Spider!”","Lin Yuan secretly raised his brows. Wasn’t it just a joke?","I haven’t logged on to the forum for three months, yet you actually reply to me so quickly. How many grudges do you have?","It’s impossible for me to apologize. Before I can be bitten by a Ghost Shadow Bristled Spider, you still have to find one first!","Being bitten by a Ghost Shadow Bristled Spider can probably be considered as luck.","I’m Not Lin Yuan: “I’ll apologize to you if you answer my question.”","I Hate Spiders the Most: “Shoot!”","I’m Not Lin Yuan: “Why do frogs fly?”","I Hate Spiders the Most: “???”","I’m Not Lin Yuan: “Because they ate biscuits that can fly!”","I Hate Spiders the Most: “???”","I’m Not Lin Yuan: “Why do snakes fly?”","I Hate Spiders the Most: “???”","I’m Not Lin Yuan: “Because they ate frogs that can fly!”","I Hate Spiders the Most: “???”","I’m Not Lin Yuan: “Why do hawks fly?”","I Hate Spiders the Most: “Because they ate snakes that can fly!”","I’m Not Lin Yuan: “No!”","I Hate Spiders the Most: “???”","I’m Not Lin Yuan: “Because hawks can fly!”","The braised egg head on the other side of the phone was screaming in anger! She was so angry that she took off her bumblebee hat and threw it on the ground.","Suddenly, she had a bright idea. You can ask questions, but so do I!","I Hate Spiders the Most: “If a gorgeous woman and an ugly woman were kidnapped, which one would you save? The gorgeous woman will marry you, but that ugly woman will give you 100,000 Federation dollars. You can only choose one!”","I’m Not Lin Yuan: “I don’t want to tell you the answer!”","I Hate Spiders the Most: “??? Say it quickly!”","I’m Not Lin Yuan: “Money doesn’t matter. Most importantly, I like ugly ones.”","I Hate Spiders the Most: “???”","Lin Yuan was mischievous for a while and did not bother with that foolish online friend, who had been bitten by a Ghost Shadow Bristled Spider. He just exited the forum."]},{"number":167,"title":"Chapter 167: Parents’ Love For Their Children","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Lin Yuan corrected how Wen Yu addressed him along the way. If she still called him ‘Young Lord’ outside, it would simply be too strange. If any passersby heard it, none of them would take it seriously. Instead, they would only think that she was delusional. After looking down upon her, they would secretly call her a lunatic.","Soon, the Sunlight Egret flew to the location agreed with Liu Jie. Lin Yuan and Wen Yu got down, and Wen Yu used her spiritual energy to store her fey.","At a glance, Lin Yuan could see Liu Jie standing not far away. The middle-aged man standing beside Liu Jie had a flat face with flat-top hair. When Lin Yuan looked over, he nearly called him ‘Brother Flat-top1‘!","Lin Yuan could not help but recall something from his previous life.","Whether or not the desert is chaotic, only the honey badger’s words count!","When Liu Jie saw Lin Yuan, he immediately greeted him and said with a smile on his face, “Young Master Lin Yuan, long time no see.”","Lin Yuan felt that Liu Jie was now a lot more spirited than two months ago. Liu Jie previously had a sense of decadence, which was now gone, making him look much younger.","Liu Jie saw Wen Yu beside Lin Yuan and nodded in greeting.","Wen Yu hurriedly returned the greeting and saw a Class 2 Creation Master retainer crest on Liu Jie’s chest. She could tell that the man before her was Lin Yuan’s retainer knight.","She may be Lin Yuan’s nominal assistant, but she was not as close to Lin Yuan as him.","Wen Yu had noticed that Lin Yuan did not wear his Creation Master crest and was aware that he was a person who kept a very low profile.","Lin Yuan smiled and reached out his hand toward Liu Jie, causing excitement, joy, and a peace of mind to flash in the latter’s eyes. Liu Jie waved his hand and clasped it tightly with Lin Yuan’s hand. He immediately knew what Lin Yuan meant when he reached out his hands.","Back when Lin Yuan had said he could heal the Insect Queen, he had shaken hands with him. Now that he extended his hands out again, it meant that his Insect Queen had been healed.","Liu Jie hurriedly collected his ecstatic emotions and introduced the flat-top man beside him to Lin Yuan and said, “Lin Yuan, this is the owner of this piece of land.”","The flat-top man looked at Lin Yuan and said straightforwardly, “Let’s go in first. See whether you’re satisfied with this piece of land. If you decide, we can talk about the price.” He sounded very sincere, clearly keen to sell this piece of land.","Based on Liu Jie’s information alone, Lin Yuan was very fond of the land.","Lin Yuan, Liu Jie, and Wen Yu followed the flat-top man into the dilapidated gate. The flat-top man then hurriedly said, “This place used to be a vacation resort. After over 100 years, most of the facilities inside are old, and many things have been moved away.”","The flat-top man sounded somewhat awkward, as he should have arranged in advance to demolish them, which he would have to spend a lot of money to do so.","It was actually easy to demolish all these facilities, but not their foundations. This would be an extensive project.","At this point, Wen Yu said, “Regardless of whether you’re going to stay here, everything inside needs to be demolished and rebuilt.” As she said that, she looked at the flat-top man, causing him to smile awkwardly.","Lin Yuan looked at the scenery before him. Although the old facilities were an eyesore, he did not intend to leave them if he bought this piece of land. Since everything had to be rebuilt, he did not really care about these old facilities. The key was the environment.","The area of this land was very large, with a small artificial lake next to it. He could even build a manor on this piece of land.","Upon seeing that Lin Yuan did not speak but continued to look at the place, the flat-top man could not stay still, so he said, “This piece of land is qualified to build a guild club. Its area is more than twice as large as those A-level guild clubs. Someone has considered buying this piece of land to build a guild club.”","But at this point, the flat-top man could no longer continue.","After the person, who had considered buying this place to build a guild club, had taken a look at the land again and thought about it, he had given up because the land was simply too big. He could not afford to develop the guild club.","However, the flat-top man did not want to divide the land and sell it because it could now only be described as a large area with magnificent scenery. If he divided the land, he could never sell it at this price.","Actually, the flat-top man also knew that whoever bought this piece of land was akin to buying a piece of empty land with nothing. Its price alone was not low, and one would need to spend a considerable sum of money on developing it.","Liu Jie followed by Lin Yuan’s side and said, “Lin Yuan, this piece of land has the largest area, as well as a wonderful environment. If you want to build on this land, however, it won’t be a small sum of money.”","Lin Yuan nodded. He indeed would have to spend a lot of money to rebuild this place. However, he was not short of money now, so there were no problems building on this piece of land. Also, he wanted to build a guild club but had not decided yet.","If he bought this land, even if he wanted to build a guild club in the future, the place was big enough no matter how he used it.","Lin Yuan’s contracted feys were Genius, Chimey, Red Thorn, Blackie, and the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly. Although he put them in the Spirit Lock spatial zone most of the time, Blackie, the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly, and Genius were stuck at their current grades.","Therefore, they could no longer evolve inside. He might as well let them out so that they could feel the blue sky and white clouds under this world.","Lin Yuan would nurture many more feys and would keep some outstanding ones, but he could not always place them in the Diamond fey storage box.","With such a large area of land, these feys he nurtured could also have a place to stay.","Just like the Leaning Moon Mountain’s Radiant Moon Palace, some rare feys were playing around everywhere. It could be called a fairyland on earth.","When the flat-top man saw that Lin Yuan still did not speak, he felt even more uncertain. He was really eager to sell this piece of land, as he currently needed money for his son so that his peers would not leave him behind because of resources.","Parents’ love for their children was far-reaching!"]},{"number":168,"title":"Chapter 168: Cruel Wen Yu and the Bullied Flat-Top Man","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","A combat-class spirit qi professional would need a huge amount of resources to grow. If they could not keep up with the resources, they would waste their talents and affect their growth. There was no shortage of geniuses in this world who progressed slowly because of insufficient resources.","Just like Chu Ci, even if she had impressive potential, she might not even have a chance to go to school without Lin Yuan.","The flat-top man had ordinary qualifications, but he came from an affluent family. However, he was in dire straits now. Although his past glory had declined, he still had an enormous piece of land left.","After being in the society for a long time, he naturally understood the principle of the strong being respected.","His son had been gifted ever since he was young. He was now studying in the Spirit Qi Occupation Academy and was even a student of the key class.","Not long ago, a B-level guild club had shown interest in his son, so the flat-top man planned to sell the piece of land his ancestors had left behind and nurture his son.","As long as his son became a formidable combat-class spirit qi professional, it was possible to revive his family’s past glory.","Wen Yu had been watching the flat-top man’s nervous and hesitant expression. In fact, she saw that Lin Yuan had been looking at this piece of land for a long time. Given her understanding of him, she knew that he really fancied it. Otherwise, given his character, he would have long gone to see another place.","Therefore, she walked to the flat-top man and said, “It’s difficult to sell your piece of land!”","The flat-top man saw that Lin Yuan had not spoken and felt uncertain. Thus, his smile froze when he heard Wen Yu speak.","Wen Yu had always been carefully observing the flat-top man’s expressions. Now that he had an obvious change in his expression, she wore a smile on her face.","Even though her smile was gentle, the flat-top man did not think so. He only felt that her smile contained 30% of coldness, 30% of cynicism, and 40% of indifference. They added up to one meaning—they did not want to buy the land.","The flat-top man looked at Wen Yu with some indignation and almost blurted out, “You evil woman.”","Wen Yu did not know that a movie had started to play in his heart. She cleared her throat and said, “There are three reasons it’s hard to sell your piece of land. First, it’s too huge. Few people will buy such a large area of land for development. Second, it’s actually far from the Royal Capital. It would take at least half an hour with a Silver avian fey. Third, it will cost a lot of money to demolish so many dilapidated facilities.”","As Wen Yu spoke, the flat-top man’s expression turned even uglier. He nearly turned into a marmot and shouted at the open space, “Ah~!”","After Lin Yuan carefully looked at it and discussed it with Liu Jie, he decided to buy this piece of land.","Although the two pieces of land Liu Jie had picked were suitable to build Lin Yuan’s store, the one in the Royal Capital’s bustling area was a bit smaller than this. It was not even 1/100 of this land.","This was actually reasonable, as it was unrealistic to buy such a big piece of land in the Royal Capital’s bustling area.","After weighing the pros and cons, Lin Yuan still felt this piece of land was more suitable for him. When he was about to negotiate the price, he saw the flat-top man standing there with a face full of grievance.","Wen Yu said to the flat-top man calmly, “The price you just stated is still unreasonable. If you are selling at this price, I don’t know how long you’ll take to sell it!”","The flat-top man gnashed his teeth in grievance and replied, “8,000,000 Radiance dollars.”","Upon hearing that, Wen Yu shook her head calmly and answered, “Not only do we have to demolish these old facilities, we still have to fill in the ground and compress it. Look at how many old facilities you have here. If you sell it at 8,000,000 Radiance dollars, you have to help us demolish them.”","The flat-top man was on the verge of wailing, but he ground his teeth and replied, “7,500,000 Radiance dollars. I’m not selling any lower than that!”","Lin Yuan was a bit dumbfounded, as he did not expect Wen Yu to have a bargaining talent.","Wen Yu spoke in a gentle voice, but she was about to make this flat-top man cry. Her bargaining skills were simply too powerful!","This made Lin Yuan want to complement something he had seen in his previous life.","A flat-top, white hair, and a silver cloak!","I’m the fiercest in this desert continent!","I’m invincible around the world!","But I don’t dare to go to Dongzhou1!","Lin Yuan had discussed this piece of land with Liu Jie. Buying it for 12,000,000 Radiance dollars would be just right, and any higher than that would be a loss.","The flat-top man had given Liu Jie a price of 10,000,000 Radiance dollars. According to the market, Lin Yuan had earned it.","However, Wen Yu had chatted with the flat-top man and managed to lower the price by 2,500,000 Radiance dollars— buying it at that price was a solid profit!","Although the flat-top man had lowered the price, he was not dumb. He had previously refused to lower the price, so he had been unable to sell it for two years.","Now that his son had grown up, he urgently needed Radiance dollars to nurture his fey. In order not to waste his son’s talent, the flat-top man could only reluctantly sell this piece of land at a lowered price.","Otherwise, based on the Radiance Federation’s news, when the dimensional rift became active in a few months, he would not be able to sell this piece of land.","Lin Yuan eventually bought the land with 7,500,000 Radiance dollars.","At that moment, Wen Yu suddenly whispered to Lin Yuan, “Actually, we can just scare him by saying we won’t buy it. I still can lower the price by at least 100,000 Radiance dollars.”","Lin Yuan felt that she was really impressive. Although Wen Yu’s contracted feys could not fight, she was really a great genius in internal affairs!","He brought Wen Yu and Liu Jie to follow the appropriate procedures with the flat-top man.","Soon, Lin Yuan became the official owner of this piece of land.","Then, Wen Yu took on the task of rebuilding the manor under the somewhat distrustful gazes of Lin Yuan and Liu Jie.","Lin Yuan clearly had to transform this place so that people could stay there. He brought Liu Jie to the Royal Capital’s Creation Master Association and was prepared to rent a breeding room, where he planned to evolve Chimey into a Fantasy Breed and hatch the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee before enhancing it.","They both arrived inside the breeding room, and Lin Yuan took out Liu Jie’s Legend Insect Queen with a flip of his hand. The moment he did that, Liu Jie widened his eyes in surprise."]},{"number":169,"title":"Chapter 169: And Faith!","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","The moment Lin Yuan took the Insect Queen out of his Spirit Lock spatial zone, Liu Jie immediately sensed it. When he saw the Insect Queen, which he had not seen in a long time, he instinctively felt its attachment to him, as well as its yearning and joy.","Without the trials and tribulations over the past two years—which had made Liu Jie fall hard from the peak to the bottom and become an ordinary person—he would not have comprehended that sometimes, not forgetting one’s own original intentions was the only answer.","If Liu Jie could shine in glory, he could also be in dire straits. Thus, his mind had become stronger.","If he did not have a mind as strong as iron, when he sensed the Insect Queen’s intimate spiritual fluctuation, tears would have streamed down his face instantly.","Liu Jie could not forget how he had felt its constantly worsening injuries and deteriorating spiritual energy until it reached the brink of death in the past two years.","Although Liu Jie knew that Lin Yuan had healed his Insect Queen when they shook hands, when he saw it fully healed and able to communicate with him through his mind, he could not help but feel all sorts of feelings well up in his heart.","However, before he had the time to relish the joy of this meeting, he realized that his Insect Queen had evolved from Epic to Legend. He started to tremble with excitement and looked at Liu Yuan, wanting to say something, but he could not utter a word.","Nobody would know better than him, its contractor, how hard it was to evolve the source-type Insect Queen. It needed extremely pure spirit qi to evolve, much purer than what was required to heal its damaged roots.","Not even the Class 5 Creation Master, Bamboo Monarch, could restore its damaged roots with such pure spirit qi. Lin Yuan was probably the only one who could do so and also raise it from Epic to Legend.","When Lin Yuan noticed that Liu Jie could say nothing due to his excitement, he could not help but smile brightly. He reached out to pat Liu Jie’s shoulder and said, “After this, it’s time for you to be reborn in nirvana along with your Insect Queen. The Radiance Federation people have always been looking forward to the return of Sequence #39, Heart of Insect Swarm.”","What Lin Yuan mentioned was a sore spot that Liu Jie had never dared to touch before. It was because he always saw how the Radiance Federation folks regarded the Heart of Insect Swarm as a hero on Star Web and how they looked forward to his return.","This degree of passionate concern and expectations made Liu Jie, whose hopes had been squashed at that time, feel nothing but helplessness and pain.","Liu Jie had wanted to return to his former days and dominate the competition with his insect swarm, but all his yearning was just like the shattered yet dappled light in a dream.","Liu Jie had never regretted resisting the dimensional lifeforms’ invasion outside Cold Frost City. While he had been commanding the Insect Queen to fight against them, he had sensed the insect swarm’s frenzy and comprehended a Willpower Rune.","But after that, the Insect Queen’s roots had been damaged, and it had been on the brink of death. Liu Jie felt it was ironic he had comprehended this Willpower Rune.","At present, everything seemed to be the best choice that could have been made so far, as he knew that as long as he fused the Willpower Rune with the Insect Queen, it would become a Fantasy Breed. He would also be truly reborn in nirvana and proclaim to the world, “I! Liu Jie! Heart of Insect Swarm, Sequence #39 of the Radiance Hundred Sequence! Am back!”","He was well aware that everything and all future glory would be all thanks to this young man before his eyes. This young man had ignited the light of hope and changed it into a warm sun that caused a layer of gold color to emerge in his gloomy heart.","At that moment, Liu Jie was so excited that he could not say a word. He just looked at Lin Yuan firmly and gave a deep bow. This salute was much lower than the one a retainer knight would give to a Creation Master.","It was not only Liu Jie’s thanks but also faith.","Lin Yuan knew that Liu Jie must be feeling a lot at that moment, so he patted his shoulders and said, “When I came into the Royal Capital’s Creation Master Association, I booked a breeding room for you. Go evolve your Insect Queen into a Fantasy Breed first.”","Lin Yuan was really happy on Liu Jie’s behalf. Although he had wasted two years, now that the Insect Queen was a Fantasy Breed, Liu Jie would not just be Sequence #39 this year.","Liu Jie nodded vigorously. Despite being a man like steel, his nose tingled because of Lin Yuan’s words that seemed like the warm sun in midwinter.","After a long time, Liu Jie only said in a hoarse voice, “Young Master Lin Yuan, I—”","Lin Yuan interrupted Liu Jie. “You swore by your Willpower Rune and became my retainer knight. Nevertheless, you’re also my friend,” he said seriously.","He had risen from humble origins and did not treat others easily as subordinates. Regardless of whether it was Liu Jie or Wen Yu, since he had lived two lives, Lin Yuan understood that human interactions would all boil down to one thing—putting himself in other people’s shoes.","Liu Jie was stunned, looking at Lin Yuan before he nodded as an indescribable sense of warmth emerged in his heart.","Friends?","Liu Jie thought about it, and an ultimate glimmer of radiance appeared in his eyes.","At this moment! To Lin Yuan—","I’m a friend!","A retainer!","And faith!","Fighting alone in Cold Frost City, where the insect swarm was as vast as the city...","Fighting against the surge outside the city, where an epiphany of willpower leads to success and failure...","Everything has turned into perfection today!","After sending Liu Jie away, Lin Yuan started to think about what he needed to do during his seclusion in the breeding room. He realized that he would have to enter seclusion for nearly two months. But after this seclusion session, he could likely have the capabilities to compete with the Radiance Hundred Sequence members.","Lin Yuan raised his hand, summoned Red Thorn, and looked at its true data. He could not help but have high hopes of it.","[Fey Name]: Red Thorn (Predator Plant)","[Fey Species]: Rafflesia genus/Vine subspecies","[Fey Grade]: Bronze (3/10)","[Fey Type]: Source/Wood","[Fey Quality]: Epic","Abilities:","[Mouth of Relinquish]: Secretes vigorous digestive fluids with powerful corrosive properties, allowing a faster speed to absorb the energy in the food.","[Armor-Piercing Vines]: Vines that wrap quickly tremble rapidly and strengthen the effect of the vines’ sharp thorns piercing through the armor.","Exclusive Skill:","[Spore Growth]: Spits a huge amount of spores, which can absorb the energy or flesh energy supplied by Red Thorn, out of its spore cavity to quickly grow ramets and child ramets that are controlled by the ortet.","Red Thorn’s real rise was when it reached Bronze and obtained its exclusive skill, Spore Growth, as it changed Red Thorn’s combat style.","If Red Thorn was a lone warrior previously, it was a commander that commanded the child ramets and ramets to fight now. However, Lin Yuan believed it would undergo its real metamorphosis when it reached Legend and became a Fantasy Breed.","At that moment, he took the source-type Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s egg out of the leaf-shaped Diamond fey storage box."]},{"number":170,"title":"Chapter 170: Bootlicking Acid Corrosion Queen Bee!","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Lin Yuan placed the egg in Red Thorn’s corrosive cavity for it to hatch. He conveyed his thoughts to Red Thorn through his spiritual fluctuation, and it soon understood his intention.","It used the thornless vine to wrap the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s egg in his hand. It did not place it in its corrosive cavity but into the Mouth of Relinquish.","When it swallowed the egg in its Mouth of Relinquish, Lin Yuan immediately fed Red Thorn with the dimensional lifeforms’ flesh from the Diamond fey storage box. He selected a lot of Class 3 alien insect flesh with strong acidity and fed them into its Mouth of Relinquish.","When Red Thorn evolved into Bronze, Lin Yuan chose Class 3 dimensional lifeforms, which were akin to Gold feys’ flesh, for it. After that, he started channeling the spiritual power within his body and made the Mouth of Relinquish quickly absorb the flesh energy.","When the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee hatched, it would immediately build its nest.","Lin Yuan did not know how much energy it would take, but it was being prepared.","After an entire day, Red Thorn stopped eating quickly and absorbed the Class 3 alien insect flesh’s energy at normal speed.","Upon seeing that, Lin Yuan stopped channeling his spiritual power. He had consumed a lot of spiritual power to help the Mouth of Relinquish digest the dimensional lifeforms’ flesh.","At that moment, a thumb-sized gray bee crawled out of the Mouth of Relinquish’s flesh-like petals. It still seemed very fragile, but the two stingers on its forelegs, as well as the stinger at the end of its abdomen, seemed sharp enough as they flashed with cold light.","Lin Yuan used True Data to check it and found that the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee was a Normal I/Normal source-type lifeform.","However, he was surprised when he looked at it because Red Thorn had devoured a huge amount of Class 3 alien insect flesh and absorbed ten times the flesh energy it would need in one day.","In other words, the newly hatched Acid Corrosion Queen Bee had used a huge amount of the dimensional lifeforms’ flesh energy to build its nest.","Lin Yuan did not know what kind of nest it would build. This was because he could not enter the Mouth of Relinquish to see the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s nest. However, he could sense through Red Thorn that the nest was not small.","The Acid Corrosion Queen Bee used the digestive fluids condensed into acid crystals to build this nest, which was a huge project. When it finished building its nest, Lin Yuan sensed Red Thorn, which had a bloodline connection with him, form a contract with the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee.","He did not know what kind of contract it would choose to form with Red Thorn right after building its nest.","What kind of degree could this contractual relationship reach?","At that moment, Lin Yuan found that the contract between Red Thorn and the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee was simply harsh.","If Red Thorn was a queen that looked down on the world disdainfully, then the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee was the subordinate who served her.","At that moment, Lin Yuan could sense that the newly hatched Acid Corrosion Queen Bee was releasing spiritual signals to please Red Thorn. It was simply more shameless than exceptional bootlickers.","Lin Yuan could not criticize the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee, as his primary task was to raise its grade.","Red Thorn commanded the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee to fly to Lin Yuan’s palm as he calmed down. Lin Yuan brought it to the Spirit Lock spatial zone and enhanced the gray and very young Acid Corrosion Queen Bee.","It evolved quickly with the help of the rich spirit qi inside.","Normal, Elite, Elite/Epic, Bronze, Bronze/Legend, Silver...","He stopped when he raised the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee to Gold.","At this point, Lin Yuan finally had a Gold fey and was considered to have the combat power of a pinnacle expert among the younger generation.","He had spent a lot of time evolving the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee to Gold in the Spirit Lock spatial zone. When Lin Yuan looked at the time on his cell phone, he found that he had spent nearly 20 days evolving one fey from Normal I/Normal to Gold I/Legend. This was the result of him evolving it with all his effort in the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","When he wanted to evolve the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee from Gold I, he realized that he could not do so at the moment. He knew that he could only easily do so when he became a B-rank spirit qi professional. He was very satisfied that he had been able to evolve it to Gold I/Legend, nonetheless.","Even if the Legend Acid Corrosion Queen Bee was at Gold I, it possessed tremendous combat power. It could probably be comparable to Epic VI or VII feys.","As Lin Yuan looked at the Gold Acid Corrosion Queen Bee in his hand, he could not help but feel a rise of emotions.","It was his first Gold fey.","This sense of accomplishment of evolving life washed away the past 20 days’ fatigue, as it was a soul-level of ascension no matter when he experienced it.","At present, the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee had grown to a length of about 15 cm. It had a long, slender body, with dark-red metallic luster hidden with strange dark-green markings, showing a hideous sense of beauty.","It had two thick stingers on its forelegs and two long, thin stingers on its abdomen. Its foreleg stingers were thick, while the abdominal stingers were sharp and slender, carrying an eerie greenish cold light.","The Acid Corrosion Queen Bee flew around Lin Yuan affectionately before landing back in his hand. Then, he sensed it emitting a kind of eagerness to see Red Thorn.","Lin Yuan could not help but diss in his heart, What a bootlicker!","Then, he left the Spirit Lock spatial zone with the Gold Acid Corrosion Queen Bee.","Despite being at Gold, it was still careful to please Red Thorn as before.","The landlord, Red Thorn, was clearly very cold to its own tenant, the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee. However, the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee did not mind. It was as if when Red Thorn paid just a little attention to it, it would be a great gift to it.","The Acid Corrosion Queen Bee flew happily among Red Thorn’s dancing vines and occasionally landed on Red Thorn’s corrosive cavity’s rose-like red flowers to rest.","At that moment, Lin Yuan carefully checked its true data."]},{"number":171,"title":"Chapter 171: The Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s Cruel Aesthetics","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Lin Yuan was very much looking forward to the Gold I/Legend Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s True Data.","[Fey Name]: Acid Corrosion Queen Bee","[Fey Species]: Vespidae/Bactrocera","[Fey Grade]: Gold (1/10)","[Fey Type]: Source/Poison","[Fey Quality]: Legend","Abilities:","[Wing Stealth]: Flaps its wings at high frequency. The fast-flapping reflective wings allow the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee to be stealthy.","[Bone-Penetrating Stingers]: The super hard and impactful rotating stingers rapidly cause deep injuries.","[Parasitic Pupa]: The stingers on the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s forelegs can release a fast-hatching parasitic pupa into the target’s body while stinging.","[Acid-Swallowing Larvae]: With sufficient acid, the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee will hatch numerous Acid-Swallowing Larvae that can be used as food for it to rapidly restore its consumed energy and venom reserves.","Exclusive Skill:","[Two-Strike Kill]: The two abdominal stingers contain two different kinds of acid-corrosion venom. If the abdominal stingers hit the same part of the target, the two types of venom will instantly disintegrate the target’s part.","When Lin Yuan saw the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s abilities, he suddenly could not help but criticize, What a cruel bootlicker!","Wing Stealth could greatly increase its stealth ability.","Red Thorn and the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee were a combination. Red Thorn would release spores to spawn child ramets and ramets and spread out the sea of flowers.","In the absence of a huge amount of flesh, Red Thorn consumed its body’s energy to spread the sea of flowers. Therefore, the sea of flowers was not as shocking as during Millstone Town, and there were not as many child ramets and ramets.","When battling in Star Web, Red Thorn, which was now a Bronze source-type lifeform, could even compete against Silver feys with its sea of flowers. However, Spore Growth’s child ramets and ramets were not meant to score a direct hit on feys of the same grades. Instead, it was a field control ability.","The sea of flowers that Red Thorn spawned could very well limit the enemy feys’ movements. At that moment, the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee that used Wing Stealth would be a perfect assassin.","The Bone-Penetrating Stingers could very well penetrate through the feys’ armor and cause severe damage to the target’s bones.","However, Lin Yuan’s pupils contracted at Parasitic Pupa.","What a cruel ability it was!","Lin Yuan had checked the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s stingers in front and found they were hollow.","He had always thought that the hollow stingers were used to inject acid into the target’s body, but he did not expect them to release a soon-to-hatch parasitic pupa into the target’s body.","It had the same conditions as the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s growth.","The pupa would search for the most acidic organ tissue in the target’s body based on its instinct before drilling into it to hatch.","This was akin to saying that when the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee injected it into the target’s body, the hatching parasitic pupa would drill into the target’s stomach according to its instinct. The pupa would then hatch with the strong gastric acid’s help.","What kind of torture would the parasitic pupa do to the parasitized target?","The pain of tearing apart the epidermis and flesh and drilling into the stomach was something Lin Yuan could not imagine!","Besides, the parasitic pupa that hatched in the stomach would absorb a huge amount of gastric acid and nutrients from the target’s body.","Lin Yuan knew how much acid and energy the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee had absorbed from Red Thorn’s Mouth of Relinquish.","Even if ordinary lifeforms had a huge amount of energy in their bodies, how would they have so much acid?","The huge amount of absorbed gastric acid would make the target’s stomach function all destroyed and withered.","If the hatching parasitic pupa sensed that the gastric acid was not enough, it would drill into other organs to absorb acid.","If the acid in the target’s body did not reach the hatching condition, it would not hatch. Nevertheless, the target’s body would probably have been destroyed beyond recognition.","But if the acid in the target’s body was barely enough for the parasitic pupa to hatch, it would be akin to hatching an enemy.","The parasitic pupa would break out of the target’s body at the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s order!","This Parasitic Pupa ability was cruel and terrifying.","Of course, the parasitic pupa had its own weakness.","The Acid Corrosion Queen Bee must penetrate the target’s epidermis to be able to release the parasitic pupa into the target’s body. However, the Bone-Penetrating Stingers perfectly resolved this weakness.","The Bone-Penetrating Stingers’ defense-breaking function allowed the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee to release the parasitic pupa under the epidermis. Furthermore, Red Thorn’s Armor-Piercing Vines could break through armor too.","Lin Yuan had never understood how the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee had gotten its name, but after seeing the Acid-Swallowing Larvae, he finally understood why.","The Acid Corrosion Queen Bee was an extremely cruel source-type lifeform by nature.","A queen bee would give birth to pupae in a completed hive, but all the pupae were nothing more than rations for her to carry out her recovery.","Because of these Acid-Swallowing Larvae, the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s endurance in a battle was significantly increased. However, these were not the most powerful means of killing. Rather, it was the exclusive skill that it learned at Bronze, Two-Strike Kill.","The Acid Corrosion Queen Bee had two sharp stingers on its abdomen that contained two different kinds of bee venom. These super toxic bee venoms might not be powerful to kill on their own, but if they came into contact, an extremely strong reaction would immediately occur and disintegrate the part of the target’s body that came into contact with the mixed bee venom.","The most powerful thing about Two-Strike Kill was that it did not need to penetrate the armor.","Even if its abdominal stringers injected the two toxins into the target’s armor, they would produce a huge reaction that would disintegrate the parts of the target’s armor.","Then, Lin Yuan tested the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s Two-Strike Kill. He looked at the corroded and disintegrated metal spiritual ingredients in his hand and gained a better understanding of its exclusive skill’s power.","If the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee stung those Platinum defense-type feys that were not super strong with its abdominal stingers, the parts that came into contact would be violently corroded and even disintegrated. However, it was hard for it to hit a part of the Platinum feys twice with its abdominal stingers.","Lin Yuan was delighted with this Gold I/Legend source-type Acid Corrosion Queen Bee.","Upon seeing it fluttering among Red Thorn’s vines with a relaxed look, he could not help but think of the cruelty behind the surface of the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee, especially the two abdominal stingers that could use Two-Strike Kill.","As the saying went, “Nothing is more poisonous than a wasp’s stinger!”","In nature, the queen bee was responsible for producing a colony in the hive, which was not the case for the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee. It produced offspring called the Acid-Swallowing Larvae that were relief food it saved in advance.","When the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee tried to please Red Thorn, it seemed like the most loyal bootlicker, but it was so cruel to her own offspring and enemies.","It could not be described as a contradiction, but this contradiction was compelling enough.","Lin Yuan stretched his body and stored Red Thorn and the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee, which was staying in its body, back into the leaf-shaped Diamond fey storage box. Both needed great nutrition, and now was the best time for them to do so.","Lin Yuan did not choose to rest but summon Chimey. It looked a little dazed when it was summoned.","It used to be boisterous and clingy. However, it was frowning with an arduous expression, making Lin Yuan worry about it.","Why was Chimey despondent?"]},{"number":172,"title":"Chapter 172: The Stars in the Clouds Appear at Dawn!","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Lin Yuan was somewhat worried as he communicated with Chimey. However, he was startled when it sent over its spiritual fluctuation.","As he watched it fly around in anticipation, he cleared his throat and said, “If you want to transform into a human form, you need to evolve into Suzerain/Myth II.”","Lin Yuan was a little confused why Chimey was asking such a question. It always had a cheerful nature and would stick to him every day and hum songs.","When had Chimey, which was carefree all day long, become so obsessed with being able to transform into human form?","If Genius was around, it would certainly hide under the chair and cover its eyes with its small paws, not daring to look at Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan had not used Genius’ Tool Transformation to turn it into glasses or a mask for the past few days. Therefore, the idle Genius had become Chimey’s live-streaming manager again in the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","Genius’s return had saved the busy Chimey. During the live-streaming, Genius had helped Chimey resolve all kinds of problems.","Just as Chimey had gone to compete with other live-streamers, Genius, a Thousand Questions Beast, had helped it resolve problems perfectly.","Without Genius’s quick eyes and paws, Chimey would have revealed its true form when the GIF disappeared during the competition.","However, a lot of things had happened to Chimey’s live-streaming room. First, the second-highest contributing fan had overtaken the top one, causing a tremendous amount of interest in its live-streaming room. Then, someone wrote about a fan meeting in the comment box. Chimey started to have some thoughts about it after learning what it was.","Upon thinking that it was just a bird, it could not help but sigh.","In Chimey’s eyes, Lin Yuan had always been almighty, so it had asked him how it could transform into human form. Indeed, Lin Yuan’s words answered its question.","After hearing Lin Yuan’s answer, Chimey immediately became happy. Its mind was filled with the idea of evolving into Suzerain/Myth II, transforming into human form, and then holding the fan meeting grandly. It felt happy just thinking about it.","As it thought about it, it could not help but become a little nervous and secretly glance at Lin Yuan while feeling diffident.","After all, Lin Yuan did not know that it was singing. Chimey wondered, What if Yuan finds out and is unhappy with my live-streaming on Star Web?","However, in its opinion, Lin Yuan was looking at it worriedly. It then happily jumped on his ears and caressed his hair at the side of his ear with its head. Chimey thought, Yuan is so good to me. He won’t be so mean to me! If he doesn’t like me singing, then I won’t sing anymore on Star Web. I’ll just sing to him alone.","Lin Yuan noticed that Chimey had a load on its mind earlier, but now, it was so happy. He couldn’t help but rub Chimey’s head with his finger.","He was still kept in the dark and thought that Chimey was so sentimental just now because it had undergone puberty.","Chimey flew down from his ear and landed on his fingertip before jumping on it. After playing with Chimey for a while and watching it return to its usual lively self, Lin Yuan was relieved. He looked at it and said sternly, “Chimey, if you want to transform into human form, evolving into a Fantasy Breed will be the most important step for your future development.”","If there were any contracted feys’ evolutions he was most worried about, they would undoubtedly be Chimey and Genius. Chimey was at first a Sound Bird that had failed to evolve into a Songstress Bird. However, it had evolved into a Stream Cloud Azure Bird and taken a path that no Sound Birds had ever taken before. Therefore, Chimey could be called a pioneer of the Sound Bird family in terms of evolution.","Lin Yuan was the person who had created this great miracle of life. He had brought Chimey, which had been abandoned when it had just been born, on a path that it needed to overcome the obstacles by itself. This path might be obstructed and difficult, but it was definitely the most dazzling.","Chimey sensed Lin Yuan’s seriousness and also became very serious. When it heard him say that it was its first step to transform into human form, its eyes lit up, and its little body was filled with an indomitable determination.","Lin Yuan summoned the Willpower Rune, which he had comprehended from the delicate rising sun, from his spiritual energy. This Willpower Rune fit Chimey’s Clear Sky perfectly, and he also wanted it to evolve on this path. This was because only when it chose a general direction of evolution could the subsequent development be broader and smoother.","The moment Lin Yuan summoned the Willpower Rune, the cloud patterns on Chimey lit up. It flapped its wings and flew toward this Twilight Willpower Rune before fusing with it. It was as if Chimey had plunged into the first glimmer of dawn. In this bright twilight, it constantly chirped, its voice full of pain.","When Lin Yuan had sensed the Sharp Iron Horn Bull undergoing metamorphosis into the Obsidian Iron Wild Bull, he learned that the evolution of life was a path taken barefoot on thorns and sharpening itself step by step toward the path of metamorphosis.","Upon hearing Chimey’s painful chirping, Lin Yuan’s heart ached, but he could do nothing, as a new life was rising behind this.","At that moment, he suddenly heard a sound very similar to Chimey’s previous cry, yet more pleasant and clearer.","This clear cry seemed to include the breeze, raindrops, wind-blown ears of wheat, the shadow of the first glimmer of dawn, the dew washing away the dust, and the cold green plums.","This sound seemed to be the most essential in the depths of nature, inscribed with all the subtlety and clarity.","After Chimey’s metamorphosis, the twilight did not vanish but became more intense.","Lin Yuan saw a small emerald-blue bird fly out of this joyful light, with a few plumes grown on its forehead that made it look unusually soft and beautiful. Its emerald-blue feathers seemed like the purest blue sky above the dome.","Mist rose from the cloud patterns on this bird when it fluttered, and the cloud patterns on its feather seemed to have produced stars. As Chimey was flapping its wings, it was as if stars were flashing in the clouds.","When it saw Lin Yuan, it did not go over but let out a clear sound in the breeding room, joyfully showing him its ability. Then, it was as if a splendor spread in the breeding room.","Lin Yuan knew that Chimey was using its exclusive skill, Clear Sky. The sunlight spilled straight from outside through the window to it. In that instant, Chimey, which was less than the size of a fist, was suddenly enveloped in this splendor.","A layer of glazed light flame ignited on its wingspan, and its original emerald-blue feathers became this faint golden color that was not the color of gold. Rather, it was the dazzling radiance and luster of the sun’s splendor.","At that moment, Chimey’s wingspan was nearly one meter long. The cloud patterns on its body swept up the clouds, and the stars among the cloud patterns suddenly brightened up. When the stars collided, it was as if they had fused into the rising sun from the east.","Lin Yuan felt the majestic energy from Chimey’s body.","It chirped and showed its transformation to him, but before it could last half a minute, the splendor on its body vanished, and it turned back into its being a small emerald-blue bird.","As Lin Yuan looked at Chimey that had fallen asleep in his arms, he revealed a helpless and doting smile. Without his quick catch, it would have fallen to the ground with its head first.","He could not help but sigh when he saw the plumes pointed slightly up on its forehead and the new stars on the cloud patterns. Based on aesthetics, few small avian feys could be compared to Chimey.","Chimey’s visuals now were really unparalleled. If it went to participate in the selection of the top ten most beautiful feys, it could rank high on the list.","At that moment, Lin Yuan used Morbius’s True Data to check the Fantasy Breed Chimey."]},{"number":173,"title":"Chapter 173: The Twilight Starbird","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Chimey was no longer a Stream Cloud Azure Bird. When it evolved into a Fantasy Breed, it also metamorphosed into a Twilight Starbird.","As Lin Yuan looked at the sleeping Chimey, an indescribable sense of pride arose in his heart.","So what about a phoenix’s nirvana?","It was just a phoenix evolving into a phoenix.","However, Chimey had evolved from an abandoned Sound Bird into a Fantasy Breed Twilight Starbird.","After a long sleep, it woke up leisurely. It was still somewhat weak, so it took a good half day to recover. Then, it flew intimately to Lin Yuan’s ears, clearly treating it as its exclusive territory.","After Lin Yuan played with Chimey for a while, he entered the Spirit Lock spatial zone with it and started enhancing it inside.","Just like the Jasmine Lily, Lin Yuan spent nearly one month evolving Chimey into Bronze X/Fantasy I. After a month, he evolved it into Silver I/Fantasy I.","He sensed its state and could not help but sigh. This Fantasy Breed fey experienced astounding changes at every grade. This was a torrent-like metamorphosis in the life history of species.","After Chimey evolved into a Twilight Starbird, its type had changed from Sound/Qi to Sound/Light. Based on normal evolutions, Chimey’s qi-type would not easily vanish due to its metamorphosis into a Fantasy Breed.","When it had been at Elite, it was because it had comprehended the qi-type attribute that it became a Stream Cloud Azure Bird, allowing it to go beyond the sound-type and take a broader path.","However, it had fused with the Twilight Willpower Rune, and its qi-type was replaced. Theoretically, its sound-type should have been replaced.","Lin Yuan did not know that Chimey, which was jumping on him, was filled with such a strong obsession with its sound-type.","When Chimey had first met Lin Yuan, it had both been introverted and self-conscious. As a Sound Bird that had failed to evolve into a Songstress Bird, it could not even sing a complete song at that time.","Lin Yuan’s company had cleared the dust from Chimey’s life and cast a light warmer than the Twilight Willpower Rune.","It was him who had taught it the first song over and over again with great pains and let it no longer think it was a weak Sound Bird that could be abandoned.","It was also him who had let Chimey know what it felt like to be pampered, as well as let it evolve step by step to the present and become a Twilight Starbird.","The simple song that Lin Yuan had taught at that time had witnessed Chimey and Lin Yuan’s meeting. Therefore, this song was the obsession in its heart. It was unwilling to erase it until death.","All this was its obsession and a miracle in the history of the Sound Birds’ evolution, for which there was no precedence.","Miracles happened in life every day because of the various miracles that the long river of life evolved on such a magnificent scale.","Lin Yuan carefully observed Chimey’s True Data.","[Fey Name]: Twilight Starbird","[Fey Species]: Plume Sparrow/Starlight Bird","[Fey Grade]: Silver (1/10)","[Fey Type]: Sound/Light","[Fey Quality]: Fantasy I","Abilities:","[Sound Thrust]: Fire three sharp spikes that are formed by sound at a designated target.","[Scattered Light]: Emits a beam of scattered light from its body with burning and control effects.","[Sunlight Rays]: Emits various rays from the sun that will cause negative weakening to the target.","Exclusive Skill:","[Clear Sky]: After a clear chirp, the clouds would disperse and clear up the sky.","[Radiant Body]: Rapidly absorb the power of the sun and form a Radiant Body from the huge amount of solar energy gathered in the body.","Due to the change in Chimey’s type, Turbulence, which it had comprehended at Elite, had come Scattered Light. While it flapped its wings, it would emit a scattered beam of light with burn and control effects.","Compared to Turbulence, Scattered Light clearly had more killing power, but its control ability was much weaker.","Lin Yuan criticized helplessly at its Sunlight Rays that it had comprehended at Silver. He could not help but want to drill into its little brain to see what it was really thinking about.","How had it comprehended all kinds of harmful rays in the twilight of such a beautiful blazing sun to weaken and control the target?","There were all kinds of harmful rays in the sunlight rays with radiation-like destructive significance to life.","When Chimey used these rays on the target, it could cause negative effects such as dizziness, nausea and allow it to break through the armor. It was counted as an all-round weakening effect.","Only those who had fought on the Star Web would know how strong the Sunlight Rays’ weakening effect was.","Lin Yuan had sensed the terrifying energy in the Radiant Body when Chimey used it earlier.","Chimey had used the sunlight power on itself, and the glazed flames that ignited on its body made its body size increase greatly. The destructive power carried in that instant could simply be called an ace in the hole.","However, it had not been in its Radiant Body for long, just 30 seconds or so. After that, its spiritual power had been overspent while its stamina had been depleted, causing it to fall into a deep slumber.","Although Chimey only had a brief burst with its Radiant Body, it was also one of Lin Yuan’s trump cards.","When it evolved into a Silver Fantasy Breed earlier, he let it use the Radiant Body and realized that Radiant Body lasted from half a minute to nearly a minute.","This time, Lin Yuan carefully sensed the energy contained in its Radiant Body.","If this energy instantly exploded, the impact caused would be nearly twice as strong as the Gold Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s full force.","Moreover, Chimey did not rely on physical attacks with its Radiant Body, but the burning ability of that glazed light flame.","Among the two exclusive skills that it had comprehended, Clear Sky could be used perfectly with Radiant Body, as it could ensure that it absorbed light from the sun or stars no matter what the situation was.","At the same time, Sunlight Rays could help Red Thorn and the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee weaken the target. This way, Lin Yuan’s current feys could complement each other into a set of the combat system.","If he went to climb the Star Tower now, he could use his Jasmine Lily to heal, the Spirit-Gather Goldfish to replenish his spiritual power, and the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly to control. At the same time, Genius’ Tool Transformation mask and glasses could allow him to see through the target’s weaknesses.","Combined with Red Thorn’s, the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s, and Chimey’s major attacks, it should no longer be considered an arduous task for him to reach the 100th floor and ascend to the Celestial Stairway."]},{"number":174,"title":"Chapter 174: The Bamboo Path Leads to a Secluded Spot, and the Stream Into the Deep Valley","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","After entering seclusion for nearly two months, Lin Yuan was a little tired. He picked up Genius, squatting at the side, and Chimey, chirping non-stop.","He leaned on the sofa in the lounge and closed his eyes to have a wonderful sleep. It was just like how Lin Yuan, Chimey, and Genius, would snuggle together to sleep in the Xia Region’s fey store five months ago. His facial expression was so quiet and peaceful.","Chimey and Genius leaned on his young man’s body as though they were leaning on the entire world. He did not have wide shoulders, but they were like a mountain, completely supporting their dependence.","Time had changed, and so did people, but not his original intentions.","Back then, there was the sick young man, the malnourished and abandoned Hundred Questions Beast, and the Sound Bird that had failed to evolve into a Songstress Bird and had been given away like trash.","They had all been given a new lease of life. This sick young man had long since become a heavenly prodigy of the young generation. The other two despised beasts also accompanied the young man to grow up and became the pioneers of the evolution of the Sound Bird and the Hundred Questions Beast, evolving into a path without precedence.","Since he almost had no rest for the past two months, Lin Yuan was simply exhausted, so he was now sleeping soundly and snoring softly. Chimey hid in Lin Yuan’s neck, looking particularly at ease. However, its slight movements obviously woke Genius up.","Genius meowed and looked at Lin Yuan before it brought over a towel blanket with its mouth from the sofa beside. It carefully helped cover Lin Yuan with it and snuggled into it, leaning in his arms and sleeping soundly.","When Lin Yuan woke up, he was a little surprised to see the time. He had actually slept for a full two days and immediately sensed his stomach protesting with a grumble.","He took out the dried food and fruits that he had stored in the leaf-shaped Diamond fey storage box and ate them. When he got up from the sofa, he was cautious, as he was afraid of waking up the sleeping Genius and Chimey.","However, the sweetness of the fruits woke them up from their dreamland. Upon seeing them awake, Lin Yuan fed Genius a Platinum Cane Luffa and Chimey a Platinum Celery Vine. They gathered around him, waiting for him to feed them. It was a warm scene.","He cut the Cane Luffa into small pieces and tore up the Celery Vine before feeding them to Genius and Chimey. Then, he stored them in the Spirit Lock spatial zone and walked out of the breeding room with full spirit.","The sunlight outside was just right. Despite being in the late autumn, the bright and beautiful sunlight shining into the breeding room through the windows was still warm.","Lin Yuan had just walked out of the breeding room when he found someone standing at the door. It was Liu Jie.","Upon seeing Lin Yuan, Liu Jie immediately revealed a smile. Lin Yuan did not expect Liu Jie to wait for him outside the breeding room, so he asked, “How’s it after the Insect Queen evolved into a Fantasy Breed?”","A dazzling brilliance flashed in Liu Jie’s eyes as he looked at Lin Yuan and replied, “Very powerful!”","Lin Yuan knew that Liu Jie was not someone who talked big. If he said that it was very powerful, then it must be so.","It seemed that the exclusive skill that the Insect Queen had comprehended after becoming a Fantasy Breed greatly improved Liu Jie’s combat power.","There was no complacency on Liu Jie’s face, but solemnity. He lowered his head and looked at the small shield inscribed above the Class 2 Creation Master crest on his chest.","This shield would be his most steadfast destiny, just like what was in his mind at the moment.","Liu Jie thought that he was merely protecting the two stars on the shield better by evolving the Insect Queen into a Fantasy Breed.","Being powerful was for the sake of protection. In the past, he had been protecting the world, but now, he was protecting the young man before his eyes.","When Lin Yuan and Liu Jie walked out of the Royal Capital’s Creation Master Association, Lin Yuan suddenly remembered Wen Yu. Before he had entered seclusion in the Creation Master Association, Wen Yu had taken a huge responsibility for the development of the manor land.","Lin Yuan had handed Cheng Wu’s beetle-shaped Diamond fey storage box containing Radiance dollars to her. No matter what, she had to spend money to develop the land. For almost two months, Lin Yuan was a little worried about her.","Although Wen Yu had taken the huge responsibility, letting a teenage girl handle the entire manor’s construction was a little too much.","Lin Yuan thought that since Liu Jie had come out of the breeding room in advance, he should know her current situation, so he looked at Liu Jie and asked, “How’s Wen Yu doing?”","Liu Jie had actually taken little time to evolve the Insect Queen into a Fantasy Breed. Before he had entered the breeding room, he knew that Lin Yuan would enter seclusion for over two months.","After he came out, he had gone to the land that Lin Yuan had bought with 7,500,000 Radiance dollars, ready to help Wen Yu. However, she had chased him back before he could help her for less than a day. This was because, under her divine operation, Liu Jie had found he was more of a hindrance than a help.","Now that Lin Yuan asked about it, he could only scratch his head in embarrassment, not knowing what to say. It was really difficult for him to tell him everything.","Upon seeing Liu Jie’s expression, Lin Yuan knew that something had happened. But when they arrived at the land, Lin Yuan had the same expression as Liu Jie, looking dumbfounded.","If anyone saw their expressions, they would probably send them to the psychiatric department for resuscitation.","Lin Yuan felt that the scene before him was astounding!","Before he had entered into seclusion, this had been an empty land full of old facilities. Now, it was an elegant manor.","The environment here was naturally incomparable to that of the Radiant Moon Palace, but it was certainly ranked among the Royal Capital’s best.","There were two beautiful rows of ponds by the man-made lake’s diversion on both sides of the path. The large manor had three floors only but occupied an area of nearly 1,000 square meters. Its design was simple and carved with all sorts of auspicious feys, looking unique.","There were also wind chimes carved from jade that produced a faint bell sound when the autumn wind blew past and contained a poetic beauty in the corners of the manor’s eaves and beams.","The open space in front of the manor had no arrangements, but a 3,000-meter bamboo forest was planted at the back of the building with a shaded path in the forest and a green-and-white pavilion at the end of the forest.","The pavilion’s four corners were white cranes spreading their wings to fly, and the pavilion was engraved with a faint lotus pattern that looked rather elegant.","A calm pool was next to the pavilion, and a fresh stream that connected to the mountain valley was behind the pavilion. It had the feeling of ‘the scenery in all directions gathered in one pavilion’.","What a divine view!","Lin Yuan could not help but wonder whether he had been in seclusion for two months or two years. Although he did not know how Wen Yu had done it, he could not help but sigh when he saw the beautiful scenery in the distance.","“The bamboo path leads to a secluded spot, and the clear stream flows into a deep valley.”","At that moment, Liu Jie could not help but grin upon hearing Lin Yuan’s words. He felt that Lin Yuan simply had high expectations!"]},{"number":175,"title":"Chapter 175: The Meaning of Extravagant?","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","The scenery in front had layers of wonders—it was like a bamboo forest in the deep valley that was accompanied with refreshing autumn wind. It was a manor that could be described with a saying, “The roar of the bear and dragon caused the fountain water to resonate, even the deep forest and mountains were also shaking1.”","Liu Jie was shocked by the beauty, but he still couldn’t help twitching his mouth!","Liu Jie involuntarily recalled the time he had visited and was thinking how Wen Yu had spent a fortune to invite three spirit qi professionals from the lifestyle-class Construction Association.","All of them possessed the Diamond Earth-Turning Giant Elephants. Using their exclusive skill, Earth-Turning Wrath, the old site of this manor, including the foundations, was turned into dust.","They then used the Earth-Turning Giant Elephants’ ability, Mother Earth Pressure, to turn the dust into compressed soil.","This huge project that would normally need a few months was completed in less than half a day under Wen Yu’s command. Even as Radiance Hundred Sequence #39, this was the first time Liu Jie had seen anyone hiring Diamond Earth-Turning Giant Elephants to tear down an old site.","It was something that no one would normally even dare to think about. These three Diamond/Elite Earth-Turning Giant Elephants might not have much potential to evolve again, but they were still the Royal Capital’s Construction Association’s distinguishing mark.","However, all these weren’t important. The most crucial point was how Wen Yu had generously used those Radiance dollars. The price for three Diamond Earth-Turning Giant Elephants to stomp the ground was just slightly lower than what was required to purchase a piece of land like this.","In the past, Liu Jie had always felt that women were very cute lifeforms, but after witnessing We Yu’s performance, he felt that this world’s most horrifying thing wasn’t the dimensional rifts. Instead, it was a woman who would use money without hesitation.","At that moment, Lin Yuan and Liu Jie saw Wen Yu holding a long list and walking out of the construction site.","When Wen Yu saw Lin Yuan, she ran happily and said, “Young Master, you have exited seclusion! Take a look at the development and see if it is good enough.”","Liu Jie involuntarily gulped down two mouthfuls of saliva.","Lin Yuan looked at Wen Yu’s expression, who was waiting to be praised, so he praised her first. “The development is going really well. But how did you do it?”","Lin Yuan was truly curious as to how this manor could reach this state in just two months.","When Wen Yu heard Lin Yuan’s question, her eyes immediately glistened as she started to speak nonstop. “Three Diamond Earth-Turning Giant Elephants to tear down the old site. But I felt that the old site’s soil wasn’t fertile enough, so I bought 500,000 catties of high-grade energy ores and two Diamond Soil-Flowing Titan Bears to bury the 500,000 catties of high-grade energy ores into the soil.”","Lin Yuan’s brows jolted as he gulped down his saliva and asked carefully, “Where did you find the three Diamond Earth-Turning Giant Elephants and two Soil-Flowing Titan Bears?”","Wen Yu revealed a sweet smile and said, “Construction Association!”","She then added, “After tearing down the old site and flattening the ground, I looked for a Class 4 Spirit Craftsmen team from the Spirit Craftsman Association to design and construct the courtyard. I asked them to work through the nights, and they finally completed this project yesterday afternoon.”","Among the lifestyle-class associations, the Spirit Craftsman Association was a huge association. The Construction Association’s job would be to balance the land and to design the estate’s blueprint. The Spirit Craftsman Association would be constructing according to the blueprint.","A Class 4 Spirit Craftsman, Scholar. Fey Observer, and Spiritual Ingredient Analyst had equivalent statuses. A Class 4 Spirit Craftsman might not be comparable with a Class 4 Creation Master, but Class 4 Spirit Craftsmen held a very important status in the Radiance Federation.","If a team of Class 4 Spirit Craftsmen worked throughout two months without rest, then it was really possible to create this huge manor within this short period.","At that moment, Wen Yu returned the beetle-shaped fey storage box that Lin Yuan had handed to her previously. Wen Yu handed it over with two hands and said, “Yesterday afternoon, I looked for a cleaning team to clean up the new manor the Class 4 Spirit Craftsmen team built.”","When Lin Yuan received the beetle-shaped fey storage box, he used his spiritual energy to scan inside and realized that not even one Radiance dollar had been used. He couldn’t help but look at Wen Yu with a puzzled expression.","Before this, Lin Yuan had still been thinking how much Radiance dollars had been spent since Earth-Turning Giant Elephants had been used to tear down the old site, Soil-Flowing Titan Bears had been used to bury 500,000 catties of high-grade energy ores, and a Class 4 Spirit Craftsmen team had been asked to expedite their work for two months.","Thus, it was surprising that not a single Radiance dollar had been used for such a huge project.","When Wen Yu saw Lin Yuan’s puzzled look, she turned to look at Liu Jie first and glanced at Liu Jie’s retainer crest before she spoke softly. “Previously, Lord Mystic came looking for the Young Master. After finding out that Young Master was in seclusion at the Creation Master Association and seeing that I was preparing to tear down the old site, he took over the project. After making the arrangements, he then handed it back to me for supervision.”","After speaking, Wen Yu stuck out her tongue. She had glanced at Liu Jue’s retainer crest to see whether it was embedded with the symbol of a moon. It was not, which meant that Lin Yuan had not replaced Liu Jie’s retainer crest with the new one after becoming the Moon Empress’ disciple.","Wen Yu didn’t know whether Liu Jie knew that Lin Yuan was the Radiant Moon Palace’s Young Lord. Thus, she had addressed Mystic Moon as Lord Mystic, instead of Lord Mystic Moon. After all, there was only one person with the title of Mystic Moon in the Radiance Federation.","Although Wen Yu had been tasked to construct the manor, even if Lin Yuan’s beetle-shaped fey storage box had enough Radiance dollars, she wouldn’t dare to squander them like that.","As Lin Yuan’s assistant, Wen Yu knew of her role. Naturally, she wouldn’t do anything","that would put Lin Yuan at a disadvantage. However, since Mystic Moon had taken over the project, Wen Yu didn’t have to hold back on the spending.","After all, it wasn’t Lin Yuan who had to pay. Lord Mystic Moon was the one that had to foot the bill.","As one of Radiant Moon Palace’s spirit attendants, Wen Yu had boundless respect toward Mystic Moon, one of the Radiant Moon Palace’s two Moon Envoys. However, now that she was Lin Yuan’s assistant, she naturally had to be more considerate toward Lin Yuan.","Hence, Wen Yu didn’t help Mystic Moon to save any money when purchasing the manor’s construction materials. All of the materials were the best that the Spirit Craftsman Association could provide.","As a spirit attendant of the Radiant Moon Palace, Wen Yu’s experience was naturally beyond regular people. The use of Diamond Earth-Turning Giant Elephants might be shocking for Liu Jie, but it was actually nothing much for Wen Yu.","The Radiant Moon Palace had plenty of rare feys, such as the two unique Diamond/Legend Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassias. Wen Yu had been able to see them on a daily basis, so she was already very accustomed to such a sight."]},{"number":176,"title":"Chapter 176: The Consecutively Shocked Liu Jie","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","If Wen Yu wished to save money for Lin Yuan, she wouldn’t even need to use Lin Yuan’s status as the Radiant Moon Palace’s Young Lord.","Once Wen Yu revealed her status as the Radiant Moon Palace’s spirit attendant, the experts in the Royal Capital would probably queue up to help with the manor’s construction. But as a spirit attendant of the Radiant Moon Palace, Wen Yu had a pride that originated from her soul and she would use that sense of pride to deal with others, apart from Lin Yuan.","The pride didn’t mean she was overbearing, but it was a kind of ego. This ego didn’t allow Wen Yu to accept any help from people trying to seek favors with the Radiant Moon Palace.","Lin Yuan knew that the Lord Mystic, which Wen Yu had mentioned, could only be Mystic Moon. However, he didn’t expect that Mystic Moon would actually help with the manor’s construction. He immediately took out his phone and made a call to Mystic Moon.","...","In the lotus pond, all sorts of lotus flowers were absorbing and exuding mist. The lotus flowers emitted a sunset-colored light, which was slowly rising up in the inner palace, projecting a pool of jade-like water.","The Platinum Spirit-Siphon Goldfish splashed around and blended into the breeze under this sunset-colored light.","However, this beautiful scenery was disturbed by a silver-robed and eminent man, who was standing by the lotus pond and letting out a wry smile.","The Moon Empress took a glance at Mystic Moon and felt the spirit tea that she was drinking was no longer fragrant.","Previously, the Moon Empress had asked Mystic Moon to visit the Chef Supreme to collect a Spirit Savory Pig. The Spirit Savory Pig was a unique fey that the Class 5 Creation Master Chef Supreme possessed.","It was just like the Radiant Moon Palace’s Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassias, but the Spirit Savory Pig didn’t have the same effects as the Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassias, which could cleanse the body’s impurities.","The Spirit Savory Pig was merely a kind of food ingredient, but those who ate the Spirit Savory Pig’s meat would know the taste of this world’s best delicacy. It was also the reason why the Spirit Savory Pig’s meat was known as the world’s No.1 meat.","The Moon Empress had originally wanted to ask Lin Yuan to eat this Spirit Savory Pig delicacy together, but when she had asked Mystic Moon to look for Lin Yuan, she found out that Lin Yuan was in seclusion again.","The Moon Empress couldn’t help lamenting. My disciple is a little too hardworking, right!? How can there be such a hardworking disciple in this world?! It is making me look very useless as a Master!","But just earlier, Wen Yu had visited the Radiant Moon Palace to settle the bill with Mystic Moon. The Moon Empress finally found out that Mystic Moon had been helping Lin Yuan build his manor. This made the Moon Empress extremely infuriated.","How can This Empress’ disciple be lacking money! Even if Cheng Wu is useless, he still has plenty of wealth and should have enough to build three manors! As a master, I didn’t even offer any help and was afraid that my disciple might not agree. But you actually went to the manor to take the merit!?","Mystic Moon naturally understood the Moon Empress’ thoughts. He might have an awkward and terrified expression, but he was still very thankful to Lin Yuan and happy for the Moon Empress.","For the past decade, the Moon Empress’ mood swings hadn’t been as lively until she accepted Lin Yuan as her disciple. When the Moon Empress had wanted to accept a disciple, Mystic Moon, one of her Moon Envoys, naturally didn’t have any opinions.","But toward Lin Yuan, Mystic Moon had merely been showing his concern due to the Moon Empress. However, after all their interactions, Mystic Moon had gradually approved of Lin Yuan from the bottom of his heart.","This was the Moon Empress’ disciple.","This was the Radiant Moon Palace’s Young Lord.","All of a sudden, Mystic Moon let out a bright peal of laughter. Now that the Radiant Moon Palace had an additional young lord, it wasn’t just the Moon Empress, the entire Radiant Moon Palace was livelier.","The Moon Empress already felt that her spirit tea was no longer fragrant, but after hearing Mystic Moon’s laughter, she suddenly felt that her spirit tea had turned bitter.","Before the Moon Empress could speak, Mystic Moon’s phone rang. When he took out the phone and saw the caller, he silently thought it wasn’t good. It was actually Lin Yuan who was calling him at this moment. Mystic Moon took a glance at the Moon Empress, who let out a snort and ignored him. Mystic Moon then picked up the phone.","...","When the call was connected, Lin Yuan spoke. “Uncle Mystic? I heard from Wen Yu that you helped me to construct the manor.”","Lin Yuan didn’t know how he should address Mystic Moon as the latter would always say it was inappropriate for Lin Yuan to call him Senior Mystic Moon. Mystic Moon and the Moon Empress were both his seniors, so Lin Yuan addressed him as Uncle Mystic now.","When Mystic Moon heard how Lin Yuan addressed him, he, who was normally clear and composed, actually choked on his own saliva and started coughing.","Even though he was rather pathetic when coughing, Mystic Moon’s heart surged with a warm current. Uncle Mystic? This is the first time anyone called me like this. It is strange yet very amiable.","“Young Lord, I am the one that found a master in the Construction Association to design your manor. I wonder if you are satisfied? If you aren’t, I can ask Wen Yu to look for the Spirit Craftsmen team to renovate the manor.”","Lin Yuan originally wanted to say something else, but after hearing how Mystic Moon was seriously considering if Lin Yuan was satisfied with the manor, he felt that he shouldn’t say anything that would make things too estranged.","Mystic Moon was a high-ranked expert and had plenty of things to do, but he had actually made the effort to construct this manor for Lin Yuan. It allowed Lin Yuan to feel that his sense of belonging to the Radiant Moon Palace wasn’t just because of his master, the Moon Empress.","“Uncle Mystic, the design of the manor is great.”","From the other side of the phone call came Mystic Moon’s clear laughter. “It is fine if you like it. Wen Yu is rather reliable when doing the tasks and has put in quite the effort for the supervision.”","Mystic Moon then praised Wen Yu. He hadn’t paid any attention to Wen Yu when she was a spirit attendant, but during the construction of the manor, Mystic Moon gave his approval of Wen Yu’s capability.","Lin Yuan’s manor’s surface area wasn’t small, and when Mystic Moon had been constructing the manor, he had thought if he should recommend two more spirit attendants to Lin Yuan. However, Wen Yu’s capability had made Mystic Moon dismiss the idea.","After hanging up the phone call, Mystic Moon saw the Moon Empress drinking her tea and looking at him. He couldn’t help shrinking his neck.","At that moment, the Moon Empress’ phone rang. She picked up the phone and immediately smiled. After hanging up the phone call, Mystic Moon received a question from the Moon Empress. “If you have a disciple, what gift should you give to your disciple?”","Mystic Moon’s brows involuntarily jumped. Isn’t the Moon Empress asking what gift she should give to Lin Yuan?","This was a matter that Mystic Moon wouldn’t dare to give any ideas. If he was the one that gave the idea and Lin Yuan rejected the gift, the Moon Empress might just send him on a desert mission.","Mystic Moon quickly replied, “Your Highness, I don’t even have a disciple, how could I know what to give?”","When the Moon Empress heard Mystic Moon’s response, her smile became even brighter as she said, “I know you don’t have a disciple. Even if you do, you will not have such a great disciple like This Empress.”","...","Lin Yuan hung up the phone and saw Wen Yu looking at him expectantly. Lin Yuan said, “Uncle Mystic praised you and said you are very reliable in your work.”","Wen Yu immediately let out a pleasantly surprised and bright smile. Wen Yu always respected Lord Mystic Moon, and she was truly surprised to receive Mystic Moon’s recognition.","Lin Yuan looked at the list in Wen Yu’s hand and asked, “Where are you going?”","Wen Yu waved the list in her hand and said, “Young Master, the manor doesn’t have any furniture now. Therefore, I wish to custom-order some furniture.”","Wen Yu’s words reminded Lin Yuan that he had placed plenty of furniture and wooden materials in the Spirit Lock spatial zone. Due to the high concentration of spirit qi in the Spirit Lock spatial zone, the furniture and wooden materials had already possessed a jade-like texture.","Actually, before Lin Yuan and Ling Xiao had arrived at the Royal Capital, those furniture and wooden materials had already turned slightly jade-like. During the past few months, Lin Yuan had already forgotten about those furniture and wooden materials as he had been enhancing feys. It was unknown how much more jade-like they had become.","Had it not been for Wen Yu’s reminder, Lin Yuan wouldn’t have recalled this.","Lin Yuan immediately waved his hand and took out some of the furniture in the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","When Lin Yuan took out the wooden materials with the jade-like texture, Liu Jie, who was originally admiring this manor’s scenery, nearly bit his tongue.","When Liu Jie carefully observed the jade-like furniture that Lin Yuan took out, he couldn’t catch his breath and got the hiccups. Liu Jie involuntarily lamented. What kind of Master did I actually follow?!"]},{"number":177,"title":"Chapter 177: Agarwood Like a Fixed Stone","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Liu Jie, who had been Sequence #39 in the Radiance Hundred Sequence two years ago, was considered to have a small fortune. His wealth accumulated in a year of competition and missions could add up to a few million Radiance dollars. However, he had used most of the Radiance dollars to raise his Insect Queen’s grade or quality.","The resources that spirit qi professionals needed to consume to nurture their feys was a bottomless pit. The stronger the expert, the more resources they would need to consume.","Nevertheless, Liu Jie looked at the furniture that Lin Yuan took out with a wave of his hand and felt his fundamental values toppled.","The jade-like furniture had always been a luxury in the Radiance Federation.","One hundred years after the Spirit Qi Awakening, jade was divided into two kinds—jadeites formed by ores or nephrites formed by jade-like wood.","Jadeites were expensive in the Radiance Federation, as they were considered a relatively rare spiritual ingredient, but nephrites were much more expensive than jadeites.","Before the Spirit Qi Awakening, there were many jadeites in the underground ore veins. After the Spirit Qi Awakening, the jadeites absorbed the world’s spirit qi and contained different functions.","Before the Spirit Qi Awakening, nephrites simply did not exist. In environments with extremely rich spirit qi, they could allow the wood surface to turn into jade, forming a thin outer layer of nephrite, which was extremely rare.","The wooden materials that formed the furniture Lin Yuan had taken out had completely turned into jade, and not just on the surface. The furniture had a uniquely mellow and transparent feeling of a nephrite.","It seemed to be able to filter the sunlight, dispersing it and turning into a gorgeous corrugated circle of light that reflected on the body as if a person was immersed in tranquility and gentleness.","Lin Yuan had taken out a lot of furniture this time. People would not bear to auction the jade-like furniture in Star Web’s Treasure Pavilion.","Although they did not have any special functions, they were luxury items wildly sought after in the Radiance Federation.","If Liu Jie had lamented at Wen Yu’s profligacy before, when he saw Liu Jie take out the furniture, he then understood.","Compared to this jade-like furniture, the money that had been spent on flattening the land and building the manor was only a small amount.","Lin Yuan currently did not expect that this ordinary furniture would actually turn out to be like that after being placed in the Spirit Lock spatial zone for some time. Even though Lin Yuan was not as surprised as Liu Jie, he still felt a little surprised upon touching the jade-like furniture.","However, Wen Yu was used to it, so she did not think that the furniture was remarkable. In her opinion, it was reasonable for Lin Yuan, the Radiant Moon Palace’s Young Lord, to have such things.","Lin Yuan and Liu Jie moved the jade-like furniture into the manor.","When they placed them inside, the furniture immediately made the simple manor different right away. Sunlight spilled in through the window, shining on the jade-like furniture that produced light ripples as if people were in the water.","At night, they would only need a lighted lamp. The furniture would immediately brighten up the manor with the light scattered from the lamp.","As Lin Yuan looked at the manor, he wore a bright smile on his face and revealed his white teeth, with a vigorous teenage spirit. This would be his home. When Chu Ci studied in the Royal Capital, she would not have to live in the school. She could just return to her home daily.","At that moment, he suddenly saw Wen Yu holding onto the table, looking somewhat dizzy, so he hurriedly asked her, “What’s wrong, Wen Yu?”","For the past few days, Lin Yuan had been completely wrapped up with evolving the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee and Chimey in the Royal Capital’s Creation Master Association’s breeding room. However, Wen Yu was also the same.","During these two months, she had supervised the work in the manor. Even if the team of Class 4 Spirit Craftsmen had worked overtime day and night to build the manor, they had also been divided into two groups. One batch would work during the day, while the other during the night. Each batch worked for 12 hours but had half a day to rest.","However, things were different for Wen Yu, as she had nearly not slept in order to better supervise the work. She would lean against the wall to take a nap when she was exhausted and hold on until the Class 4 Spirit Craftsmen finished building the manor.","Just after the manor’s construction, she also had not had the time to rest properly. She had instructed the cleaning team to clean the manor inside and out first. At present, she just could not hold on anymore.","Even though Wen Yu had consumed the drop of Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar Lin Yuan had given her and was very healthy, she was clearly experiencing hypoglycemia.","“Young Master, I’m just a little dizzy. I’ll go rest for a while after I cook for you and Big Brother Liu.”","Upon hearing that, Lin Yuan replied, “Sit here and rest for a while. We’ll order lunch.”","At that moment, Liu Jie said, “I’m familiar with the takeouts around here. I’ll order the food now.” Then, he took out his cell phone, ready to order food.","Lin Yuan took an incense burner carved with all kinds of auspicious feys from a nearby shelf. He searched with his spiritual energy in the Spirit Lock spatial zone and took out a piece of black-crystal-like wood.","It was very small, about ten centimeters long, and just two fingers thick. It was agarwood.","This agarwood had completely turned into jade, just like the wooden furniture, after being placed in Lin Yuan’s Spirit Lock spatial zone for a long time.","Lin Yuan gently broke the black-crystal-like agarwood with a snap, took a small section, and placed it in the incense burner. Then, he summoned Chimey that quickly understood what he wanted it to do. It used Scattered Light on the agarwood, causing a subtle light to land on and burn it. The burning agarwood emitted a very soothing aroma.","Before Lin Yuan’s body had recovered, he had always been prone to dizziness, so he had to prepare a lot of such wood. Agarwood was quite common, and he had stored quite a lot previously. Afterward, he had thrown them into the Spirit Lock spatial zone, as he could not use them.","The emitted aroma could be calming to the mind, and over time, Lin Yuan also liked its smell. Although the smell was subtle, the essence of the aroma was pure.","The agarwood was like a fixed stone. If the heart could be like this agarwood, why be afraid of the turmoil in the outside world?","When Wen Yu saw Lin Yuan burning the agarwood for her, she quickly said, “Young Master, this agarwood is precious. I’ll be fine after resting a while.”","Lin Yuan shook his head at her and answered, “Go take some rest after eating. It’s been hard on you.”","Lin Yuan had much jade-like agarwood in his Spirit Lock spatial zone. He would certainly have sold this jade-like furniture and agarwood when he had been short of money in the past to exchange for resources so that he and Chu Ci could improve their strength. However, he was no longer short of resources now.","The jade-like furniture and agarwood were just decorations in life. It was natural to use them when he needed them.","After Chimey had been summoned, it immediately chirped and flew from the first floor to the third floor. After circling twice and standing on the shelf, it chirped for a while. Then, it landed on Lin Yuan’s ear and intimately touched his fringe.","He looked at Chimey and could not help but reveal a pampered smile. It was really clingy."]},{"number":178,"title":"Chapter 178: Have No Choice but to Raise a Leech","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Liu Jie’s heart leaped when Lin Yuan broke the agarwood earlier. Other people with this jade-like agarwood would probably be afraid of breaking them, so they would cautiously store them and pass them down as a family heirloom.","However, Lin Yuan had actually broken it in his hand and used it.","Liu Jie had experienced the shock a few times before, so he was unconsciously used to it.","As compared to Lin Yuan using the jade-like agarwood so easily, he was more concerned about the azure blue bird standing and wheedling on Lin Yuan’s ear.","As a spirit qi professional who had comprehended a Willpower Rune, he could distinguish if a fey was a Fantasy Breed more clearly than ordinary spirit qi professionals. This was because Fantasy Breed feys emitted the Willpower Rune’s scent. To put it bluntly, they carried the world’s willpower on them.","Thus, when Lin Yuan summoned Chimey, Liu Jie could see that it was a Fantasy Breed. Liu Jie felt that Lin Yuan was like a veil of mist that could never be seen clearly.","When he had first met Lin Yuan and became his retainer, Liu Jie knew that Lin Yuan could heal his Insect Queen and was a Class 2 Creation Master. But after interacting with him, Lin Yuan had refreshed his perception, especially this Silver Fantasy Breed avian fey.","However, Liu Jie thought little of it, as he had long positioned himself as the strongest shield in front of Lin Yuan.","The better Lin Yuan’s talents were, and the stronger he was, the more he would encourage Liu Jie. This let him know he needed to work hard again and again to improve his strength. Otherwise, he might not even be qualified to become a shield over time.","Wen Yu looked at the young man, who was playing with the azure blue bird on his ear, through the white mist that rose from the agarwood in the incense burner and felt an indescribable feeling.","The hard work that she had put in for the past two months was more than just gratitude to the young man in front of her. Rather, she had gotten a new lease of life from one of his choices. What she needed to do was to fight for this new lease of life. At the same time, she was very grateful to herself for being optimistic about life.","Without her former self, how could this cheerful young man before her eyes have chosen her?","As the agarwood burned in the incense burner, its smell made it seem as if time had stopped. The quiet scene reflected the bright light from the jade-like furniture and the unspeakable quietness of the passage of time, which was disturbed by the takeout delivery.","After eating lunch, Wen Yu went to rest.","Liu Jie was going to buy some daily necessities and also spiritual ingredients with grades. As Lin Yuan’s retainer, he naturally had to live in the manor with him, so the manor was also considered his home.","Naturally, he could not order takeout for all his meals. Although it might be troublesome for him to cook sometimes, food’s fragrance could make the house cozier.","The 1,000-square-meters manor had a lot of rooms, and Lin Yuan still had to do some detailed planning for the arrangements.","He took out his cell phone and called Chu Ci. Instead of going back home during the holidays, she had gone to participate in the Redbud Hundred’s special training. She had not hidden her talents after returning to school. Her Fantasy Breed Obsidian Iron Wild Bull had attracted the school’s attention in the live combat class. Ling Xiao had also handpicked her as a seeded participant in the Redbud Hundred Sequence.","Lin Yuan was not worried about her training outside during the holidays, as Cold Moon had gone to Redbud City. With Cold Moon around, Chu Ci naturally would not face any dangers. The real danger was the people who had any opinions of her because of her talents.","After hanging up and knowing Chu Ci was doing fine, Lin Yuan suddenly realized Zhang Xiaobai had posted in his friends’ circle. Lin Yuan did not add many people as his friends on his cell phone, except for his Master, the Moon Empress, his sister, Chu Ci, Cold Moon, Mystic Moon, Wen Yu, Liu Jie, and the Extreme Guild Club’s quartet. Adding them up, there were only 11 people. However, they did not usually post in the friends’ circle except for Zhang Xiaobai.","When he opened his friends’ circle, Lin Yuan saw Zhang Xiaobai had taken a photo of a cup with a Bronze wolfberry in it. He wrote the following words:","Zhang Xiaobai: “I have no choice but to raise a leech. Soaking wolfberry in the insulated cup.”","Lin Yuan thought for a moment and replied below.","Lin Yuan: “Wolfberry can hardly stop the leech. Add angelica.”","Lin Yuan was about to put down his cell phone when Zhang Xiaobai suddenly replied to him in the friends’ circle.","Zhang Xiaobai: “Angelica can hardly stop Xin Ying’s hammer. Soak ginseng and deer antler in shaojiu1.”","Lin Yuan looked at Zhang Xiaobai’s reply and raised his brows. At that moment, Tan Ran replied below.","Tan Ran: “Brother Zhang, are you trying to ‘battle’ with Lin Yuan?”","Zhang Xiaobai: “Actually, when I was about to say, ‘Ginseng and deer antlers are not enough. I also need kidney skewers and kidney supplements.’, Lin Yuan had already lost.”","Lu Pinru: “You’re just craving roasted kidney skewers!”","Xin Ying: “Zhang Xiaobai, did you pour the wolfberry drink I gave you into the toilet bowl and didn’t flush it? Are you trying to provoke me?”","Lin Yuan found that Zhang Xiaobai was quiet after Xin Ying sent this message. He brainstormed and thought that Zhang Xiaobai should be suffering Xin Ying’s iron fist of justice right now.","He exhaled gently. It seemed that he had won the ‘battle’. He returned to his bedroom and went onto Star Web, which he had not done in a long time.","It had to be said that he had not been on Star Web much. During these four months, Lin Yuan had been busy with improving his strength. He had even just shipped four months’ worth of goods to Zhou Jiaxin in one go.","When he went on Star Web again, Lin Yuan realized there were tens of thousands of unread messages in his Star Web store. Among them, nearly 1,000 of them were from merchants who wanted to buy a lot of feys from his store, as the feys he sold were in high demand and short supply in the market.","Every time Lin Yuan put these feys for sale, those people waiting would sweep them away within a few minutes. If they did not manage to do so when Lin Yuan put the feys on sale, then they could dream about buying other feys from his store.","Lin Yuan ignored these purchasing requests. Since the feys sold in his store were in short supply and they would be sold out right away every time he put them on sale, he would not just sell them to anyone. This would not help his store’s fame.","These thousands of messages came from some customers seeking to buy his feys. For the remaining tens of thousands of messages, he realized they came from a group under his store.","Lin Yuan was puzzled, as he did not remember joining any groups. Why did he have so many messages?","He clicked on it and understood why."]},{"number":179,"title":"Chapter 179: The Purchase With No Loss Store’s Fan Club","paragraphs":["This group was actually his store’s fan club. After each completed transaction from his Star Web store, the buyers could rate his store once and choose to spend a certain price to enter his fan club.","People would usually not enter such a store’s fan club. After all, which customers would be willing to pay a certain price after buying from one’s store to join their fan club?","Some large Class 4 and Class 5 stores presided by Creation Masters might have such a privilege.","Actually, joining such a fan club was so that they could better spend in the store or communicate with the store owner.","Lin Yuan looked at his store’s fan club, where there were only 37 people.","How had these 37 people crazily created tens of thousands of messages?","Lin Yuan could not help but feel dumbfounded.","He had not put many new feys on sale in the last few months, and each time he did, the few people waiting online had snatched them away. Therefore, there were only a few buyers every time he put new ones on sale.","Presently, Lin Yuan’s Purchase With No Loss store had a little reputation on Star Web. However, his store’s reputation was somewhat interesting. The store buyers found that this store was indeed like its name, as one simply could buy nothing.","Almost all the customers who had purchased feys from his store had joined the fan club. At first, they had joined because they wanted to meet Lin Yuan and see if they could get more goods from him.","Not only had they not managed to meet the mysterious owner, Lin Yuan, but various fake news from other people in the group had also cheated them.","Every time someone shouted that the store had new feys for sale, the other people in the group who wanted to buy the goods would go over immediately, only to find out there was nothing.","The most outrageous thing was that a few people in the group had the bright idea of setting an alarm clock in the middle of the night.","It took those people great efforts to wake up in the morning, yet they would immediately become spirited once the alarm clock rang. They would shout in the fan club, “There are new feys on sale!”","They had tricked most people in the group into waiting at Lin Yuan’s store. However, after one hour, two hours, they would find nothing and end up being duped.","On the contrary, all of them were smart when there were new goods. Those who managed to snatch would boast in the fan club. Slowly, the people in Lin Yuan’s fan club had developed a competitive friendship.","Lin Yuan’s fan club numbers grew very slowly. After all, it was really hard to emerge from the dozens of hungry wolves and snatch the feys to have the qualification to join the fan club.","Lin Yuan realized that there were many familiar people in this group chat—the braised egg head(Stream in the Cloud), Zhou Jiaxin, the violent-tempered woman, and the Buddha-tempered person.","The braised egg head and Big Sister Xin were clearly the most active among them and had the potential to become the Deputy Club Leader.","Stream in the Cloud: “Deep Mountain Elder Lin hasn’t been on Star Web recently. As the store owner, he has said nothing in his fan club.”","Violent-Tempered Woman: “He might be busy.”","Stream in the Cloud: “If he is, Big Sister Xin and I will help to manage the fan club. We can’t let those who joined in late have a chance of being cheated.”","Violent-Tempered Woman: “Let them all stand in punishment at the store entrance in the middle of the night!”","Then, she tagged the Buddha-tempered person.","Buddha-Tempered Person: “The Buddha asked, why did you tag me?”","Violent-Tempered Woman: “Buddha has long cried with you bringing it up every day. Last time, you bluffed me that there were new goods and made me wait bitterly for three hours! You wait and see for the next six months!”","Buddha-Tempered Person: “The Buddha said to requite evil with good.”","Violent-Tempered Woman: “Did the Buddha tell you that what comes around goes around?”","Stream in the Cloud: “Don’t you guys think these prodigies reported on the Star Web recently are simply too powerful?”","Zhou Jiaxin: “Redbud Intermediate Spirit Qi Academy has a spirit qi professional with a Bronze Fantasy Breed defense-type fey. I’ve never heard of such a fey before. This young girl has become a benchmark for top geniuses, and she’s known as the ‘1-in-4,000-years rare genius’!”","Stream in the Cloud: “Do you guys know about the recently famous Black? Star Web reported Black has a Silver Fantasy Breed healing-type fey that can make limbs grow back.”","Violent-Tempered Woman: “The entire Radiance Federation only has a few Fantasy Breed healing-type feys.”","Stream in the Cloud: “Including Black’s Silver Fantasy Breed fey, there should currently be dozens of them. However, I’ve never heard of a Fantasy Breed healing-type fey that can make limbs grow back.”","Violent-Tempered Woman: “I heard that the king-class expert Sand King posted a message on Star Web, hoping that Black can help heal his son’s broken left leg. He’s willing to pay with a Platinum/Flawless fey.”","Stream in the Cloud: “I later heard that Sand King deleted the message. I wonder if he found Black to heal his son.”","Violent-Tempered Woman: “I wonder if Black’s healing-type fey is as powerful as reported.”","Zhou Jiaxin: “Everyone in Millstone Town said so. It certainly can’t be wrong! And Black is a hero! You’ll know when you see more posts about him!”","Stream in the Cloud: “I don’t dare to look at posts related to him. I heard that you have to be especially careful of an administrator called Ancestor Peace. If anyone dares to talk bad about Black, and they aren’t as fast as the Divine Travel Black Swallow, they won’t be able to protect themselves.”","Buddha-Tempered Person: “Big Sister Xin, are you Black’s fangirl?”","Violent-Tempered Woman: “A fangirl? She’s an aunty fan!”","Zhou Jiaxin: “None of your business!”","Although Lin Yuan knew people would pay attention to Chu Ci when she revealed her talents, and she would become a household name, he did not expect that almost everyone would know her in a span of two months. Likewise, he did not expect his identity as Black to draw so much attention.","Regarding Sand King, Lin Yuan simply could not figure out what was going on, nor did he have any idea.","Lin Yuan was going to climb the Star Tower as Black, and when he ascended to the Celestial Stairway, he would naturally be exposed to the Radiance Federation people.","This was because Star Web would record every battle after reaching the Celestial Stairway and store them in the video library. Every Stab Web user could watch these recorded battles for a certain price.","Star Web would take part of the income from these viewings and distribute the rest to the duel’s winner in the video. Only the winner could receive the proceeds from the video.","Every expert who climbed above the Celestial Stairway was akin to a star.","At present, it felt amazing with people discussing him behind his back.","After Lin Yuan observed, he silently lurked. After he put a new batch of Elite Spirit-Siphon Goldfish and Bronze Usneas in the Purchase With No Loss store, he visited Zhou Jiaxin’s store.","This time, Lin Yuan was going to buy a lot of goods from her store. He had almost consumed all the inferior energy ores and low-grade energy ores that he had stocked up."]},{"number":180,"title":"Chapter 180: Zhou Jiaxin Has Something to Say","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Originally, Lin Yuan didn’t need to purchase any more Normal Spirit-Siphon Goldfish. He was planning to wait for that batch of Five Fortune Ranchu to evolve from Normal to Elite grade and sell them. However, when Lin Yuan was in seclusion for a few months, those Five Fortune Ranchus had actually broken through to the Elite grade and had substantial growth.","Many of them had already reached Elite VI and VII. If these Five Fortune Ranchus were nurtured for a little more time, they would be halfway into the Bronze grade.","The Five Fortune Ranchu was an auspicious breed of Spirit-Siphon Goldfish, and an Elite Five Fortune Ranchu could be sold for 60 to 70 Radiance dollars. But once its grade reached Bronze, the prices of the Five Fortune Ranchus would increase by over a hundred times and reach close to 10,000 Radiance dollars.","Bronze Five Fortune Ranchus were actually no different from other Bronze Spirit-Siphon Goldfish. Nonetheless, the price difference was at least 30 times more. It was due to the vibrant multi-colors on the Five Fortune Ranchu and its adorably plump body. It signified that all five fortunes were present and also indicated health and prosperity.","Due to the auspicious signs and rarity of the Five Fortune Ranchus, they were actively sought out.","Lin Yuan was planning to grow these Five Fortune Ranchus to the Bronze grade before putting them for sale on the Star Web store. This way, his Star Web store would have an instant surge in reputation.","Lin Yuan was preparing to manage the Star Web store mainly because he had to enhance feys’ grades in order to increase the spiritual power in his body. During this time, Lin Yuan might still feel the growth of his spiritual power, but it was growing at an extremely gradual pace. It was obvious that Lin Yuan still had a rather long path before becoming a B-rank spirit qi professional.","During the past four months, Lin Yuan had been mainly upgrading his feys’ quality. Apart from Red Thorn, he had upgraded the rest of his feys’ quality to Legend. In terms of enhancing the grade, apart from the Jasmine Lily and Chimey, which had evolved from Bronze/Fantasy to Silver/Fantasy, and the Gold Acid Corrosion Queen Bee, Lin Yuan hadn’t really enhanced the grade of other feys.","This was part of the reason why Lin Yuan’s spiritual power growth was rather slow.","Therefore, for the next period, Lin Yuan would climb the Star Tower and enhance a massive number of feys to increase his spiritual power. After enhancing all the feys, Lin Yuan would naturally put them on sale in his Star Web store.","Lin Yuan wasn’t just going to separate his statuses as a Creation Master and as a combat-class spirit qi professional. He was also going to make changes to the Star Web store.","In the future, the Star Web store would only be selling high in demand feys that Lin Yuan enhanced in batches. As for those truly rare feys that he enhanced and those custom-ordered services, Lin Yuan would be conducting them in his newly built manor in the Royal Capital.","Just by looking at the fan club for Purchase With No Loss Fey Store, Lin Yuan knew that no matter how many new feys he put up, the fan club’s number wouldn’t increase significantly. In fact, recruitment was only going to get harder in the future. Before anyone would enter the fan club, they would need to see if they were able to successfully purchase any of the new feys on the Star Web store. To purchase any feys from the Purchase With No Loss Fey Store, they would need to see if these hungry wolves in the fan club would agree.","After reaching Zhou Jiaxin’s store, Lin Yuan realized that her store was twice as big as before. It seemed like when Lin Yuan had been in seclusion, her store had upgraded from Class 3 to Class 4. When he saw Zhou Jiaxin in the store, he realized that she was gnashing her teeth and harping about something.","“Buddha-Tempered Person is a shameless old hag! Her heart is simply black! This time, everything has been taken up by that old hag! Damn it!”","Subsequently, Zhou Jiaxin lifted her head and saw Lin Yuan. Her face immediately revealed a smile as she walked over quickly. “Lin Yuan, it has been some time since you visited.”","One month ago, by using the large quantities of Bronze Usneas and Elite Spirit-Siphon Goldfish provided by Lin Yuan, Zhou Jiaxin had finally and successfully promoted this Class 3 store into a Class 4 store. After the promotion, the size of the store had increased by at least two times.","This had allowed Zhou Jiaxin to rearrange the store, leading to a more comprehensive supply of feys and spiritual ingredients.","Zhou Jiaxin’s store had always had a good reputation, so when it was promoted to Class 4, her reputation had received a huge burst, allowing her business to be much better than before.","However, Zhou Jiaxin knew that everything that had happened was because of this youth in front of her. Had it not been for the huge supply of Bronze Usneas and Elite Spirit-Siphon Goldfish, even if she worked hard for ten years, she wouldn’t be able to promote this store to Class 4.","In fact, during the past few times when Lin Yuan delivered the goods to her, Zhou Jiaxin had realized that Lin Yuan’s feys were different from the ones that other Creation Masters sold. The feys’ grade and quality might be the same as the ones other Creation Masters provided, but Lin Yuan’s feys were much better in appearance.","Take the Usneas, for example. The Usneas Lin Yuan provided would have thicker stems and plumper leaves that contained more juices too. They were far better than the other Bronze Usneas in the market.","It was the same as two individuals, one was stronger while the other was weaker.","In the past, Zhou Jiaxin’s store hadn’t had the support of any Creation Masters, so she knew that a Class 3 store was already the limits of her capability. Only by relying on a Creation Master would she be able to upgrade her store to Class 4 and continue to maintain the status.","This youth in front of her was already a Class 2 Creation Master at such a young age, so it was enough to say that his talent was truly immeasurable.","Furthermore, after seeing how Lin Yuan’s store was constantly putting new feys for sale, Zhou Jiaxin knew how terrifying Lin Yuan’s capability and background was.","There were plenty of veteran Class 4 stores that were trying all methods to contact the owner of Purchase With No Loss Fey Store to cooperate. It was enough to prove the influence that Lin Yuan’s store had right now.","After hearing Zhou Jiaxin’s greeting, Lin Yuan let out a sunshine smile and said, “I have been busy upgrading the quality of my feys. Thus, I didn’t have time to visit until now. Aren’t I here to provide the goods for Big Sister Xin now that I am free?”","When Zhou Jiaxin saw the sunshine smile on Lin Yuan’s face and thought how her store was immediately promoted to Class 4, she firmed down her thoughts. She then used a serious expression to ask, “Lin Yuan, how do you think of Big Sister Xin’s store?”","When Lin Yuan heard Zhou Jiaxin’s sudden question and saw her serious expression, he took a careful look at the store that Zhou Jiaxin managed tidily and neatly after the promotion into a Class 4 store.","At present, the store had an obviously bigger influx of customers than the previous time he had visited.","“Big Sister Xin has been managing this store very well. Big Sister Xin’s business must be booming nowadays.”","In fact, when Zhou Jiaxin asked Lin Yuan about her store, he already had a vague feeling and knew what she was going to say next."]},{"number":181,"title":"Chapter 181: A Feeling as Though Life Is at the Pinnacle","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Zhou Jiaxin was at a loss for a moment. When Zhou Jiaxin had promoted her store to Class 4, she had already firmed up on the idea that had popped in her mind. However, it was useless even if she was determined, as the decision-maker for this idea wasn’t in Zhou Jiaxin’s control. It would be up to this youth’s opinion.","Zhou Jiaxin didn’t immediately speak of her thoughts. Instead, she walked to the counter and took out a document that had been drafted a long time ago and said, “Lin Yuan, take a look at this.”","Zhou Jiaxin was a decisive person and always did things with resolve. Otherwise, she wouldn’t have been able to promote this store to Class 3 without a Creation Master’s backing. In fact, her store had only been one step away from promoting to Class 4 before meeting Lin Yuan.","When Zhou Jiaxin had thought of the idea, she had immediately drafted up this document. However, this document had been in here for over a month, and every time Zhou Jiaxin had a different idea, she would take the document out. Unknowingly, she had already edited it at least three times. Each edit would cause extreme pain to Zhou Jiaxin, but she would be extremely determined when making each edit.","When Lin Yuan read the document, he couldn’t help raising his brows. He sighed silently. I guessed it correctly, as expected.","However, the content of the document gave Lin Yuan quite a shock.","Zhou Jiaxin’s document was actually a collaboration agreement, and the contents were very simple. It was to maintain the current collaboration model, and 20% of the profit from Zhou Jiaxin’s store would be the remuneration for Lin Yuan to continue supplying goods to Zhou Jiaxin. At the same time, Zhou Jiaxin even granted 30% of the store’s shares as a condition for Lin Yuan to increase the supply quantity.","The 30% of shares was an additional bonus that didn’t include the 20% profits. If the store closed down when the store was sold, Lin Yuan would still receive compensation from the 30% of shares.","Of course, there was a prerequisite. Lin Yuan wasn’t allowed to sell the 30% of shares while the store was still operating normally.","After reading this collaboration agreement carefully, Lin Yuan was rather surprised. This agreement was at least twice as good as those agreements provided by Class 5 stores when they worked with their chief Creation Master. Most of the Class 5 stores would provide huge bonuses for the Creation Master that backed them, but only a rare few would be willing to offer the store’s shares to the Creation Master.","Lin Yuan already knew that Zhou Jiaxin was a person who insisted on the quality of spiritual ingredients and was a very sincere and honest business owner. However, he didn’t expect Zhou Jiaxin to actually have such courage.","Lin Yuan silently considered the feasibility of this collaboration agreement. He didn’t try to be unreasonable with the superior conditions that Zhou Jiaxin offered. After all, Lin Yuan had been managing his own fey store since the age of eight, so he was already a businessman.","Lin Yuan was willing to supply goods to Zhou Jiaxin mainly because she risked reserving severely injured feys that might die for him to choose. Otherwise, Lin Yuan wouldn’t have the chance to obtain feys like the Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus and Cinnabar Osmanthus Haworthia.","Even with Lin Yuan’s current wealth, he might be able to obtain the Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus, but he still wouldn’t be able to obtain the Cinnabar Osmanthus Haworthia.","In essence, the Cinnabar Osmanthus Haworthia had a similar value with the Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia. The Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia could eliminate the impurities in the body, while the Cinnabar Osmanthus Haworthia could increase the spiritual energy.","The Cinnabar Osmanthus Haworthia might not be like the Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia—there were only two in the world—but it was rather rare too.","It was because of Zhou Jiaxin’s investment and effort. Lin Yuan was able to feel it, so he was willing to supply goods to Zhou Jiaxin’s store.","Otherwise, if Lin Yuan was truly out to sell feys, he might as well have placed them up for sale on Purchase With No Loss Fey Store. After all, the feys would all be snatched in a few seconds no matter how many he put up for sale.","The feys Lin Yuan provided, when compared to the high demand in the Radiance Federation’s market, his supply was just a drop in the ocean.","However, Lin Yuan had to admit that this collaboration agreement proposed by Zhou Jiaxin had conditions that didn’t allow Lin Yuan to disagree as a businessman.","Zhou Jiaxin’s store was already a Class 4 one now. Lin Yuan might not be able to sell the shares that were offered by Zhou Jiaxin, but just the dividends from the 30% of shares were already a great sum. Furthermore, the 20% of the profit was also additional, making it two levels of profits.","After all the calculations, Lin Yuan only had to provide more goods to Zhou Jiaxin and would be able to obtain a pure profit of 41% from Zhou Jiaxin’s operations. Such a profit was truly significant. In addition, Lin Yuan wasn’t providing the goods for free as Zhou Jiaxin would still need to purchase the goods at the price that they had set previously.","Zhou Jiaxin watched as Lin Yuan was constantly reading this agreement and couldn’t help feeling nervous. She was truly afraid that Lin Yuan would reject her, but if she had to increase the number of profits sharing or increase the number of shares, she couldn’t do it.","Zhou Jiaxin had already split 41% of the store’s pure profit with Lin Yuan and still had to spend additional money to purchase goods. After all the calculations, Zhou Jiaxin actually didn’t earn as much as when she was operating a Class 3 store. The Class 4 store was two times bigger than the Class 3 store, and Zhou Jiaxin had to hire two more store staff members. Coupled with the maintenance required to open a Class 4 store in the Star Web, not much money would come into Zhou Jiaxin’s hands.","From the angle of a business person, Zhou Jiaxin’s decision wasn’t wise. However, Zhou Jiaxin wasn’t just a business person. She was also a person with ambitions.","Five years ago, Zhou Jiaxin had painstakingly developed a Class 1 store until it was now a Class 4 store. Zhou Jiaxin knew clearly that if she didn’t make a deep collaboration with Lin Yuan and if he decided to stop the supply to her store one day, her Class 4 store would immediately lose its core selling point. The reputation of the store would then decline harshly.","In fact, when Lin Yuan had supplied the goods, Zhou Jiaxin had experienced a kind of joy that she hadn’t felt when operating the store.","In the past, she would be thinking of all sorts of methods for the customer to spend more money to purchase the spiritual ingredients and feys in her store. However, now, it was the customers that would say all sorts of nice words to purchase the Bronze Usneas and Elite Spirit-Siphon Goldfish that Lin Yuan supplied.","It was simply a satisfying feeling!","After investing all her efforts into the store and being begged by others to sell her goods, it was truly an utmost enjoyment that could only be felt at the pinnacle of life.","If Zhou Jiaxin had to describe such a feeling, she would probably have jumped out and yelled out, “Such a high! I feel as though life is at the pinnacle!”","The past few months’ experiences had given Zhou Jiaxin an eye-opener. She didn’t have a change of concept on how to manage her store, but at the same time, she grew something called ambition.","Zhou Jiaxin wished to promote her Star Web store to Class 5 while she was still alive!","Ever since that thought had flashed in Zhou Jiaxin’s mind, it had only been getting stronger. Finally, it was already irreversible."]},{"number":182,"title":"Chapter 182: Ostrich Guild Club","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","However, Zhou Jiaxin understood that she would need to rely on this youth if she wished to promote the store to Class 5. Just as Zhou Jiaxin felt as though her heart was thumping so much that it would jump out, and when she was so nervous that her throat was feeling dry, she saw the youth lifting his head and giving a sunshine smile.","He revealed a small set of white teeth and said, “The conditions offered by Big Sister Xin are very good. I agree to the terms stated in the collaboration agreement. We can collaborate.”","Lin Yuan’s words and sunshine smile allowed Zhou Jiaxin to put her heart back to its original place while there was a surge of ecstasy in her heart. Zhou Jiaxin knew that once this agreement was set with the youth, even if it was unknown if her store could reach Class 5, it would certainly maintain its Class 4 status.","“Lin Yuan, now that you are also a boss of the store, I shall let you see the detailed profit report during this period.”","Lin Yuan shook his hand and said, “Big Sister Xin, I will only provide the goods according to the agreement. I will not be involved with the management of the store.”","Lin Yuan’s words allowed Zhou Jiaxin’s heart to firm down. She was really afraid that Lin Yuan might want to change various management methods for the store.","Lin Yuan had very simple reasons to refuse.","Firstly, he didn’t have the time to help Zhou Jiaxin with the management of the store.","Secondly, Zhou Jiaxin was doing a great job with the management, and he didn’t have any opinions to provide.","Thirdly, the store was the same as a team of combat-class spirit qi professionals. Each team member might be able to provide their opinions, but the team could only have one leader and one main voice, especially during combat.","Otherwise, two voices might just split the full force into two, even though the objective was to push forward. But when two forces were pushing toward the same objective, there would be implications and interferences between the two forces.","Lin Yuan used a pen to sign the agreement, and after verifying it with the Star Web laws, it was now officially effective.","The load on Zhou Jiaxin’s mind had finally been resolved today.","At that moment, Zhou Jiaxin watched as Lin Yuan’s slender fingers with distinct bone structures placed the pen and document on the counter.","“Big Sister Xin, since I am already one of the bosses of the store, then I shall also contribute to this store. After some time, I might not be supplying Bronze Usneas anymore. Instead, they will be switched to Silver Usneas.”","Lin Yuan’s words overjoyed Zhou Jiaxin. If Lin Yuan could provide Silver Usneas, then the store could rely on the Silver Usneas to break through to Class 5, and it was almost certain.","Lin Yuan truly brought her a huge, pleasant surprise. Zhou Jiaxin could already imagine the customers in her store that would be going crazy as they would want to purchase those Silver Usneas in the store.","Zhou Jiaxin was actually making plans that all future customers must reach a certain purchase quota in order to qualify for the purchase of Silver Usneas.","Zhou Jiaxin’s store had been selling feys and spiritual ingredients that were fundamental but had great quality. All these fundamental spiritual ingredients were things that most Star Web stores possessed. All along, Zhou Jiaxin had never really had any ability to compete and would always rely on superior quality.","However, with the Silver Usneas now, Zhou Jiaxin could use them as the core to push the sales of all fundamental spiritual ingredients in the store. Zhou Jiaxin couldn’t help but feel that when she had tried her best to build connections with Lin Yuan, it was the most important and best decision she had made for the store after all these years.","In the past, Zhou Jiaxin had always felt that the highest level of bootlicking was to bootlick without leaving any traces or presence. But now, she had changed her original thoughts—the highest level of bootlicking was not to leave any traces and presence, at the same time, obtain a huge group of bootlickers yourself.","After verifying the agreement together with Zhou Jiaxin, Lin Yuan purchased plenty of low-grade energy ores and Normal Spirit-Siphon Goldfish, making this a fruitful trip.","Lin Yuan might be the boss of this store too, but business was still business between him and Zhou Jiaxin. Just like how Zhou Jiaxin would need to spend to purchase the feys from him, he would also need to spend to purchase spiritual ingredients and feys from the store.","However, when Lin Yuan purchased anything from Zhou Jiaxin’s store, he would also obtain a compensation of 41% in pure profits. For Lin Yuan, who purchased huge quantities of energy ores, he would be able to save up quite a bit of Radiance dollars after days and months of savings.","After selling the goods, Lin Yuan left the Star Web.","Due to the new address, Lin Yuan had changed the delivery address from the small fey store in Redbud City’s Xia Region to the manor in the Royal Capital’s outskirts. Lin Yuan realized that the Ostrich Logistics were particularly fast this time and used less than one hour to deliver the goods.","It seemed like Zhou Jiaxin’s actual address was also nearby the Royal Capital.","The Ostrich Logistics was truly a powerful organization in the Radiance Federation. When Lin Yuan traveled from the Royal Capital to Redbud City, even if he rode on the Platinum Divine Travel Black Swallow, he would also need three to four days. But for the couriers of Ostrich Logistics, they would always be able to deliver the goods within three hours, no matter the address.","It was basically due to the fact that the Ostrich Logistics nurtured a unique spatial-type fey. This kind of spatial-type fey was able to conduct long-distance teleportation. This was also why Ostrich Logistics was able to become a giant in the logistic world.","Lin Yuan could see Ah Neng carrying over a dozen Bronze fey storage boxes. As Ah Neng had become Lin Yuan’s exclusive courier over the past few months, Lin Yuan could feel that she was gradually developing into a veteran. However, some things remained unchanged—Ah Neng’s carelessness and optimism.","Ah Neng quickly waved her hand when she saw Lin Yuan and said, “Mister Lin, aren’t I fast this time? Since Mister Lin changed address, Ah Neng doesn’t have to be teleported for such a long time, making me dizzy. Aiya!”","When Ah Neng waved her hand at Lin Yuan, she seemed to forget that she was carrying the Bronze fey storage boxes. As a result, some of the boxes fell onto the ground.","Ah Neng rubbed her short purple-red hair embarrassedly and started to arrange the Bronze fey storage boxes on the ground.","Lin Yuan had purchased a huge amount of low-grade energy ores, and without over a dozen of Bronze fey storage boxes, they wouldn’t fit.","Lin Yuan walked over and helped Ah Neng with the arrangement. After arranging the Bronze fey storage boxes, Ah Neng swished her short hair, revealed her two little tiger teeth, and said in a pitiful voice, “Mister Lin, newcomer Courier 3451, Ah Neng might not be able to make deliveries for some time.”","Lin Yuan listened to Ah Neng and looked at her while waiting for her to continue.","Ah Neng blinked reluctantly twice before she revealed an extremely optimistic smile. “Ah Neng is a member of the Ostrich Guild Club’s S Tournament Reserve Team. In another two months, the S Tournament will begin, so Ah Neng has to return to the team for special training. But after the S Tournament, newcomer Courier 3451 will still be your exclusive courier.”","During the past few months, whenever Lin Yuan’s store delivered or received goods, Ah Neng would be the one making the deliveries. Therefore, Lin and Ah Neng had really become close acquaintances.","Back at the Xia Region, when Lin Yuan had learned that Ah Neng possessed the Gold Armor-Piercing Insect and Canister Shot Insect, he knew that her status in the Ostrich Logistics wasn’t simple.","As expected, Ah Neng was a newcomer that was supported by the Ostrich Logistics and even a member of the Ostrich Guild Club, S Tournament Reserve Team, which was under the Ostrich Logistics.","The Ostrich Guild Club was different from the Extreme Guild Club Zhang Xiaobai and Xin Ying were from. The Extreme Guild Club was just a B-level guild club, but the Ostrich Guild Club was among the top 16 guild clubs in the entire Radiance Federation and was part of the A-level guild clubs.","“Ah Neng, good luck with the S Tournament! By the time you return, you will no longer be the newcomer courier, Ah Neng. You will be the senior courier, Ah Neng. During this period, Ah Neng has been doing a great job.”","Ah Neng was rarely praised, so when Lin Yuan praised her, she was overjoyed and revealed her two small tiger teeth, making her particularly cute.","“Then Mister Lin shall wait for the senior courier, Ah Neng, to return from the S Tournament and be your exclusive courier again. During the S Tournament, I will use a bullet rain to extinguish my opponent’s pain.”","While speaking, Ah Neng made a fist as though to prove herself to Lin Yuan and encourage herself.","After receiving the goods, Lin Yuan stored all of these Bronze fey storage boxes that were filled with low-grade energy ores into the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","After arranging the low-grade energy ores and Normal Spirit-Siphon Goldfish he had bought from Zhou Jiaxin’s store, Lin Yuan returned to his room and changed to another Star Web Card before logging into the Star Web.","After logging into the Star Web, Lin Yuan asked Genius to use its exclusive skill and turn into a mask for him to wear. This time, Lin Yuan didn’t log into the Star Web as the store owner of Purchase With No Loss Fey Store or the Class 2 Creation Master. He was logging into the Star Web as the combat-class spirit qi professional, Black.","Lin Yuan’s objective this time was to climb the tower and break through to the Celestial Stairway. He would use this process when climbing the tower to feel his strength and weakness. He could also use this time to develop a mutual understanding and teamwork with his newly upgraded partners during battle."]},{"number":183,"title":"Chapter 183: I Admit That You Are a Fan of Black","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Back at the Guild Alliance, Lin Yuan had separated his statuses of Creation Master and combat-class spirit qi professional. They were set apart for his two Star Web Cards.","Lin Yuan’s status as Black, the healing-type spirit qi professional, was naturally bound to Lin Yuan’s record when he climbed the Star Tower.","When Lin Yuan had climbed the Star Tower previously, he had stopped when he defeated the spirit qi professional who possessed three Bronze snake-species feys.","At that time, Lin Yuan’s strongest fey had only been his bronze-grade Chimey.","If that spirit qi professional with the three snake-species feys hadn’t publicly given out his feys’ information, Lin Yuan wouldn’t have been able to gain the upper hand first. Lin Yuan had used swift commands to Chimey and used tactics, along with the exclusive skill, Clear Sky, to win the battle.","In fact, that spirit qi professional with the snake-species feys had revealed his feys’ information because he had been trying to act tough!","Lin Yuan still remembered that the highest the spirit qi professional had climbed was the 37th floor. As for Lin Yuan, he was only on the 22nd floor. Therefore, that spirit qi professional had found a reason to flaunt his superiority.","Every ten floors of the Star Tower was a jump, so for a spirit qi professional who had been to the 37th floor, he had naturally not taken Lin Yuan seriously as the highest the latter had climbed was only on the 22nd floor.","Nonetheless, in Lin Yuan’s opinion, exposing one’s trump cards to others was the most foolish choice anyone could make.","As compared to the time when Lin Yuan had fought with the spirit qi professional with the snake-species feys, Lin Yuan’s strength now had undergone an overwhelming change.","Lin Yuan had yet to lose when climbing the tower, so his win rate on the Star Tower was still 100%.","Lin Yuan checked his Star Tower personal information card.","Name: Black","Gender: Male","Height: 178cm","Weight: 61kg","Star Tower Floor: 23rd Floor","Spirit Qi Occupation: Healing-type Professional","Occupation Rank: C-Rank","Contracted Spirit-Lifeform:","Morbius (Bronze X/Legend)","Thousand Questions Beast (Bronze I/Legend)","Twilight Starbird (Silver I/Fantasy I)","Red Thorn (Bronze V/Epic)","Acid Corrosion Queen Bee (Gold I/Legend)","Duel Record: Duels: 23, Wins: 23, Losses: 0, Highest Floor: 23","While reading his personal and contracted feys’ information, Lin Yuan couldn’t help giving a satisfied nod. It was a great sense of achievement as this increase in strength was a result of his hard work over the past four months. He was no longer the same as before.","Lin Yuan’s personal information card would only display the necessary information—name, duel record, and spirit qi occupation—on the Star Web during battles.","If Lin Yuan chose to reveal any of his contracted feys, his first choice would be his Bronze/Epic Red Thorn, whose quality was the lowest among the others.","As for Lin Yuan’s other feys, their quality was at least Legend, and there were even Silver/Fantasy feys. He was afraid it would be so dazzling that it would blind his opponent and cause a huge commotion in the Radiance Federation.","The Silver I/Fantasy I Jasmine Lily, Bronze X/Legend Spirit-Gather Goldfish, and Bronze X/Legend Blue Flash Purple Butterfly were all under Morbius’ exclusive skill, Spirit Lock. Thus, even if Lin Yuan’s personal information would show Morbius as part of the data, those spirit-locked feys wouldn’t be displayed.","After checking his information, Lin Yuan took a deep breath and let the Star Tower match an opponent for him.","Soon enough, Lin Yuan got matched with an opponent on the 24th floor and checked his opponent’s personal information card.","Name: Wang Shuai","Spirit Qi Occupation: Defense-type Professional","Duel Record: Duels: 1557, Wins: 790, Losses: 767, Highest Floor: 31","Lin Yuan silently raised his brows. I got matched with a Liver Emperor1! He has actually fought 1557 duels!","However, when Lin Yuan was matched with the opponent named Wang Shuai, they were both stunned. They looked at each other and noticed they were both wearing similar silver masks. However, Lin Yuan’s silver mask had a few distinct patterns, while Wang Shuai’s silver mask was glistening with pure silver color.","The defense-type spirit qi professional, Wang Shuai, suddenly asked after snapping out of shock. “Are you also Lord Black’s fan?”","Lin Yuan finally understood why he felt something was familiar. This black attire with the silver mask seemed to be his attire back at the battle outside of Millstone Town.","Lin Yuan didn’t expect that his status as ‘Black’ had become this famous. After being absent from the Star Tower for four months, his first duel was actually against a fan of ‘Black’.","When Wang Shuai asked that question, Lin Yuan couldn’t help pondering. Since I am Black, I should probably be considered Black’s fan too, right?","Therefore, Lin Yuan nodded.","Unexpectedly, the moment Lin Yuan nodded, Wang Shuai suddenly roared, “How could Lord Black have such an unprofessional fan like you!? You might be wearing a silver mask, but you aren’t even wearing black clothes!”","Lin Yuan couldn’t help but scratch his head. He was wearing spirit qi clothes that had a mix of dark blue and light blue. Due to his clothes’ color, his identity as Black’s fan was actually being doubted, and he wasn’t qualified to be a fan.","This was a rather strange feeling for Lin Yuan. Before Lin Yuan could speak, Wang Shuai suddenly exclaimed, “What?! Your name is actually Black!? And you are also a healing-type spirit qi professional!”","Wang Shuai turned serious and looked at Lin Yuan, approvingly.","“Your attention to detail on the attire might be inappropriate, but you are rather professional in other factors! I admit that you are a professional fan of Black. Later on, I will not be as harsh against you.”","After saying his piece, Wang Shuai circulated his spiritual power to summon his two contracted feys. He summoned two Bronze feys, their quality Elite and Normal, respectively.","The Bronze/Elite Coiled Horn Goat and the Bronze/Normal Thick Wool Sheep were fundamental defense-type feys.","Seeing Wang Shuai summon his feys, Lin Yuan also summoned Chimey.","As soon as Lin Yuan summoned Chimey, he heard Wang Shuai exclaiming, “WHAT THEEEE!”"]},{"number":184,"title":"Chapter 184: Protect Your Liver Well","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","As a protector who had defended Millstone Town against the pinnacle Class 1 dimensional rift, Black could be said to have fought against the insect tide alone when the people there were in times of peril. This in itself was a miracle.","This event was even more shocking than the time when Liu Jie, Radiance Hundred’s Sequence #39, had resisted the incoming dimensional lifeforms outside Cold Frost City to buy precious time for the city.","Liu Jie was a well-known star among the Radiance Federation, and because of this, whatever he did could only be said to be the icing on the cake.","It was like a flower bed that had flowers of all colors. Even if one added many peonies into it so that the garden could become bright and colorful, it was still a flower bed.","However, Black, an ordinary person, had stepped forward in times of peril. He was more like a hero rising from the ordinary people.","Back then, he had used the Silver Fantasy Breed healing-type fey’s ability that could allow severed limbs to grow back, an astonishing feat.","Even though Lin Yuan had left quietly at that time and had not accepted any commendations or the Star Web’s interview, this had tinted Black’s identity with mysteriousness.","Although he had accepted no interviews from Ascending Dragon City’s or Star Web’s reporters, Millstone Town’s spirit qi professionals, who had fought together with him, did not know how he really looked like or his identity, but they knew a lot about other things.","There were detailed descriptions in Black’s fan club and forum about Chimey, Blackie, and Red Thorn, the feys he had used.","Some people in Millstone Town that were at drawing had even drawn the feys that Black had summoned. All the feys’ names that Lin Yuan had called, like Chimey and Blackie, had circulated among the Star Web.","However, the more popular ones were still his Fantasy Breed Jasmine Lily and Red Thorn, which had spread out the sea of flowers to fight against the sea of insects.","When Lin Yuan had summoned Chimey, Wang Shuai was not aware of it. There were many people on Star Web, so it was not unusual to chance upon duplicate names. Likewise, the same could be applied for spirit qi professionals. Even though healing-type spirit qi professionals were rare, there would always be one among the hundreds of combat-class spirit qi professionals.","They were all Black’s fans and dressed similarly, but there was nothing wrong with it, even if they did it deliberately.","The most fanatical fans would not form a contract with a fey similar to their idol just for the sake of chasing their idols in this world where strength was respected. Even if brainless fans really did so, it would also have to depend on whether their fey compatibility was the same as their idol’s.","During the battle outside Millstone Town that day, Lin Yuan had summoned Chimey to scout the dimensional rift. So many of those who had fought knew how it looked and its name.","As Black’s fan, Wang Shuai was considered a bit more fanatical. Otherwise, when climbing the Star Tower, he would not have dressed similarly to what Black had worn when he was fighting in Millstone Town.","Even this azure blue bird that Lin Yuan had summoned was similar to Black’s rumored fey.","It was said that Black’s flying fey was a blue bird that was no bigger than a fist and had cloud patterns on its wings.","When Wang Shuai saw Lin Yuan’s summoned azure blue bird, he realized that this fey seemed to be more exquisite and better-looking than in the rumors. Although the cloud patterns on its wings still seemed to be flickering with stars, which did not match the rumors, its wings’ color, size, and cloud patterns were similar.","There were many common points, and he had seen Lin Yuan’s battle record. Although he had fought 23 duels, he had a 100% winning rate.","Wang Shuai’s eyes instantly went wild, excited like a little kid. “Tell me quickly! Is your blue bird called Chimey?”","Lin Yuan found it strange that Wang Shuai called Chimey’s name.","Before Lin Yuan could speak. Chimey chirped twice and fluttered to carefully observe Wang Shuai.","Could he be Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess’ fan!?","Although Lin Yuan was not quite sure how Wang Shuai knew Chimey’s name, this fan before him had recognized him, so he nodded helplessly.","Chimey had become a Fantasy Breed and evolved from a Streamcloud Azure Bird into a Twilight Starbird. Even though there were many subtle changes in its looks, it had not changed much overall. When it used its Radiant Body, nobody could recognize it.","Upon seeing Lin Yuan nod, Wang Shuai jumped in joy. Wang Shuai’s sudden jump frightened his Bronze/Elite Coiled Horn Goat and Bronze/Normal Thick Wool Sheep, which were ready to battle at the side. They could not help but lose their battle spirit and bleat at their contractor.","Wang Shuai ignored his shocked contracted feys and exclaimed, “I can’t believe I’m actually seeing the living Lord Black!”","Lin Yuan was puzzled. “Have you ever seen a dead Lord Black?”","Wang Shuai suddenly said, “Lord Black, people like you should be sold on Star Web!”","Lin Yuan, who was unable to keep up with Wang Shuai’s thinking, asked, “Why?”","Could this fan have gone crazy to the point of delusion?","Was this the so-called ‘destroying whatever you can’t obtain’?","Wang Shuai chuckled and replied in a silly manner, “Because Lord Black is a treasure!”","Lin Yuan only had one thought. How should he deal with his crazy fan’s corny words? He was very anxious and waiting online.","He did not give an answer to Wang Shuai, as he did not know what to say.","As a result, Wang Shuai worshipped him even more because, in Wang Shuai’s heart, a god should be aloof!","Meanwhile, the tower climbing duel was still ongoing. The Star Tower’s rules did not allow any of the two sides to admit defeat voluntarily. Only in the event that one party died, suffered serious injuries, or could not fight would it be enough for the Star Tower to assess it as losing the ability to fight.","The primary purpose of this rule was to cultivate the duelists’ courage and boldness in the battle. Death in the Star Tower did not affect the real world. Hence, it was possible to be unrestrained and hone one’s combat skills.","Under normal circumstances, Lin Yuan should have asked Chimey to use Sound Thrust to kill his opponent and advance to the next level. However, he could not bear to attack his fanatic fan and kill him in one blow. Thus, he let it use Scattered Light to attack the other two feys.","Under Chimey’s control, Scattered Light could burn and cause serious injuries to the two feys, and the Star Tower would deem him as the winner.","However, Lin Yuan did not expect that after Chimey used Scattered Light, a figure with a silver mask would pounce at the Scattered Light.","Just as the Scattered Light ignited Wang Shuai’s black clothes, he took off his mask and said solemnly, “Lord Black, my name is Wang Shuai! You are the hero of my heart, and I want to take the same path as you in the future!”","Then, he started shouting, “I’m too lucky to die at Lord Black’s hands on the Star Web Tower and be blown into fireworks!”","Before Wang Shuai finished shouting, Chimey’s Scattered Light instantly swallowed him. He vanished with the Scattered Light, burning him without any ashes left.","After Wang Shuai was incinerated, Lin Yuan also became the victor. Actually, Lin Yuan was quite touched by what Wang Shuai had said after taking off his mask.","Lin Yuan had always had a firm heart and walked on the path he wanted. However, he did not expect that this path could even indirectly influence others.","Water was shaped by things, and people were shaped by their hearts.","In his opinion, people should always have a heart filled with love. Otherwise, they would not differ from a zombie.","Also, radiance was giving out the light from a heart filled with love, while the faint radiant light ignited other hearts that were filled with love. The countless points of radiant light emitted from each heart full of love would fuse together to form a belief. The power contained in these beliefs was enough to light up the dome and bring down the radiant light of miracles.","At that moment, Lin Yuan’s duel record had become:","Duels: 24, Wins: 24, Losses: 0, Highest Floor: 24.","After the battle, Lin Yuan could not help but criticize, How is this being blown into fireworks? Isn’t this being incinerated without even ashes left?","He has gone through 1,557 rounds at such a young age. Oh, that’s not right. It’ll be 1,558 after losing this round.","How exactly did Wang Shuai do in those duels?","Is he an internet-addicted teenager?","Young people nowadays need to protect their livers!"]},{"number":185,"title":"Chapter 185: Shooting Up to the First Place Out of Nowhere","paragraphs":["Lin Yuan matched all the way on Star Web without stopping until his total duels were 50.","In almost every duel before the 50th floor, Chimey would only let out a clear chirp and use Sound Thrust to end the battle easily. After these dozens of battles, Lin Yuan found that most Bronze feys he was matched with were Normal and Elite. He still had yet to see a Bronze/Flawless fey in the first 50 floors.","In the first 50 floors, he had only encountered eight Silver feys, five of which were Normal, and three were Elite.","Lin Yuan felt that his concept of the feys’ quality of the Radiance Federation’s spirit qi professionals had changed somewhat compared to before.","Since he could easily evolve Bronze and Silver feys’ quality, it was an effortless thing for him. In fact, most of the Class 2 Creation Masters in the Radiance Federation could enhance Bronze feys into Elite, but it was hard to enhance them into Flawless.","Enhancing a Bronze fey from Flawless to Epic would require at least a Class 4 Creation Master. For ordinary Creation Masters, the higher the feys’ grade, the easier it would be to enhance them.","They would use all sorts of spiritual ingredients to concoct a spirit fluid with medicinal properties to stimulate the fey’s potential. The higher the fey’s grade, the stronger its body’s potential, and the easier it would be stimulated.","However, the way Lin Yuan enhanced feys was to channel a tremendous amount of pure spirit qi into the fey’s body to optimize the genetic model and enhance the low-grade fey’s foundation. Thus, for the other Creation Masters, the higher a fey’s grade, the easier it would be to enhance it. On the contrary, it was easier for Lin Yuan to enhance feys of lower grades.","As such, Lin Yuan’s thinking gradually changed. While he was climbing the Star Tower, his thoughts had returned to the Radiance Federation’s normal standard.","Because he had been matched with those combat-class spirit qi professionals, Bronze and Silver feys of Normal or Elite were the norm for the spirit qi professionals.","This made Lin Yuan could not help but feel a little ashamed. Even though he had lived two lives, he had made a mistake that people would often make.","He was always subjective. If he had a wider scope, he would inevitably look at things differently.","Lin Yuan could not help but nod in satisfaction at this record of a 100% winning rate for 50 duels. Then he logged off the Star Web. However, he did not know that many disputes had emerged after he had climbed the Star Tower and had rounds of duels.","First of all, Black’s fan club and forums were in an uproar. After Wang Shuai had met Lin Yuan in the Star Tower, he had downloaded the video of their battle and posted it in the forum and fan club.","There were many people in Black’s fan club and forum. Except for the people who had fought alongside Lin Yuan in Millstone Town, those who came to become fans felt that Black seemed less real while they worshiped his deeds and his Silver Fantasy Breed fey that could grow back limbs, as Black had never revealed his face. This inevitably made these admiring fans feel they had no backbone.","However, things were different now as Black had truly appeared on Star Web and climbed the Star Tower.","Wang Shuai had originally joined Black’s official fan club, and the owner of it was none other than the healing-type spirit qi professional with the Bronze Spitting Turtledove, Liu Lang.","Due to Liu Lang’s name on Star Web being Ancestor Peace, many people called him ‘Ancestor Peace Berserker’. In the forum and fan club, whenever he found any outrageous keyboard warriors, he would give them a taste of their medicine and eliminate all of them.","After Wang Shuai posted the video, Liu Lang immediately recognized that he had fought against Black. This was because Lin Yuan’s aura when he had been fighting in Millstone Town had been deeply engraved in Liu Lang’s mind.","Wang Shuai’s video gave him small fame in the fan club, so Liu Lang promoted Wang Shuai into the official fan club administrator.","Soon, the news of Black climbing the Star Tower spread via postings and the fan club. But at the same time, there was a sudden change in the Star Tower’s streak list. A name that had never appeared on the streak list before appeared at the top. It was none other than Black.","With a winning streak of 50 duels, he was ahead of the second place, who only had a winning streak of over 11.","The streak list was just a small list that got little attention among the Star Tower’s many lists.","However, someone had shot up to the first place, and his name was very special. He was the Radiance Federation’s young hero who had a Silver Fantasy Breed fey.","At first, many people thought that it was the same name, but after Liu Lang’s verification in Black’s fan club and forum, Black’s identity was determined.","Of course, some were doubtful, but few of them dared to publicly question in Black’s forum and fan club for their own sake. Otherwise, if they did so and Ancestor Peace Berserker hit with a heavy fist, how would they even survive?","Soon, people quickly dug out Black’s duel record. He had an astounding 100% winning rate in 50 consecutive duels. Star Web’s matching was very fair.","Black’s identity received endless attention overnight, which Lin Yuan, who had logged off the Star Web, was unaware of.","In these few days, besides climbing the Star Tower, he would spend most of his time enhancing batches of Usneas that were not even at Normal to Silver/Elite in the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","Every time he enhanced a pot of Usnea into Silver, Lin Yuan could vaguely sense the spirit qi within his body increasing slightly. However, this subtle increase was simply not obvious enough.","Since Lin Yuan would climb the Star Tower daily whenever he had nothing to do, he had climbed to the 74th floor so far. It might be due to his luck that when he reached the 74th floor, he encountered a Gold fey. However, he could not help but smack his lips upon seeing it. This Gold fey seemed a bit strong."]},{"number":186,"title":"Chapter 186: The Bloody Flowers in the Sea of Flowers","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Lin Yuan had just been matched with an opponent on the 74th floor that summoned two tiger feys. One of them was a Gold fey based on its aura, while the other one was a Silver X fey that was about to reach Gold.","Lin Yuan did not take this Silver X/Elite Steel Tooth Tiger seriously, but the purple plasma condensed on the other Gold tiger fey’s surface, full of the aura of destruction.","He used Morbius’ True Data to check it.","[Fey Name]: Golden Forehead Lightning Tiger","[Fey Species]: Toothed Feline/Tiger","[Fey Grade]: Gold (4/10)","[Fey Type]: Lightning","[Fey Quality]: Flawless","Abilities:","[Claw Attack]: Quickly leap forward and use both claws to deal tearing damage.","[Lightning Arc Entwinement]: Can condense a lightning arc on a part of the body for defense or attack.","[Thunder Teeth Cut]: Gather thunder from thunder teeth and deal high-voltage single-target damage.","[Lightning Roar Magnetic Shock]: Condense a huge amount of lightning elements in the air through the tiger’s roar and change its magnetic field to repel a huge amount of lightning arcs in all directions, causing lighting damage and tremor damage.","Exclusive Skill:","[Overloaded Lightning Arc]: The condensed arc reaches overload mode and would explode twice when it comes in contact with bioelectricity.","This Gold tiger fey made Lin Yuan frown secretly. Its comprehended skills were not considered powerful, and the Thunder Tooth Cut was a relatively poor ability that it could comprehend at Gold. It was just a kind of single-target ability without any highlights, but this Golden Forehead Lightning Tiger’s exclusive skill was simply too outstanding.","Overload Lightning Arc gave the mediocre Thunder Tooth Cut a chance to cause secondary damage and allowed the Lightning Roar Magnetic Shock to deal double damage.","Lin Yuan summoned Chimey and Red Thorn. When Chimey was summoned and sensed the Silver X/Elite Steel Tooth Tiger and Gold IV/Flawless Golden Forehead Lightning Tiger, a stronger battle intent arose in it.","He had allowed Chimey to fight in the Star Tower battles for the past few days. Although the previous duels had been carried out with little suspense, it had also allowed Chimey to cultivate its battle aura.","It was his first time summoning Red Thorn in the Star Web duel. When Red Thorn was summoned, it thrust its thick roots straight into the ground and spread out its sharp vines to protect Lin Yuan. The thornless vine that Red Thorn had purposely evolved wrapped around his wrist obediently and affectionately.","After Lin Yuan summoned his feys, his opponent mumbled to the air, “Brothers, I’ve met another guy with a silver mask in my matchup. It’ll be exactly the tenth one with a silver mask that I kill in the past two months.”","Lin Yuan raised his brows. This fellow was quite wild!","Lin Yuan already knew what his opponent was doing. He should be a live-streamer.","Lin Yuan had encountered a nerd who was talking to himself in the air after the 60th floor. At first, he had thought it was a mental patient. But then, he had found out that this nerd kept talking about the situation and was not fighting, yet he had assessed that Lin Yuan had summoned Chimey.","He had created various theories, just like an outstanding teacher, and an eloquent King that commented on national affairs.","When they had fought, Chimey had used the Gold Sunlight Rays, Scattered Light, as well as the Sound Thrust to kill them.","Liu Jie had explained this while they were eating. Only then did Lin Yuan learn that the person he had always considered as a mental patient was actually a Star Web live-streamer. This man before Lin Yuan’s eyes was the same as the nerd after the 60th floor. He seemed to be a live-streamer as well.","His opponent was currently leaning on the Gold IV/Flawless Golden Forehead Lightning Tiger, making heart gestures and sending flying kisses toward the air. Lin Yuan could not help but feel a chill, as this fellow opposite him was simply too feminine.","This kind of femininity differed from a woman’s gentle beauty. Rather, it was a bit like a chicken that had fallen into the dough jar.","After listening to Liu Jie’s explanation, Lin Yuan also learned that it was hard to be a live-streamer in the Star Web duel.","One had to first have a live-streamer qualification to become one in the Star Web duel. The live-streamer test was very harsh, unlike those singing live-streamers who could just live-stream with a click.","After passing the test, one’s battle footage would be recorded in a third-person perspective and played in the live-streaming room. The viewers could comment and discuss the duel situation in the live-streaming room.","However, the battling live-streamer could not see it. They could only wait until the duel ended before they exited the Star Web duel and returned to the live-streaming room to see the comments.","At that moment, the feminine fellow leaning on the Gold Forehead Lightning Tiger suddenly stood up and gave charming gazes at the air, danced street dance, and sang rap. He imagined that the comments in his live-streaming room should be about him being handsome and protecting the best live-streamer.","As he thought about it, he smiled more brightly and street-danced more vigorously. He also rapped even faster. However, the feminine fellow did not know that his live-streaming room was already in an uproar when Lin Yuan summoned Chimey.","The moment Lin Yuan summoned Red Thorn, the live-streaming room’s comments completely blocked the singing feminine fellow.","Lin Yuan felt everything before him was simply an eyesore. In fact, while both of them summoned their feys, the battle had already begun.","Lin Yuan originally did not plan to use the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee. He wanted to hone Chimey’s combat skills through this Gold IV/Flawless Golden Forehead Lightning Tiger. He wanted to see if Chimey, a Silver I/Fantasy Breed fey, could stand a 50/50 chance against this Gold fey.","But now, Lin Yuan looked at the unmotivated fellow man opposite him and felt that it was clearly not an excellent opportunity to hone Chimey’s combat skills.","The feminine man suddenly stopped singing and dancing but was still rapping. “Yo! Yo! Check it out! I’ve finally fallen from the 90th floor to the 74th floor! It’s tough! Now, I’ll let you guys see how I beat this noob at the speed of light!”","Lin Yuan could no longer listen to it and said, “Red Thorn, lay out the sea of flowers.”","Red Thorn’s spore cavity shook. It actually did not spew out many spores, but a thin layer of spores still spread out at the venue. Then, it produced child ramets from the spores, changing the battle environment. The vines in the sea of flowers were sharp, and the rose-like flowers on the corrosive cavity were unusually bright.","The Golden Forehead Lightning Tiger and Steel Tooth Tiger found this sudden sea of flowers very novel. They stepped on the child ramets willfully, clearly playing.","When Lin Yuan looked at the feminine fellow who was still speaking indecent words to the air and the two tiger feys that had no intention of fighting, he could not help but shake his head. As a combat-class spirit qi professional, he should face a duel seriously, even if he was not giving it his all.","However, this feminine man had been corrupted by some other things. Since the other side had no intention to fight, Lin Yuan also wanted to quickly end this duel so that he could match with another opponent to hone Chimey’s combat skills.","Lin Yuan said softly, “Acid Corrosion Queen Bee, end the battle.”","At that moment, the feminine man was still saying to the air, “The other side is also thoughtful and actually using his most skilled move. Is he trying to extol my beauty in this trashy sea of flowers?”","The comments in the feminine man’s live-streaming room were not as crazy as when Lin Yuan had summoned Red Thorn. Although there were still many comments, there were fewer than before. At the very least, they could now see the scene of the feminine man dueling.","At that moment, all the viewers’ eyes shrunk, as something had pierced through the two tiger feys’ heads, creating beautiful bloody flowers with the tigers’ roars as they bloomed in the sea of flowers.","This bizarre and beautiful scene gave the viewers in the feminine man’s live-streaming room goosebumps, and they could not help but blurt out, “Black, so awesome!”"]},{"number":187,"title":"Chapter 187: Aggrieved Fang Duoduo","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","If the feminine man looked at the comments in his live-streaming room, he would realize that the moment the two bloody flowers had bloomed, the comments had vanished for a few seconds and instantly flooded the screen and turned it white. These comments were no longer indistinguishable.","When the feminine man saw them, he would notice that even though it was clearly his live-streaming room, none of the comments mentioned himself.","The two bewitching bloody flowers only bloomed for a moment. As soon as the warmth in the blood dissipated, it withered among the rose-like flowers and the vines with sharp thorns, leaving nothing.","Despite only existing for a brief moment, the two bloody flowers had the most shocking visual impact on the feminine man and the viewers in his live-streaming room.","The blooming flowers had vanished, and the two bloody flowers withered instantly, proclaiming Lin Yuan’s victory on the 74th floor of the Star Tower.","Lin Yuan continued to match with an opponent after his victory. When he reached the 80th floor, the strongest he had ever encountered was still the feminine man who had been stroking his hair coquettishly with no intentions of fighting.","After that, the only strong one he encountered was a combat-class spirit qi professional with a Gold III/Elite Coldwater Snapping Turtle.","However, the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly’s Silence Scale Powder restrained it a lot in the duel. When the Silence Scale Powder landed on the Coldwater Snapping Turtle, it had isolated its ability to use the water element, which was akin to nullifying its attacking means.","The Coldwater Snapping Turtle’s evolution path was more inclined toward spiritual mutation, and it made use of the water element to cause damage.","If an ordinary Bronze X/Legend Blue Flash Butterfly released the Silence Scale Powder, it would certainly not cause such a strong Silence effect on the Coldwater Snapping Turtle under normal circumstances.","However, Lin Yuan had used the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly’s scale powder with strong adhesion, making the Coldwater Snapping Turtle very passive.","It was the only fey that the combat-class spirit qi professional had. Evidently, he had invested all the resources in this Gold III/Elite Coldwater Snapping Turtle. Otherwise, if he had another fey, he could also let it release some abilities to help the Coldwater Snapping Turtle get rid of the Silence Scale Powder. Things would not have been as passive as it was now.","The Coldwater Snapping Turtle had a layer of mucus on its shell surface that made the Silence Scale Powder firmly attached to its body. Although the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly’s grade was not as high as the Coldwater Snapping Turtle, the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly simply restrained the Coldwater Snapping Turtle based on its abilities and exclusive skills.","Lin Yuan did not use the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee or Red Thorn for this duel. He only used Chimey and the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly to end the duel.","Chimey’s Scattered Light landed on the Coldwater Snapping Turtle, making its wet body surface dry and cracked with its burning ability, causing it to form a layer of blisters from the burn. When the blisters burst, the liquid flowing out adsorbed the Silence Scale Powder, leaving the Coldwater Snapping Turtle no resistance.","At that moment, the Sunlight Rays gave multiple negative effects to the Coldwater Snapping Turtle in its weakened state.","Lin Yuan found that the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly’s Scale Powder Halo could be used with Chimey’s Sunlight Rays. The reflective scale powder could reflect the Sunlight Rays. The light would produce a strong blinding effect at a certain level, causing temporary blindness after piercing the Coldwater Snapping Turtle’s eyes.","With Chimey’s soft chirp, three Sound Thrusts penetrated the Coldwater Snapping Turtle that was struggling and roaring due to the severe pain. The Sound Thrusts impacted the Coldwater Snapping Turtle’s upper jaw.","Since the Sound Thrusts hit the same point on the upper jaw one after another, no matter how hard the Coldwater Snapping Turtle’s jaw was, a small hole was blown. The tremor that occurred when the high-frequency Sound Thrust penetrated the jawbone damaged its brain tissues.","In this duel, Lin Yuan realized that Chimey had overwhelming destructive power after becoming a Silver Fantasy Breed. He still remembered that when Chimey was at Normal, its Sound Thrust could only leave faint marks on the wooden boards. But now, it could cause fatal damage to a Gold fey, provided that it attacked the target’s weak spot and when the opponent was defenseless.","As a Gold turtle fey, the Coldwater Snapping Turtle had an outstanding defense, which was based on the premise of being able to control the water element. The majestic water element would form a layer of fast-flowing water on the Coldwater Snapping Turtle’s surface.","This fast-flowing water layer was the Gold III/Elite Coldwater Snapping Turtle’s most powerful means of defense. But right now, Lin Yuan’s Blue Flash Purple Butterfly had gained the upper hand with its Silence Scale Powder.","Under the premise that the spirit qi professional did not have a second fey to help the Coldwater Snapping Turtle, it became a lamb to be slaughtered.","After Lin Yuan won the 80th battle in the Star Tower, he felt a little tired and left Star Web. He went to enhance pots of Usnea to slowly increase the spiritual power in his body.","Lin Yuan did not know what had happened in the feminine man’s live-streaming room, nor that ‘Black’ was trending on the Star Tower’s streak list.","Today, he had broken the record on the streak list and reached 80 consecutive wins, which had caused an uproar in Star Web. Many mainstream media on Star Web also started to send out notices to report this matter.","...","A competent man was sitting with a frown and flipping through a stack of information in a conference room that was decorated very simply but with extraordinary arrangements. At that moment, there was a knock on the door, and he put down the stack in his hand before saying, “Come in.”","A bowl-cut youth opened the door and revealed his head. He looked inside, walked in, and pulled a chair to sit down before he said, “Boss, is our main team still short of a healing-type spirit qi professional?”","Upon hearing that, the competent man could not help but playfully answer, “You usually are the idlest, yet you still have a recommended candidate? The S Tournament is going to start soon. Hurry and catch up on your training. I’ll help you make an appointment with the Creation Master to enhance your fourth fey’s quality.”","When the bowl-cut youth heard that, he immediately shouted joyfully, “Long live, Boss!”","After being elated, he coughed a little suspiciously and said, “Boss, our Dragon Gate Guild Club is an A-level guild club. We don’t have to go through the elimination rounds. We can just do the group matches. It’s still three months of preparation time.”","He then realized that he had said the wrong thing, so he secretly glanced at the competent man sitting down. He noticed that the competent man took out a pen and crossed out things on the information stack.","The bowl-cut youth went forward and said, “Boss, I’ve really found a particularly strong healing-type spirit qi professional!”","The man sitting looked up and asked, “What kind of person? Bring his information over.”","The bowl-cut youth scratched his head. “I didn’t prepare his information, but I think the Star Web should have his information.”","The competent man sitting down knew that this bowl-cut youth would not have prepared the information. As soon as he heard this person was from Star Web, he took out his Star Web Card, ready to enter Star Web, and asked, “How far has he gone on the Celestial Stairway?”","The bowl-cut youth blinked and replied, “He hasn’t reached the Celestial Stairway yet. He’s on the 80th floor.”","Upon hearing that, the competent man put down the Star Web Card in his hand and chased him away angrily. “Fang Duoduo, hurry up and get out to train! You also know that our Dragon Gate Guild Club is an A-level guild club. By finding someone who has reached the 80th floor of the Star Tower, are you trying to fight 4 vs. 6 during the group match and let us become a B-level guild club?”","Fang Duoduo was a little aggrieved. “That healing-type spirit qi professional who reached the 80th floor is very popular on Star Web. He has won 80 consecutive—”","Before Fang Duoduo could finish, the competent man chased him out. “Hurry up and go train!”","Fang Duoduo was thrown out, and he felt aggrieved as he muttered, “I was just trying to help. Long Tao, since you find me troublesome, then go find one yourself!” He then hummed a song and walked toward the training room."]},{"number":188,"title":"Chapter 188: White Jade Snow Orchid","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Lin Yuan was enhancing a plant fey he had found in the wild. It seemed like a weed with no characteristics. It had three long, slender leaves with thick leaf blades.","Although this weed seemed like nothing special, it seemed to exude a different kind of formidable aura.","As Lin Yuan was injecting spirit qi into it, the ordinary weed was constantly changing. After a few hours, its leaves became longer and drooped downward, with a unique texture.","When a bunch of plain white flowers that grew straight out of the leaves bloomed, it immediately emanated a beautiful and refreshing fragrance, causing the room to instantly turn cooler.","This lush fragrance was not sweet and delicate at all, but an elegant fragrance. When one touched this orchid, it was as though one’s heart calmed down.","The reserved fragrance no longer spread out, but it was exceptionally deep, as though it contained the season and climate.","Lin Yuan stopped channeling his spiritual power, and when he looked at the Bronze/Epic White Jade Snow Orchid before him, he could not help but nod in satisfaction.","The fey that he had picked up and looked like a weed was actually an orchid.","At first, Lin Yuan felt that orchids were considered relatively rare feys, so he had picked it. However, he did not expect that he would nurture this orchid into a White Jade Snow Orchid.","The orchids in the world generally looked the same before they bloomed. Only when they bloomed could their value be specifically distinguished.","Plums, orchids, bamboos, and chrysanthemums had always been the four most elegant plants. Although this White Jade Snow Orchid was not the most top-notch orchid, it was a fine fey that others could not ask for.","Just as Lin Yuan stretched his body and was about to take a closer look at the Bronze/Epic White Jade Snow Orchid, there were two soft knocks on the door, and he heard Wen Yu’s voice coming from outside. “Young Master, lunch is ready. It’s time to eat.”","Lin Yuan walked out of his room with the pot of White Jade Snow Orchid in his hands. When Wen Yu saw him come out, she was stunned.","It was said that a gentleman was like an orchid, but when Lin Yuan came out holding the orchid, Wen Yu suddenly had a feeling that an orchid was not as good as a gentleman. Perhaps it was because this young man’s aura was too outstanding that he suppressed the orchid’s aura.","When she examined the pot of orchid in Lin Yuan’s hand, she was astonished. She was also a Creation Master, so she had recognized at a glance that the orchid in his hands was an Epic White Jade Snow Orchid.","Of course, this was not what shocked her the most because she had seen many orchid feys and Epic feys. However, this Bronze/Epic fey was extremely rare, especially since it was an orchid fey.","Just like in the Radiant Moon Palace, the reward for the top spirit attendant every year was only a Bronze/Epic fey.","Wen Yu thought little of the Bronze/Epic White Jade Snow Orchid, as she had never expected Lin Yuan to nurture it. Instead, she thought that the Moon Empress might have gifted it to him.","Just as she was thinking this way, Lin Yuan said, “Come back to your senses!”","Wen Yu returned to her senses and found Lin Yuan looking at her, so she hurriedly replied, “Young Master, Big Brother Liu made lunch today. I’ll help you take this White Jade Snow Orchid.”","Upon hearing that, Lin Yuan handed it over to her and said, “Big Brother Liu’s cooking talent is definitely excellent.”","Lin Yuan had been skeptical when Liu Jie had previously said that he could cook. Based on Liu Jie’s honest face, Lin Yuan really did not think that he looked like someone who could cook.","After Liu Jie had made a meal, he had conquered Lin Yuan’s and Wen Yu’s stomachs and made them become foodies, causing them to wait for him to cook every day. It was not because the two of them could not cook. Rather, it was because Liu Jie’s cooking was simply too delicious.","Even though Lin Yuan had eaten the Spirit Food Pavilion’s chef’s dishes, they were not as good as the ones Liu Jie made.","Wen Yu carefully took the White Jade Snow Orchid from Lin Yuan and asked, “Young Master, where do I put this White Jade Snow Orchid?”","Lin Yuan answered, “Didn’t Big Brother Liu say last time that the spiritual ingredients are not fresh the next day, even after putting them in the refrigerator? Put this White Jade Snow Orchid next to those spiritual ingredients in the kitchen. It will solve his problems.”","Wen Yu was listening carefully, but when Lin Yuan told her to put it in the kitchen to keep the ingredients fresh, she opened her mouth wide. Her cherry-like mouth opened as wide as a hippopotamus’s mouth, so wide that even a pineapple could fit inside.","Fortunately, her hands were stable. Otherwise, this Bronze/Epic White Jade Snow Orchid would have dropped on the ground.","Although the White Jade Snow Orchid was not considered the best among the orchid feys, it could be called a top-notch one.","The White Jade Snow Orchid was a support-type fey. When it was placed indoors, it could lower the temperature to a soothing but not too cold state due to its properties. Its fragrance could also promote plant growth.","It was pretty useful to Creation Masters. If a Creation Master contracted a White Jade Snow Orchid, it could play a supporting role when nurturing plant-type feys.","Thus, placing such a good thing in the kitchen and using its aroma and cooling effect to keep the spiritual ingredients fresh was unheard of. It was simply a low-key luxury.","When Lin Yuan saw Wen Yu with her mouth wide open, he could not help but say, “If you’re hungry, I’ll see if I can help Big Brother Liu with anything so that we can serve quickly.” Then he walked to the kitchen.","Wen Yu could not help but criticize, Young Master is really a guy who fails to understand women.","Before Lin Yuan walked to the kitchen, Liu Jie came out with the dishes. There were four dishes for the three of them—Kung Pao chicken, sweet and sour pork, squirrel fish1, and cumin meat slices. These four were all meat dishes, as Liu Jie had figured out what Lin Yuan and Wen Yu loved to eat. They all had similar tastes and were pure carnivores.","After Liu Jie placed the dishes on the table, Wen Yu slowly came out of the kitchen and said, “Young Master, Big Brother Liu, the kitchen is going to become the most fragrant place in this manor.”","Liu Jie did not understand what she meant and thought that she was praising him.","However, Lin Yuan could not help but raise his brows. Although the White Jade Snow Orchid had a clear and aromatic fragrance, he still preferred the agarwood smell.","The White Jade Snow Orchid was not as calming as the agarwood. The White Jade Snow Orchid’s fragrance would stay on the clothes and leave traces, but the agarwood’s fragrance would refresh the mind, calm the mind, and only stay on the sleeves.","After the meal, Wen Yu and Lin Yuan praised Liu Jie, making him giggle on his firm and honest face.","Liu Jie could not help but think, When I was in the team with Bai Hao and Wang Fan, why didn’t they praise me when they ate my cooking? Such ingrates!"]},{"number":189,"title":"Chapter 189: An Undesirable Man","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Liu Jie’s contracted source-type Insect Queen had long since been healed. It was no longer in imminent danger, and it had even evolved into a Fantasy Breed.","Not long ago, Liu Jie had gone to find Bai Hao and Wang Fan with a very simple goal. He wanted to apologize.","Liu Jie had been discouraged and become an ordinary person, so he naturally had not wanted to contact his former friends again. He had thought that he would just be giving them more trouble.","At that time, he had become a useless person, and his only fey, the Insect Queen, had been his only reliance. When the Insect Queen’s roots had been damaged, Liu Jie had been ready to cut off all ties and become an ordinary person.","Although he was doing well now, he recalled that Bai Hao and Wang Fan had always been searching and missing him for two years. He felt touched yet apologetic.","When he had met Bai Hao the other time, although Bai Hao’s words had made him angry, he did not take it to heart. This was because Liu Jie knew Bai Hao very well. He was a softie at heart.","Because of mutual understanding, the three of them had become the Radiance Hundred Sequence’s members and would form a three-member team when they went out to do their missions. Men’s friendship was actually just like that, sincere and simple.","After the meal and drinking a few cups of wine, Bai Hao and Wang Fan had gotten closure. They had been concerned about Liu Jie’s past experience and missed him dearly.","For Liu Jie, his strength had returned, and he had become even more powerful. He was back on good terms with his old friends and also had the faith of this young man in front of him.","One would really feel good during a happy occasion!","Liu Jie had never felt how good life was, even when he was still at the top, but after he had fallen into the dust, his perception of life had changed. He felt happy at every bit of the present and interacting with the people close to him.","However, he was caught between laughter and tears when Wang Fan sent a message to the group. Only then did Liu Jie learn that Bai Hao and Wang Fan had pooled their money. They wanted to see if they could treat his Insect Queen’s injuries. After knowing that it had been healed, Bai Hao gave Wang Fan’s share back to him but rewarded all of his money to a live-streamer on Star Web called the Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess.","He had given tens of millions of Radiance dollars, causing Bai Hao, who had been the second top contributing fan for two months, to shoot up to the first place. Not only had he reclaimed his position, but he was also worlds apart from second place.","However, Bai Hao was stifled as no matter how hard he had sent gifts like a bootlicker, the Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess had never thanked him. At that moment, he posted something in the group.","Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess’s Little Fanboy: “Liu Jie, Wang Fan, come out and go on a mission with me to earn money!”","Wang Fan: “When did you start to want to do the missions so much? You used to refuse even when I asked you.”","Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess’s Little Fanboy: “I don’t have enough money to give gifts to the Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess! I plan to reward 99.9% of the money I earn from doing missions to the Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess! I’ll just eat two steamed buns every day.”","Liu Jie: “???”","Wang Fan: “???”","Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess’s Little Fanboy: “Are you two coming or not? If not, I’ll go alone!”","Liu Jie: “Not going!”","Wang Fan: “Not going!”","Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess’s Little Fanboy: “You singles don’t understand the happiness of chasing stars.”","Liu Jie could not help but reveal a pretty boy’s puzzled expression on his honest face.","Bai Hao made it seem as though he was not single. Based on his attitude, he wanted to date online and meet them in real life!","After putting down his cell phone, Liu Jie suddenly recalled something and said to Lin Yuan, “Lin Yuan, several king-class experts will jointly hold a private auction in the Royal Capital. Are you interested?”","Lin Yuan pondered for a moment and replied, “Have they revealed beforehand what things they’re going to auction?”","For Lin Yuan, going to your general auction was just purely to watch the fun. It was not that he could not afford them, but most of the things were useless to him.","He would need some spiritual ingredients to enhance feys from Epic to Legend. But in other cases, he did not need the spiritual ingredients to assist him in enhancing feys. As for high-grade feys, he could just evolve them into anything he wanted with time.","Upon hearing Lin Yuan’s words, Liu Jie answered, “I heard that source-type lifeforms will appear at this auction.”","Lin Yuan could not help but ask, “Source-type lifeforms?”","He did not expect someone would auction their source-type lifeforms. If it was a source-type lifeform, Lin Yuan could not help but have some interest.","Source-type lifeforms were strange in their contract and did not necessarily need spiritual energy. Each of them had unique abilities that would be excellent if used properly.","Therefore, if he could encounter a suitable source-type lifeform, Lin Yuan did not mind buying and nurturing it.","For example, the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee. It had greatly enhanced Lin Yuan’s combat ability, and it could be said to be his strongest means of attack at present.","Without the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee, given his current standard, he was not confident in saying that he could certainly win the promotion duels and ascend to the Celestial Stairway.","Even though Chimey’s Radiant Body could surpass the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s strength in a split second with a burst of power, it was only for that moment.","If it met a Gold defense-type fey and was restrained by it, when Chimey depleted all its energy, Lin Yuan would likely be the one losing the duel.","Thus, he was hell-bent on finding a way to buy a suitable source-type lifeform. Moreover, he did not lack resources for nurturing feys or source-type lifeforms.","Unlike other spirit qi professionals, he did not need to worry about resources and focus his resources toward only one of the feys.","“That king-class expert squad is very famous in the Guild Alliance. I heard that they had destroyed several dimensional rifts. There should at least be one source-type item in this auction, but I don’t think there’ll be over two.”","Upon hearing that, Lin Yuan replied, “What are the admission requirements for this private auction?”","When Liu Jie noticed Lin Yuan had the intention to go, he answered, “Leave the admission requirements to me. I’ll get three tickets at that time.”","Lin Yuan nodded and said, “I’ll have to trouble you then, Big Brother Liu.”","Wen Yu was also thrilled, as she usually had little chance to go down the mountains back then at the Radiant Moon Palace. Thus, she naturally wanted to go to such a lively place.","Even though she had been calling Lin Yuan as ‘Young Master’ and was clearly a subordinate, Liu Jie had never ignored her. As a result, she had slowly started to acknowledge him.","After the meal, Wen Yu took up the duty of cleaning the dishes.","Liu Jie was just about to freeze the prepared spiritual ingredients that were hard to store when he saw a pot of elegant orchid on the shelf where the various spiritual ingredients were placed.","As a Radiance Hundred Sequence member, he naturally knew what it was. He suddenly exclaimed in surprise after observing it, “F*ck! This is actually a Bronze/Epic White Jade Snow Orchid! Why put such a good thing in the kitchen?”","While Wen Yu washed the dishes, she calmly answered, “Young Master gave it to you to help keep the spiritual ingredients fresh.”","Indeed, Wen Yu also saw Liu Jie open his mouth wide with a dazed expression. She imitated what Lin Yuan had said earlier. “Big Brother Liu, are you hungry?”","Liu Jie came back to his senses, and when he heard Wen Yu’s words, he scratched the back of his head and asked, “Didn’t I just finish eating? I ate three bowls of rice, so how could I be hungry?”","Upon hearing that, Wen Yu could not help but criticize, Come on! Not another guy who fails to understand women!","Liu Jie asked, “Wen Yu, did you not eat enough just now?”","Wen Yu lowered her head and replied, “I’m definitely full from two bowls of rice!”","Then, Liu Jie looked at her and said in surprise, “Aren’t you afraid of getting fat from eating two bowls of rice!?”","Wen Yu suddenly felt that Liu Jie was not only someone who failed to understand women but also an undesirable man."]},{"number":190,"title":"Chapter 190: Black’s Terrifying Talent","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","During the past few days, Lin Yuan had been climbing the Star Tower. He had already fought from the 80th floor to the 100th floor, and if he went any further, he would take part in the promotion duel.","When climbing from the 80th floor to the 100th floor, all of Lin Yuan’s opponents possessed Gold feys. After the 90th floor, Lin Yuan had encountered plenty of spirit qi professionals that possessed two Gold feys. However, the grade of the Gold feys wasn’t considered high.","Nonetheless, when Lin Yuan used the Gold/Legend Acid Corrosion Queen Bee, these duels weren’t that difficult to win. In fact, even though Chimey had become a Fantasy Breed and obtained the new exclusive skill Radiant Body, Lin Yuan hadn’t used it until now.","During the climb from the 80th floor to the 100th floor, the strongest Gold fey Lin Yuan had encountered was only a Gold VII/Flawless fey. The Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s grade might be Gold I, but its quality was Legend.","The Gold I/Legend Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s actual strength was actually superior to Gold VII/Flawless feys. Furthermore, the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee was an assassin that hid in the sea of flowers, allowing it to land sneak attacks.","Lin Yuan had also encountered a spirit qi professional that had been live-streaming when fighting in the Star Tower. The live streamer had been none other than the spirit qi professional that possessed the Gold VII/Flawless fey. Therefore, it was also the first time Lin Yuan’s Acid Corrosion Queen Bee appeared in the Star Web netizens’ eyes.","This had also solved the mystery as to how Lin Yuan had instantly killed that feminine man’s two feys. The case of the two blood flowers that had blossomed in the sea of flowers had finally been cracked.","On the Star Web, Lin Yuan’s popularity was simply through the roof. At the same time, some questions were brought up in the Star Web.","Isn’t Black a healing-type spirit qi professional?","Why haven’t we seen Black using a healing-type fey?","When in combat, he actually became a combat-class spirit qi professional?","Had it not been for Red Thorn’s appearance that had immediately proved Black’s identity, even if Black’s fans and fan leader Liu Lang insisted, not many would believe that Lin Yuan was Black.","That was because Lin Yuan had never used any healing-type fey. He had been using combat-class feys to climb the tower, so everyone found the same problem—Lin Yuan’s talent.","A spirit qi professional’s talent was always viewed with different levels.","Most of the spirit qi professionals would be compatible with one species and one type of fey, like defense-type/beetle-species feys. Of course, there was also a difference in strength. For example, if a spirit qi professional was compatible with power offense-type/tiger-species feys, while the other was compatible with power offense-type/goat-species feys. The strength difference would be easier to differentiate.","Tiger-species feys did have stronger combat strength than goat-species feys when at the same grade. The law of nature determined such superiority. In the natural world, tigers would definitely eat goats.","Of course, such superiority would only exist when the grade was equivalent. However, not all tiger-species feys were able to defeat goat-species feys of the same grade. There were also some rare feys among the goat-species feys,","The Wind Speed Rapid Antelope that Lin Yuan had nurtured was such an example. It was able to fly with the use of wind elements, making it extremely fast. Therefore, regular tiger-species feys might not be able to defeat the Wind Speed Rapid Antelope.","However, ordinary folks with a poor family background who were compatible with power offense-type/tiger-species feys might wish that they were compatible with power offense-type/goat-species feys. Tiger-species feys weren’t as common, and if one wasn’t from a prestigious family, they wouldn’t be able to afford a tiger-species fey. In addition, when evolving tiger-species feys, more precious spiritual ingredients were required.","For people like Chu Ci, who was compatible with all defense-type feys, her talent was considered top-notch in the entire Radiance Federation. As a defense-type spirit qi professional, Chu Ci wouldn’t be restricted by her talent when choosing defense-type feys and could choose them freely according to her desired combination. This way, it would allow her contracted feys to form a flawless combat style that was suitable for her.","When combat-class spirit qi professionals dueled, the fey’s individual strength was one factor. When fighting against a lower-ranked opponent, one could use the difference in grade to suppress the opponent and win. But when fighting against an evenly matched opponent, the combination and coordination of the feys would be the crucial factor.","Black had far too many combinations when using feys in combat, and there wasn’t a regular rhythm. Thus, the people on Star Web had started guessing Black’s talent.","No matter how they discussed it, they couldn’t find a definite answer. They were plenty of low-ranked Scholars and Fey Observers that conducted an analysis of feys Black had used in duels. They then published their own articles based on their opinions.","Unexpectedly, when they published their articles, Star Web’s netizens flamed those Scholars and Fey Observers. Based on Black’s summoned feys, apart from defense-type feys, he had already used almost every other type of feys.","In fact, people were speculating about Lin Yuan like this largely because of Chimey. Back when Lin Yuan had contracted Chimey, it had been a Sound Bird that couldn’t even be considered a fey and naturally didn’t have any types.","Chimey was like the Usneas, which were also a kind of production-type fey without any combat-class types. But when Lin Yuan had evolved Chimey, its combat-class capability had awakened.","The matter about Black’s talent was in constant debate, and ultimately, a Class 4 Scholar published an article based on Black’s talent.","A Class 4 Scholar was already considered the pinnacle of the Radiance Federation’s knowledge world. Thus, when this Class 4 Scholar published this article about Lin Yuan’s talent, this guessing game came to an end.","The Class 4 Scholar’s article might have calmed down the commotion, but it made everyone feel more terrified of Black’s talent, or it should be his wealth.","That Class 4 Scholar gave a final verdict by using the appearance of different feys during the Star Tower’s duels. The quality of Black’s feys should be extremely high, and source-type lifeforms were also in his arsenal. The Class 4 Scholar also stated that Black would still be the Radiance Federation’s top prodigy, even if the source-type lifeforms were out of the picture.","Finally, the Class 4 Scholar teased a little in his conclusion, guessing that Black’s feys were all source-type lifeforms.","Of course, everyone treated that part as a joke. Putting aside the rarity of source-type lifeforms, the harsh requirements to form the contract would already cause plenty of people to get stuck.","However, the fact that Black possessed source-type lifeforms was basically the Class 4 Scholar’s inarguable verdict.","Now that Lin Yuan was at the Star Tower’s 100th floor, he would need to fight in the promotion duel if he continued fighting the duels. He was already rather tired now, so he wasn’t in a hurry to fight in the promotion duel. Instead, he opened up his personal information card.","Name: Black","Gender: Male","Height: 178cm","Weight: 61kg","Star Tower Floor: 100th Floor","Spirit Qi Occupation: Healing-Type Professional","Occupation Rank: C-Rank","Contracted Feys:","Morbius (Bronze X/Legend)","Thousand Questions Beast (Bronze I/Legend)","Twilight Starbird (Silver I/Fantasy I)","Red Thorn (Bronze V/Epic)","Acid Corrosion Queen Bee (Gold I/Legend)","Duel Record: Duels: 100, Wins: 100, Losses: 0, Highest Floor: 100","When looking at the 100% win rate and recalling how he had climbed up the 100 floors, one floor at a time, Lin Yuan felt deeply that he had obtained something called growth.","From the first duel until now, Lin Yuan and his contracted feys had much better teamwork than in the beginning. At the same time, he had a clearer understanding of his fey’s abilities.","Lin Yuan had transformed from a combat newbie into a combat veteran who had his own attitude and perspective. His timing and opportunity to use the abilities would become more proficient with constant duels. But even now, Lin Yuan understood that he still had more room to grow.","Lin Yuan knew that from the start of the promotion duel in the Celestial Stairway, he would encounter significantly stronger opponents than the opponents he had met previously.","When climbing the Star Tower, every 10 floors would be considered a small segment, and every 20 floors would be considered a major segment. But when climbing the Celestial Stairway, the opponents might have just declined from the top. An unlucky Celestial Stairway 5-star expert might even fall down to the promotion duel and had to restart all over again.","Therefore, Lin Yuan understood that the next few duels weren’t going to be easy. His consecutive victories might also be stopped.","Lin Yuan wasn’t really worried about his consecutive victories, as he had never imagined he would be able to win 100 duels consecutively and reach the Celestial Stairway.","Lin Yuan felt that when fighting in the Star Web, one should constantly be amending their combat style and temper their combat skill. Therefore, an evenly matched duel was much more precious than a one-sided duel.","As of now, Lin Yuan had yet to feel that he had fought a duel that was considered evenly matched. He was in need of such a duel in order to squeeze out his and his contracted partners’ potential in battle.","Only by failing would Lin Yuan be able to understand what he was lacking.","In fact, after the 100 duels, Lin Yuan had already noticed a weakness he had when commanding the feys in combat.","When fighting in the Star Tower, there were two methods to achieve victory. The first was to kill the spirit qi professional, and the second was to kill all of the opponent’s feys.","Only by achieving either one of the conditions would the duel end.","Lin Yuan had also encountered danger before, and if Red Thorn hadn’t helped him, he would have been killed by the opponent’s sneak attack and lost that duel.","Of course, even though Red Thorn had suffered grave injuries to block the attack, the impact had still smashed Lin Yuan’s left shoulder bone. Only after such an injury appeared did Lin Yuan understand the importance of survivability for a combat-class spirit qi professional.","This allowed Lin Yuan to have an accurate objective and direction as to his next contracted fey. Lin Yuan wanted to form a contract with a fey that could protect him. Unfortunately, Lin Yuan wasn’t compatible with defense-type feys.","As such, Lin Yuan could only choose to imitate Xin Ying, whose contracted fey had awakened the exclusive skill, Transformation Possession. Otherwise, he would need to contract a source-type lifeform that could protect him."]},{"number":191,"title":"Chapter 191: Refusing to Accept Any Messages From Others","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Lin Yuan pondered for a moment and gave up on feys that could learn Transformation Possession to attach onto the body just like Xin Ying’s contracted fey. Transformation Possession and Tool Transformation were both very rare, and one could only hope to encounter such exclusive skills.","If Lin Yuan was to enhance feys in huge quantities, it would be possible to produce a Bronze fey that awakened the Transformation Possession exclusive skill. However, given Lin Yuan’s current spiritual energy, he wouldn’t be able to form a contract with a Bronze fey. His remaining spiritual energy wouldn’t be enough.","Therefore, Lin Yuan knew that he could only choose a source-type lifeform with great defense if he wanted to increase his survivability.","Nevertheless, source-type lifeforms were extremely rare, and every source-type lifeform had different abilities. Hence, source-type lifeforms that could be used for protection and defense were also things that one could only hope to encounter.","Even if Lin Yuan could find one, putting aside whether he could afford it, it was unknown if Lin Yuan could fulfill the conditions to form a contract with it.","Lin Yuan had only decided on a direction, and as for how he was going to obtain a source-type lifeform to protect himself, there was a need for further planning.","After finishing the duel on the 100th floor, Lin Yuan didn’t immediately log out of the Star Web; instead, he clicked on the notification box that had constantly been flashing.","Lin Yuan had never checked on the notifications for Black because he didn’t know a lot of people with his Black identity. The only people he knew as Black were Zhang Xiaobai, Xin Ying, Lu Pinru, and Tan Ran. Furthermore, they contacted each other with their mobile phones and not through the Star Web. Therefore, Lin Yuan felt that it was fine for Black not to reply to any of the messages.","However, when Lin Yuan logged in as his Creation Master identity, he would look at the notification box from time to time. Every time Lin Yuan logged into the Star Web as a Creation Master, he would feel that all the fans of Purchase With No Loss store were true ‘warriors’. Otherwise, they wouldn’t have been able to send out close to 10,000 messages in just one or two days.",",000 messages were already a lot for Lin Yuan. Nonetheless, when he checked the notification box for Black, he was flabbergasted.","Isn’t this too many messages!?","Lin Yuan counted and realized the number of messages had reached six digits. These were a few hundred thousands of messages!","Not even five days had passed since Lin Yuan started using his Black identity to climb the tower. He took a glance at the messages and realized that the first message was from the Star Web officials.","The Star Web officials hoped that Lin Yuan could open up a Star Web live stream and receive an interview from the Star Web. At the same time, there was a reporter’s contact information at the bottom of the message, Tian Ningning.","Lin Yuan didn’t even consider and immediately closed the Star Web officials’ message. He didn’t have any plans to start a live stream, nor did he wish to give any interviews.","If he wanted to give an interview, he would have already given it back at Millstone Town when the reporters from Ascending Dragon City and Star Web had all been there. He wouldn’t have chosen to leave with Xin Ying, Zhang Xiaobai, and the others.","After closing the Star Web officials’ message, Lin Yuan continued scrolling down the list. He noticed that the next message was from Tian Ningning, the reporter the Star Web officials’ message had mentioned.","When Lin Yuan clicked on Tian Ningning, he noticed that this Star Web reporter had been sending him messages since yesterday morning. She had already sent close to 20 messages. Lin Yuan didn’t expect that this Tian Ningning would actually be so persistent.","Lin Yuan looked through a few other messages and noticed they were from a few guild clubs that wanted to recruit him. There was even a B-level guild club that hoped he could go to their guild club for an interview among the guild clubs. After the interview, they would make the necessary arrangements according to his needs.","Lin Yuan didn’t even think about it and refused. He already planned to build his own guild club, but that thought wasn’t firm yet. Otherwise, he wouldn’t have bought such a huge piece of land without hesitation.","As such, Lin Yuan would never agree to join other guild clubs. The objective of joining a guild club was to compete in the S Tournament. If Lin Yuan wanted to compete in the S Tournament, he would build his own guild club and gather his own team.","The messages in the Star Web’s notification box were sorted out by their importance level. In order to prevent messages from officials and guild clubs from getting overlooked, they were all pushed to the top.","After reading most of the important messages, Lin Yuan felt that these messages were similar in content. They were either requests for interviews or hoping Lin Yuan could go and join their guild clubs.","Lin Yuan felt bored and swept a glance at the messages that weren’t indicated as important. He couldn’t help raising his brows.","No More Sorrow: “Lord Black, can you take off your mask and send me a private photo? If you think you are ugly, then treat it as though I didn’t ask.”","Oh White: “Black, I wish to have a baby with you!”","Extra Dream Several Rain: “Husband, what do you like to eat? Just give me your address, and I will buy your favorite food every day!”","Finding Myself Back: “Black! I will not forgive you in this lifetime! My girlfriend broke up with me because I am not your fan! You better watch out!”","Write a Will: “.”","Lin Yuan felt a waterfall of sweat forming on his body. What were these messages about?","When did I get married? I don’t even have a girlfriend, and someone is calling me husband? Furthermore, what does it have to do with me when your girlfriend breaks up with you? It is not as if I am breaking up with you!?","Lin Yuan paid most attention to that full stop as he had a feeling that it had a hidden meaning.","After skimming through the messages, Lin Yuan emptied his notification box and set a restriction, refusing to accept others’ messages. He then logged out of the Star Web.","Lin Yuan didn’t know the shock and commotion his 100th win created. The Star Tower’s consecutive wins board was also refreshed.","It had taken Lin Yuan only 100 duels to climb from the 1st floor of the Star Tower to the 100th floor, giving him a 100% win rate. Others might attain such a result, but at least no one had achieved it until now.","In fact, Lin Yuan had already broken the record for consecutive wins previously, but having 99 consecutive wins and 100 consecutive wins had a totally different shocking factor.","99 consecutive wins were like a flawless painting that had one of the edges torn off, but 100 consecutive wins meant that the torn edge was mended, making it truly flawless.","Black’s reputation mainly stemmed from his heroic deed when he had fought against the pinnacle Class 1 alien insect dimensional rift at Millstone Town. Subsequently, he gathered more attention because of his exposed talent when climbing the Star Tower.","Now that he reached the 100th floor with a 100% win rate and obtained the qualification for the promotion duel, he might still not be as popular as the Radiance Hundred Sequence members, but his popularity was already comparable with those celebrity contestants from the S Tournament.","Nonetheless, Lin Yuan was unaware of such things. After logging out as Black, he logged back into the Star Web with his Creation Master identity.","He then put up the Silver Usneas for sale in his store. This time, Lin Yuan set a sale restriction for these ten pots of Silver Usneas. It was still first come, first serve, but each individual could only purchase one pot.","In just three minutes, Lin Yuan realized that all ten pots of Silver Usneas had been sold!"]},{"number":192,"title":"Chapter 192: This Thing Is a Little Too Valuable","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","As soon as the ten pots of Silver Usneas were sold, Lin Yuan noticed that Purchase With No Loss Store’s fan group had also exploded.","Lin Yuan was amazed at the speed of these fan members—they were truly fast!","The Silver Usneas might have only been on the store for three minutes before selling out, but the news of Purchase With No Loss Store selling Silver Usneas still created a commotion. When this piece of news was spread out, the store’s reputation instantly burst upward.","The price that Lin Yuan had set for the Silver Usneas wasn’t low. As compared to the Silver Usneas’ auction price in the Rare Lifeform Pavilion, the selling price for Lin Yuan’s Silver Usneas was similar.","However, Silver Usneas were simply too rare, and hardly anyone would choose to sell Silver Usneas through an auction on the Star Web’s Rare Lifeform Pavilion. If the Silver Usneas branches were cut and nurtured with a special method, they would quickly grow into Elite Usneas.","The price of Elite Usneas was already rather high, so a Silver Usnea could actually be said to be a hen that could lay eggs.","Lin Yuan didn’t bother about the explosive commotion after he put up the Silver Usneas for sale in the store. In any case, he wasn’t planning to put up new species of rare feys in the future. But the grades of the Usneas and Spirit-Siphon Goldfish would only continue getting higher.","...","Inside a high-class office building situated within the Radiance Federation’s Royal Capital, a short-haired yet abnormally cute woman was sitting in a sulky mood. She was holding onto a pen and clicking on it repeatedly.","At that moment, the colleague of the cute woman walked over and asked, “Ningning, has Black not replied to you yet?”","The cute woman nodded and said, “There is still no news yet. But I can see that Black’s consecutive wins are still increasing on the Star Tower.”","The colleague patted on Tian Ningning’s shoulder and said, “Ningning, there is plenty of news on the Star Web for you to report on. You don’t have to go on a wild goose chase. If Black isn’t willing, isn’t it the same to find someone else for the interview?”","Tian Ningning shook her head and pouted before replying stubbornly, “Big Sister Feng, I still wish to interview Black. I feel that Black has potential!”","Tian Ningning felt rather conflicted right now. She was one of Star Web’s special columnists, whose numbers didn’t exceed 300 in the entire Star Web. One could even say that every special columnist possessed a huge flow of resources on the Star Web.","As for Tian Ningning, she had just passed the test officially at the start of this year, becoming the Star Web’s special columnist. During this year, Tian Ningning had written plenty of exceptional articles, but she had never found a person that she truly wanted to interview.","In fact, Tian Ningning had plenty of good opportunities this year too. Not long ago, one of the ex-Sequence members of the Radiance Hundred that had been eliminated had started a live stream on the Star Web. That ex-Sequence member wanted to invite a special columnist to be his exclusive reporter.","That ex-Sequence member had privately looked for Tian Ningning and wanted her to be his exclusive reporter, but she politely rejected him.","An exclusive reporter was a truly special existence. If Tian Ningning was to sign a contract with someone else to be an exclusive reporter, she would only be able to write reports about the person she had signed the contract with. Simultaneously, only she was eligible to write reports about the person who signed a contract with her.","Given this binding form of relationship, Tian Ningning had to be abnormally cautious when making a choice. Only when Black appeared did Tian Ningning have the intention to take the initiative to conduct an interview. However, Tian Ningning’s hard found passion was facing a very realistic problem—Black not replying to her messages.","At that moment, Tian Ningning suddenly heard footsteps at the entrance, and she saw her superior walking in. Just as Tian Ningning wanted to say something, she realized that her superior walked straight toward her.","“Tian Ningning, have you scheduled for a special interview with Black?”","Tian Ningning felt dejected when she heard the question and shook her head. As a result, her superior said, “Black has already achieved 100 consecutive wins on the Star Tower. With a win rate of 100% from the 1st floor to the 100th floor, he is now qualified to participate in the Celestial Stairway promotion duels. Follow up on this. If you cannot get the special interview in another three days, I will ask someone else to follow up on this.”","Tian Ningning wasn’t especially surprised to hear that Black had reached the 100th floor with a 100% win rate. After all, when Tian Ningning had been preparing the interview for Black, she had already thought of the possibility. However, when she heard the actual news, her heart still made a huge thud as she settled on something.","“Chief, if I get Black’s special interview, I wish to apply to become Black’s exclusive reporter.”","When Tian Ningning’s superior heard the statement, he was instantly stunned.","When Tian Ningning made that statement, she felt Big Sister Feng pulling her from the side. After a moment, the superior responded, “If this is what you want, then as long as you obtain Black’s approval, I can consider.”","Tian Ningning turned back to see Big Sister Feng looking at her with a disappointed expression after the superior left. “Ningning, with your capability, you can strive to become an exclusive reporter for a Radiance Hundred Sequence member. Even if Black is popular now, he has yet to climb to the Celestial Stairway. In addition, Black has never revealed his true appearance to anyone. You should know better than me that most of the fame these days is built upon heroism and mystery. Most importantly, do you know the age of the person behind that mask?”","Tian Ningning let out a sweet smile and revealed two little dimples as she said, “I know that Big Sister Feng is concerned about me. But I trust my instincts.”","Big Sister Feng couldn’t help but get enraged. “Ningning, this year, the Radiance Hundred Sequence is going to be sorted out again. Why don’t you make contact with the newly recruited Sequence members first? It will definitely be better than to become Black’s exclusive reporter.”","Tian Ningning smiled and shook her head. “Big Sister Feng, I will go to the Star Web and see if Black has replied.”","After saying that, Tian Ningning logged into the Star Web to see whether there was any news from Black. After logging in, she was disappointed to see the same outcome.","Tian Ningning didn’t lose heart and sent another message, only to realize that her message couldn’t get through. She found out that Black had activated the reject-all-messages setting.","Tian Ningning was fretting. What should I do now?","Finally, Tian Ningning ground her teeth and thought in her heart, I don’t believe that I cannot see Black even once! Black should have some ties with the Extreme Guild Club’s S Tournament Reserve Team’s four reserve members. Then I shall visit the Extreme Guild Club to see if I can get a chance to speak with Black through those four reserve members.","While thinking like that, Tian Ningning immediately logged out of the Star Web and exited the office building. She rode on a flying fey and flew toward the Extreme Guild Club’s address.","At present, Lin Yuan was enhancing feys. He was enhancing the three fish he had found in the icy pool back then. Even with Lin Yuan’s experience, the feys he enhanced still shocked him.","“These are too valuable! How can I have enhanced such a lucky thing!?” he exclaimed."]},{"number":193,"title":"Chapter 193: Dragon-Phoenix Landscape Carp","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Lin Yuan had seen these three fish at the edge of the pool in the depths of the Endless Forest and felt that they were rather familiar, so he had subconsciously used True Data to check them. If he had not done so, he would not have brought them back.","The three fish looked gray and were only half a finger long, so they were simply not conspicuous in the water. But thanks to True Data, Lin Yuan found out that they were actually the legendary Myriad Form Carps.","He was familiar with them, as there were many of them in the pond in the center of the garden outside the Radiant Moon Palace. However, those fish were not ordinary Myriad Form Carps, but a famous koi-species of the Myriad Form Carps’ evolution.","As the name implied, the Myriad Form Carp was a kind of carp that could evolve into different kinds of koi under the catalysis of various spiritual ingredients and spirit qi.","Koi was auspicious because it was always linked to good luck. Therefore, the Radiance Federation would also regard koi as the most inferior auspicious feys. Only ordinary koi feys were considered as inferior auspicious feys. However, this was not the case with the evolved koi in the pond in the center of the garden outside the Radiant Moon Palace.","The Pine Snow Fallen Cherry Koi, the Golden Mountain Blowing Koi, and the Nine-Patterned Dragon Koi were the finest among the koi. Each of them was extremely complex and different in the way spiritual ingredients and spirit qi catalyzed them. The spiritual ingredients used might even be hard to find.","Take the Pine Snow Fallen Cherry Koi as an example. Its body was red and white, and the gap between the colors was not that big. Rather, it was just like a cherry blossom rain on the white snowy ground.","The cherry blossom rain on the fish carried a gradation of aesthetics, as though some cherry blossoms had been buried deep in the white snow, some had fallen on the snow surface, while some were still dancing in the cold snow, unwilling to fall.","In addition, the Pine Snow Fallen Cherry Koi’s red-and-white body had a light pattern of pine needles, which was very beautiful. In the water, it was also like, ‘the pine needles blending with the cold snow, and the fallen cherry blossoms and snow are suddenly warm.’ It was as though a sudden warm cherry blossom rain had bloomed in the water’s extreme coldness.","The koi in the pond in the center of the Radiant Moon Palace’s garden was not a question of whether one could get them for a price in the Radiance Federation. Many people from affluent families who loved koi feys might not even have the chance to see it once in their lives.","Even though Lin Yuan was used to seeing those koi in the pond, he was still amazed at the three koi he had evolved in the Spirit Lock spatial zone. He had never expected the three Myriad Form Carps would actually evolve into truly auspicious feys after he enhanced them.","When he used True Data to check them, he found out that they had evolved into Dragon-Phoenix Landscape Carps. Each of them was nearly one meter long, which, of course, referred to their bodies. Their elegant fishtails were even longer than their bodies, and their fins were about half a meter long. A fin cartilage supported the fin and did not look messy at all, only endlessly outstanding.","Lin Yuan placed the Dragon-Phoenix Landscape Carps in the spirit pool. Based on their swimming posture, they did not seem like they were swimming but soaring unrestrainedly. They spread their fins like a phoenix and swung their tails like a dragon. They had a very beautiful posture.","Of course, this was not the best thing about them. Their fins and tails that resembled a phoenix and a dragon accounted for the ‘Dragon-Phoenix’ in their name. The ‘landscape’ word in their name came from details on their snow-white bodies.","The details were like a few drops of pine soot in ink, and the ink would enter a clear pool, creating a ‘vast landscape painting.’","The rivers and mountains were blended into one scene, the mountains and river drew an outline, the pavilions and kiosks were in myriad forms, and the myriad forms gathered in the magnificent landscape of the rivers and mountains.","The plants were decorated with various colors in the landscape, and the Dragon-Phoenix Landscape Carp was a depiction of the beautiful rivers and mountains.","The mountains and rivers did not remain motionless on the carp’s body. As it swam, the details on its body would constantly change.","Despite the slow change, if one looked at it closely, one would notice the picturesque landscape’s endless evolution. The worldly landscape and various scenery were all on the Dragon Phoenix Landscape Carp.","But if this was the case, even if the landscape’s beautiful evolution was converged on it, its auspicious dragon-phoenix posture could still not allow it to be called a superior auspicious fey.","In fact, the Dragon-Phoenix Landscape Carp’s exclusive skill was the key as to why Lin Yuan had defined it as a superior auspicious fey.","[Place of Life]: Plants do not wither, water does not freeze, and everything that grows under Place of Life would be in the most comfortable environment and away from disease.","Since ancient times, people had been debating about what were auspicious signs and had different definitions on them. Plums, orchids, bamboo, and chrysanthemums were elegant and not considered auspicious.","The osmanthus’ fragrance contained a touch of nobility, and it could be used as an antidote. Therefore, after the Spirit Qi Awakening, it was reasonable for the osmanthus to be treated as an inferior auspicious thing.","But with the evolution of living things containing spirit qi, many rare and exotic alien beasts, such as dragon-like snakes, phoenix-like birds, cranes, and turtles, were not truly auspicious. Thus, people were now having more and more debates about auspiciousness, with increasingly harsh judgment on it.","Because of this, auspicious creatures were also becoming more and more precious. However, one part of the definition of true auspiciousness that had not changed since ancient times was that those being born as auspicious could protect other living things.","This Dragon-Phoenix Landscape Carp’s exclusive skill could protect the living things and set the meaning of landscape beauty.","Since Lin Yuan had only enhanced the three fish swimming freely in the pond to Bronze X/Epic, the Place of Life could not show much power. If the Dragon-Phoenix Landscape Carps were raised in Lin Yuan’s manor, they could ensure that the grass, trees, river, and pond within three kilometers outside the manor would be under their exclusive skill.","The air in Redbud City was dryer and not humid, unlike the air in Redbud City, so it was not suitable for bamboo feys’ growth, which was a type of fey that loved the humidity.","If Wen Yu had not buried 250,000 kilograms of high-grade energy ores in the 3,000-meter bamboo forest behind the manor, the bamboo leaves would have long dropped due to the dry air.","Due to Place of Life, the manor would remain lush and verdant even in midwinter, and the man-made lake would not freeze and would still be surging.","At that moment, a Dragon-Phoenix Landscape Carp suddenly jumped out of the water. Its sudden posture was like the flood dragon coming out of the water and the phoenix breaking through the clouds.","As Lin Yuan looked at it suddenly leaping out of the water, he felt that the moment it did that, a part of its details changed suddenly.","The corner of the outlined mountains and rivers turned into a rustling river. When he looked at the change, he suddenly felt amazed."]},{"number":194,"title":"Chapter 194: Lin Yuan’s Anguish","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Lin Yuan suddenly felt as if a magnificent landscape of mountains and rivers had appeared before his eyes. The mountains and rivers were flowing and changing, and the mountains, rivers, canyon, and ocean were changing with the world’s transformations.","He looked at the ink-dyed rivers and mountains on the Dragon Phoenix Landscape Carp that had leaped out of the water, as though 10,000 years had passed in one glance. But when he returned to his senses and looked at the time, he found that only a few seconds had passed.","At that moment, Lin Yuan felt a Willpower Rune that seemed to have a layer of ink-color, flowing and changing in the pure whiteness, emerge in his spiritual energy. It was the Myriad Form Willpower Rune.","He could not help but touch the back of his head. How had he comprehended a Willpower Rune by just looking at the Dragon Phoenix Landscape Carp that had leaped out of the water?","He had heard people say that it was very difficult to comprehend a Willpower Rune, but he really did not feel that way now.","Lin Yuan had comprehended a Willpower Rune from watching the green hills that had been burned by the blazing fire but still grew out new plants. This Willpower Rune had fused with the Jasmine Lily and allowed it to become a Fantasy Breed.","The second Willpower Rune had formed as the wolves’ pack was hunting and massacring the alien insects under the dark night. This Willpower Rune also long belonged to Red Thorn.","He had comprehended this third Yin-Yang Willpower Rune on the way to the Royal Capital with Ling Xiao. He had just been sitting on the Blue Jade Pegasus and observing the alternation between day and night. Lin Yuan had not given this Yin-Yang Willpower Rune to any of his feys.","He had comprehended the fourth Twilight Willpower Rune from watching the dawn outside Millstone Town and had fused it with Chimey, allowing it to become a Fantasy Breed Twilight Starbird.","At present, this Myriad Form Willpower Rune was his fifth one. The acquisition of this Willpower Rune made him fall into contemplation.","Among his feys, the Spirit-Gather Goldfish, Blue Flash Purple Butterfly, and Genius still did not have suitable Willpower Runes yet.","This Willpower Rune had an all-embracing sense and seemed to have some versatility. It seemed that Genius, the Spirit-Gather Goldfish, and the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly were suitable with it. However, if he had to choose among them, it was very obvious that Genius was more suitable.","The manifestation of nature itself meant encompassing everything, just like Genius’ intelligence.","After Lin Yuan carefully comprehended this Myriad Form Willpower Rune, he found that it was perfectly compatible with Genius because this Willpower Rune caused more of a change in appearance rather than knowledge.","If other people comprehended a Willpower Rune that had something in common with their fey, they would be happy to use it immediately. But for his contracted fey, especially Genius, which was the first fey to accompany him, he did not want to be negligent on the Willpower Rune’s choice.","In Lin Yuan’s opinion, he should pair it with the most suitable Willpower Rune to evolve it into a Fantasy Breed.","If other spirit qi professionals knew about his thoughts, they would probably kneel on the floor and call him ‘Boss’.","Comprehending a Willpower Rune could not be controlled, and it was always a kind of natural gift. The kind of Willpower Rune one would comprehend was always an unknown.","Hence, after most spirit qi professionals comprehended a Willpower Rune, they would look for a Bronze fey with high quality that was compatible with their comprehended Willpower Rune and nurture it. However, such feys were very rare.","Therefore, if spirit qi professionals could come across a high-quality Bronze fey that was somewhat compatible with their Willpower Rune, most of them would consider it to be a stroke of luck. Not anyone could be like Lin Yuan, who wanted to match his fey with a perfect Willpower Rune.","Lin Yuan was now somewhat helpless, as he did not know when Red Thorn would evolve into Legend, so he still could not use the Willpower Rune he had comprehended from the massacre.","Although the Yin-Yang Willpower Rune and this Myriad Form Willpower Rune were two completely different kinds, they were essentially related to change. But so far, Lin Yuan simply did not have such change-related feys or source-type lifeforms to go with these two Willpower Runes.","He could not help but mumble, Having too many Willpower Runes is really sweet anguish.","If it was said before that, the other combat-class spirit qi professionals would kneel and call him ‘Boss’. Then, after they heard his words, they would probably want to fight him.","As Lin Yuan looked at the three Bronze/Epic Dragon-Phoenix Landscape Carps in the spirit pool, he had his own plans. They were superior auspicious feys without any combat abilities. He did not intend to contract them, nor would he sell them away. Instead, he planned to raise them in his own manor.","With the Place of Life, he would no longer need to take care of the flowers and plants. He made up his mind. When he became a spirit qi professional of a higher class, he would evolve the three Dragon-Phoenix Landscape Carps from Bronze/Epic to Bronze/Legend.","Regarding such superior auspicious feys that could protect a party of living things, Lin Yuan planned to evolve them into Fantasy Breeds.","Of course, with Lin Yuan around, they did not need to rely on themselves to raise their quality or grade, as he could solve that.","Therefore, the hurdle that the three Dragon Phoenix Landscape Carps needed to overcome would depend on whether they could comprehend the Willpower Rune at Diamond X/Legend and reach Suzerain. Of course, it was still too far to say this right now.","Lin Yuan stroked his chin, looked at the three Dragon Phoenix Landscape Carps, and pondered for a while before leaving the Spirit Lock spatial zone. He did not intend to keep the carps in the manor’s pond but raise them in the manor.","The change of the details on their back was just like looking at three great ages constantly changing. As the saying went, ‘Myriad colors are not as good as ink.’ Only when the Dragon Phoenix Landscape Carps that swam like a dragon and phoenix were raised in the manor could he regularly observe them and enjoy their elegance.","The manor had a total of three floors, and the kitchen, dining hall, and living room were interconnected. Therefore, it was good to set up a fish tank that could be used as a wall decoration to separate the kitchen and dining hall from the living hall.","Lin Yuan roughly measured the wall’s length and realized it was not much different from the fish tank he imagined. He planned to set up a 9.9-meter-long and two-meter-wide fish tank as a wall decoration.","Its length was 0.1 meters away from a whole number. When life was too complete, it would not last, so with less of a perfection, it was more in line with being auspicious.","The two-meter-wide fish tank could also completely let the three Dragon Phoenix Landscape Carps swim and be used to raise them. As for the water in the tank, he could just connect it to the man-made lake outside.","Since the Dragon Phoenix Landscape Carps could purify water, if he connected the fish tank and the man-made lake, the man-made lake’s water quality could also be improved most perfectly. But such an enormous fish tank was not readily available and needed to be custom made.","At present, Lin Yuan’s manor was filled with an ancient feeling.","In the past few days, Wen Yu had purchased many compatible appliances with the manor, and together with the jade-like furniture, the house looked rather appealing.","Although Lin Yuan did not have OCD, he did not want to use something out of place to destroy the mansion’s overall beauty, so he did not intend to custom-make a huge metal fish tank. Instead, he decided on the fish tank material."]},{"number":195,"title":"Chapter 195: How Pretentious","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","There were many jade-like wooden materials and red sandalwood in the Spirit Lock spatial zone. Lin Yuan had gotten the completely jade-like sandalwood when he had cleaned up the backyard in the Xia Region’s fey store and disassembled the old shelves.","When he had taken over the store, there had been six shelves in the store. He then later supported the store alone, and due to health reasons, only one shelf was left.","After disassembling the five shelves, he had gotten a huge batch of red sandalwood and placed them in the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","At present, the red sandalwood had turned into a jade-like red-purple color, with a faint red sandalwood grain on it. The grains made it seem as though a faint purple cloud was vaguely rising, looking like a propitious omen.","As Lin Yuan looked at this jade-like red sandalwood material and the rising purple cloud, he felt it was a wonderful message. These red sandalwood materials were worthy of the three superior and auspicious Dragon Phoenix Landscape Carps.","At that moment, Wen Yu was instructing some gardeners, who were taking care of the mansion greenery, to plant some Normal plant feys in the various parts of the mansion.","With the 250,000 kilograms of high-grade energy ores and the protection from the Place of Life, perhaps after some time, these Normal plants would have the opportunity to become Elite.","Liu Jie went out to buy spiritual ingredients at that moment. Ever since Lin Yuan had put that pot of White Jade Snow Orchid in the kitchen, he particularly liked to buy a bunch of spiritual ingredients and put them on the kitchen shelves.","Anyway, with the White Jade Snow Orchid around, these spiritual ingredients would not deteriorate. Even if some plant spiritual ingredients had their roots broken, they would still become fresher the longer they were kept.","Lin Yuan called a Speed-Hoofed Donkey Car and headed toward a very famous Spirit Craftsman store in the Royal Capital. He preferred to travel in the Royal Capital with a Speed-Hoofed Donkey Car than a flying fey.","The Speed-Hoofed Donkey Car could let him experience the bustle and noise in the Royal Capital, feel the earthly food fragrance, and let him calm down.","The driver chatted with Lin Yuan about his family’s daily life along the way and was very enthusiastic. The car was traveling on the road when a young girl about the same age as Chu Ci ran on the side of the road and reached out to stop it with a particularly anxious look.","The middle-aged driver turned around and looked at Lin Yuan, which was him asking Lin Yuan. If there were passengers on the Speed-Hoofed Donkey Car and the driver wanted to take another passenger on the way, they had to obtain the passengers’ consent.","Lin Yuan naturally would not mind it, so he waved his hand and said, “Uncle, I have no opinions.”","The driver was actually very willing to take another passenger, as this was akin to earning more money. He stopped at the side of the street, and the young girl got in the car and hurriedly thanked them, “Thank you, Uncle, Young Brother.”","She was very cheerful, and after she got in the car, she no longer looked anxious. It was difficult to get a car here, and one had to wait for some time, even if they booked one on the Star Web. The young girl was now relieved.","Lin Yuan noticed that she was carrying a frog-shaped school bag and thought that she was a student.","After the young girl thanked them, she immediately looked at Lin Yuan and asked pleadingly, “Young Brother, can you let the driver take me to the Royal Capital Spirit Qi Intermediate Academy for lessons first? Last night, my mother got drunk and forgot to wake me up this morning.”","Lin Yuan did not expect this young girl to be a student of the Royal Capital Spirit Qi Intermediate Academy.","It was an academy affiliated with the Spirit Qi Advanced Academy. Most of the students who graduated from the Spirit Qi Intermediate Academy could go straight to the Spirit Qi Advanced Academy.","“No problem. The place I’m going to happens to pass by the academy.”","Then, he said to the middle-aged driver in front, “Sir, she looks quite anxious. Send her directly to the Royal Capital’s Spirit Qi Intermediate Academy’s teaching building before dropping me at my place.”","The academy allowed Speed-Hoofed Donkey Cars that had been certified in the Royal Capital.","Because the academy was huge, students who went to school by the Speed-Hoofed Donkey Car were allowed to drop at the teaching building entrance.","Upon hearing Lin Yuan’s words, the middle-aged driver smiled and replied, “Young Brother, you’re so nice.”","Lin Yuan could not help but feel a little dumbfounded. He should not be considered being nice, as he was on his way. People would always meet with difficulties outside, so they needed to understand each other. Why did this driver deem him as a nice person?","Lin Yuan looked at the young girl sitting next to him, who was holding a frog school bag, and thought, This young girl is pretty quiet. Such girls tend to calm down when they learn some theoretical knowledge.","At that moment, a cell phone rang in her little frog bag. The young girl took out her cell phone and looked at it before roaring, “Fatty Wang, you bastard! We’ll just break up! Why did you have to use my account to scold our teacher-in-charge?”","When Lin Yuan heard this, he quickly erased his earlier thoughts. How did she have a quiet character?","Then, the young girl said, “My mother drank too much. When she saw me looking at the information of a Spiritual Ingredient Analyst, she beat me up, with the reason that I was too pretentious. Let me tell you, Fatty Wang! I’m in a very bad mood now. When I reach school, I’ll find your teacher-in-charge and tell him that I was the one who helped do all your homework before.”","Lin Yuan almost snorted out loud. The reason of her being pretentious was acceptable!","She already had a partner, and they were torturing each other. Young people nowadays were really not simple.","At the teaching building entrance, the young girl bade farewell to Lin Yuan and the driver before she rushed in with her frog school bag.","Lin Yuan could not help but be dumbfounded. Her speed could probably reach an Elite Black Back Mountain Boar’s.","Soon, the Speed-Hoofed Donkey Car sent him to his destination, which was a very famous Spirit Craftsman store in the Royal Capital.","There were many kinds of Spirit Craftsmen. A Class 4 Spirit Craftsmen team had built Lin Yuan’s mansion based on the blueprint.","There were more of such Spirit Craftsmen who did construction, while those manufacturing small pieces of furniture and ornaments were relatively rare because rough carving was simpler.","Besides carving an ornament into an exquisite shape, one also had to pay attention to depicting the demeanor, texture, and style.","The Class 4 Spirit Craftsman in this store specialized in manufacturing furniture and ornaments. However, the reviews of this Spirit Craftsman store on Star Web were very extreme.","One-tenth of the people expressed that the store’s items were great, while the remaining people said that the store owner was a lunatic.","When Lin Yuan was about to enter the store, he noticed two people coming out. They looked rather annoyed and muttered, “He’s really crazy!”","Lin Yuan now knew how those ratings that the store owner was a lunatic had come about. When he walked into the store, he realized that the store was simply jaw-dropping. He was not amazed at how exquisite the store had been built, but because the store was built exactly like a KTV studio."]},{"number":196,"title":"Chapter 196: Crane Shadowed Censer","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Lin Yuan couldn’t help lamenting as to what kind of taste the owner had to design the store in this manner. He was looking at the hanging lamp that was shining with seven different colors in broad daylight. When he exchanged looks with the burly man that was seated on his recliner, the burly man let out a sinister smile and said, “Gather at the village entrance! Bring along your own cement1!”","The burly man didn’t even take a look at Lin Yuan, who had just walked in and used his most accustomed greeting. “Today’s rule is to prepare your own spiritual material. If the spiritual material reaches my standard, each carving I make will be 100 Radiance dollars. If the spiritual material is bigger than this piece I have on my hand, I will carve it for you for free. But the shavings shall be left behind as my compensation.”","After speaking, the burly middle-aged man lifted his hand and placed an abnormally exquisite censer on the table. Lin Yuan actually doubted this burly man’s sense of beauty at first, but he was immediately attracted after seeing the censer. The craftsmanship on this censer was truly too detailed.","The censer looked as though it was carved with 1,000 Red-Crowned Cranes that were ready to take flight. When illuminated by the lamplight, it looked as if crane images were flying out of the censer. If some agarwood incense and swirling with white smoke, along with the crane images, were added to the censer, it would truly be graceful.","Lin Yuan didn’t waste any time and took out a piece of red sandalwood that had turned jade-like in texture. It was glowing with reddish-purple luster and looked as though it was wrapped in a bundle of purple aura.","As soon as Lin Yuan took out this jade-textured red sandalwood, the burly man who was originally reading his book jumped off from his recliner and said, “It is actually red sandalwood that has complete jade texture! This is a precious item that is very rare! Tell me, what do you wish to carve?”","Lin Yuan wasn’t in a hurry to reply. Instead, he pointed at the crane shadowed censer and asked, “Senior, how many carves did it take you to make this censer?”","The burly man immediately replied. “I used 30,000 carves.”","While speaking, he picked up the crane shadowed censer and rubbed it with his palm. It was obvious that he was fond of this crane shadowed censer.","Lin Yuan didn’t expect that just the craftsmanship of this crane shadowed censer cost 3,000,000 Radiance dollars, and the material cost wasn’t even factored in yet.",",000,000 Radiance dollars wasn’t a small sum, and it was enough to purchase a regular Platinum fey. No wonder this burly man was a Class 4 Spirit Craftsman; the price of his craftsmanship was truly extraordinary.","When the burly man noticed that Lin Yuan didn’t talk after hearing the price, he said, “If you use this jade-textured red sandalwood as the base, I can carve one for you for free. But the shavings of the jade-textured red sandalwood will be left for me.”","Lin Yuan shook his head in response, as he had other use for the shavings of this jade-textured red sandalwood. When building the fish tank with this jade-textured red sandalwood, the amount of carving required would certainly produce plenty of shavings. If all the shavings were left for this burly man, Lin Yuan felt that he would be making a loss.","In addition, Lin Yuan was planning to use the shavings of this completely jade-textured red sandalwood as a decoration at the fish tank’s bed.","Lin Yuan extended his hand to break off a piece of this jade-textured red sandalwood, which was the size of half a fist, and said, “I can give senior this piece of jade-textured red sandalwood as compensation. I wonder what the senior thinks?”","The burly man’s eyes nearly popped out when Lin Yuan broke off a piece of this completely jade-textured red sandalwood. If this piece of jade-textured red sandalwood belonged to him, he would have already beaten up Lin Yuan.","In the eyes of a Spirit Craftsman, for any kind of material, the bigger the size of the material, the better it was to create exquisite designs. As for small-sized materials, the design would be restricted. However, the burly man didn’t have any opinion in regards to Lin Yuan’s proposed compensation.","Even as a Class 4 Spirit Craftsman, the burly man might be rich, but if he wanted to get his hands on materials like this jade-textured red sandalwood, he would have to depend on his luck as such things were always rare in supply. Every usage would only decrease the overall supply.","On the market, most of the products were already carved and sculpted. It was very rare to find such a material that wasn’t carved at all. As for this small piece of jade-textured red sandalwood that was only the size of half a fist, it shouldn’t be a problem to carve out two signets.","In this burly man’s heart, he might still think that the youth’s suggested compensation was too much, but he wouldn’t refuse such an offer. However, the burly man quickly understood why he deserved such compensation as it was simply a huge project.","When Lin Yuan saw the burly man nodding, he immediately took a huge batch of jade-textured red sandalwood out of his Diamond fey storage box.","Even though the burly man was experienced, knowledgeable, and had carved all sorts of rare materials, he was still dazzled by this batch of jade-textured red sandalwood that took up a fifth of his store’s space.","If he didn’t support himself by holding onto the table, he would have fallen back into his recliner.","When so much jade-textured red sandalwood was brought out, it immediately overwhelmed the seven-colored hanging lamp and covered the entire store with a purple aura.","After a long period, the burly man finally came back to his senses but was still unable to make a single statement. Lin Yuan then informed the burly man of his request for the fish tank. Subsequently, he weighed this batch of jade-textured red sandalwood together with the burly man before signing an agreement for this project.","For precious materials like the jade-textured red sandalwood and in such huge quantities, the agreement for the project was extremely harsh. Therefore, Lin Yuan wasn’t afraid that this Class 4 Spirit Craftsman would violate the agreement and embezzle his material. If the Class 4 Spirit Craftsman did so, what awaited this Class 4 Spirit Craftsman wouldn’t just be a review of being lunatic by 90% of the customers. He would really be facing a reputation default.","At the same time, he would have to repay the debt and be punished severely.","Lin Yuan had plenty of requests for the red sandalwood fish tank and had discussed the details with the burly man.","As Lin Yuan continued to look at the crane shadowed censer, he couldn’t help but feel it was extremely exquisite and increasingly pleasant to the eyes. He then asked the burly man, “Senior, I wonder if you have any plans to sell this crane shadowed censer?”","If anyone else asked like this previously, the burly man would have chased them out of his store. This crane shadowed censer was the burly man’s adored masterpiece, as he had carved it when he became a Class 4 Spirit Craftsman. He had always cherished it like a treasure.","However, after seeing so much jade-textured red sandalwood, the burly man was tempted and finally gnashed his teeth before saying, “Give me another piece of jade-textured red sandalwood of the same size, and you can take this censer.”","Lin Yuan picked up this crane shadowed censer and observed it. He realized that the material used to carve this censer was the Dragonblood Golden Silk Bamboo that wasn’t completely jade-textured. Lin Yuan had to admit that carving Red-Crowned Cranes on the Dragonblood Golden Silk Bamboo was truly fitting for the concept.","While the cranes rested in the bamboo forest, their shadows were so relaxed.","Furthermore, the Dragonblood Golden Silk Bamboo was a wood material that was more precious than the red sandalwood. In terms of value, the Dragonblood Golden Silk Bamboo, which wasn’t completely jade-textured, wasn’t as valuable as the jade-textured red sandalwood that had the same size. However, the price difference wouldn’t be too significant.","Moreover, Lin Yuan could see that the Class 4 Spirit Craftsman was rather hesitant to sell this crane shadowed censer. Lin Yuan knew that if he continued hesitating, this burly man might just change his mind, and Lin Yuan would lose the chance of owning this crane shadowed censer.","The lesson Lin Yuan had learned when purchasing the butterfly cocoons was something that he had yet to forget, so he accepted the deal decisively.","This crane shadowed censer might not be completely jade-textured, but it was a small matter for Lin Yuan. As long as he placed it in the Spirit Lock spatial zone for some time, the Dragonblood Golden Silk Bamboo used to carve the crane shadowed censer would undergo a transformation.","After making the arrangements, Lin Yuan left his address. The burly man would deliver the fish tank to Lin Yuan after half a month.","After completing his objective, Lin Yuan returned to the mansion. He was preparing to challenge the promotion duel after reaching the Star Tower’s 100th floor."]},{"number":197,"title":"Chapter 197: Source-Type Lifeform Earth Rush Golden Lotus","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","When Lin Yuan returned to the manor, he noticed that Wen Yu was holding a sprinkling can and watering an Earth Rush Golden Lotus that was planted in front of the manor. This Earth Rush Golden Lotus wasn’t a decorative fey for the manor, but in fact, it was a source-type lifeform contracted by Wen Yu.","Wen Yu originally didn’t have the Earth Rush Golden Lotus. However, after becoming Lin Yuan’s assistant, in order to allow Wen Yu to be of better help to Lin Yuan, the Moon Empress had bestowed this precious source-type lifeform, Earth Rush Golden Lotus, to Wen Yu.","This Silver/Flawless Earth Rush Golden Lotus could be said to be an exceptional helper for Creation Masters, but it had a habit, and that was to bask in at least six hours of sun every day. The Earth Rush Golden Lotus would only develop well only with six hours of sun a day. If it didn’t have at least six hours of sun, the Earth Rush Golden Lotus would look like it was going to wither and lifeless.","As for the Bronze/Epic White Jade Snow Orchid and Lin Yuan’s Silver/Fantasy Jasmine Lily, those were plants that didn’t have an especially high requirement for sunlight.","The indoor refraction of light was already enough for the White Jade Snow Orchid and the Jasmine Lily.","Recently, Lin Yuan didn’t release all of his feys on the outside and allowed them to live in the mansion. The Silver/Fantasy Jasmine Lily, the Silver/Fantasy Chimey, and the Bronze IV/Epic Red Thorn all required to increase their grade and evolve.","Therefore, Lin Yuan had placed the Jasmine Lily and Chimey into the Spirit Lock spatial zone. The high concentration of spirit qi in the Spirit Lock spatial zone was able to constantly enhance the Jasmine Lily and Chimey. As for Red Thorn, Lin Yuan placed it inside the leaf-shaped fey storage box, allowing Red Thorn to pick its preference among the dimensional lifeforms to consume and evolve itself.","As of now, Lin Yuan truly didn’t have any method to enhance Red Thorn, so it was the slowest to advance in grade among his feys. Red Thorn’s evolution speed was even slower than Chimey’s and the Jasmine Lily’s, even though the two latter feys were Silver/Fantasy.","If Lin Yuan wanted, he could enter seclusion for a few months and would be able to upgrade Chimey and the Jasmine Lily from Silver I to Silver II.","However, Red Thorn could only rely on itself to consume massive amounts of flesh and blood in order to evolve. In fact, Red Thorn’s progression was the normal progression of a spirit qi professional’s fey. Nonetheless, Red Thorn’s progression should still be significantly faster than other feys. At the very least, Red Thorn didn’t need to fret about not having even blood and flesh from dimensional lifeforms.","At present, Red Thorn was consuming massive amounts of Class 1 dimensional lifeforms and consuming small quantities of Class 2 and Class 3 dimensional lifeforms.","The corpse of a Class 3 dimensional lifeform was already equivalent to a Gold fey corpse. Therefore, Red Thorn’s daily food expenses would be at least 500 Radiance dollars. This was because Red Thorn was only eating the cheaper Class 3 dimensional lifeforms first.","After days and months, it was unknown how much more resources Red Thorn would require. Such a supply of food and resources was something that many regular spirit qi professionals wouldn’t be able to provide.","Thus, it was easy to see how difficult it was for regular spirit qi professionals to upgrade the grade and quality of their feys.","Since Red Thorn was in the leaf-shaped fey storage box, as Red Thorn’s tenant and also no.1 bootlicker, the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee was naturally staying in the same place as Red Thorn. For the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee, any place with Red Thorn was paradise.","The Acid-Swallowing Larvae was already absorbing massive amounts of acid from Red Thorn and starting to produce and store Acid-Swallowing Larvae.","Genius, the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly, and the Spirit-Gather Goldfish, couldn’t upgrade into a Fantasy Breed because of Willpower Runes. Although he had to stall their quality and grade, they were all getting busier with their lives.","Recently, Chimey had always been around Genius and researching something. Every time he saw Genius and Chimey together, he would be able to feel Chimey’s expectation and excitement while also feeling Genius’ helplessness.","As for the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly, ever since the Jasmine Lily had upgraded into a Fantasy Breed, the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly would land on the jade-colored flower of the Jasmine Lily whenever it had nothing to do. It was truly living a carefree and peaceful life.","On the other hand, the aloof and tyrannic Spirit-Gather Goldfish, Blackie, was now constantly fetching the Butterfly Shells at the bottom of the spirit pool to feed the female Five Fortune Ranchu in order to gain its favor.","Upon seeing that his feys were getting busier, more carefree, and more loving, Lin Yuan was rather delighted as their contractor.","Wen Yu saw Lin Yuan and immediately put down her sprinkling can. She smiled and said, “Young Master, I just boiled a pot of tea. It is on the table.”","Lin Yuan nodded. The tea leaves in this mansion weren’t bought by Lin Yuan; they were delivered from the Radiant Moon Palace. These tea leaves were planted by the tea attendants in the Radiant Moon Palace to make spirit tea.","There was quite a mix of the Platinum Dark Dream Fragrant Tea’s leaves among the tea leaves. In this deep, chilly autumn, when drinking a sip of the tea that was fused with Platinum Dark Dream Fragrant Tea, it would immediately expel the chilly feeling from the body and invigorate the spirit.","After entering the house, he poured a cup of spirit tea. The teapot that was made of Dehua porcelain1 didn’t have any traces of patterns, giving it a clean and comfortable feeling. A glazing color also accompanied it.","The teacups were also made of the same Dehua porcelain material. This clean teacup was poured with amber-colored tea. When the tea emitted that elegant fragrance, it was truly soothing.","Lin Yuan took out a piece of ink-black jade-textured agarwood. He then put some shavings of the jade-textured agarwood into the Crane Shadowed Censer before lighting up the shavings.","When put together with the jade-textured furniture, the censer was emitting a gentle halo. It looked as though shadows of cranes were flying around in a lively manner. The crane shadows had a sunset color and were spiraling upward.","It was unknown if the sunset color was fusing into the smoke, or the smoke was fusing into the sunset color.","The spiraling of smoke and sunset color mixture gave off a feeling that was close to being an illusion. This illusory feeling from the crane shadows made it feel as though one was ascending to immortality.","The smell of agarwood was mixed with the fragrance from the Dark Dream Fragrant Tea. This mixture and fusion didn’t have any conflict, as though the calm and steady agarwood was placed in a dream-like place. It was totally able to let a person’s tense up mind relax.","Once the fragrance entered the nose, it would disperse the entire body of fatigue.","It just so happened that when Liu Jie came out of the kitchen, he saw this scene. After the repeated surprises, Liu Jie was already accustomed, and his eyes were already opened up significantly. However, when seeing this scene, Liu Jie couldn’t help being amazed again.","Instead of being amazed, it was better to say he was intoxicated.","As the crane shadows swirled with the sunset color, one could only describe this scene as ‘seagulls and herons flying freely without worries’.","When Lin Yuan saw Liu Jie, he conveniently poured a cup of spirit tea for Liu Jie in the Dehua porcelain teacup. Liu Jie then put down the spoon sweets1 that he had just prepared in the kitchen."]},{"number":198,"title":"Chapter 198: A Duel","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","The spoon sweets were made with dozens of different Silver ingredients mixed with the Gold Elder Maple’s maple syrup. It was a kind of extremely nutritious pre-meal dessert.","Liu Jie took the tea from Lin Yuan and said, “Lin Yuan, I’ve already received the invitation to the private auction that I mentioned previously. It will be held at seven o’clock in the evening three days later on the third floor of the Rare Lifeform Pavilion.”","Lin Yuan nodded and asked, “Has news of the source-type creatures spread?”","Liu Jie nodded solemnly and said, “The reason why the private auction is held is that two of the five members of this king-class team have comprehended a Willpower Rune in a Class 3 dimensional rift. In order to gather resources to exchange for high-grade feys that are suited to one’s Willpower Rune, I heard that a total of three source-types items will be put on auction.”","Liu Jie’s words immediately piqued Lin Yuan’s interest.","Lin Yuan had thought that there would only be one source-type item at this private auction.","It was normal to use source-type items as an attraction to promote this private auction.","However, he never expected that this private auction would auction off a total of three source-type items.","Lin Yuan thought that even if he couldn’t obtain the source-type items that could provide him protection, at the very least, he could see if any spiritual energy items were suitable for the additional Willpower Rune in his spiritual energy.","As for this king-class team, others might not be able to produce Bronze feys with high quality, but for Lin Yuan, it was just a piece of cake.","Since the king-class team had chosen to auction these three source-type items, it meant that the conditions for the contract were not compatible with the king-class team.","However, the conditions of contracting each source-type creature were completely different.","These three source-type items weren’t compatible with the king-class team, but they weren’t necessarily incompatible with others. Lin Yuan wasn’t too worried about this.","After lunch, Lin Yuan returned to his room.","Just as he was about to log in to Star Web, Lin Yuan’s phone rang.","Lin Yuan picked up the call when he saw that it was from Zhang Xiaobai.","The moment he picked up the phone, Lin Yuan heard Zhang Xiaobai say:","“Black, do you have any exclusive reporters from Star Web?”","When Lin Yuan heard Zhang Xiaobai address him in that manner, he knew that it had something to do with his identity as Black.","If he called him in private, Zhang Xiaobai would directly call him Lin Yuan.","After hearing Zhang Xiaobai’s words, Lin Yuan probably knew that it was because he had set up an automatic rejection of everybody on Star Web.","Star Web couldn’t contact him, but they knew that he was familiar with Zhang Xiaobai and the others because of the battle outside Millstone Town. Thus, they sought him out through Zhang Xiaobai and the others via the Extreme Guild Club.","“I don’t have any exclusive reporters, but I don’t accept any interviews. It’s too troublesome.”","Zhang Xiaobai strongly agreed with him and said, “I think so too. Interviews are too troublesome.”","At that moment, Lin Yuan heard Zhang Xiaobai exclaim right on the heels of Xin Ying taking the phone.","“Lin Yuan, I’m Xin Ying. You’ve already started the advancement matches for the Celestial Stairway. After you get on the Celestial Stairway, there will be recordings of your Star Web Tower battles in the Star Web Tower’s video library. An exclusive reporter isn’t just doing interviews, but is also responsible for all the news articles and combat reports related to you.”","Xin Ying said it very seriously.","This was because there were less than 300 special columnists in the Star Web Tower.","If Lin Yuan could have such a Star Web column reporter and have them become an exclusive reporter, it would undoubtedly help his future development.","Furthermore, with an exclusive reporter, it could reduce a lot of unnecessary trouble for Lin Yuan.","Xin Ying treated Lin Yuan as a friend, so she naturally had to consider many things from his perspective.","Xin Ying was a carefree person, but she was also meticulous, so she didn’t want Lin Yuan to suffer from missing opportunities.","Lin Yuan thought for a moment and said, “Sister Ying, help me reply to that Star Web reporter. I’ll contact them on Star Web in a few days.”","When Xin Ying heard that, she said, “The column reporter for Star Web is called Tian Ningning. I’ll tell her to wait a while. When the time comes, if you and Tian Ningning have any requests you find disagreeable when discussing private, just reject them. Choose your exclusive reporter. The decision of the conditions is in your hands.”","Xin Ying was previously afraid that Lin Yuan would miss the opportunity.","But now, Xin Ying was afraid that Lin Yuan would be at a disadvantage when discussing the exclusive reporter contract with Tian Ningning.","After hanging up the phone, Lin Yuan couldn’t help but give a knowing smile.","In the life-and-death battle under Millstone Town, perhaps Lin Yuan’s greatest gain was four friends who had experienced life and death with him.","During the conversation he had with Xin Ying on the phone just now, Lin Yuan could sense that Xin Ying was concerned and considerate for him.","Lin Yuan didn’t care much about the matter regarding an exclusive reporter.","However, since this Star Web column reporter named Tian Ningning had gone all the way to the Extreme Guild Club, she had already shown her sincerity.","Putting aside the matter of signing the contract, it was not a big problem to discuss it on Star Web.","After hanging up the phone, Lin Yuan logged into Star Web.","Lin Yuan was already prepared for the Celestial Stairway advancement match. This was likely the biggest challenge since he had started climbing the tower.","When Lin Yuan arrived at the advancement zone, which was over 100 levels in Star Web Tower, he directly did a match-up.","There were a total of three rounds in the advancement match in Star Web Tower. Lin Yuan only needed to win two rounds to directly ascend the Celestial Stairway.","Soon, Lin Yuan was matched to his opponent.","Lin Yuan took a look at the other party’s information and couldn’t help but feel that the Wang Shuai he had met before couldn’t be considered a Liver Emperor.","The person called Chen Hongfeng was the true Liver Emperor.","Lin Yuan was observing Chen Hongfeng’s Star Web battle results, while Chen Hongfeng was also observing Lin Yuan’s results.","Chen Hongfeng couldn’t help but curse.","“You’re Black! How did you achieve a 100% win rate? Have you never climbed Star Tower before?”","With that said, Chen Hongfeng looked up and said to the air, “Hey guys, I’ve encountered Black. Boss, I’ve encountered Black! This is awesome!”","At that moment, in the meeting room of the Dragon Gate Guild Club, Long Tao asked the bowl-cut Fang Duoduo, “Duoduo, who’s Black? Why is Little Feng so agitated?”","Fang Duoduo, who was chewing on his chewing gum, couldn’t help but roll his eyes when he heard Long Tao.","Boss, how long has it been since you went on Star Web to read the forums? Now, how many people who browse the forums on Star Web wouldn’t know about Black?","However, Fang Duoduo naturally didn’t say those words. Therefore, he chose his words carefully."]},{"number":199,"title":"Chapter 199: Smooth-Toothed Elephant Lizard and Huge-Tailed Swamp Lizard","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Fang Duoduo had a sudden inspiration, and his eyes lit up as he said, “Boss, I heard that he’s a healing-type spirit qi professional who has reached the Star Tower’s 100th floor with a 100% winning rate and obtained the qualification for the Celestial Stairway promotion duels.”","When Fang Duoduo said this, he emphasized the words ‘healing-type spirit qi professional’. It was as though he was reminding Long Tao that he had told him about this before.","However, Long Tao did not get Fang Duoduo’s meaning and said with considerable interest, “A healing-type spirit qi professional can climb the tower with a 100% winning rate? That’s interesting!”","As soon as Long Tao spoke, Fang Duoduo could not help but ridicule, How is that interesting? It’s simply too interesting!","Then, Long Tao suddenly asked, “Didn’t I let Hongfeng hone his combat skills lately? How would he know Black?”","Fang Duoduo chuckled and replied, “How would I know? But Chen Hongfeng is very hardworking.”","Despite saying so, he was already observing a moment of silence for Chen Hongfeng.","Chen Hongfeng was the Dragon Gate Guild Club S Tournament reserve team member. As the Radiance Hundred Sequence #3, Long Tao was the Dragon Gate Guild Club S Tournament Team’s captain. Long Tao thought highly of Chen Hongfeng, who was currently in the reserve team and planned to focus on his training.","However, in Fang Duoduo’s opinion, whoever Long Tao thought highly of and wanted to train was simply unlucky.","Chen Hongfeng used to be such an affable fat nerd. In four months, Long Tao had trained him into a skinny nerd.","Sure enough, Long Tao said, “He’s not serious in his training. After he logs off Star Web, tell him to train with another 100 duels.”","Fang Duoduo silently lit a white candle for Chen Hongfeng in his heart.","At that moment, Long Tao exclaimed, “How come he looks so familiar?”","Long Tao looked at Black, who was standing opposite Chen Hongfeng, and felt that this silver-masked person’s aura made him feel like he had a deep impression of him. It was as if he had seen him somewhere before.","Fang Duoduo interrupted, “You’ve trained Chen Hongfeng for almost six months. Of course, you’re familiar with him.”","Long Tao looked at Fang Duoduo as though he was looking at an idiot. Then, he ignored Fang Duoduo and looked at Chen Hongfeng’s live-streaming room.","Regardless of whether this silver-masked Black had a familiar aura, Long Tao would really like to see how a healing-type spirit qi professional had reached the Celestial Stairway promotion duels with a 100% winning streak.","When Fang Duoduo received Long Tao’s gaze, he shuddered. Why did I have to slack off and watch Chen Hongfeng’s live streaming with Long Tao?","Wouldn’t it have been good if I had gone to train with my teammates in the training room?","After Chen Hongfeng had said that to his live-streaming room, he completely ignored the fact that he was live streaming. Instead, he focused all his energy on the duel at the moment. However, his live-streaming room was in an uproar.","Breeze Supporting the Willow: “Just now, Chen Hongfeng shouted ‘Boss’. Does it prove that Sequence #3 Lord Overflowing Sea is also watching this live stream? I can actually watch a live stream with Lord Overflowing Sea! This is really too blissful!”","Dark Moon Falling Wind: “Ahhh! It’s Lord Black! I want to see how strong he is!”","Your Little Fairy Is With Me: “I can’t deal with this! I’m going to faint from excitement!”","Why Is Chemistry So Hard: “That’s nothing! I’ve already peed my pants! I didn’t even move and was ready to watch this duel first.”","Chen Hongfeng did not rush to summon his fey. He looked at Lin Yuan and said, “Black, I’m going to end your winning streak after this duel.”","Lin Yuan did not say a word and summoned Chimey and Red Thorn. The moment he did that, Chen Hongfeng also summoned his two feys.","Lin Yuan’s pupils contracted upon seeing that. These two feys were lizards. One of them had blue-and-black skin, with teeth baring outward. Each of its teeth was over four inches. Its body was as strong as a giant elephant, with thick and strong limbs. This was a humongous hideous-looking lizard with an eight-meter body and four-meter height. Its body seemed to be brimming with energy and a burst of power.","The other fey was a strange-looking lizard over one meter. Its entire body was covered with dark-green-and-brown stripes. It had a huge tail on its back like a shield protecting the front of its body. This lizard’s body was only the size of a watermelon, but its tail was over ten times larger than its body.","Lin Yuan used True Data to check these two feys’ data.","First fey:","[Fey Name]: Smooth-Toothed Elephant Lizard","[Fey Species]: Toothed Lizard/Monitor Lizard","[Fey Grade]: Gold (6/10)","[Fey Type]: Water","[Fey Quality]: Flawless","Abilities:","[Tragic Claws]: Rapidly swing claws. While it tears the target, the claws’ mucus will penetrate the target, causing blood retention.","[Smooth Tooth Tear]: After biting the target, it will quickly shake its head and tear the target while rotating its body to twist off large pieces of flesh.","[Oily Mucus]: The body secretes a lot of Oily Mucus, which can effectively resist physical damage.","[Wave Stepping Strike]: Stimulate the water-element energy in the body to smash with full strength.","Exclusive Skill:","[Blood Burning Strike]: Burns all the water-element energy and blood in its body to launch a fatal attack through its tongue. It will enter a near-death state after the attack.","Second fey:","[Fey Name]: Huge-Tailed Swamp Lizard","[Fey Species]: Tailed Lizard/Scaled Lizard","[Fey Grade]: Gold (8/10)","[Fey Type]: Water/Earth","[Fey Quality]: Flawless","Abilities:","[Stinky Mud]: Shoots out highly corrosive and stinky mud containing pathogenic bacteria.","[Stinky Swamp]: Creates a stinky swamp within a small area around itself. If a target steps on it, he will be dragged deeper into the swamp by the sinking force.","[Mud Evasion]: Can hide in the stinky swamp and rely on it to avoid damage.","[Corrosive Mud Downpour]: Channels the earth-element and water-element in the body to make a downpour formed by Stinky Mud.","Exclusive Skill:","[Broken Tail Regrowth]: When the Huge-Tailed Swamp Lizard faces a fatal attack, it can use its tail to block the damage. It will break its tail and escape before rapidly using its body’s energy to grow out a new tail.","Upon seeing these two feys’ data, Lin Yuan knew that he was about to face an arduous battle. They were very outstanding in terms of abilities and exclusive skills.","One of them had returned to its ancestry line, while the other had undergone spiritual mutation. They were an excellent match with their control and burst of power.","Lin Yuan knew that if he made a mistake or was careless, he would lose this duel. But at the same time, this disadvantageous battle made him ignite his warm blood. This fervor was just like when he had resisted the insect tide outside Millstone Town.","On the dueling ground, Lin Yuan commanded Red Thorn to launch an offensive attack."]},{"number":200,"title":"Chapter 200: Black, You’ve Been Fooled","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Red Thorn spewed a huge amount of spores out of its spore cavity and formed a large sea of flowers thanks to its energy transmission.","It was not stingy with its energy for this duel. Under Lin Yuan’s command, it had spread the sea of flowers as much as possible to cover the dueling ground.","The Huge-Tailed Swamp Lizard was not idle either. It had used its ability, Stinky Swamp, to create a swamp nearly ten square meters. Since it was a spell-type unit, this ability allowed it to hide and avoid damage. That way, it could constantly use Stinky Mud or Corrosive Mud Downpour to attack from the back.","It lifted the mud toward Red Thorn’s child ramets, but what happened next secretly surprised Chen Hongfeng.","Its highly corrosive mud caused little damage to the sea of flowers. Lin Yuan did not find this surprising, as everything was within his expectations.","Red Thorn had to devour a large amount of dimensional lifeforms’ flesh daily. So far, it had devoured much flesh from Class 3 dimensional lifeforms, which were equivalent to Gold feys. This included the highly corrosive Class 3 alien insect, Acid Tapeworm. It had eaten the Acid Tapeworm with relish, without being affected at all. Therefore, its child ramets and ramets had high immunity against corrosion.","At that moment, the Huge-Tailed Swamp Lizard wanted to expand the swamp into the sea of flowers. It jumped to the edge of the sea of flowers and was prepared to use its Gold ability, Corrosive Mud Downpour.","Just then, Lin Yuan immediately summoned a fey that he had never summoned in the duel, the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly. He had released its skill, Silence Scale Powder, through Morbius on his wrist in the past.","Unfortunately, Morbius’ Silence Scale Powder was not as powerful as the one the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly released.","Once the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly appeared, a blue-purple glow flashed. As it flashed a few times, it disappeared into the sea of flowers. The scattered scale powder appeared as though it had created a light-purple mist. However, this magnificent mist was a complete disaster for the spiritually mutated Huge-Tailed Swamp Lizard.","The adhesive Silence Scale Powder landed on its body. As a result, the Huge-Tailed Swamp Lizard tried to form the Corrosive Mud Downpour but failed.","As soon as the Silence Scale Powder came in contact with it, it caused it to lose its sensing ability of the water and earth elements.","The Blue Flash Purple Butterfly, a legendary lifeform that had only existed in ancient texts, appeared for the first time in this duel before everyone’s eyes. It set off a storm no less than when Black had appeared.","After the Spirit Qi Awakening, the top ten most beautiful feys would be evaluated every year. The Blue Flash Butterfly could have been in the top five based on its beauty, but due to its weak ability at high grades, it had been ranked ninth.","Now that Lin Yuan had summoned the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly, it proved that the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly did exist among the Blue Flash Butterflies. At the same time, it also confirmed the authenticity of the ancient texts.","This year, the Blue Flash Butterfly might even have the qualification to reach the top three among the ten most beautiful feys.","When Chen Hongfeng saw the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly, he fell in a daze.","At that moment, Lin Yuan controlled Red Thorn to transmit most of its energy near the Huge-Tailed Swamp Lizard that the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly’s Silence Scale Powder had controlled.","Soon, Red Thorn’s most powerful ramets quickly spawned. The ramets’ vines grabbed the Huge-Tailed Swamp Lizard, which had been controlled by the Silence Scale Powder and could not sense the water and earth elements.","Chen Hongfeng had come back to his senses from his trance. Upon seeing that the vines had thorns, he felt things were bad.","The Huge-Tailed Swamp Lizard was a helpless target. If it was dragged into the large sea of flowers, how could it still make it out alive?","Thus, he shouted and ordered the Huge-Tailed Swamp Lizard to use its exclusive skill, Broken Tail Regrowth. After breaking its tail, it immediately became the size of a watermelon, and its tiny body scurried back into the swamp it had spawned. The swamp was slowly dispersing the Silence Scale Powder on its body.","At that moment, Lin Yuan supplied his spiritual power to the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly, which immediately released a large amount of Silence Scale Powder. This light-purple mist was like cherry blossom snow in the midsummer.","The scale powder fell with a unique halo, reflecting the swamp like a fairyland.","Lin Yuan used the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly to seal the Huge-Tailed Swamp Lizard’s movements.","The swamp that the Huge-Tailed Swamp Lizard had created was too small, and its body had been covered with the Silence Scale Powder, so it could not create the swamp again.","Therefore, the entire stinky swamp, which was less than ten square meters, was heavily mixed with the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly’s Silence Scale Powder, causing it to become a forbidden ground that isolated any elements. This forbidden ground had restricted its movements.","Red Thorn’s sea of flowers had surrounded this swamp, and a large number of Elite ramets encircled it.","Although the Huge-Tailed Swamp Lizard was a Gold VIII/Flawless fey, it did not have a powerful defense. If it scurried out, it would not have so many tails to break in the sea of flowers. Thus, it would be torn apart by the large sea of flowers into pieces.","Chen Hongfeng had a hideous expression at present, as he had not expected that Black would cripple his fey. It made him feel very passive. Likewise, Lin Yuan did not have it easy either.","Since Lin Yuan did not use the Spirit Qi Imprint, he had almost used up his body’s spiritual power. He had supplied a large amount of spirit qi to the Blue Flash Purple Butterfly and Red Thorn’s ortet, which allowed the Huge-Tailed Swamp Lizard to be sealed.","Although he could solve this problem with the Spirit-Gather Goldfish’s Spirit Qi Imprint, he did not plan to use it in any of the tower-climbing duels. Once he used the Spirit Qi Imprint and the spiritual power inside was released, it could only be stopped after exhausting all the spiritual power.","The Spirit Qi Imprint was one of Lin Yuan’s trump cards to survive in the real world. If he had not unsealed the Spirit Qi Imprint, he would not have been able to create a sea of flowers at Millstone Town that was enough to fight against the pinnacle Class 1 insect tide.","Thus, up to now, this duel was his real tough battle.","Chen Hongfeng’s remaining Gold VI/Flawless Huge-Tailed Swamp Lizard was a fey that relied on brute force. Although it would enter a near-death state after using one of its exclusive skills, Blood Burning Strike, its burst of power would likely finish off Lin Yuan.","Chen Hongfeng had commanded the Smooth-Toothed Elephant Lizard to charge toward Lin Yuan and Red Thorn’s ortet.","Even though the small sea of flowers that Red Thorn had spawned could cause damage to the Huge-Tailed Swamp Lizard, it could do nothing about the Smooth-Toothed Elephant Lizard, which had returned to its ancestry line.","Lin Yuan could even vaguely sense a trace of a dragon-species fey from the Smooth-Toothed Elephant Lizard’s body. It seemed that this Smooth-Toothed Elephant Lizard’s body vaguely had the possibility of returning to its ancestral line of a Liopleurodon.","The Smooth-Toothed Elephant Lizard used its Gold ability, Wave Stepping Strike, and dashed. Just as it was running, it suddenly experienced intense pain and roared in pain.","Lin Yuan’s Gold I/Legend Acid Corrosion Queen Bee had been hidden in an inconspicuous child ramet. When the Smooth-Toothed Elephant Lizard was close, the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee used Wing Stealth, allowing it to cover her tracks silently and use Two-Strike Kill on the Smooth-Toothed Elephant Lizard’s abdomen. Two long, slender abdominal stingers stung into the abdomen and injected venom into the body.","The Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s two abdominal stingers contained two kinds of acid-corrosion venom that instantly disintegrated the Smooth-Toothed Elephant Lizard’s abdomen into a bucket-sized hole. As soon as this hole appeared, many of its internal organs were affected by gravity and congested in this hole.","The Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s sudden attack had completely caught the Smooth-Toothed Elephant Lizard off guard.","Even though the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee had gotten an advantage, it did not retreat right away. Instead, it stung the Smooth-Toothed Elephant Lizard’s weakest organs congested in the hole.","It was still not over yet, even when it had shattered the organs. It even cruelly gave birth to a Parasitic Pupa.","When the Smooth-Toothed Elephant Lizard roared in pain and swept over with its tail, the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee used Wing Stealth to dodge into the flowers.","This large sea of flowers was the best battlefield and most helpful protection for the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee.","Because of the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s set of abilities, the spirit qi in Lin Yuan’s body had almost reached rock bottom. If it wasn’t for Red Thorn’s thornless vine supporting Lin Yuan, he would have instantly collapsed to the ground due to the spirit qi’s exhaustion that caused him to be weak.","As Lin Yuan used the last bit of spiritual power in his body to use the Spirit-Gather Goldfish’s Spirit Injection, he commanded Red Thorn to use its vines to block the action of him doing so.","At that moment, Chen Hongfeng did not worry about the Smooth-Tooth Elephant Lizard’s injuries. Instead, he suddenly wore a smile on his face, showing that he was determined to win, and said, “It’s close enough. Black, you’ve been fooled!”"]}]);
